window.AKK_GREAT_GRANDMOTHER_CHAPTERS=(window.AKK_GREAT_GRANDMOTHER_CHAPTERS||[]).concat([{"number":201,"title":"Chapter 201: This is not a place for celebrities to walk the red carpet.","paragraphs":["The capital was engulfed in a heavy snowfall.","Early in the morning, after Rong Yu finished washing up, the living room was empty. She pushed open the door to the adjacent bedroom and saw Ji Mohan still buried under the covers, sleeping. A pile of draft papers was scattered on the floor beside the bed.","Which meant this guy had been working on his research late into the night.","\"Great-grandma, I'm getting up right now!\"","Hearing the sound, Ji Mohan jolted upright, brushed his teeth with his hair a mess, and simultaneously pulled out his phone to order breakfast.","He actually didn't have the habit of eating breakfast.","But the old master had repeatedly instructed him to take good care of Great-grandma.","Ji Mohan ordered some local specialties of the capital.","Rong Yu sat in the living room waiting.","Ten minutes passed.","Twenty minutes passed.","Almost an hour passed... the breakfast still hadn't arrived.","Ji Mohan wore a miserable expression: \"Almost there, the delivery rider says two more minutes.\"","As soon as the words left his mouth, the rider's call came through, \"The delivery is at the door. No one answered when I knocked, so I left it outside.\"","Ji Mohan got up to open the door.","Suddenly, he remembered.","This was his second brother's home. The breakfast... seemed... was probably delivered to his own bachelor apartment instead.","Going there and back would take at least forty or fifty minutes.","Ji Mohan shrunk his head, slowly turned around, and looked guiltily at Rong Yu who had been waiting on the sofa for an hour: \"Great-grandma, I...\"","Rong Yu stood up: \"It's fine. We can buy something on the way to the Materials Institute.\"","Ji Mohan heaved a huge sigh of relief: \"Yes, Great-grandma.\"","He quickly looked up online to see which breakfast shops along the way had good reputations.","The car pulled out of the garage and stopped by the roadside: \"Great-grandma, this is an old Beijing breakfast shop highly recommended by netizens as the most authentic.\"","Rong Yu looked up at the signboard, which read: Old Beijing Douzhir.","Her eyelid twitched: \"Are you sure?\"","\"Absolutely.\" Ji Mohan, wanting to salvage his image, loudly asked the owner for douzhir. \"Netizens say this shop's douzhir has the most traditional fermentation process. One sip, and you'll remember it for life... Pfft!\"","He had just taken a sip when he couldn't help but spit it out.","Rong Yu, who had probably anticipated his reaction, blocked it with the scrap paper in her hand and called out, \"Owner, zhajiangmian.\"","She smiled and looked at her dear great-grandson. \"You've been in the capital for so many years now, and you still don't know what douzhir tastes like?\"","Ji Mohan counted on his fingers: \"I've probably only had breakfast about twice in the capital.\"","Rong Yu shook her head.","This child was exactly like her in her youth, completely devoted to research. Meals could be skipped, sleep could be forgone, bathroom breaks could be held if possible. Whether it would ruin one's health was unknown, because she had already died long ago...","She spoke up: \"If you're busy, you should hire a housekeeper to clean and cook three meals for you.\"","\"Forget it. When I get busy, I often don't go home for days on end. Hiring someone would just be a waste of money.\" Ji Mohan finished the zhajiangmian in two or three bites, picked up Rong Yu's bag for her, and said, \"Great-grandma, let's go.\"","The car drove all the way to the CAS Materials Institute.","As it was still the Spring Festival period, most people at the institute were on holiday, but some were on duty.","Ji Mohan led Rong Yu inside.","Just as they entered the main gate, they ran into a tall girl wearing glasses.","Rong Yu recognized her; this seemed to be the girl who had talked with A'Mo for a long time at the restaurant that day.","Lu Jiaojiao had been staying at the Materials Institute these past few days. After being promoted to Senior Researcher, she had been assigned a research project.","Others only knew she had achieved a senior title at a young age, but they didn't know her abilities were limited, requiring her to spend a great deal of time making up for the shortfall.","Afraid of being questioned, she was determined to do this research well.","She hadn't expected it to be so difficult.","Last night, she had messaged Ji Mohan, hoping for help. She truly hadn't expected Ji Mohan to come back early for her on the fifth day of the Lunar New Year.","Lu Jiaojiao adjusted her glasses and said, \"Mohan, you came at the right time. My work here has just started. You can work with me. You can be listed as the second author later, which will also be good for your promotion to Intermediate Researcher.\"","Rong Yu raised an eyebrow.","She hadn't spent much time with A'Mo and only knew he was a researcher, not his specific rank. From the sound of it, A'Mo was only a junior?","She had seen this kid's draft papers; the angles were novel, and his thinking and logic were sound. He should at least be at a senior level...","\"I came to the institute for something else,\" Ji Mohan said apologetically. \"And I have my own project to work on. Jiaojiao, why don't you find someone else?\"","Lu Jiaojiao pursed her lips.","No one else would unconditionally give her the first author position.","Moreover, collaborating with others would put a lot of pressure on her.","Only Ji Mohan didn't care about such gains and losses.","She was about to speak when she noticed the girl standing beside Ji Mohan. This girl was too beautiful, with outstanding features and a unique aura. Standing next to Ji Mohan, she was like a bright pearl next to a lump of charcoal.","This girl...","Lu Jiaojiao suddenly remembered: \"Is this Rong Yu, the celebrity who filmed the aerospace promotional video?\"","Ji Mohan nodded: \"We need to head in now. See you later.\"","He stepped aside to let Rong Yu go first.","\"Wait a moment.\" Lu Jiaojiao reminded him coolly, \"Mohan, this is a national first-class materials institute, not a red carpet for celebrities.\"","Ji Mohan frowned: \"What red carpet? We're here on official business.\"","\"Official business referring to filming a promotional video?\" Lu Jiaojiao's voice remained flat. \"The Aerospace Institute needs to cooperate with national publicity, but currently the Materials Institute does not. A celebrity coming to a key scientific research facility, besides causing trouble, I can't think of any other possibility.\"","Rong Yu looked up: \"That's because your perspective is narrow.\"","Lu Jiaojiao's calm expression cracked: \"You, a celebrity, telling me, a research scientist, that my perspective is narrow? I really don't know where you get such audacity...\"","\"Lu Jiaojiao!\" Ji Mohan's voice rose slightly. \"Watch your tone. Show some respect.\"","Lu Jiaojiao looked utterly incredulous.","Ji Mohan regarded her as his savior and had always been pleasant to her. No matter what unreasonable requests she made, Ji Mohan never spoke to her in such a tone.","Who was this female celebrity?","Could she be Ji Mohan's girlfriend?","If Ji Mohan had a girlfriend, would he still respect her, his savior?","Suppressing her emotions, Lu Jiaojiao said coldly, \"The Materials Institute is not a place where just any Tom, Dick, or Harry can waltz in. Non-staff must have a pass. Otherwise, I will report this matter to the higher-ups. Mohan, don't challenge the institute's discipline.\"","Ji Mohan clenched his fist.","How had he never known Lu Jiaojiao could be so mean-spirited?","Yes, mean-spirited.","He rarely used such a word to describe a girl.","Rong Yu glanced at Ji Mohan before speaking unhurriedly, \"The pass you mentioned, is it this one?\"","She opened her phone. The screen clearly displayed an electronic pass stamped with two electronic seals: one from the Fourth Aerospace Institute and one from the CAS Materials Institute."]},{"number":202,"title":"Chapter 202: I Must Prove My Ability Once Again","paragraphs":["Lu Jiaojiao's expression changed.","A pass jointly signed by two major research institutes was, of course, more than sufficient.","But the question was, why would Rong Yu, a minor celebrity and not a researcher, have obtained this pass?","She looked carefully; it indeed bore Rong Yu's name.","Rong Yu put her phone away. \"Now, may I enter?\"","Lu Jiaojiao stepped aside, clearing the path.","Ji Mohan led Rong Yu up the steps to the main entrance, swiped the pass, passed the facial recognition, entered, took the elevator, and proceeded into the experimental area.","Although Ji Mohan was only a junior researcher, he was the primary discoverer of the new substance, granting him the authority to retrieve it. He placed it before Rong Yu.","Rong Yu immediately began her research.","The materials institute had already provided the basic data and properties, which mostly aligned with her expectations. Now, her task was to determine how to make this substance the optimal material for space applications.","\"Ah Mo, I'll need samples of each of these substances,\" she instructed. \"I'm going to start synthesizing elements and running experiments to collect data. You'll assist me.\"","Ji Mohan nodded. \"Yes, Great-Grandmother.\"","Rong Yu's greatest expertise lay in mathematics and physics. While she had some involvement in the field of chemical materials, she wasn't as proficient as Ji Mohan, the specialist. Many details relied on his oversight.","\"Calculations indicate that Shi can form a strong coupling with graphene...\" Rong Yu frowned. \"But the change in Shi's electrical conductivity under microgravity doesn't fit the underlying model...\"","The two of them stayed in the lab until late into the night.","Rong Yu was still fully engrossed.","It was only when Ji Mohan's stomach growled with hunger that he realized they hadn't eaten all day.","He hurried out to buy food.","Once outside the experimental area, his phone regained signal. He saw a message from Lu Jiaojiao sent half an hour prior: \"Mohan, I had a minor car accident on the road. Can you come pick me up?\"","Ji Mohan called back. \"Jiaojiao, is the accident situation resolved? Are you okay?\"","\"Why did you only call me back now?\" Lu Jiaojiao complained. \"The car is undrivable, it's been towed. This place is in the middle of nowhere, I can't get a taxi. I don't even know how to get home.\"","Ji Mohan said, \"Send me the address. Wait a moment.\"","He brought the food in for Rong Yu. \"Great-Grandmother, a friend of mine had a car accident. I need to go help. I'll come back to pick you up later.\"","Rong Yu, immersed in her experiment, waved a hand dismissively.","Ji Mohan drove to the outskirts. After over half an hour, he saw Lu Jiaojiao waiting at a service area.","Lu Jiaojiao opened the car door and got in.","As a woman in the sciences, her interpersonal skills were poor. Her circle consisted only of senior fellow students and colleagues, with no close friends to speak of. As for family, it was better not to mention them.","She looked touched. \"Thank you, Mohan.\"","Ji Mohan drove her home.","Just as they pulled up to the Lu residence, his phone screen lit up with a new message.","Lu Jiaojiao glanced over casually and saw the preview of the sent content on the screen—","It was a file.","The title was: Shi-TaSe2.","Ji Mohan picked up his phone and opened it, his face a picture of astonishment.","He had only been gone for a little over an hour, and Great-Grandmother had already cracked this key problem. Some details needed filling in, a task that would fall to him.","Lu Jiaojiao was equally shocked.","She had been rather smug about becoming the discoverer of the new element, Shi.","Yet, Ji Mohan was already researching its synthesis with other elements and its applications across various industries.","Her achievement was, at best, theoretical.","What Ji Mohan was working on belonged to practical application, carrying far greater substantive value.","\"Mohan.\" They had arrived at the Lu house, but Lu Jiaojiao didn't get out. She turned in her seat. \"I am the discoverer of the Shi substance. I think I should be involved in your current project. Of course, you would be the primary researcher, the first author. Letting me be the second author would be enough.\"","Ji Mohan looked up, his voice devoid of emotion. \"Jiaojiao, last time, you said it was the final time.\"","Lu Jiaojiao looked at him. \"After being promoted to senior researcher, many people have been gossiping behind my back, saying I don't deserve the position. Such talk has hurt me deeply. I must prove my capabilities once again. Mohan, please, help me, okay?\"","She reached out and grabbed Ji Mohan's sleeve.","Ji Mohan frowned and pulled away. \"This isn't my project. I don't have the authority to decide.\"","Moreover, even if it were solely his project, he no longer wished to indulge Lu Jiaojiao in this manner.","\"I need to get back to the lab. You should get out now.\"","Having been given his dismissal, Lu Jiaojiao could only step out of the car, visibly reluctant.","When the car reached the lab, Rong Yu was still busy, and the food Ji Mohan had bought remained untouched on the side.","\"Great-Grandmother, stop working.\" Ji Mohan took the pen from Rong Yu's hand. \"If you don't take better care of your health, the Old Master will probably come storming over from Haicheng.\"","Rong Yu was indeed hungry.","Stepping out of the lab, she checked her phone—dozens of unread messages, all from her 'old son'.","She called back. \"Ying Bao, don't worry, everything's fine here. I'm having a meal now...\"","\"It's past ten at night, Mom. Are you only eating now?\" Old Master Ji shrieked. \"Put that brat Ji Mohan on the phone! How is he looking after Great-Grandmother? Letting her go hungry is utterly disgraceful!\"","Ji Mohan shrank his neck slightly. \"Old Master, my mistake. I'll do better tomorrow, definitely improve...\"","Old Master Ji couldn't be bothered with him and turned to give orders to Ji Yanting. \"Second Son, don't just stay at home either. Go to the capital and keep your great-grandmother company. You're the more reliable one.\"","Ji Yanting smiled, pleased by the praise. \"Yes, Old Master.\"","That very night, Ji Yanting took the last flight to the capital.","The next morning, when Rong Yu woke up, she was greeted by an enticing aroma. The dining table was laden with a variety of breakfast dishes.","Ji Yanting respectfully pulled out a chair. \"Great-Grandmother, please sit.\"","He glanced at Ji Mohan, who had just emerged from his room with messy bedhead and sleep in the corner of his eye, and shook his head. \"Ah Yan, you're so unkempt. You might have a hard time finding a girlfriend.\"","Ji Mohan looked up. \"Second Brother is well-groomed, and he doesn't have a girlfriend either.\"","Ji Yanting was left speechless.","Rong Yu enjoyed a comfortable breakfast and then took a car to the materials institute to continue her research.","For several days in a row, the research progressed exceptionally smoothly. She amassed a thick stack of raw data.","On the seventh day of the Lunar New Year, the materials institute officially resumed work.","As soon as Rong Yu and Ji Mohan entered,","someone approached and said, \"Mohan, Professor Li wants to see you in his office.\"","Ji Mohan handed his bag to Rong Yu. \"Great-Grandmother, please go to the lab first. I'll join you shortly.\"","Having been at the materials institute for a few days, Rong Yu was quite familiar with the layout. As she approached the lab door, she saw the light panel was on, indicating 'In Use'.","She frowned.","While Ah Mo might be a bit unreliable in daily life, when it came to scientific research, he ensured everything was done meticulously. He had clearly booked this lab for seven days. Had someone taken it over?","As she was pondering this,","The laboratory door opened, and Lu Jiaojiao stepped out."]},{"number":203,"title":"Chapter 203: It Seems My Elder Brother Wants to See You Again","paragraphs":["Lu Jiaojiao was dressed in a white lab coat, wearing glasses, appearing scholarly and meticulous.","She had only learned yesterday that the Fourth Aerospace Institute had applied to jointly research the new substance \"Shi\" with the Materials Institute of the Chinese Academy of Sciences.","The employee sent by the Fourth Aerospace Institute was actually Rong Yu.","And the researcher from the Materials Institute assigned to interface with them was Ji Mohan.","She pushed her glasses up and spoke with a smile: \"I have been in charge of the research on 'Shi' all along, so I'm relatively familiar with it. Professor Li asked me to participate in this collaboration project with the Aerospace Institute to help move things along faster. Miss Rong, I hope we have a pleasant cooperation.\"","Rong Yu glanced at her ID badge—Senior Researcher.","She nodded: \"We are short-handed, so thank you for your assistance, Researcher Lu.\"","Lu Jiaojiao's smile stiffened.","Why did she feel that Rong Yu had an air of superiority, as if granting her permission to join?","She had specifically asked around. Rong Yu was an assistant to a Professor Lin at the Fourth Research Institute, and she had also heard that Rong Yu was only a high school student with no official rank.","How could someone like that try to act superior to her?","Just as she was about to speak, she saw Ji Mohan walking over from the end of the corridor.","Seeing him, Lu Jiaojiao felt a bit guilty and lowered her head, pretending to organize the documents in her hands.","Ji Mohan glanced at her.","He had just been called over by Professor Li, who informed him that Lu Jiaojiao would also participate in this collaborative project with the Fourth Aerospace Institute.","Lu Jiaojiao had hit a wall with him, and then immediately turned to Professor Li.","Professor Li was the laboratory director and had the authority to make such arrangements. As a junior researcher, he could only comply.","\"In which areas is Researcher Lu proficient?\" Rong Yu had already automatically shifted into work mode. She put on her lab coat as she asked, \"Sample preparation, instrument operation, data recording, theoretical support, or safety control?\"","Lu Jiaojiao was taken aback.","A high school student who dabbled in the entertainment industry actually knew the detailed division of labor in a laboratory so well?","And why was it Rong Yu questioning her?","Shouldn't it be her questioning Rong Yu?","However, before she could speak, Ji Mohan answered for her: \"Jiaojiao is proficient in instrument operation and can handle safety control. I will handle sample preparation and data recording and analysis.\"","He put on his gloves and had already started retrieving samples.","Rong Yu was also repeatedly confirming the overall experimental plan.","Lu Jiaojiao wore an expression of disbelief.","How could such an important experiment be led by Rong Yu? On what grounds?","If these precious materials were wasted, could Rong Yu bear the responsibility?","But no one answered her doubts.","Rong Yu's cold voice came through: \"Researcher Lu, it's time to check the instruments and start them up. Pay attention to safety.\"","Her command made Lu Jiaojiao obey almost involuntarily. She put on her gloves and began preparing for the experiment earnestly.","Although her abilities were somewhat lacking, she was still among the more outstanding of her generation. Even relying solely on herself, she would eventually be promoted to senior rank. But because she was too eager to prove herself, she had borrowed Ji Mohan's help...","When she immersed herself in work, her attitude was beyond reproach.","With an extra helper, Rong Yu also felt much more at ease.","After who knows how long, the experiment finally concluded.","Lu Jiaojiao thought it was still afternoon, but when she looked outside, it was already dark—past nine o'clock at night.","She had actually been so influenced by Rong Yu's presence that she became completely immersed in her work, forgot to eat lunch, and had been busy until now.","Although, the feeling of being absorbed in work was quite good.","But—","She, a senior researcher, had been ordered around by a high school student who dabbled in the entertainment industry.","More crucially, she discovered that Rong Yu actually had some real substance. Sometimes, she, a senior researcher, couldn't even keep up with Rong Yu's train of thought.","After Rong Yu and Ji Mohan left the laboratory,","Lu Jiaojiao still needed to review the entire experimental process to fully understand the logic.","When she finally walked out of the lab, a few colleagues were still working overtime and casually greeted her: \"Leaving so late? How's the experiment progress?\"","Lu Jiaojiao smiled and said: \"With Mohan here, there's nothing to worry about. And Rong Yu, arranged by the Fourth Aerospace Institute, is quite diligent and was a great help.\"","\"What help can a celebrity be?\" a mid-level researcher said. \"I think this starlet is treating our Materials Institute as a stage for her show. Who knows how she'll boast about her own contributions later.\"","\"Don't say that,\" Lu Jiaojiao interjected. \"The fact that Rong Yu can be the spokesperson for China's aerospace industry shows she truly has capability. Those who can come to a place like ours are no simple individuals.\"","The mid-level researcher looked incredulous: \"She... she has connections, right?\"","Lu Jiaojiao pushed her glasses up: \"Stop speculating about others. I'm heading off now, see you tomorrow.\"","As soon as Rong Yu and Ji Mohan returned to the large penthouse,","a video call from the old son came through. She picked up an apple, lazily leaned back on the sofa, and then answered the call: \"Yingbao, didn't I tell you, I...\"","\"Xiao Yu!\"","Old Master Ji loudly called her name, cutting her off.","Only then did she notice that in the video, besides the old man's face, there were also two younger faces.","It was actually Sheng Ciyuan.","And Sheng Ciyuan's older brother with autism.","Rong Yu immediately sat up straight: \"Classmate Sheng, you and your brother, why are you at the Ji family home?\"","Sheng Ciyuan wore an expression of being at a loss for words.","After he called Rong Yu that day, Rong Yu had express-mailed the key to the Sheng family in Beijing.","He thought his older brother wanted the key.","But, his brother kept staring at the address on the express delivery packaging.","His brother couldn't communicate or interact. He went through great effort to guess that perhaps his brother wanted to go to the place on the express delivery.","He had almost risked his life... hiding it from the family, secretly taking his brother out.","The address showed a certain road and number. When they arrived, they discovered it was actually a vast private estate.","The Sheng family had some background, so he had someone investigate.","This was the old manor of the Ji family, one of the four major families in Haicheng.","But he didn't know why Rong Yu would be living here.","When they reached the estate gate, his brother acted as if stunned, standing dazedly at the main entrance, staring at the lintel, gazing at the eaves, looking at the ancient towering trees. His glass-like eyes were pitch black, like unfathomable ancient pools.","He had no idea what his brother was thinking.","After knocking on the Ji family's door and introducing themselves, the butler led them to see Old Master Ji.","As a result, the moment his brother saw Old Master Ji, it was as if he had been hit by a immobilizing spell, just staring blankly.","Old Master Ji frowned deeply.","One of these two, the younger one, had participated in a competition with his mother, so they were somewhat acquainted.","The other looked about twenty-three or twenty-four, very tall, with a cold countenance. Especially his eyes—they stared straight at a person, unmoving, not even blinking, making one's scalp tingle.","\"Old Master Ji, I apologize,\" Sheng Ciyuan said softly. \"My older brother has autism. I beg for your understanding. Could I please speak with Rong Yu for a moment?\"","Old Master Ji handed the phone over.","Sheng Ciyuan said, \"Rong Yu, it seems my elder brother... wishes to see you again.\""]},{"number":204,"title":"Chapter 204: This notch is a mark of height.","paragraphs":["Old Master Ji bristled at those words.","This tall, imposing man wanted to see his mother?","Was his mother some kind of casual acquaintance, available to see anyone who asked?","\"I'm in the capital, living at...\" She gave the address. \"I'm at the lab between 8 AM and 9 PM.\"","Sheng Ciyuan was annoyed.","If only he had contacted Rong Yu first, he wouldn't have made this pointless trip to Haicheng.","After ending the video call, he respectfully handed the phone back with both hands: \"Thank you for your trouble, Old Master Ji.\"","Faced with such a polite young man, Old Master Ji found it hard to keep a stern face. He feigned courtesy and said, \"It's so late. Do you have a place to stay? Would you like to make do here for the night?\"","\"No, no, that's quite alright,\" Sheng Ciyuan waved his hand. \"The Sheng family has property in Haicheng, not far from here. I...\"","Before he could finish his sentence,","Sheng Qingyan, who was standing beside him, had already stepped into the manor.","Old Master Ji's eyes widened.","Hold on, he was just being politely perfunctory. How could this person take it seriously?","\"Big brother, big brother!\" Sheng Ciyuan felt a headache coming on. He chased after him and grabbed Sheng Qingyan's arm. \"This is someone else's home, not our own. It's not convenient. Big brother, come with me to stay at the Sheng family villa, okay?\"","Sheng Qingyan shook off Sheng Ciyuan's hand and stopped under a very tall, tall tree just inside the manor entrance.","Winter hadn't stripped its leaves, and the night breeze rustled through them, whispering.","He reached out and touched the tree trunk, where several crooked marks had been carved, their edges smoothed by time.","Old Master Ji was taken aback.","These marks were height records.","The earliest ones were from his father's childhood, carved by his grandfather with a penknife. After he was born, his mother would also add a new mark for him every year.","The tree had grown taller, but the marks remained forever fixed in their original places.","\"Big brother...\" Sheng Ciyuan whispered, \"Don't wander around in other people's homes. It's impolite. Weren't you looking for Rong Yu? She's in the capital. How about we head back to the capital overnight?\"","Sheng Qingyan's glass-like eyes paused.","He nodded slowly.","Sheng Ciyuan let out a huge sigh of relief. Grabbing his big brother's wrist, he said to Old Master Ji, \"I'm truly very sorry to disturb you so late...\"","Old Master Ji watched Sheng Qingyan.","For some reason, a strange feeling surfaced in his heart, unclear and hard to define.","He wrestled with it internally for a moment. \"Well... perhaps you should stay after all.\"","\"No, really, we couldn't.\"","Sheng Ciyuan, terrified his brother might get another fixed idea, hastily bid farewell.","Old Master Ji's gaze lingered on Sheng Qingyan's retreating figure for a long, long time.","Early in the morning, when Ji Yanting's assistant arrived at the penthouse to deliver breakfast, he spotted two suspicious individuals squatting in the hallway.","The assistant thought they might be obsessive fans or paparazzi.","He was just about to call the police.","Sheng Ciyuan jolted awake. \"Don't call the police! We're friends of Rong Yu. We're waiting for her.\"","He was nearly driven mad by the ordeal.","One idea from his big brother, and he had rushed from the capital to Haicheng.","Then, in the middle of the night, back from Haicheng to the capital.","His plan was to go home first, get a proper night's rest, and arrange to meet Rong Yu after she finished work.","But his big brother was having one of his episodes, insisting on coming over immediately in the dead of night.","His relationship with Rong Yu wasn't even close enough to be called friendship; how could he dare knock on her door late at night?","He had desperately held back his brother's hand from knocking, dragged him to sit in the hallway, closed his eyes, and fell asleep. When he opened them again, it was daylight.","He quickly checked to see if his brother was still beside him.","Thank goodness, he hadn't wandered off.","Ji Yanting's new assistant was a man in his thirties. He said warily, \"Wait outside for a moment.\"","He opened the door, slipped inside swiftly, and closed it quickly. Looking towards Rong Yu on the balcony, he said, \"Miss Rong, there are two people outside who say they want to see you. Do you know them? If not, I'll call the police.\"","The assistant picked up a tablet and pulled up the surveillance feed from the entrance.","Rong Yu had been up for a while, having read on the balcony for over half an hour. She looked at the monitor, and her composure cracked.","Sheng Qingyan and Sheng Ciyuan, two handsome faces squeezed in front of the camera lens. Their stylish hair was disheveled, their eyes drooping. Their expensive cashmere coats were wrinkled like dried vegetables, resembling stray cats battered by a typhoon all night.","She could even hear Sheng Ciyuan whispering instructions: \"Big brother, this is someone else's home. If we go in, you must take off your shoes first. Don't sit down without the host's permission, don't look around randomly, and absolutely don't touch things...\"","No emotion showed on Sheng Qingyan's face.","Rong Yu walked over and opened the door.","As soon as the door opened, Sheng Ciyuan bowed at a ninety-degree angle, his face full of apology. \"I'm sorry, Rong Yu. I know showing up like this is very presumptuous, but my big brother can be very single-minded sometimes. When he decides to do something, he has to do it. Otherwise, he might exhibit severe stereotyped behaviors... It's really too much trouble for you...\"","He turned his head and saw his big brother staring fixedly at Rong Yu.","Sheng Qingyan's gaze was so intensely focused that all surrounding sounds, light, and smells seemed to collapse into a void—only the outline of Rong Yu remained sharply defined in the center of his dark pupils.","\"Big brother, it's impolite to stare like that.\"","Sheng Ciyuan reminded him softly.","Sheng Qingyan seemed to snap out of his trance.","Rong Yu spoke: \"You haven't rested all night, have you? Come in first, wash up, and have some breakfast.\"","Sheng Qingyan didn't move.","He pulled out a thick stack of black-and-white photos from his pocket.","Sheng Ciyuan was dumbfounded.","His big brother had brought these things he usually treasured like treasures when he left the house?","Every photo featured the same woman.","Sheng Qingyan looked at Rong Yu for a moment, then compared her repeatedly with the photos.","He flipped through the photos rapidly, his eyes darting between Rong Yu and the pictures.","Rong Yu noticed a thick wave of disappointment surfacing in his glassy, indifferent eyes.","Her long, curled eyelashes trembled slightly. She pointed to the woman in the photos and asked gently, \"Do you know the person in these pictures?\"","Sheng Qingyan's lips parted slightly.","His thin lips opened, closed, then parted again. His voice was hoarse: \"No.\"","It was like a child just learning to speak—each word slow, very clear, and heavily enunciated.","Sheng Ciyuan's pupils shook. \"B-b-b-big brother? Just now... w-was that you talking? You... you can speak? Big brother, say something else, let me hear... wait, no, big brother, where are you going? Why are you leaving!\"","Sheng Qingyan turned around silently.","Pressed the elevator button silently.","Walked inside silently.","\"I'm sorry, Rong Yu. I'll treat you to a meal next time.\"","Sheng Ciyuan hurriedly chased after him.","He pulled out his phone, opened the video recording app, and coaxed, \"Big brother, say something again. Just say what you said earlier. Mom and Dad would be overjoyed if they knew you could speak. Big brother, just cooperate a little, please? Big brother, don't ignore me...\"","Sheng Qingyan was like a wooden puppet.","He showed no reaction.","Rong Yu pinched the bridge of her nose.","This Sheng Qingyan, with his peculiar behavior, was someone she should naturally find off-putting.","She didn't know why she had given her address and allowed these two brothers to intrude into her private space.","Perhaps it was because Sheng Ciyuan was a mathematics and physics genius, making it hard for her to feel aversion.","Or perhaps it was because Sheng Qingyan was ill—with autism—and a sense of compassion had stirred within her."]},{"number":205,"title":"Chapter 205: Her So-called Genius Is Merely the Threshold to Witnessing True Genius","paragraphs":["Rong Yu continued to immerse herself in scientific research.","Lu Jiaojiao, no longer wanting to be constantly ordered around by Rong Yu, brought in a newcomer to participate—an assistant assigned to her by the institute after she was promoted to senior researcher.","With the assistant's help, she was much more at ease and spent her time learning beside Ji Mohan.","Outsiders called her a genius, but she knew in her heart that her so-called genius was merely the threshold to meeting a true genius. And Ji Mohan was a genius in the truest sense.","At sixteen, Ji Mohan had won gold medals in physics, chemistry, and mathematics, and was admitted early to Huaqing University. It was said that Jing University had also tried to recruit him at the time, even causing a minor scandal between the two top institutions.","She, on the other hand, had barely scraped into Huaqing with her college entrance exam scores. There was no comparison.","In his freshman year, Ji Mohan became a campus celebrity at Huaqing for participating in major projects and publishing papers.","Back then, she was still busy attending classes and getting various certifications...","Perhaps heaven favored her, giving her an extra layer of connection with Ji Mohan. That was how she entered the world of geniuses, got into the Materials Institute of the Chinese Academy of Sciences, and step by step became a senior researcher... If she had relied purely on herself, it would have taken at least over a decade, probably not until she was in her thirties or forties, to reach this position.","Lu Jiaojiao focused intently on staying by Ji Mohan's side.","But she soon noticed that Ji Mohan seemed to be constantly at Rong Yu's beck and call... Such a genius, actually playing second fiddle to Rong Yu.","She looked at Rong Yu in disbelief.","Immersed in her research, Rong Yu's face showed no expression. Her eyes were fixed on the data, like an emotionless experiment machine.","Suddenly, a flicker in her gaze, she spoke: \"Mo, quick, record this.\"","Ji Mohan's voice was filled with disbelief: \"The dielectric constant has exceeded 2000...\"","Rong Yu let out a soft sigh: \"Shi is exhibiting quantum resonance on a cosmic scale within the simulated deep-space environment...\"","This material, despite having many, many flaws, happened to perfectly compensate for existing shortcomings.","It was truly a perfect material.","But—","\"Mo, look, this noise peak. There's regular interference every time at 9.7 GHz.\" She frowned slightly. \"I suspect the dielectric loss of the superconducting resonant cavity wasn't factored in. We need at least three more sets of control experiments.\"","Ji Mohan swiftly recorded the experimental data and began preparing for the next round of control experiments.","Lu Jiaojiao picked up the data: \"I'll start on the report.\"","She was very skilled at theoretical analysis and summarization. With the data neatly laid out, it hardly required any brainpower. In less than two hours, a paper was completed.","A look of awe appeared in her eyes.","Earlier in the year, her paper on the new substance was at the basic theoretical level, simply describing where Shi was discovered, what its form and structure were like, its properties...","But this paper involved synthesizing Shi with existing elements to form an entirely new material applicable in the aerospace field. This was a brand-new breakthrough in materials science.","She printed the paper, bound it into a booklet, left the lab, and went straight to Professor Li's office.","She knocked and entered: \"Professor Li, our collaborative project with the Fourth Aerospace Institute has yielded preliminary results. Please take a look.\"","Professor Li hadn't placed much importance on this project.","After all, it was a newly discovered substance. Generally, it takes a long time for humanity to grasp its properties and begin to utilize it gradually.","He picked up the paper, quickly scanned it, and was immediately stunned: \"Using Shi-silicon synthetic crystals as a coating for deep-space probes? Can increase aerospace probe speed by five times? And extend service life? How did you think of synthesizing silicon with the new substance? Whose idea was this?\"","Lu Jiaojiao's eyelashes fluttered.","She had overheard conversations between Ji Mohan and Rong Yu and clearly knew this direction was first proposed by Ji Mohan.","She had saved Ji Mohan.","Everything of Ji Mohan's was, in effect, hers.","She looked up, her expression unchanged, and said: \"Last year, while studying the basic properties of Shi, I considered synthesizing it with various existing substances. Besides silicon, there was also...\"","She spoke eloquently.","\"Your thinking is indeed unique. The key is, the experiment actually succeeded.\" Professor Li's face was full of pleasant surprise. \"Jiaojiao, your unique perspective and experimental innovation explain why you became a senior researcher at such a young age. I wouldn't be surprised if you become an associate professor within two years. Having a rising star like you is a blessing for our Materials Institute.\"","Lu Jiaojiao wore a look of modesty: \"You flatter me, Professor. The success of this experiment is largely thanks to Mohan. Although he's only a junior researcher, his talent in experimentation is something I can hardly match... Also, the staff assigned by the Fourth Aerospace Institute provided all the aerospace knowledge. Otherwise, it would have been impossible to complete the experiment and paper in such a short time.\"","The smile instantly vanished from Professor Li's face.","There was another, deeper reason he hadn't valued this project: the staff assigned by the Fourth Aerospace Institute was actually a minor celebrity.","Since the Aerospace Institute didn't take the collaboration seriously, why should he invest his energy in it?","He spoke: \"The Aerospace Institute only provided theoretical support in aerospace science. In this research paper, that portion accounts for less than one percent. Therefore, even though the project was initiated by the Aerospace Institute, this paper should be published under the name of the Materials Institute. Jiaojiao, please arrange that.\"","Lu Jiaojiao curved her lips into a smile: \"Yes, Professor.\"","She immediately set about publishing the paper.","Back in the lab, Rong Yu and Ji Mohan were still busy.","They worked until six in the evening.","Ji Mohan looked up and said: \"My teacher invited me for a meal. Great-grandmother, would you like to join?\"","When a teacher invites you to dine, you must go.","But he was worried his Great-grandmother would get absorbed in work and forget to eat.","Rong Yu took off her gloves: \"What is your teacher's main research focus?\"","\"My teacher is Professor Chi from the Chemistry Division of the Chinese Academy of Sciences,\" Ji Mohan replied. \"He mainly researches polymer fiber materials.\"","\"Perfect. I'd like to chat with a professional in that field.\" Rong Yu tidied up the various equipment. \"The second set of control experiments still isn't quite right. Talking with your teacher might lead to a different breakthrough.\"","Ji Mohan quickly contacted Professor Chi. After confirming the location, he drove there with Rong Yu.","The dining spot was a hotpot restaurant by the window. As soon as they entered, they saw a small man in his fifties waving at them.","Ji Mohan, who had been standing quite straight, seemed to shrink into his shoulders like a mouse seeing a cat the moment he spotted Professor Chi. Scratching the back of his head, he called out: \"Hello, Teacher.\"","Seeing him, Professor Chi felt a surge of irritation: \"You keep making excuses when I ask you for a meal. A junior researcher, I don't know what you could possibly be so busy with every day...\"","Halfway through his sentence, he finally noticed the person standing beside Ji Mohan. His brow furrowed instantly, and he lowered his voice, saying, \"Don't tell me you've gotten a girlfriend? Your career is just taking off, and you're already getting involved in a romance. It seems to me you don't want to keep your position at the Chinese Academy of Sciences!\""]},{"number":206,"title":"Chapter 206: Becoming a Senior Researcher at a Young Age","paragraphs":["Ji Mohan's face paled in alarm.","\"Professor, you've misunderstood, she's not my girlfriend!\" he hurriedly explained. \"She is, is...\"","The words \"great-grandmother\" stuck in his throat, refusing to come out.","\"Hello, Professor Chi,\" Rong Yu said with a smile. \"My name is Rong Yu. I'm employed at Haicheng Fourth Aerospace Research Institute. Currently, I'm involved in a collaborative project with the Materials Institute concerning the application of the new substance 'Shi' in the aerospace field. I have a few questions I'd like to consult you on, Professor Chi. I wonder if you might be interested?\"","Professor Chi looked at her with disbelief.","As a traditional academic researcher, he didn't pay much attention to entertainment news, so he was unaware that Rong Yu had starred in an aerospace promotional video.","Instead, what struck him was how young Rong Yu looked—definitely not even twenty.","At such a young age, probably not even graduated from university, and she's already employed at an aerospace institute?","Professor Chi's interest grew. \"Have a seat. Order whatever you'd like to eat first. We can talk over the meal.\"","It was Rong Yu and Professor Chi's first meeting, so she didn't dive straight into work talk. After taking a few bites of the hotpot, she took out a printed experimental report and handed it over. \"Professor Chi, please take a look. The second set of control experiments showed an anomalous Tyndall effect...\"","Professor Chi immediately forgot about the hotpot, focusing intently on the report.","This wasn't the polished kind of report meant for publication, but more like casual notes. It lacked formal structure, yet every part was insightful.","He spent nearly half an hour reading the few pages.","After finishing, he looked up. \"The experiment simulated vacuum, radiation, and temperature differences, but it overlooked one point.\"","He took a pen from his chest pocket and circled a string of data on the report. \"Look here. When the pH value fluctuated from 6.8 to 7.2, your Zeta potential suddenly changed. These tiny, cumulative changes led to deviations in the results. Have you considered the possibility of cosmic dust?\"","Ji Mohan's eyes flickered. \"The latest external deposit analysis report from the International Space Station indicates that the main components of cosmic dust are silicates and iron-nickel microparticles.\"","\"Do you know why lunar module windows get scratched?... The surface hydroxyl groups on these nanoparticles, when excited by cosmic rays, can act almost like solid acid catalysts,\" Professor Chi explained. \"There should be some interaction between the silicon-oxygen tetrahedra on the surface of Shi crystals and the iron nanoparticles...\"","\"Thank you, Professor Chi.\" Rong Yu understood instantly.","Ever since her rebirth, every conversation with professors and academicians of this era had been immensely beneficial to her.","The ocean of knowledge was vast and boundless; she still had so much to learn.","Professor Chi looked at her with admiration. \"Young lady...\"","Hearing this address, Ji Mohan nearly choked on his food.","His family's ancient ancestor being called \"young lady\" felt utterly incongruous, no matter how he thought about it.","Professor Chi shot him a glare, then turned back to Rong Yu with a kindly expression. \"How about taking on another teacher?\"","Rong Yu replied, \"I'm sorry, Professor Chi, I already have a teacher.\"","Professor Chi sighed with regret.","Of course, such an outstanding young person was probably already under the tutelage of a renowned master. He just wondered who had acted so quickly.","Professor Chi didn't press further. He looked at Ji Mohan with mild annoyance. \"I originally asked you to join me for a meal today to discuss a project I wanted you to work on with me. But since you're already involved in this major project, we can talk about it after you're done.\"","The three of them chatted and ate, thoroughly enjoying the hotpot meal.","Early the next morning, Rong Yu and Ji Mohan went to the lab to continue verification tests for the control group.","As soon as they swiped their access cards and entered the main hall of the laboratory building, they saw a large crowd gathered around Lu Jiaojiao, talking animatedly.","\"Jiaojiao, your paper on Shi crystals is truly a milestone!\"","\"With this new synthetic substance, aerospace endeavors will take a great leap forward. You're simply brilliant.\"","\"To become a senior researcher at such a young age, Jiaojiao is naturally outstanding. Once this project is implemented, she'll probably be promoted directly to associate professor.\"","\"...\"","Lu Jiaojiao wore a carefully restrained smile on her face.","Previously, these very people had been whispering behind her back, saying she didn't deserve to be a senior researcher.","Now, they were finally convinced.","She looked up and saw Rong Yu and Ji Mohan walking in. The smile on her face instantly froze.","She cleared her throat and said, \"This wasn't just my effort; it was primarily a team achievement.\"","\"Your team only has four people,\" one researcher pointed out. \"One is Ji Mohan, a junior researcher—what significant contribution could he make? One is your assistant, a new intern at the Materials Institute who mostly runs errands. And as for the other...\"","Everyone noticed Rong Yu entering.","Her appearance was too striking among the crowd of researchers to ignore.","The people here were highly educated professionals with basic decorum. No matter how much they might privately look down on a celebrity, they were unlikely to gossip openly.","Another researcher turned to Ji Mohan. \"For this milestone paper, Jiaojiao even added your name as the second author. You might even be promoted to intermediate researcher by the end of the year based on this second-author paper. Since Jiaojiao is mentoring you like this, you really should treat her to more meals.\"","Lu Jiaojiao pressed her lips together and spoke to Rong Yu, \"Ms. Rong, as the representative of the Fourth Aerospace Institute participating in this project, your name should have been included as well, but...\"","Before she could finish her sentence, Rong Yu interrupted her.","Rong Yu's gaze was icy. \"Researcher Lu, the experiment is not yet complete. Please withdraw this paper immediately.\"","Her eyes were too cold.","And in Lu Jiaojiao's view, her attitude was particularly arrogant.","It sounded like an order.","Lu Jiaojiao, who initially felt some guilt and unease, was provoked by Rong Yu's demeanor and let out a scornful laugh. \"Is the big celebrity here to instruct us researchers on how to conduct science?\"","The surrounding onlookers regarded Rong Yu with even more peculiar looks.","They genuinely couldn't understand why someone from the entertainment industry would try to mix into the scientific research circle.","Could it be that nowadays, celebrities also needed to publish papers to secure resources?","Ji Mohan looked at Lu Jiaojiao with visible anger.","Before, when she appropriated his research findings, he let it slide because he truly owed her an enormous debt of gratitude.","But now, Lu Jiaojiao had published a paper without even mentioning it. First author: Lu Jiaojiao. Second author: Ji Mohan. No third author.","His great-grandmother was the initiator and primary researcher of this study. Lu Jiaojiao, who forcibly inserted herself as a supporting member midway through, where did she get the audacity to publish a paper? Moreover, there were still unresolved aspects of this experiment...","Under Ji Mohan's intense stare, Lu Jiaojiao's composure began to crack. She pressed her lips together and said, \"Let's go over there to discuss this.\""]},{"number":207,"title":"Chapter 207: Such a Great-Grandmother, Actually Subjected to All Kinds of Insults","paragraphs":["Lu Jiaojiao looked at the crowd. \"Everyone, please get back to work.\"","Without so much as a glance at Rong Yu, she lifted her chin, brushed past Rong Yu's shoulder, and walked into her office.","Rong Yu smiled. \"Mo, forget it if she doesn't want to retract the paper. There's no need to force her.\"","Ji Mohan understood what Great-Grandma meant.","He carried Rong Yu's bag, escorted her into the lab, and then strode into Lu Jiaojiao's office.","Lu Jiaojiao sat in her swivel chair, idly playing with the senior researcher badge in her hands. Her eyes traveled upward from beneath her glasses, calmly meeting Ji Mohan's gaze. \"Have you come to demand justice for Rong Yu?\"","\"So, you know perfectly well what you're doing is wrong, but you're going ahead with it anyway?\" Ji Mohan braced his hands on the desk. \"Let's not discuss anything else for now. This paper's experiments aren't even finished. Senior Researcher Lu, I'm asking you to retract this paper immediately.\"","\"Those few unfinished control group experiments don't affect the core findings,\" Lu Jiaojiao pushed her glasses up. \"Do you know how the field is evaluating this paper? They're calling it groundbreaking research. Do you know why Professor Li was so eager for me to publish? Because the Materials Institute has gone too long without any innovative research. This paper can restore the Institute's prestige... and it can help me become an associate professor in the shortest possible time.\"","She continued slowly, \"You're the second author. This will be a shining entry on your resume too. Or do you intend to stay in the junior researcher position forever?\"","\"As for Rong Yu,\" her voice turned icy, \"she doesn't even have a professional rank. How could I possibly add her name? It would make us a laughingstock.\"","Ji Mohan laughed, a sound born of extreme anger. \"Suit yourself.\"","The key points of this experiment hadn't even been cracked, yet she couldn't wait to publish first and claim the first authorship.","Fine. Let's see if she can handle the consequences.","Ji Mohan turned and left without another word.","It was the first time Lu Jiaojiao had seen such an expression on Ji Mohan's face.","Her own face tightened involuntarily.","What if Ji Mohan, for Rong Yu's sake, started spreading word about her past? She would definitely face scrutiny from all sides.","Forget it. Consider it giving Ji Mohan some face.","After all, he had genuinely helped her a lot these past few years. No need to ruin things over this.","She took out her phone and made a call. \"...I'm sorry, about the paper I sent yesterday, we're missing a third author's name. Is it still possible to add it now?\"","The person on the other end was very accommodating. \"Of course. Please provide the third author's name, professional rank... and a personal photo.\"","Lu Jiaojiao found a photo of Rong Yu online and sent it over.","Rong Yu and Ji Mohan worked in the lab until late at night, finally completing the control experiments. Rong Yu analyzed the data, Ji Mohan compiled the report. They worked together seamlessly, quickly finishing up and starting to clean the lab.","\"Mo, come here for a moment.\"","Professor Li suddenly appeared at the lab door, knocking with a very stern expression.","Ji Mohan put down his things and walked over.","The moment he entered the office, Professor Li picked up a stack of documents from his desk and threw them at Ji Mohan's head, his face furious. \"I heard from Jiaojiao that you insisted she add Rong Yu's name as the third author. Is that true?\"","Ji Mohan frowned. \"How could that be? I...\"","It was an immature research paper. He wished he could remove his own name as second author. Why would he ever ask Lu Jiaojiao to add Great-Grandma's name?","\"Look at the mess online!\" Professor Li's face was livid with anger. \"They're saying our Institute is corrupted by capital, guilty of academic misconduct. They're not just attacking Rong Yu, they're dragging the entire Materials Institute through the mud...\"","Ji Mohan leaned in to look at the computer screen.","After Lu Jiaojiao published the paper, it caused a significant stir within the academic circle, but it was just news within that community, unrelated to the entertainment world.","Until 3 PM, when the paper editors retracted and re-published it, this time with an added third author: Rong Yu. The news page listed the three authors in order.","First author: Lu Jiaojiao.","Second author: Ji Mohan.","Both were from the Materials Institute and had previously published significant papers, so netizens didn't find that odd.","But the third author: Rong Yu.","An excessively beautiful photo stood out glaringly on the page introducing this scientific achievement.","The internet exploded.","\"This is the most authoritative domestic platform for publishing papers. A celebrity's name actually appears as the third author?\"","\"Holy crap, isn't this Rong Yu, the one who starred in the milestone Chinese aerospace promotional film? What, playing a researcher on screen wasn't enough, she has to play one off-screen too?\"","\"A celebrity doing scientific research? Don't make me laugh. She probably can't even tell the difference between quantum mechanics and cosmetic ingredients.\"","\"Pay attention, everyone. The official platform retracted the paper first, then added Rong Yu's name. Did capital buy its way in?\"","\"Hah, researchers work their fingers to the bone, and she just waltzes in to pick the fruit? Does she think the research community is the entertainment industry?\"","\"...\"","Since the end of the talent show, among the nine who debuted, only Rong Yu, due to two national promotional films, had gained massive exposure, secretly making countless enemies.","Once this public opinion emerged, rival fans eagerly took the chance to kick her while she was down.","Even the Materials Institute was affected.","\"This is a major academic achievement, and a celebrity can still latch onto it? All I can say is the Materials Institute's integrity is probably compromised.\"","\"I heard she has powerful backing. This forced inclusion of her name on the paper is just to gild her resume and maintain her 'scholar' persona.\"","\"Her fans are still bragging in her fan community about how 'big sister is bringing glory to the country.' Hilarious. So researchers go bald from hard work, but it's the celebrity who gets the credit for posing in a promo?\"","\"The Materials Institute is rotten to the core, letting a celebrity meddle in academia. They should be thoroughly investigated...\"","Professor Li slammed the table. \"If you hadn't forced Lu Jiaojiao to add Rong Yu's name, our Institute wouldn't have become public enemy number one. Tell me, how should we handle this?\"","Ji Mohan looked up, his voice low and serious. \"For this project, Rong Yu was the initiator and the principal lead. The experiments weren't even finished before Lu Jiaojiao rushed to publish the paper. I believe, Professor Li, you should first hold Lu Jiaojiao accountable.\"","Professor Li let out a short laugh. \"You're telling me a celebrity, a high school student without any professional rank, is the lead on a major project?\"","Ji Mohan's voice was heavy. \"Professor Li, perhaps you should consider this: if Rong Yu had no capability, why would the Fourth Aerospace Institute trust her so completely, letting her shoulder such a major responsibility alone?\"","\"Because she has capital backing her,\" Professor Li said coldly. \"She's from the Fourth Aerospace Institute, so it's not convenient for me to take direct action against her. You go tell her that since the paper is already published, this project is hereby terminated. She doesn't need to come in tomorrow.\"","A wave of anger surged through Ji Mohan.","But he quickly let it go.","His emotions settled into calm. \"Fine. Let it be so.\"","He returned to the lab and saw Rong Yu still tidying the equipment. She carefully put every device back in its place, as if handling precious treasures.","This Great-Grandma of his was being subjected to all kinds of insults.","For some reason, a pang of sourness hit his nose, and his eyes instantly reddened."]},{"number":208,"title":"Chapter 208: Interpersonal Relationships Are Like a Piggy Bank","paragraphs":["Rong Yu heard the sound of someone sniffing.","She turned her head and saw Ji Mohan with red-rimmed eyes. She quickly walked over and asked softly, \"Did the leadership criticize you?\"","Ji Mohan shook his head gloomily.","The lab had signal jammers, so Great-Grandma's phone had no signal. She probably didn't know about what happened online yet.","But she would find out sooner or later.","He picked up Rong Yu's bag for her, and they walked out together.","As soon as they stepped outside, just as he was about to bring up the matter, Rong Yu's phone started vibrating.","Many messages flooded in simultaneously.","Yingbao, A-Yuan, A-Yan, A-Chuan, A-Ye...","Her teacher, Yun Xiaoyuan, Academician Min Shenyan...","Many classmates from Class Twenty.","And also Su Tian, Li Ying'er, Tian Tian, and others she met during the talent show.","With a quick glance, she understood what was going on.","She had gained a new nickname: Academic Daji.","Modern netizens were quite interesting, actually able to come up with such a fitting nickname.","Ji Mohan saw that she was actually smiling. \"Great-Grandma, aren't you angry?\"","Rong Yu patted his shoulder. \"Life is short. How can we waste our emotions on such trivial matters? You and I both know the truth of the matter, don't we?\"","Meeting her clear and resolute gaze, the frustration in Ji Mohan's heart slowly dissipated.","\"A-Mo, go get the car first. I need to return some calls.\" Rong Yu first dialed her \"old son's\" number, her voice gentle and smiling. \"Yingbao, are you angry again? Haven't I told you before, no matter what happens, you're not allowed to get angry...\"","Old Master Ji was very aggrieved. \"But those people are saying such terrible things.\"","\"Soon, those people will come to apologize on their own,\" Rong Yu said with a laugh. \"You, as the head of the fan club, need to play your role. Pay attention to guiding the fans, don't let them argue with netizens, stay rational. Tell the fans to please trust me.\"","Old Master Ji hurriedly took notes in his little notebook.","Just after hanging up on her old son, Rong Yu's phone screen displayed Shen Lin's name.","She thought for a moment and answered.","Shen Lin's voice was full of concern. \"Xiao Yu, I was in classes all day. I just got home, picked up my phone, and saw the news online. Is everything okay on your end?\"","Rong Yu: \"Thank you for your concern, Auntie. I'm fine.\"","Shen Lin said, \"You still haven't registered a Weibo account, so many things aren't clear to your fans. Would you like Yaoyao to help post a Weibo message to reassure them?\"","Rong Yu: \"No need, I have things to attend to. I'll hang up now.\"","After hanging up, Rong Ruoyao, sitting next to Shen Lin, frowned. \"Mom, didn't you see how badly Rong Yu is being cursed by netizens? My comment section is also a mess because of it. Why would you want me to help Rong Yu reassure her fans? It'll drag me down.\"","\"Yaoyao, why don't you understand? Interpersonal relationships are like a piggy bank. If you don't put coins in regularly, you'll have nothing when you need to use it,\" Shen Lin said earnestly. \"Rong Yu won the National Physics Competition gold medal, she's Professor Lin Rang's assistant, she's only eighteen and has already entered the Fourth Aerospace Research Institute... She definitely has the ability to resolve this crisis... If you proactively help her during her low point, then when she shines brightly in the future, you can justifiably ride on her coattails. Understand?\"","Rong Ruoyao bit her lip. \"But what if this crisis gets her blacklisted?\"","\"I don't think it will,\" Shen Lin said softly. \"She... probably isn't that easy to bring down.\"","Although Rong Yu didn't have Weibo, she had WeChat.","She didn't have the patience to reply to each friend individually, so she simply posted a moment: \"Thank you all for your concern. I'm fine.\"","Arriving home, Ji Yanting rushed up to meet her. \"Great-Grandma, I have a professional PR team here. Do you need them to step in and suppress these news headlines and hot searches?\"","Rong Yu shook her head.","This project had already concluded. The final experimental report was in her computer.","According to the usual procedure, she would report it immediately for internal disclosure.","But now...","For someone who plagiarized academic work, in her book, there was no forgiveness. They had to be removed.","Rong Yu did not make any public clarification.","A night passed, and the online controversy grew even more intense. Some uninformed bystanders also joined in, causing the heat to continuously rise.","Lu Jiaojiao sat in her chair and smiled.","Ji Mohan wanted to seek justice for Rong Yu, right? Well, this was justice.","Perfect. This Rong Yu was now not only notorious in academic circles, but her public persona in the entertainment industry was also ruined.","And she, Lu Jiaojiao, had become famous beyond her usual circle.","In the future, for academic endorsements in this field, the institute should probably feature her.","Lu Jiaojiao was lost in these thoughts when suddenly her assistant knocked and entered, head bowed. \"Sister Lu, Professor Li wants to see you in his office... Professor Li looks extremely angry.\"","Lu Jiaojiao chuckled lightly.","The institute was being cursed online, and the higher-ups were blaming Professor Li entirely. No wonder he was angry.","She walked into Professor Li's office, about to speak.","Then she saw Professor Li slam a printed thesis onto his desk. \"I just got a call from the aerospace institute. They conducted an internal simulation test based on your thesis. Why does the detector coating degradation situation completely contradict the stability description in your paper?\"","Lu Jiaojiao was stunned. \"That's impossible.\"","Professor Li's face was icy. \"Because the news is blowing up, many professionals have read your thesis. Take a look for yourself!\"","A group of big shots offered sharp critiques:","\"This thesis looks impressive overall, but the risk section is glossed over.\"","\"Why is there no relevant data for the risk control experimental verification? The Tyndall effect appeared earlier; a control group experiment should have been redone in a simulated environment.\"","\"The experiment is incomplete. Why was this thesis published? What's the rush?\"","\"Anyone capable of conducting this research experiment couldn't possibly fail to understand the importance of risk verification. What's really going on?\"","\"New substance, new research, new application—it is indeed an innovative milestone. But it still lacks risk data support. Recommend withdrawing this thesis...\"","Lu Jiaojiao's face instantly turned pale.","When she submitted this thesis, Rong Yu and Ji Mohan were precisely conducting the control group experiments.","Based on her experience of thousands of experiments, the data from these control groups wouldn't ultimately change the result.","Why did the simulation test show discrepancies?","Did the control group discover something different?","So that's why Rong Yu and Ji Mohan repeatedly asked her to withdraw the thesis?","Why didn't they just say it directly?","They deliberately let her make such a huge mistake and become a laughingstock.","\"You have twenty-four hours to produce the experimental data and supplement it,\" Professor Li said coldly. \"Otherwise, in twenty-four hours, this thesis will be withdrawn. You know what negative impact withdrawal would have.\"","Lu Jiaojiao lowered her head in humiliation. \"Yes.\"","She walked into the lab, looked at the equipment, and her mind went blank.","She put down the documents, walked to an area with signal, and dialed Ji Mohan's number. \"Mohan, I'm sorry. I was willful and reckless, and I've caused a huge disaster. But no matter what, I did save your life. You have to help me...\""]},{"number":209,"title":"Chapter 209: Scientific Research Is No Child's Play, Truth Tolerates No Tarnish","paragraphs":["Early spring in the capital was still cold.","In the early morning, after breakfast, Ji Yanting took Rong Yu and Ji Mohan to listen to traditional opera.","He thought that since Great-grandmother was from that era, she would probably enjoy listening to opera and watching plays. Sure enough, Rong Yu sat there with a look of intense concentration, and he knew his gamble had paid off.","Ji Mohan, however, couldn't settle his mind.","He kept glancing at the news online, where the focus seemed to have shifted.","It had moved from vilifying the big star for meddling in academic circles to questioning the research paper itself. Besides netizens, students from various universities and majors had joined the fray, analyzing the paper from every angle.","A frenzy was sweeping across the internet.","\"Buzz, buzz, buzz!\"","While scrolling through the news, Ji Mohan's phone suddenly vibrated with an incoming call. The screen showed it was Lu Jiaojiao.","He hesitated for a moment, then got up and walked to the side to answer the call.","\"Mohàn, you have to help me...\" Lu Jiaojiao adopted a humble tone, her voice soft. \"The institute is demanding supplementary risk control experiment data for the paper within twenty-four hours. I know you and Rong Yu are currently working on that part of the experiment... Don't misunderstand, I'm not asking for your results. What I mean is, since you've already done the control experiment once, you must have the experience. Can you come to the Materials Institute now and work with me to continue the experiments?\"","She planned to record the entire experimental process to silence her critics.","She intended to use this media storm to make a name for herself in the field.","However, Ji Mohan on the other end of the line remained silent, not uttering a word.","\"Mohàn, Mohàn...\" Lu Jiaojiao called his name softly. \"I still remember when we first met, on the tree-lined path at Huaqing University. We didn't know each other then, but my backpack was knocked over, and everything inside spilled out. That's how we discovered there was actually a connection between us long before...\"","Ji Mohan's fingers tightened slightly around the phone.","Back then, he was only sixteen, admitted to university early on a scholarship, completely immersed in his studies. He was reading by the lake when, suddenly feeling dizzy from low blood sugar, he fell headfirst into the water.","Fortunately, a passing student rescued him and sent him to the hospital, saving his life.","He never found out who saved him, only remembering it was a girl who wore a gold and jade pendant around her neck.","Much later, he unexpectedly met Lu Jiaojiao and saw the same gold and jade pendant fall from her bag. When he approached her to ask, he learned that it was Lu Jiaojiao who had saved him.","Before meeting Lu Jiaojiao, he had imagined countless times what the girl who saved him might be like. She didn't have to be exceptionally beautiful or outstandingly talented, but she must, without a doubt, possess a truly good and kind heart.","To jump into a lake without a second thought to save someone.","To leave without leaving a name after the rescue.","Such a person could undoubtedly be called truly good and beautiful.","But, Lu Jiaojiao was not.","Not sincere enough, not kind enough... As for beauty, perhaps she had some.","He asked her softly, \"You're someone who prioritizes personal gain above all else. I really want to know, why did you jump into the lake to save me back then?\"","Lu Jiaojiao bit her lip. \"Saving someone doesn't need a reason. I saw you were about to die and just gave you a hand. What, Ji Mohan, you don't want to help me through this difficulty, and now you're starting to question the debt of a life saved?\"","Ji Mohan's lips parted, and he spoke with difficulty, \"Jiaojiao, you are well aware of Rong Yu's capabilities. I can help you, but Rong Yu must be the first author. Otherwise—\"","Suddenly, a figure appeared beside him.","He turned his head and met Rong Yu's clear eyes.","Rong Yu reached out and took the phone from his hand. Her icy voice carried through to Lu Jiaojiao's ear.","\"Trying to claim repayment for a favor? Researcher Lu, you've truly broadened my horizons.\"","\"Before doing research, learn how to be a proper person first. Didn't your mentor teach you the most basic principles of academic ethics?\"","\"Scientific research is not child's play, nor is it a tool for you to seek personal gain!\"","\"If you dare use a life-saving favor to coerce Ji Mohan today, then tomorrow, will you use national projects to hold the entire academic community hostage?\"","\"I'm giving you time to publicly clarify this matter. Otherwise, you'll bear the consequences.\"","Rong Yu hung up the phone with a sharp click.","It was rare for her to show her emotions so openly, but matters concerning scientific research and academia made it hard to remain calm.","She tossed the phone back.","Ji Mohan fumbled to catch it.","\"I don't know Lu Jiaojiao well, but from collaborating with her these past couple of days, she hasn't demonstrated the competence or sense of responsibility a senior researcher should have.\" Rong Yu looked coldly at Ji Mohan. \"Am I justified in suspecting that she climbed the career ladder by stepping on you?\"","Ji Mohan hung his head low.","\"By condoning others appropriating academic work, you become an accomplice to academic misconduct.\" Rong Yu reprimanded him without mercy. \"As a researcher, if you can't even uphold the most basic academic integrity, do you feel ashamed when you put on your lab coat?\"","\"I... I...\"","Ji Mohan couldn't lift his head, his voice hoarse.","\"If you stay silent and condone this today, someone might pay with their life tomorrow because of this paper lacking proper risk warnings.\"","\"This data concerns the safety of astronauts' lives. It's not some bargaining chip for personal favors.\"","\"Scientific research is not a game. Truth cannot be tarnished. If you still wish to continue on this path of research, you should step forward and expose Lu Jiaojiao's academic appropriation.\"","She had thought this young man had firm principles.","She never expected he would wilt as soon as Lu Jiaojiao mentioned the life-saving favor.","She had said all she needed to say.","Lu Jiaojiao gripped her phone tightly, her lips pressed into a thin line, her whole body trembling.","If that bitch Rong Yu hadn't interfered, Ji Mohan would probably be by her side right now.","It was all Rong Yu's fault. Why did a celebrity have to come and compete with her for academic credit...","How could there be such a despicable person in this world...","The public uproar grew more intense.","Song Huai, who had been working non-stop for over twenty hours at the Fourth Aerospace Institute, had just stepped out when he saw many people in his class group chat discussing Rong Yu.","\"Rong Yu has really overplayed her hand this time.\"","\"Her abilities are fine for playing the 'academic genius' in the entertainment industry, but coming to the research circle to seek attention is just absurd.\"","\"One should be down-to-earth. Rong Yu is too flighty.\"","\"The teacher said we shouldn't look at things from just one perspective. Why not let things play out a bit longer?\"","\"Zhang Haoyu, why are you always defending Rong Yu? Do you have a crush on her?\"","\"...\"","Song Huai opened the news and skimmed through it rapidly.","He was instantly filled with disbelief.","For a major, top-tier research paper like this, Rong Yu actually managed to get listed as the third author?","These past few days, besides collecting data for the Fourth Aerospace Institute, he had also been helping several senior fellow students organize and publish their papers. One senior, who greatly appreciated his abilities, said he would list him as the third author.","—And this was just for a very ordinary research paper. The prospect of being the third author had nearly made him ecstatic.","But Rong Yu, she...","Was Rong Yu really that exceptional?","The internet was flooded with doubts and insults... Song Huai turned off his phone. He was busy and had no time to pay attention to all this."]},{"number":210,"title":"Chapter 210: I hope everyone will not involve other members of my team.","paragraphs":["Lu Jiaojiao had been in the laboratory all morning.","All the risk control group experiments for the new synthetic material at the aerospace institute had failed.","She directly applied to hold an internal press conference.","Extremely irritated, she took off her glasses and pinched the bridge of her nose.","In the scientific research field, errors in papers were not uncommon. After all, to err is human; occasional mistakes were normal, and one could simply retract the paper and re-demonstrate the findings.","But unfortunately, this matter had blown up too much and required a public explanation.","When it came down to it, it was all Rong Yu's fault.","If Rong Yu, a public figure, hadn't gotten involved, this wouldn't have become common knowledge.","\"Sister Lu, the reporters are all in position. You can go out now.\"","Her assistant knocked on the door to remind her.","Lu Jiaojiao put her glasses back on, straightened her white lab coat, fastened her senior researcher ID badge to her chest, picked up a stack of reports, and only then stepped out.","The hall outside wasn't large, accommodating only about a hundred people. More than half were industry professionals, the rest were media personnel.","As soon as she appeared, camera flashes went off.","A reporter was the first to ask: \"This paper has three authors. May I ask why only Researcher Lu is participating in this press conference?\"","Lu Jiaojiao walked up to the podium, first bowed to the audience, and then picked up the microphone.","She spoke calmly: \"I am the discoverer of the Shi element and the primary person in charge of this project. If problems arise, naturally I should be the one to take responsibility. I hope everyone will not involve other members of my team.\"","Professor Li looked at her with an appreciative gaze.","After the incident occurred, having the courage to take responsibility instead of pushing it onto the celebrity Rong Yu—this was indeed the attitude a senior researcher should have.","Lu Jiaojiao's image of a scholar who knew her mistakes and was willing to correct them made it hard for people to be overly critical of her.","She continued, \"Regarding the instability of Shi crystals under extreme conditions, it was indeed an oversight by our team. Scientific exploration is inherently a process of continuous trial and error. We humbly accept criticism and will continue in-depth research to ensure the safety and reliability of Shi element applications across various industries.\"","The professors seated below nodded one after another.","\"The Shi substance was only discovered a little over a month ago; it was inherently full of uncertainties. Expecting a thorough understanding in such a short time was somewhat demanding.\"","\"The completion rate of this research paper is as high as 98%. For a researcher as young as Lu, that's truly remarkable. She can completely be considered exceptionally gifted, a genius among geniuses.\"","\"Moreover, Researcher Lu's candid attitude is worthy of respect. Scientific progress precisely needs this kind of courage to admit limitations.\"","It's not terrible for young people to make mistakes; the key is to have the awareness to correct them, like Lu Jiaojiao. Such talents should be key cultivation targets.","\"...\"","These remarks reached Lu Jiaojiao's ears.","She lowered her head, a slight curve appearing at the corner of her lips.","Even without Ji Mohan's help in providing the control group experimental data, she could still extricate herself from another angle.","Once the controversy had died down, she naturally had ways to supplement the data for this paper and republish it.","Just as the atmosphere was perfectly harmonious—","The hall door was suddenly pushed open, and a man and a woman walked in side by side.","Ji Mohan was only a junior researcher, not qualified to make a public appearance on any occasion, so not many people here knew him... except, of course, for Professor Chi.","Professor Chi was a veteran in the chemistry department. He had also been invited to this press conference concerning the new substance.","Sitting next to him was Lu Jiaojiao's supervisor, Professor Zhou.","Since the press conference began, Professor Zhou had been recounting Lu Jiaojiao's scientific research achievements over the years into the microphone: \"...Back then, you didn't want to accept Lu Jiaojiao as a student, so the Lu family sent her to me instead. Over these years, the student who has given me the least worry is Jiaojiao. For her to achieve such great success has truly exceeded my expectations... Young people make mistakes, it's normal. What's frightening is that some people don't even have the opportunity to make mistakes.\"","Professor Chi was choking.","This was clearly a veiled jab at him for taking on a worthless student.","That kid Ji Mohan, clearly gifted, yet somehow, after all these years, still hadn't made a name for himself.","\"If there's a problem with Jiaojiao's project, it's very likely because of that celebrity called Rong Yu,\" Professor Zhou said, tugging at the corner of his mouth. \"Even celebrities these days can adopt the persona of a researcher. The world really is going downhill. The country should properly regulate it.\"","Professor Chi frowned.","Taking digs at Ji Mohan was one thing—after all, that kid really was hopeless; he could just lie back and take the ridicule.","But as for Rong Yu...","That night, while they ate hot pot together, they talked for a long time, in great depth. In his view, Rong Yu even had more talent than Ji Mohan.","He couldn't help but retort: \"Professor Zhou, your student's apology is moving, but it doesn't clearly explain the key issues...\"","He had only gotten halfway through his sentence.","Everyone in the hall turned their heads in unison.","Professor Chi saw Rong Yu and his underachieving student, Ji Mohan.","Professor Zhou snorted, \"A celebrity—what significant contribution could they have made to this paper? And yet they're even listed as the third author. Without a clear explanation, it's hard to calm the public's anger.\"","On the stage, Lu Jiaojiao, looking at the two who had walked in, was momentarily stunned.","Ji Mohan was nothing to fear.","As for Rong Yu, a celebrity—who would believe a celebrity had any real substance?","When a celebrity is embroiled in such a public controversy, no matter what they explain, the public probably wouldn't believe it.","The public's doubts would be enough to cause Rong Yu to drown.","There were quite a few reporters present. Their cameras turned and aimed at Rong Yu's face.","Professor Li quickly stood up: \"Rong Yu, what are you doing here? This is the materials institute's press conference, not a celebrity publicity event. Please leave.\"","Rong Yu stood at the entrance. The lighting seemed to especially favor her; the moment she appeared, all attention automatically shifted to her.","She said softly, \"Researcher Lu, I have a few questions I'd like to ask. I hope you can clarify them for me in public.\"","Lu Jiaojiao's expression began to give way.","She had worked with Rong Yu for only two short days. During those two days she had been treated like a menial. She knew full well that Rong Yu was the real deal and didn't need her to clear anything up.","She knew this was no friendly visitor.","So, she gave Professor Li a look.","Everything that needed to be explained had been said, the apology had been made, and the press conference should be over. Professor Li stood up: \"Everyone, that's all for today...\"","\"Hold on.\" Professor Chi stood up. \"I'd like to hear what questions Rong Yu has. If Researcher Lu cannot clarify them for her, then we old pedants here present should be able to answer.\"","Professor Zhou even laughed: \"A celebrity, what questions could they possibly have? Could it be they want to ask whether the synthesis of Shi crystals is physical vapor deposition or chemical vapor deposition? After all, for people in your industry, being able to tell a test tube from a beaker is pretty good already.\""]},{"number":211,"title":"Chapter 211: Researchers focus solely on scientific research, while female celebrities concentrate on building their public personas.","paragraphs":["Rong Yu paid no mind to the gazes of the others.","Her expression was placid, her gaze falling on Lu Jiaojiao's head like an intangible blade.","\"In extreme environments, the surface of the Shi crystal will develop nanopores due to atomic oxygen erosion, with a one-in-a-thousand probability of causing quantum state collapse. Why did Researcher Lu's paper avoid this issue?\"","\"NASA confirmed as early as last century that reactive hydroxyl groups on interstellar dust surfaces accelerate material aging—why was this item omitted from your control group?\"","As soon as she posed these questions, everyone present was stunned.","Wasn't she a celebrity?","Why did she know so much about scientific research?","Her consecutive questions were not without logical structure; on the contrary, they tightly grasped the most core issues of Lu Jiaojiao's research paper, which were also the key points of public skepticism towards the paper.","Lu Jiaojiao bit her lip.","This Rong Yu was indeed here to cause trouble.","She took a deep breath and said, \"Regarding this issue, we previously discussed it in the lab. Rong Yu, if you don't understand, I can explain it to you slowly in private. There's no need for you to ask these questions in public; it's rather pointless.\"","Some onlookers in the hall were immediately swayed by this narrative.","\"A big celebrity dabbling in the entertainment industry asking these questions really is pointless.\"","\"Researcher Lu has already publicly apologized, and she's still nitpicking here. Isn't she deliberately making things difficult?\"","\"Researchers dedicate themselves to science, while female celebrities are busy building their personas. The difference is clear.\"","\"Tsk tsk, just kick her out already.\"","\"...\"","Lu Jiaojiao looked at the crowd with an apologetic expression. \"It was my oversight that led to such serious consequences. I apologize once again to the public. Let's end here for today. Please leave in an orderly manner.\"","\"Researcher Lu is in such a hurry to end the event. What are you worried about?\" Rong Yu casually pulled a notebook from her backpack.","Ji Mohan quickly connected via Bluetooth to the large screen in the hall.","Key data from the control group experiments appeared on the screen.","First set of data: Atomic oxygen extreme environment test.","Second set of data: Cosmic dust catalysis experiment.","Third set of data: Solar storm extreme simulation.","Several pages of data, not a single superfluous word; even the punctuation was essential.","Most shocking was a real-time recording—under simulated CME (coronal mass ejection) conditions, the Shi crystal underwent chain disintegration in just three hours, its fragments forming a deadly metallic cloud within the vacuum chamber.","Lu Jiaojiao's face instantly turned deathly pale.","Professor Li had suspended the lab's usage privileges that very day. She had thought Rong Yu and Ji Mohan's experiment was interrupted and yielded no results, which was why she dared to hold this public press conference.","In such a short time, just the two of them had completed three sets of highly challenging control experiments?","How... how was this possible?","It was absurd.","The professors seated in the hall looked utterly shaken, rising abruptly to their feet.","\"This... this is in-situ observation using synchrotron radiation? Our country just recently broke through this technical bottleneck; very few can achieve this!\"","\"She actually replicated the quantum tunneling effect at the interface between solar wind plasma and the material! As an old hand, I might not succeed once in a hundred attempts.\"","\"The design of this control experiment is too perfect—temperature gradient, particle flux, dust, even cosmic ray fluctuations were considered...\"","\"...\"","Everyone looked at Rong Yu with disbelief.","Was such a flawless experimental demonstration process her work?","Was... was this even possible?","Rong Yu lifted her eyes. \"This is the complete risk assessment report. The blame should not be placed on the instability of the Shi element.\"","Lu Jiaojiao, her face pale, adjusted her glasses and said, \"Excellent. With this supplemental experimental data, this paper can truly become an innovative milestone in the industry.\"","Saying this eased her tension considerably, and she immediately smiled. \"These past few days, there have been many voices online questioning my team member, Rong Yu. Now, everyone has seen that Rong Yu is not what many believed her to be. She is a highly capable individual, fully qualified to be the third author of this research paper.\"","The looks directed at Rong Yu in the hall did indeed change.","In the face of genuine ability, all rumors and slander are paper tigers, collapsing on their own.","\"Is that so?\"","Ji Mohan, who had remained largely unnoticed until now, suddenly spoke.","His skin was very dark, and standing next to the strikingly beautiful Rong Yu, he was easily overlooked.","However, when he straightened his back, drew himself up, raised his head, and fixed his intense gaze on Lu Jiaojiao, people finally noticed him.","He raised his voice. \"Lu Jiaojiao, do you truly believe Rong Yu is only qualified to be the third author?\"","Lu Jiaojiao's heart was suddenly gripped by panic.","She reached up to adjust her glasses, inadvertently brushing aside her bangs and revealing a scar. Her gaze at Ji Mohan held a trace of annoyance, but also a plea.","She had saved him.","Did he have to embarrass her publicly?","\"Your silence is because you dare not face this question squarely.\" Ji Mohan walked step by step onto the stage, stopping beside Lu Jiaojiao, standing under the spotlight.","He looked at the audience below, then at Rong Yu's gratified expression, and found courage within.","A life-saving debt was one thing.","Academic plagiarism was another.","The two should not be conflated.","\"This is the project initiation document.\" Ji Mohan pressed a remote, and the screen changed to show an approval document from the Fourth Aerospace Institute and the Institute of Materials Science, Chinese Academy of Sciences.","The field for \"Initiator\" clearly bore Rong Yu's name.","\"She's the initiator?\"","\"The Aerospace Institute actually let a female celebrity be the project initiator? You must be joking.\"","\"Doesn't this sufficiently prove she indeed has the capability? Should we deny her ability just because she's a public figure?\"","\"...\"","\"Yes, Rong Yu is the project proposer.\" Ji Mohan enunciated each word clearly. \"She is the primary responsible person, the one who finalized the research plan. All experiments were first framed by Rong Yu... As for Lu Jiaojiao, she joined only on the fifth day of the experiment. The work she did isn't even sufficient to warrant her being listed as the third author.\"","Lu Jiaojiao's face was ashen. \"You're lying! I am the discoverer of the Shi element. All experimental demonstrations related to this aspect in the study were conducted by me...\"","Ji Mohan did not look at her.","He clicked to the final page on the large screen.","It displayed his chat history with Lu Jiaojiao, line by line, laid out before the public like ironclad evidence.","\"Mohan, the oxidation behavior of ultra-high-temperature ceramic matrix composites in thermal protection systems for aircraft—this argument is insufficient. Can you help me supplement it?\"","\"Mohan, my advisor wants me to research topological insulators. You're more skilled in this area. Could you help me with the preliminary work?\"","\"Mohan, I just can't figure out the key technical points of this research. Could you help...\"","All the chat records were one-sided requests for help from Lu Jiaojiao."]},{"number":212,"title":"Chapter 212: Professors Compete to Enroll the Celebrity as Their Student","paragraphs":["The crowd was utterly stunned.","\"A senior researcher, needing to ask a junior researcher for help?\"","\"Aren't these supposed to be Lu Jiaojiao's most authoritative scientific achievements over the years?\"","\"If she's not proficient in these topics, why did she conduct research in these areas? What on earth has she been doing?\"","\"Ji Mohan solved the vast majority of the technical challenges. Shouldn't these be Ji Mohan's achievements?\"","\"...\"","Professor Chi's face changed dramatically.","So that was it. No wonder Ji Mohan had faded into obscurity over just a few short years, while Lu Jiaojiao had grown increasingly outstanding.","So, his student's work had truly been appropriated by Lu Jiaojiao.","Furious, his old face flushed red. \"Professor Zhou, have you not taught your student how to conduct herself? In this field, academic misconduct is the most intolerable offense!\"","Professor Zhou was also aghast. \"Impossible! Jiaojiao would never do such a thing!\"","He stood up and said loudly, \"Jiaojiao, explain yourself immediately!\"","If this were confirmed, not only Lu Jiaojiao, but even he, as her advisor, would face serious repercussions.","Lu Jiaojiao felt dizzy.","Since university, she had relied on Ji Mohan to complete various highly technical research papers, and there had never been a single issue.","She had thought that no matter what, Ji Mohan would never humiliate her in public.","Yet, he was being this ruthless.","She had saved his life.","How could he possibly destroy her?","She saw countless fingers pointing at her, felt the weight of everyone's skeptical gazes. She knew she needed to explain, but how?","What if someone asked questions about those papers? She might not be able to answer a single word. That would make it even harder to recover...","\"I condoned Lu Jiaojiao's appropriation of academic work, a serious violation of the fundamental principles of research integrity. I am deeply ashamed,\" Ji Mohan bowed his head. \"As a researcher, I have betrayed the trust of the Materials Institute and am willing to accept any disciplinary action from the leadership.\"","He removed his work ID and placed it on the table.","Professor Li, the head of the Materials Institute laboratory, was so enraged he threw a file at Lu Jiaojiao's head. \"Speak up! What is the meaning of all this?\"","Lu Jiaojiao could barely stand, swaying unsteadily.","Seeing this, the crowd understood everything. The hall erupted in an uproar.","Several senior professors were filled with indignation.","\"This is a desecration of the academic temple! In thirty years, I have never seen such brazen academic theft!\"","\"Back in our day, we worked ourselves to the bone in the Gobi desert to verify a single data point. She just opens her mouth and someone else does the work for her. What kind of researcher is that?\"","\"In all future materials science classes, the name Lu Jiaojiao will serve as a cautionary tale, a reminder of what constitutes academic disgrace.\"","The editor-in-chief of the journal side said coldly, \"We will retract all papers from Lu Jiaojiao's team from the past five years and initiate an academic integrity investigation.\"","\"...\"","Live news from the scene was streamed online in real-time.","\"What's going on? Rong Yu, an actress, just publicly exposed a professional researcher?\"","\"She only filmed that aerospace promotional video, right? No one told me she was also a professional. This is unbelievable.\"","\"She won the national physics competition gold medal and got a special contribution award from the Aerospace Institute to enter Huaqing University. That proves she has real talent. Shouldn't the netizens apologize now?\"","\"Got to admit, this Lu Jiaojiao is something else. She actually became a senior researcher through academic misconduct.\"","\"This is an 'academic Daji'—using her looks to gain resources and easily reach heights ordinary people can't.\"","\"Lu Jiaojiao isn't even that good-looking, is she?\"","\"You guys don't know? Lu Jiaojiao is the heiress of the Lu family. You know, that huge national real estate conglomerate.\"","\"Well, well. So Miss Lu is the real capital behind it all.\"","\"Poor Ji Mohan, sucked dry by capitalists for so many years. If it weren't for Rong Yu's celebrity influence, who knows how much longer Miss Lu would have stayed hidden.\"","\"My sympathies to Ji Mohan.\"","\"Poor leek.\"","\"...\"","Back at the scene, Professor Zhou said coldly, \"Lu Jiaojiao has committed academic fraud. My mentorship relationship with her ends here.\"","He turned and left, not wanting to face further embarrassment.","Laboratory Director Professor Li, regaining his composure, picked up the microphone. \"Regarding this matter, our institute will arrange a special investigation team to conduct a thorough inquiry. We will definitely provide the public with an explanation. That's all for today. Please exit through the main doors.\"","The reporters were reluctant to leave.","They still wanted to interview Rong Yu.","After all, someone from the entertainment industry getting involved with academia was a first in the domestic entertainment scene in years—an absolute exclusive story.","But they were all a step too late. Rong Yu was already surrounded by a group of senior professors.","\"Young lady, would you be interested in being my student?\"","\"Young lady, I saw your experimental demonstration just now. You seem to have a particular sensitivity to numbers. Would you consider me as your teacher...\"","A large crowd encircled Rong Yu.","This scene was captured by reporters and featured in news segments under the headline: \"Professors Vie for Celebrity as Their Student.\"","Netizens found it absurd.","\"Other celebrities: street style, scandals, livestream sales. Rong Yu: research, professors, mentorship.\"","\"An actress, this impressive? Having professors fight to take her as a student?\"","\"I know she's talented, but this is a bit much. It's too unbelievable.\"","\"These professors can't possibly be acting for the capital, can they?\"","\"...\"","It was just past noon.","Song Huai had been invited for a meal at the Rong family home.","When the news broke, their phones received push notifications, and people were discussing it in group chats.","For the past few days, Rong Yu's name had been all over the trending searches, facing doubt and criticism. Rong Ruoyao had also been affected, and she had been blaming her mother, Shen Lin, for not publicly distancing themselves from Rong Yu sooner.","Now, seeing the latest news, she realized Shen Lin had been right.","Netizens were like weathervanes. One moment they were cursing Rong Yu, the next they were flooding her Weibo comments to apologize profusely... even pulling her onto the tail end of the trending list.","Shen Lin spoke up, \"Xiao Yu has cleared her name of the public's doubts this time. If she could secure a mentor, it would be greatly beneficial for her future development.\"","Rong Wangtian was beaming with joy. \"Yao Yao is in the entertainment industry, Xiao Yu is in the research field. Both sisters are achieving great things. Excellent, excellent! Our Rong family ancestors must be smiling from the grave. Qing'an, you need to learn more from your two older sisters.\"","Rong Qing'an didn't dare utter a word.","Before, with his grandfather's protection, he could afford to be willful and immature.","Ever since his grandfather was sent back to their hometown, he had been subjected to almost daily scoldings from both parents and had long since been tamed.","Song Huai remained silent.","These senior professors surrounding Rong Yu, having reached this age and still being professors, showed they lacked the innate talent to become academicians.","For Rong Yu to take a professor as her mentor meant, to some extent, she would never surpass him.","Because his own mentor, Liu Jinyue, was an academician.","He also had two senior brothers who had become professors.","With the guidance and support of his mentor and senior brothers, he would go far on this path."]},{"number":213,"title":"Chapter 213: Unless It Wasn't You Who Saved Mohan in the First Place","paragraphs":["The press conference came to an end.","Rong Yu was surrounded by senior professors, fielding questions left and right. It took over ten minutes before she could finally, with some difficulty, extricate herself and Ji Mohan from the main hall.","Just as they turned a corner, a figure suddenly stepped out.","Lu Jiaojiao's research lab coat had been reclaimed, and her senior researcher ID badge, the symbol of her status, had also been confiscated. She stood there dejectedly, her eyes fixed on Ji Mohan, her voice hoarse: \"Mohan, we need to talk.\"","Ji Mohan saw her flushed face, likely from Professor Li's slap. He spoke: \"Jiaojiao, what you need to do now is cooperate with the institute's investigation.\"","\"Investigation? Investigate what? What is there to investigate?\" Lu Jiaojiao's voice suddenly turned shrill. \"Ji Mohan, you've ruined me, do you know that? My career, my future, you've destroyed it all... What am I supposed to do now? What should I do?\"","This matter didn't even require an investigation.","Because the core, difficult techniques in her research achievements all came from Ji Mohan. Just a few probing questions on the relevant topics would leave her utterly defenseless.","She would be expelled from the institute.","She would become a stain on the industry.","She would be forever nailed to the pillar of shame.","And, she could never again set foot in the field she loved.","She had studied so hard since childhood, learning day and night while others ate, drank, and had fun, burying herself in books while others traveled... She had struggled so hard to reach this height, only to plunge into an abyss at the peak of her life. How could she possibly accept this...","Large tears rolled down Lu Jiaojiao's cheeks, her crimson eyes locked on Ji Mohan. \"I saved you. I am your savior, Ji Mohan. How could you do this to me!\"","Ji Mohan's lips tightened.","Once the debt of life-saving was brought up, normal conversation became impossible.","\"Harm you?\" Rong Yu's voice chimed in. \"Ms. Lu, perhaps you haven't quite grasped that it was your personal transaction with Ji Mohan that nearly harmed the nation's scientific research endeavors!\"","Lu Jiaojiao's eyes slowly shifted and landed on Rong Yu.","She stared fixedly at Rong Yu, unable to control herself. \"It's all because of you. It was you who incited Ji Mohan to do such a thing at the press conference. How have I wronged you, for you to harm me like this! You accuse me of academic theft, but what about you? Aren't you also leaching off Ji Mohan? If it weren't for Ji Mohan's unconditional help, his willingness to work tirelessly for you, could you have produced research results so quickly? What right do you have to stand on moral high ground and accuse me...\"","Ji Mohan said coldly, \"After working alongside Rong Yu these past few days, can't you still see the gap between yourself and her?\"","Lu Jiaojiao broke down, leaning against the wall.","She covered her face, unable to hold back her sobs.","Rong Yu felt not an ounce of sympathy for her.","She spoke calmly, \"Back then, you would leap into the lake without hesitation to save a complete stranger, Ji Mohan. It was precisely that pure-hearted courage that left Ji Mohan feeling indebted all these years. But now, in your pursuit of status, you've taken credit for research results and disregarded academic ethics. Does this version of you still live up to that brave young girl who did what was right?\"","Leaning against the wall, Lu Jiaojiao suddenly let out a laugh—tears on her face, a smile on her lips—an expression that was profoundly unsettling.","\"Unless—\" Rong Yu looked at her, \"Unless the person who saved Ji Mohan back then wasn't you at all.\"","Lu Jiaojiao shuddered violently.","Just as Rong Yu stepped away, Lu Jiaojiao's phone vibrated. Seeing the caller ID, despair filled her eyes. Her hand trembled as she answered. \"Dad...\"","\"You disgrace! You've shamed the entire Lu family! Had I known you were such a useless thing, I never should have brought you back to the Lu family!\"","Lu Jiaojiao bit her lip. \"But when I got into Tsinghua University, I brought honor to the Lu family. Later, working at the Chinese Academy of Sciences, I helped the Lu family connect with major families in the capital. I...\"","\"Enough! No more of this useless talk!\" Mr. Lu's voice was icy. \"Before, when you said you wanted to pursue a career in research, I indulged you. Now that path is closed. Come home obediently and prepare for an arranged marriage!\"","The call ended with a sharp click.","Lu Jiaojiao slid down to sit on the floor, weeping softly.","Her surname was Lu. She was the Lu family's illegitimate daughter. The year she turned ten, her biological mother died. She went to the Lu family to claim her place, only to be turned away at the door.","From that moment, she vowed that one day, the Lu family would come to take her home themselves.","There was only one path to change her fate: study hard.","With excellent grades, she tested into Beijing's best middle school. Only then did her father start giving her a living allowance. When she tested into the best high school as the city's top scorer, the Lu family finally accepted her.","Her academic achievements were her greatest source of confidence.","But now, it was gone. Everything was gone.","She, too, would become a pawn for the Lu family to manipulate at will...","Rong Yu walked to the building's back door where her teacher, Yun Xiaoyuan's car was parked.","Even before the press conference began, her teacher had called, asking if she needed her to step in and clarify things. Rong Yu had refused.","Yun Xiaoyuan was an academician, a leading figure in mathematics, a globally renowned mathematician. A person of such talent should not be dragged into these disputes.","Yun Xiaoyuan immediately noticed Ji Mohan following Rong Yu.","This young man, having his work plagiarized for so many years, had actually kept silent. If not for Little Yu stepping in, a fine talent like him would likely have been buried.","She spoke up, \"What's the Materials Institute's punishment for you?\"","Ji Mohan scratched his head. \"Suspended for half a month to cooperate with the investigation. I don't know the final ruling yet.\"","\"Get in the car,\" Yun Xiaoyuan said. \"Let's go for a meal.\"","Rong Yu and Ji Mohan got in.","Ji Mohan was a researcher who paid little attention to the world outside his work. He only knew the person before him was his great-grandmother's teacher, but had no idea who she really was.","When they arrived at the restaurant and entered the private room, there were seven or eight people. A few looked familiar, but he couldn't recall where he'd seen them.","Then he heard the roomful of people greeting each other.","\"Academician Yun.\"","\"Academician Min.\"","\"Academician Tian.\"","\"...\"","Ji Mohan was instantly stunned.","These people were all academicians.","How many academicians did China have? And here were seven or eight of them. In all his years, this was the first time he'd seen so many academicians gathered in one place. For a moment, he even had the absurd feeling that academicians weren't such a rare commodity.","The group surrounded his great-grandmother, talking.","\"Little Yu, how did you think of using topological insulator theory to explain the anomalous conductivity of Shi crystals?\"","\"Little Yu, your quantum confinement model seems different from the traditional ones. Did you reconstruct an algorithm?\"","Rong Yu answered the various professional questions with composure.","Min Shenyan sighed.","Such an outstanding student should have been his. It was all because he was one step too slow.","And his son was no help either, obsessed day and night with archaeological mummies and bog bodies, completely disregarding his old father's feelings...","Ji Mohan watched in a daze.","When he first met his great-grandmother, he had deeply doubted her authenticity. But to humor the old master, he had held his nose and accepted it.","But as time went on and they spent more time together, a genuine affection grew between them. Regardless of whether it was entirely real or not, addressing her as \"Great-Grandmother\" felt like no loss to him.","Later, when they worked together at the materials research institute, the extraordinary talent and ability she displayed made him realize she truly was the Matriarch of the Ji family, the esteemed Professor Rong who was so highly revered in the early days of the nation's founding.","And now, seeing the circle of distinguished figures gathered around Great-Grandmother, he understood with crystal clarity the vast, immeasurable gap that lay between them."]},{"number":214,"title":"Chapter 214: Young Master Sheng, don't tell me you don't even have a sense of pain.","paragraphs":["A group of academicians looked on with envy.","Right in front of Yun Xiaoyuan, they were practically itching to poach Rong Yu as their own student.","Yun Xiaoyuan couldn't fend off everyone at once, so she quickly spoke up, \"Xiao Yu, go to the kitchen and see if the dishes are ready.\"","Rong Yu couldn't help but smile.","In a private restaurant like this, would a customer really need to check on the food?","But since her teacher asked, she might as well step out and get some fresh air.","She walked out of the private room, through the corridor, and was just about to head to the main hall when she suddenly heard the sound of a group laughing and joking.","At the far end of the restaurant's corridor, a small courtyard was open, furnished with sofas and chairs for patrons to gather around a stove for tea after meals. It was currently peak dining hours, so the place was empty except for a group of young men in their early twenties, surrounding a tall man and laughing heartily.","The leader was a young master, a cigarette dangling from his lips, who said with a loud laugh, \"Young Master Sheng, I heard you're a mute who can't speak. Is that true or not?\"","Sheng Qingyan stood by a tree, his face devoid of any emotion, not even a flicker of his eyelashes, as if these sounds had nothing to do with him.","\"Really can't talk, huh? Can you at least make a sound?\"","Someone gave Sheng Qingyan a shove. Caught off guard, he stumbled back a step, his back hitting the large tree, but he didn't utter a single sound.","\"Hey, Young Master Sheng, does that hurt? Don't tell me you don't even feel pain?\"","Sheng Qingyan's eyes were vacant, like a statue without a soul.","One of them pulled out his phone, his face full of malicious amusement. \"Pour some wine over his head, let's see what reaction he has. It'll definitely be hilarious.\"","Another frowned. \"He's from the Sheng family. Isn't this going too far?\"","\"What's going too far? He's an idiot. Can't talk, can't tattle. Who would know what we did?\" The man blew a smoke ring into Sheng Qingyan's face and burst out laughing. \"He finally reacted! He's coughing! This is too funny...\"","Crash—","Suddenly, a glass shattered at their feet. The group, lost in their cruel teasing, snapped back to reality and turned to look. They saw that a woman had appeared in the courtyard at some point.","The woman wore a simple coat, wasn't very tall, and seemed quite young. Yet, standing there, an aura radiated from her—authoritative and intimidating without her even being angry, making people inexplicably uneasy.","\"Isn't that...\" one man recognized her first, \"isn't that the actress Rong Yu who's all over the hot search lists right now? She's really popular.\"","\"An actress, interesting.\" The leader, Du Mian, walked towards Rong Yu. \"A mere entertainer dares to meddle in men's business? Do you know who I am?\"","He was one of the Capital's Four Young Masters, Du Mian.","Even the top stars in the entertainment industry couldn't touch the lowest rung of the capital circle.","So, a minor celebrity like Rong Yu was even more beneath his notice.","He approached Rong Yu, got a clear look at her face, and was instantly struck by her beauty. He reached out to hook a finger under her chin.","However—","He saw that Rong Yu was actually toying with a shard of glass in her hand, its sharp point aimed directly at his jaw.","Rong Yu smiled. \"You seem to enjoy seeing if others react. How about letting me see what reaction you'd have if this glass shard pierced your carotid artery?\"","\"You!\"","Du Mian flew into a rage and reached out to teach this woman a lesson.","Rong Yu grabbed his arm and shoved him hard. His back slammed into a pillar, mirroring the exact treatment Sheng Qingyan had just received.","The other young masters with Du Mian were about to jump in together.","Rong Yu picked up wine glasses from the table and hurled them one after another, shards flying everywhere.","She's a tough one.","That was everyone's first impression of Rong Yu.","While the group was stunned, Rong Yu took out her phone and snapped a picture of Du Mian.","Du Mian was furious. \"Bitch! What do you think you're doing?\"","Rong Yu dropped the photo into a search bar, and a series of information popped up.","She let out a light laugh. \"So it's the Capital's Four Young Masters, the eldest son of the Du family. My apologies for not recognizing you sooner. Your grandfather is a founding hero of the nation, and here you are, disgracing the Du family's reputation outside. Tell me, if I were to publicize what you've done here, how would Elder Du discipline his disappointing descendant?\"","Du Mian felt as if his lifeline had been grabbed.","The thing the old man hated most was the Du family bullying the weak. Although the Sheng family wasn't weak, Sheng Qingyan was undeniably vulnerable...","If the old man found out, he was finished.","\"Fine, fine, fine!\" Du Mian, enraged to the point of laughter, said, \"Rong Yu, right? I'll remember you. You just wait and see.\"","He turned and stormed off, his pack of followers quickly scurrying after him.","Rong Yu wiped her fingers with disgust, the ones that had touched Du Mian.","She looked up towards the other side. Sheng Qingyan stood there, his dark eyes quietly watching her.","When he was being bullied by that group moments ago, he had shown no fluctuation.","Now, his pupils reflected her figure.","For some reason, this person always easily stirred a sense of pity in her heart.","She kicked aside the glass shards on the ground and walked over. \"Sheng Qingyan, why are you here alone? Where's your brother? Your family?\"","Sheng Qingyan didn't answer.","She looked down and saw dirt on his hand, probably grime rubbed off from the tree.","She took his hand and wiped it clean with a tissue. After wiping, she tried to let go, but couldn't.","Sheng Qingyan's large hand, like an iron clamp, held tightly onto her five fingers.","Headache.","Big headache.","Rong Yu used her other hand to pull out her phone and called Sheng Ciyuan. \"Your big brother is missing. Didn't you notice?\"","\"Oh my god!\" Sheng Ciyuan's voice was full of anxiety. \"I'm going crazy looking for him! Thank you, Rong Yu! Where are you? I'll be right there!\"","In less than a minute, he arrived in the courtyard, panting.","He saw his older brother, who usually showed no reaction to anything or anyone around him, actually sitting with Rong Yu, holding her hand, his eyes fixed intently on her...","While Rong Yu looked utterly exasperated.","\"B-big brother!\" Sheng Ciyuan rushed over, blocking Sheng Qingyan's line of sight, trying to pry his fingers open. \"This isn't polite, it's really not polite. Could you please let go...\"","Sheng Qingyan wouldn't let go. He just wouldn't.","Stubborn as a five- or six-year-old child.","\"Ugh... Rong Yu, my big brother can be really unreasonable sometimes,\" Sheng Ciyuan was on the verge of tears. \"Big brother, could you please behave?\"","He had come out for a meal with classmates. His big brother insisted on following. Their grandmother, feeling sorry for the brother being cooped up at home all day, insisted he bring him along. So he did.","He was chatting with his classmates, turned around, and his big brother was gone.","God only knew what went through his mind in that instant.","Thankfully, his brother wasn't lost.","But now, his brother had latched onto Rong Yu.","If not for the clear innocence in his brother's eyes, he might have suspected his brother was using this as an excuse to harass the girl."]},{"number":215,"title":"Chapter 215: Your surname is Sheng, go back to your own home, understand","paragraphs":["Rong Yu was utterly helpless.","She suddenly remembered Yingbao from childhood.","Around four or five years old, when she needed to go to the research institute, Yingbao would stubbornly cling to her hand, refusing to let go. But Yingbao wasn't as well-behaved as Sheng Qingyan; instead, he would throw tantrums, rolling on the floor, wailing and making a huge fuss, with tears and snot all over his face... In the end, she had no choice but to take Yingbao to the institute.","Yingbao was a boisterous child. In the quiet environment of the research lab, he lasted less than ten minutes before clamoring to go home.","She met Sheng Qingyan's gaze: \"Forget it, you can come in with me.\"","Then she looked at Sheng Ciyuan, \"You too.\"","Sheng Ciyuan obediently followed behind.","When they first met, both he and Rong Yu were gold medalists in the National Physics Finals. He felt they were on equal footing.","Now, he inexplicably felt one step below Rong Yu.","It made him feel like a grandson.","He shot a resentful look at Sheng Qingyan. It was all his big brother's fault.","Once they entered the restaurant's private room, his eyes widened in shock. Could someone please tell him why his dear teacher was having a meal here!","Sheng Ciyuan's teacher was an academician in the Department of Mathematics and Physics, surnamed Lin, named Lin Guangqu.","Lin Guangqu waved him over: \"You came just in time. Sit down and listen to how outstanding Rong Yu is. That research paper in the news today was spearheaded and completed by Rong Yu. So far, you haven't produced any forward-looking results like that.\"","Sheng Ciyuan looked ashamed: \"I'm sorry, teacher. I'm too useless.\"","\"Old Lin, I suspect you're using scolding your student as an excuse to subtly criticize me,\" Min Shenyan huffed. \"If you're really dissatisfied with Sheng Ciyuan, just give him to me.\"","Back then, he had also been a step too late; otherwise, Sheng Ciyuan would have been his student.","Lin Guangqu gave a slight smirk: \"I say, Old Min, what do you need so many students for? You have nearly forty already. Are you planning to start a class?\"","Yun Xiaoyuan said leisurely, \"He's short of people to carry his coffin.\"","Min Shenyan: \"...\"","He silently shut his mouth.","Yun Xiaoyuan asked Rong Yu, \"And this is?\"","She looked curiously at Sheng Qingyan, secretly guessing, could this be Rong Yu's boyfriend?","But it didn't seem so.","This man's eyes were off, not like a normal person's.","\"This is my elder brother,\" Sheng Ciyuan explained. \"My brother just had a bit of trouble earlier, and Rong Yu helped resolve it. My brother... well, how to put it, became a bit dependent.\"","Min Shenyan spoke bluntly: \"A grown man, why is he so clingy? And with so many elders present!\"","Sheng Ciyuan's eyes reddened.","But Sheng Qingyan showed no reaction.","Lin Guangqu said coldly, \"Old Min, before you speak each time, could you please think about your own name?\"","He knew his student Sheng Ciyuan had an elder brother, said to have had autism since childhood. Because the eldest brother couldn't shoulder the family business, his student was destined to inherit the Sheng family and couldn't devote himself wholeheartedly to research.","Sheng Ciyuan was a promising seedling, very smart, capable, with a truly pure heart.","He could have shone brilliantly in scientific research. It was such a pity.","This was his first time meeting Sheng Qingyan.","Sitting there quietly, not causing any disturbance, isolated from everything. Except, he kept staring at Rong Yu.","Min Shenyan belatedly realized something was off and quickly apologized.","Yun Xiaoyuan immediately changed the subject: \"Xiao Yu, tell everyone about your experimental concept...\"","Rong Yu began explaining methodically.","\"You young people's minds are too daring,\" one academician asked. \"This project initiated by the Fourth Aerospace Institute, what is it intended for?\"","Yun Xiaoyuan smiled: \"That, for now, is confidential. You'll know once the project's prototype phase is completed.\"","The space debris cleanup project, tentatively named \"Eagle Eye,\" involved nearly a thousand people.","The small sections each person was responsible for were individually named as separate projects. Only a very few knew the overall project name was Eagle Eye.","The meal lasted over two hours before it ended.","Rong Yu had thought Sheng Qingyan would grow restless and leave early.","Unexpectedly, he had sat by her side the entire time, holding her hand from start to finish, utterly unwilling to let go.","After leaving the restaurant, the academicians departed one by one.","Ji Mohan had been holding back for a long time.","With so many big shots present earlier, he hadn't dared to speak carelessly.","Now that they were gone, he could finally speak up, his brows tightly furrowed: \"Shouldn't you let go now?\"","Sheng Ciyuan was so embarrassed he wished he could find a crack in the ground to crawl into: \"Big brother, it's very late now, past nine o'clock. If we don't go home, grandmother won't let you go out in the future. Come on, let's go home?\"","Sheng Qingyan seemed not to hear.","Rong Yu looked at the man who stood a head taller than her and spoke softly: \"Can you hear me when I speak?\"","The man's vacant dark eyes showed a slight ripple. Slowly, he gave a gentle nod.","Sheng Ciyuan swallowed hard.","At home, anyone, even their grandmother, had to repeat a sentence nearly ten times for his big brother to process it.","Rong Yu had effortlessly made his big brother nod.","He remembered the last time his big brother suddenly spoke was also because Rong Yu had asked a question.","When he told his family at home, everyone said he was imagining things.","Sheng Ciyuan silently took out his phone, turned on recording mode, and took a few steps back.","Rong Yu continued: \"It's dark, very late. It's time to rest. You need to go home, understand?\"","Sheng Qingyan's lips parted slightly, slowly uttering a few words: \"Go home. With you.\"","Sheng Ciyuan's eyes widened.","He got it on recording.","He recorded it!","The scene of his big brother speaking was recorded!","But?","What on earth did his big brother say?","\"You're a Sheng,\" Ji Mohan poked his chest with a finger. \"You go back to your own home. Can you understand that?\"","He really didn't want to argue with someone with autism.","But this patient was really pushing his luck. Holding hands and not letting go was one thing, but now he wanted to follow her home?","If the old master found out his great-grandmother was being taken advantage of by a man right under his nose, he'd be torn to shreds by the old man.","Sheng Ciyuan pocketed his phone, quickly stepped forward, had a sudden idea, and whispered in Sheng Qingyan's ear: \"Big brother, grandmother's friend bought some photos overseas. Do you want to go home and see?\"","Sheng Qingyan's black pupils contracted.","He instinctively released Rong Yu's hand.","After walking a few steps away, he turned back to look at Rong Yu again, only to be blocked by Ji Mohan's domineering stance.","\"Big brother, let's hurry.\"","Sheng Ciyuan, without another word, ushered Sheng Qingyan into the car.","As the car drove away, Rong Yu felt relieved, yet also an inexplicable sense of loss.","It was like taking care of a child.","When you're taking care of them, it's incredibly annoying.","When you're not, you feel strangely empty.","Forget it, no use thinking about it. Better go home and hug Duoduo more."]},{"number":216,"title":"Chapter 216: The Moment the Bullet Hit Him, Rong Yu Woke Up","paragraphs":["The Sheng Residence.","By the time Sheng Ciyuan and Sheng Qingyan returned to the Sheng family home, it was already ten o'clock at night.","The matriarch of the Sheng family was sitting in the courtyard, playing with a cat. Before her two grandsons even stepped through the gate, the cat leaped down from the flower stand and ran out to greet them.","\"Pangpang.\"","Sheng Ciyuan called out.","But the orange tabby didn't even glance at him, jumping directly onto Sheng Qingyan instead.","Sheng Qingyan carried the cat, stroking it all the way as he walked up to Old Mrs. Sheng. He stretched out his hand, looking like he was asking for something.","Sheng Ciyuan frantically signaled with his eyes.","Old Mrs. Sheng understood immediately. \"The photo, right? Because it's so old, it needs restoration. It'll take a few days... Auntie Liu, please take the young master to freshen up and rest.\"","Auntie Liu had been taking care of Sheng Qingyan in all aspects of life since he was born. She took his hand and led him inside.","Sheng Ciyuan immediately moved closer with his phone. \"Grandmother, look quickly! Big brother spoke!\"","Old Mrs. Sheng hurriedly took the phone.","\"Go home. With you.\"","Sheng Qingyan's four words were exceptionally clear.","\"Heavens be praised! Yan'er really spoke!\" Old Mrs. Sheng was overjoyed to the point of tears. \"I knew it, I always knew there was nothing wrong with our Yan'er. He's not mute, he can speak. He just never encountered something that would make him want to talk... Wait, Yuan'er, who is this girl in the video? What's her name? You must invite her to our home. She deserves the highest courtesy from the entire Sheng family...\"","Sheng Ciyuan replied, \"Her name is Rong Yu. She's from Haicheng, currently a senior in high school. She...\"","\"What did you say?\" Old Mrs. Sheng stood up abruptly. \"Rong Yu? You said her name is Rong Yu?\"","Sheng Ciyuan was taken aback. \"What's wrong? Does Grandmother know Rong Yu?\"","\"Oh my! The photo your older brother cherishes like a treasure has Rong Yu in it,\" Old Mrs. Sheng said, her words tumbling out. \"I specifically asked your father to investigate. That Rong Yu in the photo was a professor from the early days of the nation's founding. She was the one who spearheaded the establishment of the Mathematics Division of the Central Academy of Sciences of China. It's a pity she died in a car accident before the mathematics institute could be fully established... What I don't understand is why your older brother is so particularly obsessed with that period of history, especially with searching everywhere for photos of Professor Rong...\"","\"And now, a girl with the exact same name appears and actually made your big brother speak?\" Old Mrs. Sheng wore a look of deep regret. \"If only we had known, the Sheng family should have searched for everyone in the country with that name. Perhaps your big brother would have recovered long ago.\"","Sheng Ciyuan recounted what happened at the restaurant and added, \"There's definitely more than one person named Rong Yu in the country. But not everyone would step forward in such a situation. Rong Yu offended Du Mian. I'm afraid it might affect her career.\"","Old Mrs. Sheng's heart ached with distress. Sitting back in her chair, she rubbed the head of Pangpang, the orange cat who had wandered over, and said, \"Alright then, Yuan'er, you invite this girl named Rong Yu to the Sheng residence as a guest. Just say... just say...\"","The old lady racked her brains and finally slapped her thigh. \"Just say it's your father's birthday, and we're inviting her for a meal.\"","Sheng Ciyuan: \"...\"","His father's birthday was in the height of summer. Spring hadn't even arrived yet.","Oh well. His father had never held a birthday banquet anyway, and no one knew his actual birthday date. This would work just fine.","Old Mrs. Sheng's expression turned serious. \"Also, invite that whole bunch of good-for-nothing young masters from the Beijing social circle. How dare they secretly bully my Yan'er? Just see if I don't strip the skin off their backs.\"","Sheng Ciyuan nodded in agreement.","Rong Yu didn't sleep well that night.","She actually had a dream, and it was about her time studying abroad.","She was an international student upon whom the nation placed great hopes.","He was a soldier tasked with escorting this group of students abroad, hidden among the ordinary people.","Once overseas, she spent her days studying at the university.","While he had to carry out many, many secret missions.","It seemed every time they met, he was injured. For the rise and fall of the nation, he risked his life time and again.","His final mission was to escort these overseas students back to China.","The moment the bullet struck him, Rong Yu woke with a start.","By then, the sky was already bright, and it was actually snowing again outside, the window covered in snowflakes.","Ji Yanting had gone to the film set early in the morning. As the male lead, his scenes were heavy, and he was busy from dawn till dusk, as busy as a dog.","Just as Rong Yu stepped out of the bedroom, she received a call from Sheng Ciyuan: \"So, today happens to be my father's birthday. We've arranged a small gathering. Could we invite you to my home for a meal?\"","Rong Yu found it amusing. \"Classmate Sheng, even if it were your birthday, there wouldn't be a need to invite me.\"","She wasn't close to Sheng Ciyuan.","As for Sheng Ciyuan's father, she had never even met him.","Showing up uninvited would be rather strange, wouldn't it?","\"Please, Rong Yu, just come.\"","As soon as the words left his mouth, Sheng Ciyuan knew his image was ruined.","In front of Rong Yu, he was no longer the physics gold medalist, no longer the physics genius, but rather, a shameless person.","\"My grandmother specifically instructed me that I must invite you. If I fail, she said I'll have to share a bowl with Pangpang from now on,\" Sheng Ciyuan whined. \"Oh, Pangpang is a cat. He loves eating mice and has stinky breath. I don't want to share a bowl with Pangpang! Rong Yu, please come.\"","Rong Yu: \"...\"","She planned to return to Haicheng tomorrow and was indeed free today.","After some thought, she agreed.","Although this was Ji Yanting's place, ever since the Old Son came by last time, he had designated a room specifically for her and filled her wardrobe with beautiful dresses.","Ji Yanting, being a celebrity, had contact with many brands. Whenever he saw pretty dresses or clothes, he would have his assistant send them back.","Consequently, she had taken over about one-third of Ji Yanting's walk-in closet.","Rong Yu chose an elegant dress, paired it with a beige overcoat and a light-colored scarf... As she emerged from the closet, she saw Ji Mohan standing there in a suit.","She raised a slight eyebrow. \"And you are?\"","\"Ahem!\" Ji Mohan straightened his tie. \"The Old Master has ordered me to ensure I serve the Great-Grandmother properly. So, I'm coming along, responsible for driving, carrying bags, and pulling out chairs.\"","He had heard perfectly clearly—it was the Sheng family inviting the Great-Grandmother over.","That clingy man from yesterday, who kept holding the Great-Grandmother's hand, was really an eyesore. What if, in his absence, that man behaved even more inappropriately?","Rong Yu nodded. \"Alright, come along then.\"","This kid had been suspended from the Materials Research Institute for half a month. Someone used to being busy, suddenly idle—she was afraid he might overthink things and get stuck in a rut.","Might as well take him along for some liveliness.","The two of them drove to the Sheng residence.","The master of the Sheng household, Sheng Ciyuan's father, was named Sheng Dian. A businessman, he carried the aura of a top executive.","He originally had matters to attend to today but was firmly kept at home by his elderly mother, who insisted today was his \"birthday small banquet.\"","For nearly fifty years, his birthday had always been in the summer. With a mere opening and closing of his old mother's mouth, his birth date had changed. Wonderful, just wonderful."]},{"number":217,"title":"Chapter 217: Marrying This Type of Person Means Your Whole Life Is Predictable","paragraphs":["The Sheng family's courtyard house was situated by the river.","Ji Mohan parked the car, opened the door for Rong Yu, then followed her towards the Sheng residence, carrying a handbag in one hand and the newly purchased gift in the other.","Just as they reached the entrance, a familiar figure came into view.","Ji Mohan's face was filled with disbelief; he was actually seeing Lu Jiaojiao.","Lu Jiaojiao had shed her lab coat and glasses. She wore a rose-red dress with a camel-colored coat over it, high heels on her feet, her hair cascading over her shoulders, and her face adorned with delicate makeup, looking every bit the part of a socialite.","Her lips were pressed tight, her entire expression one of reluctance.","\"What are you still being so proud about?\" The man beside her, the eldest son of the Lu family, a few years her senior named Lu Rui, stared at her coldly. \"In the past, you brought fame to the Lu family, but now you're notorious in the research community, condemned by everyone. The fact that the Lu family hasn't disowned you, a bastard child, shows our magnanimity. Who are you putting on this miserable face for?\"","Lu Jiaojiao bit her lip in humiliation.","\"You caused that scandal, with over twenty million in research funds being reclaimed by the institute. Did you think the Lu family was a charity, just filling that hole for you?\" Lu Rui sneered. \"You know Du Mian, right? One of the four young masters of the capital. The Du family has power and money, something our Lu family can hardly aspire to match. If it weren't for my good relationship with Du Mian, he would never have met you, let alone proposed a marriage alliance. He'll also be attending the Sheng family's small banquet. Get your head straight, don't ruin this.\"","Lu Jiaojiao's face grew even paler.","She, a top student, had actually fallen to the point of needing to marry for alliance.","And that Du Mian had been married twice before and had a one-year-old son. Marrying him meant becoming a stepmother.","She had worked so hard all these years, only to end up as a wealthy man's second wife... What was the point of all her studying?","But, having come this far, she had no other choice.","She followed Lu Rui towards the Sheng residence. Just as they reached the gate, she saw two people approaching and froze.","\"Ji Mohan?\"","For a moment, she thought she was seeing things.","Because Ji Mohan was actually wearing a suit, completely different from his usual lab coat attire. She took a closer look at the suit—it seemed to be a limited edition from a certain brand.","Having known Ji Mohan for so many years, she never knew he had this kind of money.","Noticing her intense stare at his suit, Ji Mohan felt a bit self-conscious.","This was the most low-key and simple outfit he could dig out from his second brother's wardrobe. Was it ill-fitting somewhere?","Lu Jiaojiao glanced at the Sheng family gate right before her and asked incredulously, \"Ji Mohan, what are you doing here?\"","The guest list for the Sheng family patriarch's small birthday banquet wasn't very long.","Even a prominent family like the Lu family had barely made it onto the list. Was Ji Mohan invited too?","And Rong Yu, wasn't she just a minor celebrity? Why could she attend a banquet of a major family?","What other identities did these two have?","Rong Yu stepped over the threshold of the Sheng residence and walked in.","Ji Mohan, carrying a lady's handbag, hurriedly followed after her.","\"Rong Yu, you're here.\" Sheng Ciyuan quickly came forward to greet them. \"Mr. Ji, you're here too...\"","He had been to the Furong Manor.","He knew Rong Yu lived with the Ji family. Ji Mohan was probably from the Hai City Ji family.","He racked his brains but couldn't figure out the relationship between Rong Yu and the Ji family. In any case, it wasn't simple.","He said warmly, \"Rong Yu, you saved my elder brother. My grandmother said she wants to thank you in person. Please come with me this way...\"","Rong Yu followed him into the Sheng family's inner courtyard.","Lu Jiaojiao, who entered a step later, happened to hear this.","Her face was full of disbelief.","Rong Yu had saved Sheng Qingyan, that simpleton?","So that's why she received an invitation from the Sheng family?","Then, Ji Mohan... he must have tagged along with Rong Yu to get through the Sheng family gates?","\"What are you still standing there for!\" Lu Rui said impatiently. \"Du Mian is over there. Go, quickly.\"","Lu Jiaojiao reluctantly walked in that direction.","Seeing her, Du Mian immediately brightened up: \"Miss Lu, oh no, I'd rather call you Researcher Lu. Our Du family is precisely lacking cultured people with sharp minds like yours. Although your reputation is tarnished now, the fact remains that you got into Huaqing University on merit and worked at the Chinese Academy of Sciences for so many years. Any children we have should inherit your talent, right?\"","Lu Jiaojiao clenched her jaw.","Although the Du family had money and power, she had never even glanced at playboys like Du Mian, let alone one who was on his third marriage with a child.","Marrying someone like this meant her whole life was laid out predictably before her.","But what choice did she have?","Rong Yu and Ji Mohan entered the main hall of the Sheng residence. As soon as Old Madame Sheng saw Rong Yu, she stood up and pulled her to sit beside her: \"Miss Rong, you are not only beautiful but also kind-hearted. If you hadn't stepped forward, who knows how badly our Yan'er would have been bullied. The key is Yan'er can't speak up for himself; if he's bullied, it's done, and no one would ever know... Thankfully, there was you, Miss Rong, letting an old woman like me see the true faces of those people.\"","Rong Yu smiled and said, \"You are too kind, Madame. I merely acted on impulse. It's nothing worth mentioning.\"","Sheng Dian spoke up: \"Our Sheng family owes Miss Rong a great debt of gratitude. If you have any requests, Miss Rong, please feel free to make them.\"","Rong Yu still wore a smile: \"Sheng Ciyuan and I are friends. His elder brother is also my friend. Helping a friend in passing doesn't warrant such a grand gesture of thanks. If I were to actually make a request, wouldn't that change the nature of our relationship?\"","Sheng Dian looked at her with admiration.","Having entered the Sheng residence and understood the Sheng family's standing in the capital, yet still maintaining such clarity and normalcy—few in this world could do that.","\"Yan'er, slow down!\"","Madame Sheng had just gone in to tell her eldest son that Rong Yu had arrived.","Sheng Qingyan, who had been petting a cat, immediately dropped the plump feline and rushed out of the room, jogging all the way over.","Tall and sturdy, Sheng Qingyan headed straight for the seat next to Rong Yu as soon as he saw her.","To Rong Yu's right sat Old Madame Sheng, and to her left was Ji Mohan.","There was only about an elbow's width of space between Ji Mohan and Rong Yu, not enough to fit a person, yet Sheng Qingyan somehow squeezed himself in.","Caught off guard, Ji Mohan was nearly pushed off his seat onto the floor.","\"Yan'er!\" Sheng Dian's face immediately darkened. \"Even though this is our home, we must still observe basic courtesy. Apologize, apologize to our guest at once!\"","\"Yan'er doesn't understand what an apology means.\" Madame Sheng hurried over, crouching down to help Ji Mohan up. \"My son has been ill since childhood, no different from a child. He doesn't understand social interactions or manners. I am truly sorry.\"","With the Sheng family being so solemn about it, Ji Mohan naturally wouldn't make an issue of it and quickly waved his hand. \"I'm fine.\"","Rong Yu set down her teacup.","Her clear, calm eyes turned to Sheng Qingyan.","She seemed to say nothing, but Ji Mohan could detect a hint of displeasure in her gaze.","Displeasure was good.","He was really afraid his great-grandmother would continue to suffer this kind of imposition from Sheng Qingyan.","Just as Madame Sheng was about to quickly move past the incident, Sheng Qingyan suddenly stood up.","His dark, glassy eyes rested quietly on Ji Mohan. Slowly, he parted his lips and spoke, each word deliberate and clear: \"I'm sorry...\""]},{"number":218,"title":"Chapter 218: It was just children playing around and they went too far.","paragraphs":["The entire Sheng family was utterly astonished.","From the moment he was born, Sheng Qingyan was different from other children—exceptionally quiet, well-behaved, and he never once cried.","By the age of two, when other children could already recite poems, he still couldn't even call for his mom or dad.","It was then that the family panicked, seeking doctors everywhere. At first, they thought there was a problem with his vocal cords, that he was mute, but after visiting over a dozen hospitals, no physical ailment could be found.","Later, in his fifth year, he was diagnosed with Autism Spectrum Disorder.","For over twenty years, this person who had never opened his mouth to speak had done so three times in just these past few days.","The first time, when Yuan'er told them about it, not a single one of them believed it.","The second time, Yuan'er captured a video on the spot. Those four words brought the entire Sheng family to the brink of joyful tears, finally offering a glimmer of hope.","The third time was now.","Seeing it in a video and hearing it live in person were completely different experiences.","\"Yan'er, say it again,\" Grandmother Sheng's voice trembled. \"Let your grandmother hear your voice properly.\"","However,","Sheng Qingyan closed his mouth.","He looked left and right, then sat down directly opposite Rong Yu. It was the empty seat closest to her.","His eyes fixed intently on Rong Yu.","Rong Yu asked him, \"Why do you keep looking at me?\"","Sheng Qingyan thought for a long moment, then spoke like a child who had just learned to talk: \"I don't know.\"","Rong Yu recalled how he looked at the photographs and pressed further: \"Then why did you collect those photos? Do you know the professor named Rong Yu in the pictures?\"","Sheng Qingyan's glass-like eyes paused for half a beat: \"No.\"","Rong Yu sighed: \"Then why did you collect so many artifacts related to that group of overseas students?\"","Sheng Qingyan lowered his head, his voice growing softer: \"I don't know...\"","Every member of the Sheng family gaped in shock.","Even the family patriarch, Sheng Dian, shed his usual aura of authority and stared dumbfounded at Sheng Qingyan, as if he had never truly known this son before.","Madam Sheng covered her mouth with her hand.","Yan'er could actually understand others' questions and answer them fluently... He wasn't completely closed off to the outside world, he wasn't incapable of understanding human speech, he wasn't mute after all...","Only Rong Yu frowned slightly.","She felt the exchange had been futile; she hadn't managed to find out anything.","She was genuinely very curious about the reasons.","But, with the other party telling her \"I don't know\" with such apparent sincerity, how could she possibly question him further?","\"The master I consulted has indeed proven effective,\" Grandmother Sheng's voice still shook. \"The master said that in Yan'er's birth year, his fate would undergo a change. Isn't this the change? The master also said Yan'er is missing a part of his soul; rituals are needed to restore him to normal. None of you believed it, not a single one, wasting all these years for nothing. Now, shouldn't you believe it!\"","Sheng Dian frowned: \"A charlatan deliberately speaking in vague terms, and you actually believe that, Mother, it's really...\"","Madam Sheng cut him off: \"Let's just give it a try. What if it works, right?\"","Rong Yu was a rigorous researcher who believed in science.","But ever since she defied all reason and traveled from seventy years ago to the present, she had begun to view the concept of science more dialectically.","As they were speaking, the Sheng family steward entered: \"Madam, all the guests have arrived. Shall we begin the banquet?\"","Grandmother Sheng stood up: \"Let's all go over.\"","Seven or eight banquet tables were arranged in the Sheng family courtyard. For such a large family, a birthday banquet with only these few tables was indeed a very small affair.","The moment Du Mian sat down in his seat, he sensed something was off.","Why did it seem that everyone attending the banquet was someone he was privately on good terms with?","Yet, the Sheng family's in-laws and business partners were conspicuously absent.","He turned his head and saw Rong Yu following beside Grandmother Sheng.","His scalp instantly prickled with dread.","He had bullied Sheng Qingyan countless times before, and it had always been without consequence... So, it must be that bitch Rong Yu who had tattled.","\"Thank you all for attending our Sheng family's modest gathering,\" Sheng Dian raised his wine glass, looking at the guests. \"Especially President Du and Young Master Du, who, despite your busy schedules, have come to offer congratulations. We are immensely grateful.\"","President Du, unaware of what his son had done, raised his glass: \"You're too kind, President Sheng. It's our pleasure.\"","Du Mian sat as if on pins and needles.","Grandmother Sheng said with a smile, \"Just eating is a bit dry. How about we listen to a little tune?\"","Music immediately began playing in the courtyard.","The attending guests looked around in confusion, unsure what was going on.","Just as the song reached its climax, it abruptly stopped, replaced by a segment of noisy surveillance audio.","\"Young Master Sheng, I hear you're a mute who can't talk. True or false?\"","\"Hey, Young Master Sheng, does it hurt? Don't tell me you don't even feel pain?\"","\"He's an idiot. Can't talk, can't tell on us. Who would know what we did?\"","\"...\"","Du Mian's face instantly changed color.","That place had no surveillance, and Sheng Qingyan couldn't speak. That's why he had dared to bully him so brazenly.","Where did this recording come from?","Although the Du family wasn't inferior to the Sheng family, he was clearly in the wrong. If this got to the old man, he'd be skinned alive...","Despite the chilly weather, Du Mian's clothes were soaked through with sweat.","The banquet guests began murmuring among themselves.","\"Is that surveillance audio of Young Master Sheng being bullied?\"","\"Who has such nerve, bullying a member of the Sheng family? Everyone knows Grandmother Sheng treats her eldest grandson as the apple of her eye.\"","\"The voices sound like Young Master Du Mian of the Du family, and the young masters from the Zhou and Qian families...\"","\"These young masters usually act all proper, but it turns out they pick on those who can't fight back or tell on them.\"","\"...\"","President Du's eyes widened.","He knew his son was a troublemaker, but he never imagined he could be this despicable.","Bullying others was one thing, but to humiliate the eldest young master of the Sheng family...","This matter could be handled lightly or severely...","President Du stood up, forcing a smile: \"It's just horseplay among kids that got out of hand. Rest assured, Madam, I will definitely teach this little bastard Du Mian a proper lesson...\"","He gave Du Mian a not-too-light, not-too-heavy kick on the leg. \"Hurry up, apologize to Madam Sheng.\"","The families of the Zhou and Qian households also hastily pulled their disgraceful sons to their feet, joining in the apologies.","A group of people stood apologizing, but it did nothing to lessen Grandmother Sheng's anger.","Her smile widened: \"Indeed, it's just horseplay among children. No need to make such a fuss. No apology is necessary. Everyone, please sit. Steward, serve the first course.\"","Du Mian let out a heavy sigh of relief.","It seemed the Sheng family was letting the matter drop, but as far as he was concerned, it wasn't over.","He glared coldly at Rong Yu.","Dare to tell on me, huh? He'd make this bitch learn the meaning of regret.","Just then, servants entered the banquet hall carrying trays. But what the trays held wasn't food—it was a photograph.","President Du shot to his feet.","The person in the photo was him, intimately embracing a woman. That woman was not his lawfully wedded wife, but the mistress he kept hidden away.","He had hidden this woman very carefully. How had the Sheng family exposed her so publicly?"]},{"number":219,"title":"Chapter 219: Is Ji Mohan a member of the Ji Group in Haicheng","paragraphs":["The scenes at the other tables were quite similar.","All were photographs, only the subjects in them were different.","The Du family kept mistresses on the side.","The Zhou family had an illegitimate child hidden away.","The Qian family's second master abused his first wife...","Everyone's faces changed color. This, this was clearly a banquet set as a trap!","Only then did these people understand that the Sheng family would never let the matter rest so easily. If they didn't adopt the correct attitude, these scandals would undoubtedly hit the media immediately...","Lu Rui, sitting beside Lu Jiaojiao, trembled all over.","He had also joined Du Mian in bullying Sheng Qingyan, but happened to be absent yesterday. The Sheng family's invitation was a warning to him.","He kept his head down, trying to minimize his presence.","Lu Jiaojiao gave a light laugh.","That good-for-nothing Du Mian was truly finished now.","The head of the Du family was a military man, and it was said he had once been a subordinate of the late Sheng family patriarch—a man of particularly upright character.","His own grandson bullying the family of his former superior? Old Mr. Du would never let this slide lightly. Du Mian would absolutely not be able to stay in the capital.","\"Smack!\"","Mr. Du, without a word, backhanded a slap across Du Mian's face.","He was well aware of his own father's stance. Even though the old Sheng patriarch had passed away many years ago, his own father still treated the Sheng family with deference.","If the Sheng matriarch insisted on pursuing this matter, his father would undoubtedly support it wholeheartedly.","He looked towards the unshakably poised Sheng matriarch and said, \"Du Mian's actions have brought disgrace upon our Du family. I will arrange for him to go abroad. Unless it is for his grandfather's funeral, Du Mian is not to set foot back in the country.\"","Du Mian's eyes widened. \"On what grounds? I...\"","He was the eldest son of the Du family, the future heir. To be exiled abroad over such a trivial matter? On what grounds?","Mr. Du delivered another slap.","On the grounds that if Du Mian didn't go abroad, the scandal of him keeping a mistress would become common knowledge.","\"Madam, my son is unruly. I shall take him home for discipline first.\" He glanced sideways at the photos on the dining table. \"These...\"","The Sheng matriarch smiled. \"Consider them a parting gift. Please take them with you, Mr. Du.\"","Mr. Du hastily gathered the photos, dragged Du Mian, and quickly departed from the Sheng residence.","With the Du family setting the precedent.","The other families immediately followed suit.","\"Madam, I will strip my son of his president position and send him to Africa for experience.\"","\"Madam, our Qian family will publish a notice in the papers severing ties with this unfilial son...\"","About a third of the guests from the seven or eight tables left.","Those remaining dared not even breathe too loudly.","Lu Rui was drenched in sweat, his clothes clinging to his skin like a shroud.","Lu Jiaojiao's voice sounded by his ear. \"Do I still need to curry favor with Du Mian for a marriage alliance?\"","Lu Rui gritted his teeth. \"Shut up.\"","\"It seems the earlier dishes were served by mistake,\" the Sheng matriarch said cheerfully. \"Steward, bring fresh dishes and wine. Everyone, please eat and drink heartily. Don't stand on ceremony.\"","Among those present were many of Du Mian's lackeys who, having fortuitously been absent yesterday and lacking recorded evidence, had narrowly escaped. This meal was exceptionally difficult for them to swallow, as if they were gulping down stones. When they left, it was almost a frantic escape.","After the meal concluded, Rong Yu and Ji Mohan also rose to take their leave.","Sheng Qingyan stuck close to Rong Yu, looking as if he intended to follow her.","\"Yan'er, come here.\" The Sheng matriarch beckoned affectionately. \"Miss Rong is about to leave. Come to your grandmother's side, and we'll see Miss Rong off together. That's what a polite, well-behaved child does.\"","Upon hearing the word \"polite,\" Sheng Qingyan immediately took several steps away from Rong Yu and stood beside the matriarch.","The Sheng family members escorted Rong Yu and Ji Mohan to the gate.","At the entrance, Sheng Dian turned to Ji Mohan and said, \"Our Sheng family has business dealings with the Ji family as well. Another day, I will certainly pay a visit to Old Mr. Ji.\"","Ji Mohan was very awkward with such formal social interactions. Scratching the back of his head, he said, \"Alright, I'll let my grandfather know when I get back.\"","The group chatted at the main gate.","Standing under a tree by the gate, Lu Jiaojiao was utterly astonished.","She had waited here hoping to catch Ji Mohan as he left, to speak with him and minimize the fallout from the academic plagiarism incident...","She never expected to overhear such a conversation.","Ji Mohan, was from the Ji family?","The Ji family of the Ji Group in Haicheng?","Though not part of business circles, she often heard her family mention the Ji family.","In Haicheng, the Ji family held a position comparable to the Sheng family in the capital—both were top-tier, powerful families, far beyond the reach of the Lu family.","She had been associating with such a top-tier heir all this time, and she had never known...","\"It's fine to see us off here,\" Rong Yu said with a smile. \"We'll take our leave now.\"","She looked at Sheng Qingyan.","Sheng Qingyan had been staring at her.","She reached out and patted his shoulder. \"Goodbye.\"","She turned and left with Ji Mohan.","Sheng Qingyan continued to stare fixedly at her retreating figure.","\"Alright, that's enough looking,\" the Sheng matriarch shook her head. \"It's cold. Let's go inside.\"","Madam Sheng pulled Sheng Dian aside and whispered, \"Yan'er acts so differently towards that Miss Rong. I have an idea. Why not arrange for Yan'er to marry Miss Rong? That way, Yan'er might quickly become normal...\"","\"What nonsense are you talking?\" Sheng Dian frowned. \"Miss Rong is a national talent. How is Yan'er worthy of her?\"","Madam Sheng's eyes reddened. \"Do you think so little of Yan'er?\"","\"He can stay sheltered within the Sheng family for life. Don't think about ruining some other girl's life.\" Sheng Dian pinched the bridge of his nose. \"The old lady mentioned taking Yan'er to visit some master. Pay attention to that; don't let us get swindled.\"","The Sheng family members chatted as they went inside.","Just as Rong Yu and Ji Mohan reached their car, a figure appeared.","\"Moham.\" Lu Jiaojiao stepped forward. \"We attended the same banquet, yet you didn't say a word to me. Are we strangers now?\"","Seeing her made Ji Mohan's scalp prickle. \"What do you want me to say?\"","Lu Jiaojiao glanced at Rong Yu. \"Let's talk over there.\"","\"What can't be said in front of me?\" Rong Yu crossed her arms. \"Are you afraid your schemes will be exposed, Miss Lu?\"","Lu Jiaojiao felt a pang of irritation.","She bit her lip and asked softly, \"Moham, is Rong Yu your girlfriend?\"","Ji Mohan's eyes widened. \"Don't talk nonsense! Rong Yu isn't my girlfriend. Our relationship isn't what you think!\"","Lu Jiaojiao lifted her gaze. \"Before, you helped my career. That settled the debt for saving your life. But now, my career is completely ruined. So, you need to repay the life-saving favor again.\"","Ji Mohan was taken aback. \"How do you want me to repay it?\"","As long as it didn't involve anything like academic plagiarism, he could agree to other conditions.","Better to settle it early and be free from the moral blackmail.","Lu Jiaojiao enunciated each word clearly. \"I want you to marry me.\""]},{"number":220,"title":"Chapter 220: The Person Who Saved Me That Day Was Not You at All","paragraphs":["Ji Mohan felt as if struck by lightning.","He thought he must have misheard. Rubbing his ears, he asked blankly, \"What... what did you just say?\"","Lu Jiaojiao felt a slight pang of humiliation.","She and Ji Mohan had entered university in the same year, but she was admitted through the regular process, while Ji Mohan had been guaranteed admission since his first year of high school. She was a full two years older than him.","Later, at the Materials Research Institute, her rank was higher, his lower.","When facing Ji Mohan, she had always been the one in the superior position... Yet now, she had to lower her head and ask Ji Mohan to marry her.","It was truly ridiculous.","But if she didn't do this, the Lu family would treat her like a commodity and marry her off to some disgusting older man.","The Ji family of Haicheng was powerful enough to make the Lu family compromise...","She took a deep breath and said, \"For saving a life, one should offer oneself in return. Mohan, I want you to propose to the Lu family as soon as possible and take me as your wife.\"","\"Are you... are you out of your mind?\"","Ji Mohan quickly took a step back, putting distance between himself and Lu Jiaojiao.","He only felt gratitude for her saving his life; he had no romantic feelings for her whatsoever. How could he possibly propose to the Lu family?","\"Tsk.\"","A mocking laugh made Lu Jiaojiao's humiliation complete.","She turned to look at Rong Yu, who was laughing, and said angrily, \"What does this have to do with you? What are you laughing at!\"","\"What era is this, still talking about 'offering oneself in return'?\" Rong Yu genuinely found it amusing. \"You think you can bind another person for a lifetime with just a life-saving favor? Do you really think that's possible? Besides, whether it was even you who saved A-Mo is still up for debate. Do you have any proof?\"","Lu Jiaojiao opened her handbag, took out a pendant from the inner compartment. It was a gold-and-jade style piece, a very old item. But the moment she produced it, Ji Mohan's expression changed.","Rong Yu frowned.","So it was this trinket that made A-Mo believe Lu Jiaojiao was his savior?","This was far too childish.","Lu Jiaojiao pursed her lips and said, \"Mohan, my current situation is very difficult. If you don't marry me, my family will make me marry some forty or fifty-year-old man to be a stepmother. That shouldn't be my fate. For the sake of saving your life, please help me, okay?\"","She took a step forward, her gaze pleading.","\"If you find it hard to develop romantic feelings for me, I won't force you. We can have a marriage of convenience first. Once the Lu family lets me go, we can get a divorce later...\"","Lu Jiaojiao spoke with heartfelt emotion.","Suddenly.","\"Click!\"","Rong Yu took out her phone and snapped a photo of the gold-and-jade pendant.","Lu Jiaojiao's voice cut off abruptly. \"Rong Yu, what exactly are you trying to do?\"","Rong Yu curved her lips into a smile. \"I want to buy the same style.\"","She looked at Ji Mohan, her smile vanishing. \"The Ji family won't interfere with your marriage, but if you marry someone with no academic integrity, then you might as well stop using the Ji surname.\"","She pulled open the car door, got in, and slammed it shut with a bang.","Ji Mohan's face paled dramatically.","Oh no.","Great-grandma is angry.","He always seemed to be angering Great-grandma. If the old master found out, he really might not be considered a Ji family member anymore.","Without even glancing at Lu Jiaojiao, he hurried to the driver's side, got in, closed the door, and said quickly, \"Great-grandma, please don't worry. I'm not that confused. I would never mix up a life-saving favor with marriage. Please don't tell the old master, okay?\"","Rong Yu couldn't be bothered with him.","She found Ji Zhiyuan's contact and sent the photo of the pendant over: \"A-Yuan, investigate this item's purchase records. It would be even better if you can find the buyer.\"","Ji Zhiyuan: \"Understood, Great-grandma.\"","The drive back to the luxury apartment took about twenty minutes. They had just sat down on the sofa when Ji Zhiyuan's reply came through.","\"Great-grandma, it's been found. This is a counterfeit product from a factory in Jiangcheng over a decade ago. The gold and jade are both plastic. This batch produced 500,000 pieces, with a wholesale price of 0.6 yuan and a market price of three to five yuan. They were sold to over thirty provinces nationwide, with a small portion exported. Due to the time elapsed and the huge volume, it's impossible to trace the specific buyer.\"","Rong Yu immediately laughed.","In other words, this cheap accessory could have been owned by anyone.","She looked up. \"A-Mo, you should really think back carefully. Was the person who saved you that day really Lu Jiaojiao?\"","Seeing the \"500,000 pieces,\" Ji Mohan was also stunned.","He knew Lu Jiaojiao had been ceremoniously welcomed back into the Lu family during her middle school years.","Although the Lu family couldn't compare to the great aristocratic families, they were still among the top-tier wealthy. How could a young lady like Lu Jiaojiao possibly carry a cheap accessory worth a few yuan?","Lu Jiaojiao might not be decked head-to-toe in luxury brands, but she would absolutely never buy low-end goods.","\"A-Mo, the person who saved you shouldn't have such character.\" Rong Yu patted his shoulder. \"Think it through yourself.\"","Ji Mohan sat on the sofa thinking for a long time, perhaps an hour or more. He sent a WeChat message to Lu Jiaojiao: \"Do you remember, it was raining heavily the day you saved me?\"","After a while, Lu Jiaojiao replied: \"I think so.\"","Ji Mohan: \"The day you saved me, you were wearing a white polka-dot ankle-length dress. I never saw you wear it again after that.\"","Lu Jiaojiao: \"I stopped liking it.\"","Ji Mohan stared at his phone screen, his eyes filled with disbelief.","That day, it hadn't rained. The sun was blazing, which was why he was sitting under a tree by the lake reading and then fell into the water.","The person who saved him that day was wearing a black T-shirt and long pants. That's why he could clearly see the gold-and-jade pendant but didn't see the face.","Now, he vaguely remembered... it seemed to be the face of a girl with chubby cheeks... The specific outline was already blurry, but it seemed... she had dimples.","Did Lu Jiaojiao have dimples?","Ji Mohan's memories became momentarily chaotic.","Another message from Lu Jiaojiao arrived: \"Mohan, if I hadn't jumped into the lake to save you that day, there would be no you as you are now. I'm only asking you to marry me. Is that so difficult?\"","A bitter smile escaped Ji Mohan's lips.","Yes, he should have seen it clearly long ago. The person who risked their life to save him must have had an inherently kind nature, definitely not a vampire like Lu Jiaojiao.","She had been leeching off him for so many years, stepping on him to become a senior researcher.","And now, after everything collapsed, she still wanted to keep leeching.","How could a person be so greedy?","He dialed her number.","Lu Jiaojiao quickly answered, a hint of joy on her face. \"Mohan, have you come around?\"","\"I remember now,\" Ji Mohan said, word by word. \"The person who saved me that day wasn't you at all, was it?\"","\"Wh-what are you saying?\" Lu Jiaojiao shuddered, then angrily retorted, \"Are you starting to twist the facts just to shake off your savior?\"","Ji Mohan laughed. \"Then can you describe every single detail of that day when you saved me?\""]},{"number":221,"title":"Chapter 221: He Was Actually Deceived by Such a Person for So Many Years","paragraphs":["Lu Jiaojiao bit her lip hard.","She couldn't say it, of course she couldn't, because the person who saved Ji Mohan wasn't her at all.","That gold and jade pendant was not her belonging.","During her freshman year, there was a competition for the university celebration party host. She and another female classmate both made it to the finals. On the day of the final round, she had a cold and, afraid of losing, she secretly took that girl's gold and jade pendant...","She had heard the girl say it was a keepsake from her deceased elder sister.","When the pendant went missing, the girl searched everywhere for it and consequently missed the final round.","Lu Jiaojiao had casually thrown the pendant into her backpack.","One afternoon, she unexpectedly ran into Ji Mohan. Her backpack was knocked over by someone, and the gold and jade pendant fell to the ground, catching Ji Mohan's eye.","She still remembered Ji Mohan's trembling voice that day: \"Classmate, was it you who saved me by the lake a few months ago? I've been looking for you for so long. Was it you?\"","The female classmates around her all started teasing.","Ji Mohan, a bit embarrassed, added her contact information and then hurried off.","She quickly found out that Ji Mohan was actually the top genius among their entire year...","Everything fell into place naturally.","After all these years, having the truth ripped open like this—how could she possibly accept it?","Ji Mohan said coldly, \"Was that gold and jade pendant something you found, or did you steal it from someone else?\"","The word \"steal\" shattered Lu Jiaojiao's composure.","\"I didn't steal it.\"","She gritted her teeth, emphasizing the words heavily.","Ji Mohan's eyes were full of disappointment.","Before, bound by the moral shackle of her being his lifesaver, he would subconsciously attribute all sorts of positive qualities to Lu Jiaojiao, unwilling to speculate about her with the worst intentions.","But now, he only wanted to describe her with one word: thief.","Stealing the lifesaving token.","Stealing academic achievements.","He had been deceived by such a person for so many years.","He was a complete and utter fool.","He didn't want to say anything more to Lu Jiaojiao. He hung up the phone and blocked and deleted all her contact information.","Early in the morning.","The capital was unusually blessed with bright sunshine. Rong Yu got up early, packed her luggage, and prepared to return to Haicheng.","Ji Yanting had filming to do.","Ji Mohan was under investigation and couldn't leave the capital.","She returned to Haicheng alone.","As soon as she got off the plane, she saw her old son standing at the arrival gate, standing on tiptoe and looking around.","A smile appeared on her face, and she waved. \"Yingbao.\"","Old Master Ji rushed forward. If it weren't for the crowd, he would have given her a bear hug.","Since being reunited with his mother, this was the first time they had been apart for so many days. He was even a little afraid that their reunion was just an illusory dream.","Rong Yu took a lollipop out of her pocket. \"The flight attendants were giving candy to the kids on the plane. Those eight or nine-year-olds really love these, so I shamelessly asked for two. Try one.\"","Old Master Ji almost burst into tears.","So, in his mother's heart, he would always be that eight-year-old child from back then.","He unwrapped the lollipop and popped it into his mouth, reaching for the other one to unwrap it too.","But Rong Yu slapped the back of his hand. \"One for you, one for Duoduo. Don't hog them both. Learn to share.\"","Old Master Ji obediently replied, \"Okay, Mom.\"","Mother and son walked out together. The driver helped Rong Yu with her luggage and loaded it into the car.","\"Yingbao, you go home first,\" Rong Yu said. \"I need to go to the Fourth Aerospace Institute first to submit the project data.\"","Old Master Ji took a lick of his lollipop. \"I'll go with you. I'll wait for you outside.\"","Otherwise, once his mom got immersed in her work, she might forget to come home.","The car drove to the Fourth Aerospace Institute. Old Master Ji stayed in the car enjoying his lollipop. Rong Yu ruffled his white hair and went inside.","As soon as she entered the core area, she heard a celebratory atmosphere.","\"Xiao Yu, you came back at just the right time,\" Dr. Wang Xiaoli grabbed a big handful of candy for her. \"Have some wedding candy, share in the joy.\"","Rong Yu saw the flowers, chocolates, and candies on the desk and immediately understood. The team leader from the neighboring project group had proposed to Wang Xiaoli.","She took the wedding candy and put it in her pocket. \"Congratulations! When's the wedding?\"","Wang Xiaoli coughed. \"Well, this project of ours has just started. Let's talk about marriage after the first phase launch is successful.\"","The man beside her wore a pained expression. \"Heavens, does that mean I have to wait at least three to five more years?\"","\"How can you be thinking about romance when the nation's great undertaking is not yet accomplished?\" Wang Xiaoli snorted. \"Besides, with a genius like Xiao Yu here, the first phase definitely won't take three to five years...\"","After chatting for a while, the group quickly changed the subject and got back to work.","The element Shi was indeed a good thing, perfectly solving the problems they were currently facing...","Rong Yu delegated the work and prepared to leave since her old son was waiting outside. Just as she stepped out of the core area, she saw Song Huai walking towards her.","Song Huai said with a complex expression, \"I never imagined you were in charge of such an important project.\"","He didn't know what the overall project was.","But being responsible for a separate branch was enough to prove Rong Yu's excellence.","At that press conference, over a dozen professors surrounded her, wanting to claim her as their student. He heard she didn't acknowledge any of them in the end.","He didn't know what she was thinking.","But he had to admit, Rong Yu's ability might be above his.","He spoke up, \"Since you're unwilling to acknowledge professors as teachers, what about an academician? My mentor, Liu Jinyue...\"","Rong Yu frowned slightly.","She acknowledged that Song Huai was a very good student.","But sometimes, he was really too annoying.","Always saying these things, over and over, endlessly.","She said calmly, \"Classmate Song, I already have a teacher, a truly remarkable master. Please stop randomly introducing teachers to me.\"","Song Huai was taken aback. \"Who is it?\"","But Rong Yu had already walked away.","She hurried outside to the car. The driver respectfully opened the door for her. As soon as she got in, she pulled the candy from her pocket. \"Now you don't have to fight Duoduo for it. Have as much as you want.\"","Driving home.","Rong Yu sighed with contentment; it was still most comfortable in one's own home.","As soon as mother and son entered the hall, they saw a huge bouquet of roses on the coffee table. It looked like ninety-nine roses, very large and particularly eye-catching.","Old Master Ji pulled the lollipop from his mouth, his eyes wide. \"A Yuan, investigate immediately! Find out which scoundrel had the nerve to send flowers so openly to your great-grandmother! They must be tired of living!\"","The corner of Ji Zhiyuan's mouth twitched. \"Old Master, here's the card from the sender. Please take a look.\"","Old Master Ji snatched it grumpily, glanced at it, and was completely stunned.","Rong Yu also wanted to know.","Who on earth sent her flowers.","She leaned over to look, but Old Master Ji dodged her. \"Mom, Mom, don't look. It'll dirty your eyes.\"","Rong Yu's curiosity was piqued. \"Hurry up, let me see.\"","Old Master Ji tore the card into pieces and stuffed them into the mouth of Songguo, the dog who happened to run in wagging its tail.","Rong Yu: \"...\"","Now her curiosity was even stronger, itching like a kitten scratching at her heart.","Ji Zhiyuan said leisurely, \"Great-grandma, that bouquet... was sent by an elderly lady... for the Old Master...\"","\"Old Master Ji, shut your mouth!\" Old Master Ji's face flushed crimson. \"No, where's my cane? Where has my cane gone?\""]},{"number":222,"title":"Chapter 222: Tang Jin stood on tiptoe and actively kissed Ji Jingchuan's face.","paragraphs":["Rong Yu was dumbfounded.","Had she heard correctly? An elderly lady was sending flowers to her elderly son?","Her son, an octogenarian, at this age, still had an admirer, and it seemed, a rather fervent one...","Old Master Ji's face flushed crimson.","Having such a private matter exposed before his own mother felt utterly mortifying.","Ji Zhiyuan pressed his lips together and explained, \"Old Madam Mei and the old master were classmates. I heard she pursued him with great fanfare back then, but the old master firmly refused and ended up happily marrying our grandmother.\"","He avoided the old master's murderous glare and braced himself to continue, \"Later, when the old master lost his wife in middle age, and Old Madam Mei also lost her husband around the same time, she launched a new round of pursuit... However, the old master didn't agree, and Old Madam Mei eventually quieted down. Now, after... let me calculate, roughly over thirty years, is Old Madam Mei... rekindling an old flame?\"","\"Shut up, shut up!\" Old Master Ji's face burned redder. Muttering, he said, \"Back in school, Mei Wan was the class monitor, and I was the teacher's headache. She was always on my case about studying. I genuinely have trauma from that, I couldn't avoid her fast enough. Who would be so foolish as to marry her... It's been quiet for over thirty years, why is she suddenly pestering me again?\"","Rong Yu spoke up, \"Could this sudden behavior of hers be due to some change in her life circumstances?\"","\"I don't know.\" Old Master Ji's eyes grew slightly red. \"A Yuan's grandmother... she died too early. I really wish Mother could have seen what an excellent wife I married...\"","Rong Yu took his hand. \"The fact that you still miss her so deeply proves she didn't marry the wrong man.\"","\"Wah...\"","Old Master Ji felt like crying.","He had no parents, struggled to grow up alone, and finally met the love of his life, started a family, and had a child. That family of three was so happy.","But the good times didn't last. His wife fell ill and passed away, and all that happiness vanished like a bubble.","His son was just a tiny little thing back then, and the times were rather turbulent, even Furong Manor was sealed off... Those years, he truly didn't know how he endured them.","Finally, when the situation stabilized, his son grew up, married, had children, and the cold, quiet Ji household gradually became lively again.","But then, his son and daughter-in-law both met with misfortune and passed away...","He raised his five grandsons one by one, just as he had raised his son...","Over seventy years of life had made him taste every kind of heart-wrenching pain the world has to offer.","\"Mother—\"","Old Master Ji wailed.","Rong Yu held him, her own eyes also welling up despite herself.","The two elders weeping in each other's arms put Ji Zhiyuan on high alert, completely at a loss for how to console them.","Just then, someone returned at the entrance. He quickly said, \"Great-grandmother, Old Master, A Chuan and Tang Jin are here.\"","Old Master Ji, concerned about face, hurriedly pretended to look for his cane and went to secretly wipe his tears.","Rong Yu took a tissue, dabbed the corners of her eyes, and by the time she looked up, she had regained her usual composure and calm.","\"Grandpa Ji, Brother Ji, Miss Rong.\" Tang Jin greeted them with a smile. \"Tomorrow is the Lantern Festival, right? My mother made some yuanxiao by hand and asked me to bring some over. The taste might not be that great, but it's the thought that counts.\"","She already knew that Rong Yu was the old master's lifesaver, Ji Laowu's tutor, and lived with the Ji family.","\"Please thank your mother for me.\" Old Master Ji had already composed himself and suddenly remembered something. \"Tomorrow's the Lantern Festival, so that means today is Valentine's Day, right? A Chuan, didn't you prepare anything?\"","Rong Yu was taken aback.","So today was Valentine's Day.","No wonder someone proposed at the aerospace institute, no wonder her elderly son received flowers.","She thought of the Valentine's Days that belonged to her and Ji Zheng.","That man wouldn't send flowers, but he would cook for her. Those hands that held guns could actually make a whole table of delicious food.","He would weave all sorts of ornaments from dried leaves and grass—rings, necklaces, bracelets...","When he was busy, he'd be gone for over half a year. During his breaks, he'd disguise himself as a student and 'coincidentally' meet her in class...","That was the romance that belonged to her and him.","A bitter smile escaped Rong Yu's lips.","For her generation, love was a letter left unfinished amidst gunpowder smoke, a lovesick knot tied around a rifle barrel, a gaze so intense it felt scalding when looking at each other across a sea of people, yet not daring to even call out the other's name...","Young people today could finally walk openly under the sun, enjoying the beauty of love.","She saw Tang Jin blush shyly, saw Ji Jingchuan awkwardly drink water, and couldn't help but smile along.","Old Master Ji invited Tang Jin to stay for dinner.","Tang Jin sat openly beside Ji Jingchuan.","After the meal, Tang Jin spoke up, \"A Chuan, I heard you know how to garden. Could I see the flowers you grow?\"","Ji Jingchuan nodded. \"I'll take you to the greenhouse.\"","With about a meter between them, they walked one after the other towards the greenhouse.","Old Master Ji wore a worried expression. \"Why do I feel like these two haven't officially gotten together yet? This pace is way too slow.\"","Rong Yu said, \"It's only a matter of time.\"","She could clearly sense the spark between them.","\"It'll definitely happen today,\" Ji Zhouye said mischievously. \"Old Master, come on, let's go listen to what they're talking about.\"","Old Master Ji nodded vigorously.","The old and the young, followed by Duoduo, the three of them crouched outside the greenhouse.","Voices came from inside.","\"This type of tree is very hard to keep alive, yet it's growing so well here. I heard it can be used to make tea.\"","\"The soil in this pot seems different from the others, no wonder this orchid survived.\"","\"What kind of grass is this...\"","Old Master Ji's eyes widened. \"When these two kids are together, why do they only talk about plants and flowers?\"","Ji Zhouye was exasperated. \"Fourth Brother is too dawdling... Wait, hold on, what did I miss? How did they suddenly end up in an embrace?\"","Tang Jin swore she didn't slip on purpose.","Perhaps the servants had just watered the floor. It was wet, she didn't notice, her foot slipped, and she almost fell, but Ji Jingchuan caught her just in time.","Somehow, she found herself in Ji Jingchuan's arms.","Pressed against his chest, she heard his heart pounding strong and steady. Her face instantly flushed crimson, and she quickly pushed away from Ji Jingchuan to stand properly.","\"A Jin,\" Ji Jingchuan began. \"The old master asked if I had prepared anything for Valentine's Day. Actually, I had it ready a while ago...\"","He crouched down, picked up a pot of orchids from the floor, and offered it to her.","Old Master Ji almost fainted. \"At this season, the orchid isn't even blooming. This is practically a pot of dirt with a blade of grass. This child has no sense of romance at all. This is just tragic.\"","\"Stay calm, Old Master,\" Ji Zhouye whispered, suppressing his excitement. \"That shiny thing on the orchid leaf, what is it?\"","Duoduo widened her eyes. \"It's a necklace! Oh my, what a beautiful necklace.\"","Tang Jin was stunned.","A few days ago, while searching for inspiration, she had asked Ji Jingchuan to accompany her shopping. At the time, she had glanced at this necklace a few extra times. How could she have imagined this man had secretly bought it?","The necklace itself wasn't particularly expensive. What was precious was his thoughtfulness.","Ji Jingchuan stepped closer.","Tang Jin lifted her face.","\"This isn't suitable for kids, don't look!\" Old Master Ji covered Duoduo's eyes. After a moment, he let go. \"Oh, never mind, you can look. Your Fourth Uncle is too much of a coward, he doesn't even dare to kiss her... Wait, no, you'd better not look after all!\"","Then, Tang Jin stood on her tiptoes and actively kissed Ji Jingchuan on the cheek."]},{"number":223,"title":"Chapter 223: Those Who Cannot Get into College Are Not Worthy of Having a Wife","paragraphs":["Ji Jingchuan's face instantly flushed crimson.","He looked like a boiled shrimp, even his ears turning red. His hands didn't know where to put themselves, and he didn't dare look at Tang Jin, glancing left and right instead. Then, he spotted a few sneaky figures outside the greenhouse.","Tang Jin also looked over and froze completely.","Had... had Old Master Ji seen the scene of her actively kissing Ji Jingchuan?","Would the old master think she was a frivolous girl?","She nearly dropped the pot of orchids she was holding.","Ji Jingchuan put an arm around her shoulders. Despite his own face burning with embarrassment, he managed to say, \"Duoduo, Fourth Uncle sees you.\"","Old Master Ji's face stiffened.","Ji Zhouye wiped his own face.","Seeing Duoduo meant they had been seen too.","Getting caught eavesdropping was really quite awkward.","Old Master Ji coughed. \"It was this kid, Ah Ye, who insisted on dragging me over.\"","Before Ji Zhouye could defend himself, the old man gave him a kick. \"School's starting soon. Shouldn't you hurry back to your room and study? Always sticking your nose where it doesn't belong. Someone who can't even get into university doesn't deserve to get a wife.\"","Ji Zhouye: \"...\"","Always picking on him, just because he was an easy target. Just wait, he'd get into Tsinghua University and then strut around the house.","\"Now that you two have settled your relationship, my mind is at ease,\" Old Master Ji said, putting on a dignified elder's air. \"Shall we pick an auspicious date and start preparing for the engagement?\"","Ji Jingchuan looked at Tang Jin. \"What do you think?\"","Tang Jin was still feeling dizzy. \"An-anything is fine. Um, Grandfather Ji, it's getting late, I should head home.\"","Duoduo waved, saying sweetly, \"Goodbye, Fourth Auntie!\"","That \"Fourth Auntie\" nearly made Tang Jin faint.","Ji Jingchuan quickly saw Tang Jin out.","He had gotten his driver's license and bought a modest, sensible car. Finally, he didn't need to be driven around by a girl anymore.","Inside the car, in the confined space, an inexplicable sense of intimacy flowed.","Ji Jingchuan found it a little hard to breathe.","He glanced at Tang Jin, saw her looking straight ahead with a calm expression, quickly adjusted his breathing, and turned on the music. With other sounds filling the air, he finally relaxed a bit more.","Tang Jin tilted her head slightly, looking at Ji Jingchuan's profile.","His features were truly outstanding, and he looked so well-behaved, making it hard for anyone not to feel fondness for him.","During these days together, he did whatever she said, went wherever she suggested. Who wouldn't like such an obedient boyfriend?","The drive continued until they reached the small villa where Tang Jin lived with her mother.","He got out, opened the car door for Tang Jin, and said, \"I'll walk you in. It's a good chance to pay my respects to your mother.\"","Tang Jin led him inside.","Upon opening the door, they saw there was actually a guest inside—Tang Jiaquan, the eldest grandson of the Tang family's current generation.","\"Well, well, if it isn't Little Jin,\" Tang Jiaquan chuckled. \"It's Valentine's Day today. Been out on a date?\"","Tang Jin frowned. \"What are you trying to say?\"","Tang Jiaquan stood up.","He had come to visit his second aunt to find out exactly what the relationship was between Tang Jin and Ji Jingchuan. Now, seeing them together, it was perfectly clear.","He patted Ji Jingchuan's shoulder. \"There's a guys' gathering later, lots of young people. Ah Chuan, why don't you come along and have some fun, see a bit of the world?\"","A well-mannered smile appeared on Ji Jingchuan's face. \"No need, Brother Jiaquan. I still have to go home and study.\"","Tang Jiaquan's eyes revealed disdain.","As expected of a kid raised in the countryside, too honest and simple. This kind of person was easy to manipulate.","He would never allow Tang Jin to marry into the Ji family. Otherwise, his position as the eldest grandson would be under immense threat.","He smiled. \"We must hang out together sometime, for sure.\"","With that, he strode out.","\"Jingchuan, it's getting late. I won't keep you,\" Mrs. Tang said, seeing him out. She then turned back to Tang Jin with a worried expression. \"Tang Jiaquan is the eldest grandson of the main branch. It's only natural for him to inherit the Tang family. Why are you wading into this muddy water? If he gets ruthless, you won't be able to handle it.\"","Tang Jin said calmly, \"If I can't even handle Tang Jiaquan, then I truly don't deserve to inherit the Tang family. Mom, don't worry about these things.\"","The winter break passed in the blink of an eye.","On the first day of the new semester, the school gate was bustling. Rong Yu brought her two \"grandsons\" to school.","Classmates in the classroom were sharing stories from their winter break.","The class monitor and the class secretary wrote a line on the blackboard at the back of the classroom: 109 Days Until the College Entrance Exam.","\"Classmates, from now on, every single day, you must double your efforts in studying. Every drop of sweat you shed now will be the confidence you feel when opening your admission letters in the future. Top universities don't hand out passes to the lazy,\" Pei Yaru declared loudly. \"Look at the countdown on the classroom wall. Doesn't it look like the sign for the last hundred meters of a marathon? Can't catch your breath? Legs feel like lead? Pressure overwhelming? But those who cross the finish line are always the tough ones who grit their teeth and never stop...\"","The study atmosphere in Class Twenty grew even more intense.","Somehow, without anyone quite noticing, the label of \"the class of underachievers\" had been quietly shed.","The boys who used to skip class no longer missed a single lesson.","The girls who loved reading novels now took notes seriously.","Their precious youth was being poured out in the classroom... In such an atmosphere, even Rong Yu felt particularly motivated. By the end of the day, she had broken through two data nodes.","The day's studies concluded.","Driving home, before even entering the main gate, Rong Yu heard her \"old son\" roaring: \"Mei Wan, you're of an age now. Aren't you afraid the younger generation will laugh at you for doing such things? I really don't have time for your antics.\"","In the living room sat an elegant lady in her seventies, wearing a graceful dress. Her face was pale, her eyes glistening with tears, her voice hoarse. \"Shunying, I just... don't want to leave any regrets in this life.\"","Old Master Ji turned his head away. \"You know very well my feelings for my late wife. Some things cannot be forced.\"","\"Alright then,\" Mei Wan stood up. \"I'll come again tomorrow. Don't worry, I won't do anything. Just keep me company for some tea and conversation.\"","She took one last look at Ji Shunying and walked out, her steps somewhat unsteady.","Old Master Ji was exasperated. He instructed, \"Old Yu, if she comes again tomorrow, tell her I'm not in.\"","Rong Yu watched Mei Wan leave the estate before getting out of the car, frowning. \"That old lady's health doesn't seem very good.\"","\"Great-grandmother is right,\" Ji Zhiyuan said quietly. \"Grandson Mei just contacted me. The old lady was recently diagnosed with brain cancer. The tumor's in a tricky spot, inoperable. Her life expectancy is less than a month...\"","Old Master Ji was stunned. \"What did you say?\"","Mei Wan was his high school classmate. They had shared the most passionate years of their youth. While there were no romantic feelings, they had a deep friendship as classmates.","Moreover, the Mei and Ji families often interacted and had a very good relationship.","To hear that a friend his own age was nearing the end of her life... how could it not be heartbreaking?"]},{"number":224,"title":"Chapter 224: I think I heard Lao Ji calling Miss Rong \"Mom\".","paragraphs":["Any disease, with the word \"cancer\" attached, becomes filled with despair.","Old Master Ji sat in a daze for a long time before speaking slowly, \"Old Yu, when Mei Wan comes tomorrow, make a pot of her favorite flower tea. Oh, and she likes sweet pastries. The younger generation in the Mei family won't let her have them, afraid of diabetes... She didn't get diabetes, but ended up with brain cancer instead. Let her eat and drink what she wants, so she won't be longing for those sweets after she's buried.\"","Steward Yu noted down each point.","Rong Yu comforted her old son, practiced piano with Duoduo until nine o'clock, took a stroll to Ji Zhouye's room to explain a few physics problems, and only then returned to her own room to rest.","She was sleeping fitfully, unsure of the time, when she suddenly heard noises from downstairs.","She threw off the covers and hurried down. Pushing the door open, she saw her old son sitting by the bed, continuously wiping his tears.","\"Yingbao, what's wrong? What happened?\"","Seeing his mother, Old Master Ji threw himself into her arms, his tears flowing even more uncontrollably.","Rong Yu looked down and saw the message on the phone screen. It was an obituary notice sent by the head of the Mei family a few minutes ago: \"Our beloved mother, Mei Wan, passed away unfortunately at 3 a.m., at the age of 78. The memorial service will be held on...\"","\"If I had known she wouldn't make it through tonight, I would have insisted she stay for a meal,\" her old son said, his voice choked. \"If it weren't for her pushing me to study back then, I never would have gotten into university. I've always been grateful to her... but I never thanked her to her face...\"","He wiped his tears fiercely, but more overflowed, tracing the wrinkles on his face, gathering into droplets at his chin, and falling onto Rong Yu.","She patted his back gently. \"When it's light, Mom will go with you to see Madame Mei off on her final journey.\"","Old Master Ji couldn't sleep. He sat on the balcony, his voice hoarse, telling Rong Yu amusing stories from his school days.","The sky gradually brightened.","Ji Zhiyuan arranged for a car to accompany the two elders to the Mei residence.","At the entrance of the Mei family home, they met Old Hai and Old Si who had also come. These two were also classmates of Mei Wan.","The portrait was placed at the front. The person in the photo wore a bright, radiant smile. This was probably Mei Wan over thirty years ago, in her early forties, a woman's most mature and beautiful age.","A member of the Mei family said, \"Our mother passed away peacefully. After she was diagnosed with brain cancer, she said she hoped to leave this world beautifully, and for everyone to send her off to the next life with happiness.\"","Old Master Ji spoke softly, \"Mei Wan, thank you. Rest in peace.\"","Old Hai said optimistically, \"I heard the late stages of brain cancer are particularly painful. For her to pass in her sleep is quite a blessing. Let's get a share of that good fortune.\"","Old Si wiped a tear. \"A few days ago, on Valentine's Day, I even sent Mei Wan a bouquet of flowers. She didn't pay me any mind. Hopefully, in our next life, fate will let us be husband and wife.\"","Old Hai's eyes widened. \"You had a crush on Mei Wan?\"","Old Si, deeply saddened, remained silent.","After Rong Yu had offered incense, the group left.","Seeing the three old fellows in low spirits, she thought for a moment and said, \"I think there's a concert in Haicheng this afternoon. How about going to listen and clear your minds?\"","The three had no objections.","Ji Zhiyuan drove the group of elders to the concert venue. As they came on short notice, VIP boxes were unavailable, and they could only get seats in the back row. The four of them had to squeeze into a row with the rest of the audience.","Old Hai complained, \"Old Ji, your eldest grandson isn't very capable. He actually made us old folks sit in such cramped seats.\"","Old Si frowned. \"What worries me most is hygiene. Who knows how many people have sat in these ordinary section seats?\"","Old Master Ji said, \"If you don't want to listen, then get lost.\"","Old Hai and Old Si fell quiet.","The concert began.","Rong Yu was someone who loved music, but in past years, she hadn't had much time to indulge in her passions.","She was looking forward to this unexpected concert.","The lights dimmed, the conductor raised the baton, and they all unconsciously straightened their postures.","It turned out to be a piece about mothers. The melody gradually unfolded like a slowly opened letter. The violin notes were as gentle as a breeze, then the clarinet joined in with a warm tone. Suddenly, when the cello solo began, the mood sank, turning melancholic and sorrowful. One could tell immediately the composer was mourning a departed mother...","Rong Yu's heart skipped a beat.","She turned to look.","Goodness, the three old fellows, each with tears welling in their eyes, were all beginning to think of departed loved ones.","They had come here to comfort them, but instead, it seemed to have made them sadder.","\"Mom...\" Old Master Ji leaned on Rong Yu's shoulder, sobbing. \"When you passed away so suddenly back then, my world collapsed. I don't even know how I got through it! Mom, you don't understand how painful it is for an eight-year-old child to lose his mother. Mom...\"","Old Si, who had been secretly wiping tears, froze. \"Old Hai, I think I heard Old Ji call Miss Rong 'Mom'.\"","Old Hai said in a muffled voice, \"If your ears are playing tricks, go see a doctor. Don't spout such nonsense.\"","He turned to look.","He got a huge fright.","That shameless Old Ji was actually crying on Miss Rong's shoulder and wiping his tears and snot all over her clothes.","The key point was, Miss Rong had a look of... benevolence? Wait, benevolence?","A high school girl, showing a benevolent expression?","But thinking about it carefully, whenever they faced Miss Rong, he and Old Si always felt inexplicably diminished... Could it really be?","Old Si: \"Old Ji's birth mother was named Rong Yu. Same name. Could it be Aunt Rong reincarnated?\"","Old Hai: \"That doesn't make sense.\"","Old Si: \"Look at Miss Rong's demeanor. It's completely different from an eighteen-year-old girl. At such a young age, she's already in the aerospace institute. Aunt Rong was a professor back then. It must be the same person!\"","Old Hai: \"I don't think so.\"","Old Si: \"Old Ji has become less and less steady, acting like a brash young punk. I knew there had to be a reason...\"","Someone in front turned around and snapped, \"Will you two be quiet? You're disturbing everyone.\"","The two successfully shut their mouths, but their eyes remained restless, constantly stealing glances at Rong Yu.","When the concert ended and they walked out,","Old Hai spoke up: \"By the way, Aunt Rong... ahem, I mean, Miss Rong.\"","Believe in science! He had to believe in science! He couldn't be influenced by that fool Old Si!","Old Si pulled Old Master Ji aside and asked in a low voice, \"Miss Rong is Aunt Rong, isn't she?\"","Old Master Ji acted as if his tail had been stepped on. \"Of course not!\"","He said with a serious expression, \"Old Si, philosophically speaking, matter determines consciousness. My mom passed away long ago, so her consciousness no longer exists. Don't entertain such wild thoughts. If people found out that you, the head of the Si family, are engaging in feudal superstition, your family's stocks would plummet!\"","Old Si felt something wasn't quite right, but couldn't put his finger on it.","Forget it. Among the three of them, he was the dumbest. Dumb people should listen to the smart ones.","Rong Yu, standing nearby, couldn't help but laugh softly.","Old Hai stood there dumbfounded.","That laugh, it really was... very much like Aunt Rong."]},{"number":225,"title":"Chapter 225: Being able to reunite and gather again is a gift from heaven.","paragraphs":["Feeling the impermanence of life, Rong Yu wanted to see Tang Che.","The three old fellows hadn't been to the Tang family for a while either, and they all nodded in agreement.","Tang Che's health had deteriorated further. He was sitting in the courtyard watching new buds sprout from a withered tree, his cloudy eyes showing no flicker of emotion.","It wasn't until the butler announced, \"Miss Rong is here,\" that the old man's eyes finally shifted.","He coughed and said, \"I just woke up, I'm a mess. Quickly, wheel me to the mirror.\"","The butler pushed the wheelchair into the house.","In front of the mirror, Tang Che combed his silver hair. Looking at the deep wrinkles covering his face, he suddenly let out a bitter laugh.","He was no longer young. No matter how he tried to tidy up, he was just an old man shrouded in twilight, devoid of vitality.","\"Uncle Tang!\"","The voices of the three old fellows arrived first.","Tang Che's face broke into a wide smile. \"You've all come together. Sit, have some tea.\"","Rong Yu saw how much effort it took for him to lift the teacup, and her nose suddenly stung with emotion.","She knew that all lives must eventually reach their end.","She knew that living to a hundred was already considered a long life.","She knew even more that being able to reunite and gather like this was a gift from heaven.","Yet, it was still hard to accept that she would have to watch him leave this world.","Old Master Ji said bluntly, \"Uncle Tang, the relationship between Chuan and Little Jin is settled. How about picking a date for their engagement?\"","Old Master Hai hurriedly chimed in, \"Our Chang'an and Tang Mi's relationship is settled too. Let's have a joint engagement ceremony!\"","Old Master Si widened his eyes. \"You're ganging up on me!\"","Old Master Hai snorted. \"Blame your own descendants for not being up to par.\"","Old Master Si wanted to retort.","His phone vibrated. Looking at the message, his own grandson, Si Lin, had just gotten into a fight at the racetrack and suffered a minor arm injury. He had posted a photo in the \"Loving Family\" group chat, playing up his misery.","Seeing Si Lin's pathetic look, Old Master Si nearly spat out blood in frustration. Day in and day out, it was either horse racing or car racing, either chasing romance or picking fights. It was a headache just looking at him. The old man promptly kicked Si Lin out of the group chat and blocked him.","After doing this, his mood instantly improved.","Tang Che smiled and instructed, \"Youyi, go contact a master to calculate an auspicious date. Let's settle on the day today.\"","Tang Youyi nodded and went to arrange it.","The master, based on the birth dates of the four individuals, calculated a favorable day: April 21st.","With two months until the engagement day, it was ample time for the Tang, Ji, and Hai families to prepare properly.","After the group left, Madam Tang frowned. \"What exactly are the old master's thoughts on the matter of the successor?\"","Tang Youyi said calmly, \"When the time is right, Uncle will naturally make it public. There's no need for idle speculation.\"","\"In my opinion, Jiaquan is the most suitable,\" Madam Tang said. \"He is the eldest grandson of the eldest branch, and he has held the position of General Manager at Tang Corporation for over a decade without a single mistake. As long as the old master isn't confused by illness, he should finalize the successor's identity soon to prevent unrest among the people.\"","Tang Youyi lowered his eyes.","Times of unrest are the best test of character.","He hoped his descendants would hold fast to their principles and avoid causing trouble.","As soon as he returned home, Old Master Ji happily said to Ji Jingchuan, \"Don't shave your head again. For the engagement banquet in two months, you'll need a proper hairstyle. Don't let that grandson Hai Chang'an outshine you.\"","Ji Jingchuan's ears reddened slightly. \"What's the exact date for the engagement?\"","Ji Zhouye couldn't resist teasing, \"Hahaha, Fourth Brother is anxious. He's getting anxious!\"","\"Shut up, you brat,\" Old Master Ji glared at him, then turned back with a kindly expression. \"Chuan, the date is April 21st. You just focus on your studies. You don't need to worry about the arrangements.\"","Ji Jingchuan gave a low hum of acknowledgment.","Then he looked at Ji Zhouye. \"A'Ye, you only scored a little over a hundred on today's math quiz. Upstairs. I'll go over the problems with you.\"","Ji Zhouye: \"...\"","He hadn't forgotten. During winter break, just because he'd casually remarked that Tang Jin used to cry a lot as a child and looked a bit ugly when she cried...","Fourth Brother had tortured him for a whole day. For every wrong answer, he had to copy the problem ten times. Get it wrong again, copy it a hundred times. Wrong again... Well, there was no 'wrong again,' because copying it a hundred times had already engraved that type of problem into his bones.","He put on a woeful face. \"Fourth Brother, a tutor is coming later. The tutor can explain it to me.\"","\"No,\" Ji Jingchuan smiled. \"Be good. Upstairs.\"","Ji Zhouye was on the verge of collapse.","Old Master Ji kicked him in the backside. \"Chuan is helping you with your studies, and you're still reluctant? You brat just need a good lesson!\"","Rong Yu said with a smile, \"How about I explain the problems to you instead?\"","Ji Zhouye covered his backside and ran upstairs.","Great-Grandma explaining problems was even more terrifying.","She would expand from a simple problem type to extremely complex knowledge and even recommend advanced mathematics books for him to browse in his spare time... He was just a useless slacker! What was the point of learning such profound stuff!","The next morning at school.","Right after morning self-study, Rong Yu was called over by her homeroom teacher.","Pei Yaru took a competition notification letter from her desk drawer. \"The gold medal winner of last year's National Physics Finals will represent China in the International Physics Finals. It's next Wednesday in Hong Kong, a three-day event. Are you available to participate?\"","She knew Rong Yu was involved in a very important, highly classified project at the Aerospace Research Institute.","The competition was important, but the project was more so.","Rong Yu looked at the notification. Over forty countries and regions were participating, including the United States, Japan, France, Germany... Seeing these country names, the painful history of the Eight-Nation Alliance's invasion of China automatically surfaced in her mind.","She nodded without hesitation. \"I have time.\"","Pei Yaru pointed to a QR code. \"Scan this to submit your personal information. The school will arrange your flight and hotel.\"","Right after submitting her information, Rong Yu was added as a friend by the team leader teacher and joined a group chat.","In the group, she saw two familiar faces: Song Huai and Sheng Ciyuan.","Team Leader Teacher Huang: \"Hello everyone. You will soon represent China in the Global Physics Finals. I now announce that the captain of the Chinese team is Rong Yu, and the vice-captain is Su Ronghua. The captain and vice-captain must take up their responsibilities and lead the Chinese team to win the gold medal...\"","Sitting in his classroom, Song Huai saw this message, and his gaze darkened for a moment.","He remembered during the domestic physics finals, he was the captain, Zhang Haoyu was the vice-captain, and Rong Yu was nothing.","And now.","Rong Yu was the captain.","To be honest, this feeling was quite unpleasant.","Just then, someone spoke in the group.","Su Ronghua: \"Teacher Huang, why is Rong Yu the captain? What is the reason for appointing her?\"","Song Huai knew of Su Ronghua.","He was a genius from an experimental high school in Su City, currently only a second-year high school student. He had already won various gold medals in competitions, participated in research projects, and published papers, being fought over by Tsinghua and Peking University for early admission.","But he had refused.","It was said he wanted to earn his way into the world's top-ranked university.","Teacher Huang: \"Rong Yu is the project initiator for the Shi Research and Application project. This is a national-level key project. She is worthy of the team captain position.\""]},{"number":226,"title":"Chapter 226: This kid can act even more silly and coquettish than Yingbao did in childhood.","paragraphs":["Su Ronghua remained silent for about two minutes.","Then, he flung two news article links into the group chat.","\"Shocking! Actress Listed as Research Paper Author? Deep Dive into the Academic Scandal Behind Shi Research\"","\"Celebrity Attached to Top Scientific Achievement, Why Are the Real Researchers Collectively Silent?\"","Seeing the messages, Song Huai was astonished.","He never imagined that someone would dare post such things in the group. Given his personality, no matter what he thought internally, he would keep it to himself first.","But.","On second thought, it was indeed reasonable for Rong Yu to face skepticism.","She was a repeat student, originally from the arts stream, had never appeared in any academic competitions before, had never published any journal papers... Suddenly, she was placed above everyone else. Who would be willing to accept that?","Song Huai initially wanted to say something, but after some thought, he let it go.","Other members in the group also didn't speak up.","Amidst the heavy silence, Sheng Ciyuan patted Su Ronghua.","Immediately after, he sent three consecutive links.","\"A Breath of Fresh Air in Entertainment! Actress Rong Yu's 24-Hour Lab Grind Leads to Groundbreaking Results\"","\"Shattering Stereotypes! Ministry of Education Cites Rong Yu to Emphasize 'Diverse Paths to Success' in Education\"","\"Editorial from National Science Daily: Don't Let Prejudice Stifle the Next Celebrity Scientist\"","Sheng Ciyuan: \"Did the Su family not pay your internet bill this year? How can you keep up with academic news with this kind of connection speed?\"","Su Ronghua: \"What you call news is just fluff praising academic bubbles.\"","Teacher Huang, who had been absent for a while, suddenly posted a photo.","Teacher Huang: \"This is the on-site vote by the organizing committee members. Rong Yu was elected team leader with six votes. Su Ronghua was elected deputy leader with three votes. If anyone disagrees, an internal team vote can be held again after the preliminary rounds.\"","Song Huai was taken aback.","There were twelve teachers on the organizing committee. Rong Yu got six votes, Su Ronghua three, Sheng Ciyuan two, Ding Zhe one, and he and another person received zero votes.","He knew that the higher one goes on this path, the more geniuses one encounters, but he never thought he would be utterly crushed, not even a speck left.","During lunch in the cafeteria, most students had heard about the incident and were discussing it nonstop.","\"Representing the country in an international competition, facing top students from around the world, Song Huai and Rong Yu are truly amazing.\"","\"Rong Yu is really the pride of Haicheng No.1 High School. Several of my younger siblings and cousins asked me to get Rong Yu's autograph, I'm just a bit too intimidated to ask.\"","\"I'm so envious of Class 20 students, getting personal tutoring from Rong Yu...\"","Sitting by the window in the cafeteria, Rong Ruoyao felt a sour taste in her heart.","In the past, such topics always revolved around her and Song Huai. Gradually, everyone's attention had shifted entirely to Rong Yu.","It seemed no matter where she went, Rong Yu was the center of attention.","Seeing Song Huai also looking in Rong Yu's direction, she couldn't help but bite her lip and say, \"Song Huai, there are a few math problems I don't quite understand. Could you explain them to me in the library?\"","Song Huai withdrew his gaze. \"Okay.\"","Amidst the noisy chatter, the two left the cafeteria.","Rong Ruoyao's lips were pressed tightly together.","With a hundred days left until the college entrance exam, she had turned down all her acting roles, advertisements, commercial deals, and events in the entertainment industry... She had to get into Capital University. She couldn't let the gap between her and Rong Yu grow too wide...","The news of Rong Yu leading the Chinese team in the international competition acted like a powerful stimulant for everyone in Class 20. Even during breaks, everyone was focused on studying.","Due to a lack of educational resources growing up, Ji Jingchuan's weak point was English. He spent most of his day working on it.","Just after finishing an English essay, he glanced down at his phone. The message he had sent to Tang Jin in the morning still hadn't been replied to, a whole day later.","Yesterday, their elders had set a date for their engagement. He and Tang Jin, the two people involved, hadn't even discussed it yet.","As evening classes ended, he quickly stepped out of the classroom and called Tang Jin. He planned to ask her out for dinner, then a walk, and take the opportunity to propose.","Although everything was already settled, he hadn't actually proposed yet.","For a girl, a proposal should be very important.","The call went through, but no one answered.","\"Let's go, school's out!\" Ji Zhouye threw an arm around his shoulder and with his other hand hooked Rong Yu's neck, swaggering along. \"I've got the school heartthrob on my left and the school belle on my right. The most envied person in this school, male or female, has got to be me, hahaha!\"","Rong Yu wore an expressionless face. \"Let go, or I'll chop your paws off.\"","Ji Zhouye grinned cheekily and leaned in. \"In class today, the chemistry teacher said I've made great progress. Great-Grandma, please give me a little reward. Let's be clear upfront, no Huanggang Secret Test Papers, and no 'Five Years of College Entrance Exams, Three Years of Simulation,' okay? Please...\"","After cramming all winter break, this kid's grades had indeed improved significantly.","Rong Yu wasn't an unreasonable person. She thought for a moment and said, \"Your reward is five minutes of game time today.\"","\"Great! Games!\" Ji Zhouye's smile vanished. \"Wait, no, Great-Grandma, just five minutes? That's useless! How about half an hour? Come on, Great-Grandma, let me play for half an hour... Fourth Brother, you tell her, is this fair?\"","Ji Jingchuan was clearly distracted. Suppressing his emotions, he said, \"Then accumulate five minutes a day. In ten days, that's fifty minutes. That should be enough.\"","Ji Zhouye whined and complained the whole way home.","Rong Yu found it hard to handle. This kid was even better at acting silly and cooing for favors than Yingbao was when he was little. In the end, she, a person of principle, compromised and allowed him six minutes of game time.","Ji Zhouye: \"...\"","Fine, fine, picking on the academically challenged, are we?","He'd just save it up. Six minutes a day, in a hundred days that's six hundred minutes. He was going to play until the world went dark.","They rode home in the car.","Ji Jingchuan checked his phone. Still no reply from Tang Jin.","Later that evening, after finishing his English essay book, he once again dialed Tang Jin's number. Just as he thought no one would answer, a voice came through: \"Chuan, I've been very busy these past two days. Let's not talk for now.\"","Before Ji Jingchuan could say anything, the call was disconnected.","A trace of self-mockery tinged Ji Jingchuan's dark eyes.","In the beginning, she was always the one initiating contact. She would wait for him in her car outside the school gate, make restaurant reservations, ask him what he liked to eat.","She would also send him English journals recommended by others to help him improve his English.","He had gradually opened up his heart too.","But he forgot that he and Tang Jin were only together, only arranged to be married, because of the needs and ties of their two families.","Now that their relationship was official, naturally, she no longer felt the need to put in the effort.","He could understand.","After all, he hadn't given his whole heart either.","Ji Jingchuan barely slept all night.","After leading her \"old son\" through his exercises, Rong Yu entered the dining room and saw the dark circles under his eyes. She said gently, \"Don't overwork yourself studying. Make sure to rest.\"","Ji Jingchuan nodded. \"I know, Great-Grandma.\"","Ji Zhouye came downstairs with messy bedhead, a steamed bun dangling from his mouth, and said bluntly, \"Fourth Brother, why do I get the feeling you look like you've just been dumped?\"","Rong Yu didn't pay much attention to the comment.","But after school, she remembered that before, Tang Jin used to wait for Chuan at the school gate every day after classes. The young couple was so lovey-dovey, it made people's teeth ache just watching.","Now, Tang Jin hasn't been seen for several days. Have they had a falling out?"]},{"number":227,"title":"Chapter 227: Young People, Take the Initiative to Communicate","paragraphs":["From the very first day Ji Jingchuan returned to the Ji family, Rong Yu knew this was a child who would only bury things in his heart.","She asked, \"Did you have a fight with Tang Jin?\"","Ji Jingchuan smiled and said, \"No.\"","He wasn't someone who showed his emotions easily, and Tang Jin's temperament was also quite steady. How could they possibly argue?","\"Young people, you should take the initiative to communicate about things, don't keep them bottled up inside,\" Rong Yu said. \"Although I don't understand dating, I think you could take the initiative to go find her.\"","Ji Jingchuan nodded. \"Okay.\"","He had Ji Zhouye accompany Rong Yu home.","He drove his own car towards Tang's Jewelry Company.","He knew Tang Jin was a workaholic; at this hour, she was definitely still working overtime at the office. While waiting at a red light on the way, he even booked a table at a Western restaurant.","When he drove up to the company entrance and had just parked, he saw Tang Jin standing at the main entrance with a man.","Ji Jingchuan's hand loosened from the car door handle, and he sat there quietly.","He sat there for about ten minutes, and the two of them talked for about ten minutes. The man used body language from time to time. At a glance, the relationship between them clearly went beyond the scope of mere friends.","He pursed his lips.","Unable to control himself, he picked up his phone, rolled down the window, and took a photo.","He had never been a paragon of virtue. Being well-behaved, sensible, obedient... these were merely his survival disguises.","The dark side within him was sometimes beyond even his own control.","The photo captured the man's face clearly.","Ji Jingchuan had spent the entire winter break working on the top floor of the Ji Group headquarters and had gotten to know many secretaries and assistants. He thought for a moment and sent the photo to the Chairman's secretary, Secretary Jiang: \"Could I trouble Secretary Jiang to help find out what relationship this person has with the Tang family's Third Young Lady?\"","Five minutes later, Secretary Jiang sent over several pages of information.","Ji Jingchuan only noticed one sentence: \"...was once Tang Jin's boyfriend.\"","He deleted the messages and drove away.","At the entrance of Tang's, Tang Jin's face was icy cold. \"...So it was you who logged into my account and fabricated the evidence. I must have been blind before, actually finding a boyfriend in the trash!\"","\"There's only one way to clear your name, and that's to get back together with me.\" The man reached out and stroked her hair. \"That kid from the Ji family grew up in the countryside. How could he possibly be worthy of you, Jin Jin? I was wrong before. I'll change, I promise I'll treat you well from now on, I'll never let you suffer any grievance again...\"","Before he could finish his sentence,","Tang Jin raised her hand and delivered a resounding slap across his face. \"Back when we were dating, you openly cheated. I let it go lightly then, but that doesn't mean I'm someone without a temper!\"","Before the man could react, she backhanded him with another slap. \"A good ex should be as quiet as if they were dead, not colluding with Tang Jiaquan to scheme against me. I've noted this debt, and I'll settle it with you slowly later!\"","She cast a look of disgust at the man, then quickly got into her car in her high heels.","She had twenty minutes left. If she couldn't prove her innocence, she would be expelled from Tang's and lose everything.","For the past two or three days, she had barely slept, opening her eyes only to audit accounts.","Fortunately, she had figured it out.","She drove to the headquarters building of Tang's, went up to the top floor at the fastest speed, and knocked on the door of the CEO's office.","\"Grandfather.\" Tang Jin walked to the desk and handed over a piece of evidence. \"The accounts at Tang's Jewelry do indeed have problems, but this particular issue started going bad eight years ago...\"","Tang Youyi's expression was grave.","A week ago, the head of the headquarters finance department reported a major discrepancy in the finances of the jewelry company. He had ordered a comprehensive investigation.","This matter was assigned to Tang Jiaquan to handle. In the end, it was found that Tang Jin had remotely accessed the jewelry company's financial database... causing the account issues. Tang Jin became the prime suspect.","Naturally, he didn't believe Tang Jin would do such a thing.","But all the evidence pointed to Tang Jin.","He had given Tang Jin three days.","\"And I've only been at the jewelry company for half a year. This blame should not fall on me no matter what.\" Tang Jin's voice was clear. \"I checked the annual news about the Tang family from that year. That year, cousin Jiaquan had some issues in his personal life. There was news saying cousin Jiaquan bought a fifty-million property for a model... I suggest Grandfather arrange for someone to thoroughly investigate where that money came from.\"","\"And also—\" She paused and produced another piece of evidence. \"I also found out that cousin Jiaquan has been inappropriately close with several of Tang's clients in private, accepting antiques worth tens of millions from them. May I assume that cousin Jiaquan is accepting bribes by exploiting his position?\"","After reading the documents, Tang Youyi was instantly overcome with fury, his lips trembling.","Tang Jiaquan was his first grandson, the child he had invested great effort in nurturing, and also the child he had once placed the highest hopes in.","To seize power, he had actually framed his own cousin.","\"Grandfather, please calm your anger.\" Tang Jin brought over a cup of tea. \"These are just things I found. There might be discrepancies with the facts. Grandfather can arrange for someone to investigate further, so as not to wrong cousin Jiaquan.\"","Tang Youyi looked at her with appreciation. Even with ironclad evidence, she wasn't rushing to condemn her opponent. Such steadiness was indeed sufficient for an heir. He nodded. \"You've worked hard these past three days. Rest for a couple of days before returning to work.\"","Tang Jin nodded and withdrew.","Once outside, she let out a deep sigh of relief. She had won this tough battle.","As soon as she stepped into the elevator, she took out her phone, found Chuan's name, and dialed.","Ji Jingchuan's car had just reached the main gate of Furong Manor. A servant was opening the iron gate to let the car in, but the car stopped halfway through.","The person in the driver's seat was holding his phone, motionless.","Ji Jingchuan looked at the name flashing on the screen, his lips pressed tightly together. Only when the phone stopped vibrating did he relax his taut lips and call back.","His voice was very flat. \"I'm busy. Is there something?\"","\"Busy with homework?\" Tang Jin's lighthearted voice came through. \"Why don't you just bring your homework over? After dinner, I'll keep you company while you do it. I've sent you the address. Come quickly.\"","Ji Jingchuan very much wanted to say he didn't have time.","But... he thought about it. Forget it, he'd still go.","So he turned the car around and drove out.","The car stopped in front of a hot pot restaurant. Tang Jin was sitting by the window, waving at him with a bright, beaming smile.","He walked in. Before he could even speak, Tang Jin couldn't wait to say, \"Chuan, you know what? I pulled off something big these past couple of days. You know my eldest cousin, Tang Jiaquan, right? He actually tried to set me up. Luckily, I minored in accounting in college. Not only did I prove my innocence, I also found evidence of him embezzling company funds and taking bribes... I barely slept these past two days, didn't have time to contact you. I'm really sorry. Let's have some hot pot first. Later, I need to go back and sleep for a full day and night...\"","Ji Jingchuan was momentarily stunned.","So she hadn't been intentionally ignoring him. She had been caught up in trouble.","And the moment the trouble was resolved, she came to find him first.","Joy gradually filled his heart.","Simultaneously, it also bred a great deal of guilt."]},{"number":228,"title":"Chapter 228: Call Four Beauties Over, Jingchuan, Take Your Pick","paragraphs":["The hotpot restaurant was bustling with noise and excitement.","Amidst the clamor of voices filling his ears, Tang Jin sat vividly before him.","Ji Jingchuan placed a slice of meat in her bowl, gazing at her: \"Actually, you could tell me. I can help you.\"","Tang Jin replied dismissively, \"You're still a student. Your primary task is to study hard.\"","Ji Jingchuan sighed. As an older high school student, there were indeed many matters he couldn't easily handle.","He paused, then asked, \"What will ultimately happen to Tang Youyi?\"","\"He's the eldest grandson of the main branch of the Tang family, the General Manager at Tang Group headquarters.\" Tang Jin propped her chin on her hand. \"Grandmother dotes on Tang Jiaquan the most. With her protection, no matter how angry Grandfather is, things will always be minimized in the end. However, even so, Tang Jiaquan won't be able to stay at Tang Group anymore.\"","Ji Jingchuan's eyelashes lowered slightly.","The two happily finished their hotpot, and he drove Tang Jin home.","Tang Jin fell asleep in the car. He carried her out gently, knocked on the Tang family door, and handed her over.","After leaving the Tang residence, Ji Jingchuan sat in his car and checked his social feed. Sure enough, he saw Tang Jiaquan once again rallying people for a gathering.","He opened the chat window with Tang Jiaquan: \"Brother Jiaquan, where are you heading to play? Can you take me along?\"","Seeing the message, Tang Jiaquan was instantly delighted.","He had been worrying about how to find a breakthrough, and now this kid was delivering himself to his doorstep.","Tang Jin at Tang Jewelry had used her position for personal gain, the evidence was solid. Yet, Grandfather had given Tang Jin three days to prove her innocence. Now, those three days were up, and Grandfather still hadn't announced any punishment. He figured it was probably out of consideration for the Ji family.","As long as he ruined the engagement between Tang Jin and Ji Jingchuan, Tang Jin would lose all her support.","Tang Jiaquan made a call: \"Jingchuan, come to the Night Charm bar. Give my name at the door, and someone will bring you to the private room.\"","Ji Jingchuan drove to the bar.","This bar wasn't as quiet as the one Ji Zhouye had taken them to before. As soon as he entered, it was packed everywhere. Dancers in revealing outfits were performing hot dances right on the tables. The men's rowdy cheers mixed with deafening music, creating an unpleasant assault on the ears.","He crossed the main hall and arrived at a private room door.","An attendant opened the door for him.","Upon entering, he saw seven or eight scantily clad women sitting on the sofas. The young masters, wine glasses in their left hands and women in their right arms, looked utterly at ease.","Besides Tang Jiaquan, he recognized one other person: the second young master of the Si family, Si Lin.","Si Lin was the first to stand up: \"Hey, Tang Jiaquan, why did you call Chuan here? A good kid like him doesn't belong in a place like this.\"","\"You can come and enjoy yourself, so why can't Young Master Ji have a taste of the world?\" Tang Jiaquan pushed Si Lin aside, stepped forward, and slung an arm around Ji Jingchuan's shoulders. \"Jingchuan, you're part of our circle. You should learn to enjoy life. Waiter, bring four girls over. Chuan, pick any you like. It's on me.\"","Under the strobe lights, a blush spread across Ji Jingchuan's face. \"Brother Jiaquan, that's not necessary. I'm fine just watching you all have fun.\"","Tang Jiaquan waved his hand grandly, and four women were ushered in, surrounding Ji Jingchuan. One offered him a drink, another fed him fruit, one massaged his shoulders, and another patted his legs...","Si Lin couldn't bear to watch. \"I'm telling you, Chuan, you're still a high school student. Don't get into such wild stuff. Even Ji Zhouye never went this far. How about this, I'll call Aye and have him pick you up.\"","\"Get lost, go away!\" Tang Jiaquan kicked Si Lin aside. \"Aren't you a student too? You have the nerve to say that.\"","Si Lin: \"...\"","He almost forgot, he was indeed a student.","He was a sophomore at a third-rate university. The school was so terrible he didn't want to attend, so he spent his days wandering around...","Tang Jiaquan picked up a glass of wine and handed it to Ji Jingchuan with a smile. \"Here, drink this. After this, we're good brothers.\"","Ji Jingchuan took it, took only a small sip, and frowned. \"It tastes a bit awful.\"","\"Hahaha, you're just not used to the taste of alcohol yet.\" Tang Jiaquan laughed heartily. \"This wine costs tens of thousands a glass. Drink it slowly, don't waste it.\"","Ji Jingchuan nodded obediently. \"Thank you, Brother Jiaquan.\"","He wiped his mouth with a tissue, discreetly spitting the sip of wine into it.","The room was dimly lit and crowded, with glasses scattered all over the coffee table. He stood up and subtly switched the position of his glass.","Soon, the glass he had sipped from ended up in Tang Jiaquan's hand. Tang Jiaquan threw his head back and drained it in one go, not leaving a single drop.","Ji Jingchuan stood up at the right moment. \"Brother Jiaquan, I'm feeling dizzy. I should head out.\"","\"I've arranged a hotel room. You can just rest here for the night.\" Tang Jiaquan stood up unsteadily. \"That guy... forget it. I'm feeling a bit dizzy too. I'll personally take Chuan to rest. The rest of you, have fun. Eat, drink, don't hold back on my account.\"","He supported Ji Jingchuan as they walked out.","Exiting through the bar's back door led directly to a five-star hotel. As soon as they entered the elevator, Ji Jingchuan seemed to lose consciousness.","Tang Jiaquan sneered coldly.","He had drugged that glass of wine. Not a sedative, but an aphrodisiac... If he got a video of Ji Jingchuan fooling around with a woman and showed it to the old man, the old man would be furious and would definitely cancel the engagement between Tang Jin and the Ji family.","Then, Tang Jin would have no backing left.","He would kick Tang Jin out of Tang Group.","He made a call. \"Arrange a few women... actually, one is enough.\"","Arranging too many women would constitute a group activity, which could easily lead to police involvement. If the police started investigating and it traced back to him, that would be troublesome.","Entering the room, Tang Jiaquan's head spun even more.","He didn't think he had drunk that much, so why did his head feel like mush? Walking felt like treading on cotton. He stumbled and fell to the floor, wanting to get up but unable to.","An inexplicable heat surged in his lower abdomen, a wave of restless desire sweeping through his entire body.","It was unbearable, truly unbearable.","He couldn't help but undo his belt and pull down his pants.","Just then, a woman walked through the door. That smoldering heat ignited, instantly blazing into an inferno. He eagerly pounced on her.","\"What's the rush, Young Master Tang?\" The woman was an old acquaintance of his. She giggled coyly, \"I'm not quite ready yet...\"","The two entangled and tumbled onto the large bed.","Ji Jingchuan stood quietly behind the curtains, listening to the sounds from the room. He pressed the shutter button, then silently left the suite.","As soon as he appeared in the hallway, Si Lin spotted him and hurried over. \"I just stepped out to use the restroom, and you were gone. I heard they said Tang Jiaquan brought you to stay at this hotel. This place isn't clean. Let me take you back.\"","Ji Jingchuan looked at him, pausing before asking, \"What do you mean, not clean?\"","\"It's just...\" Si Lin scratched his head. \"Ah, it's hard to explain. Anyway, you shouldn't hang out with Tang Jiaquan anymore. He plays too rough. Don't let him corrupt you.\"","Ji Jingchuan knew that Aye and Si Lin were close, very good friends.","He asked, \"Since you know Tang Jiaquan isn't a good person, why do you still run with him?\"","Si Lin smiled wryly. \"Maybe because Tang Jiaquan and I are the same kind of people?\"","Ji Jingchuan said nothing.","Tang Jiaquan is a truly despicable man. He cheated on his wife during their marriage, kept a mistress, meddled in the Tang Group's affairs, and is nothing but a cancerous tumor to the Tang family. That man is beyond redemption.","But Si Lin... he had seen some news about Si Lin. He was known for dating celebrities and models, changing partners every three months at most, or even within a week. Yet, after breaking up, not a single one of those stars or models ever accused him of having a chaotic private life.","Ji Jingchuan shook his head: \"Thank you for your concern, but I haven't been drinking. I can drive myself back.\"","He got into the car and sent all the photos and videos he had just taken to Tang Youyi."]},{"number":229,"title":"Chapter 229: Tang Family Publicly Severs Ties with Tang Jiaquan","paragraphs":["The night was already deep.","The clock hands pointed to midnight. Tang Youyi still sat in the chairman's office, a thick stack of gathered evidence lying on the desk before him.","He hadn't known until he investigated, but upon looking, he discovered his eldest grandson was thoroughly rotten.","To date, the public funds he had misappropriated amounted to over eighty million.","The bribes and valuables he had accepted, just counting those on the surface, totaled more than one hundred million.","He had trusted this grandson so much, nurturing him with all his heart for so many years, only to raise a major parasite.","His uncle was right; the boy was completely incapable of becoming the helmsman of a great family. If the Tang family were handed to him, their century-old legacy would be ruined sooner or later.","The chairman's secretary stood trembling to the side. \"Should we have the young master come over?\"","Tang Youyi was about to speak.","His phone vibrated. It was Ji Jingchuan sending him dozens of pictures.","He opened them. They were all of Tang Jiaquan and a woman, naked and entangled together...","He knew Tang Jiaquan's private life was messy, but he had never seen it so directly... These photos were too explicit, making him almost vomit.","Was the money embezzled from the Tang Group used to support these loose women?","Originally, he planned to simply send Tang Jiaquan abroad. That's how major families typically handled errant children.","But on second thought, abroad with no supervision, wouldn't he become even more lawless? What if he produced a bunch of illegitimate children? What if he got involved with drugs? The Tang family, as one of the four great families, would truly struggle to maintain its standing.","For someone this rotten, he should be locked up.","Now, as the head of the Tang family, it was time he did something to satisfy his uncle.","He said calmly, \"First announce to the public that Tang Jiaquan is no longer a descendant of the Tang family. Then call the police... Actually, never mind. It's the middle of the night; let's not disturb the police. First thing tomorrow morning, contact them. Say Tang Jiaquan misappropriated public funds and accepted bribes, and the Tang Group will pursue full legal accountability.\"","The secretary nodded in agreement.","A spring rain fell through the night, pattering softly.","Ji Jingchuan slept well. Upon waking, he received a call from Tang Jin.","\"Chuan, good news! The Tang family has publicly severed ties with Tang Jiaquan. His own grandfather personally sent him to prison. He embezzled up to a hundred million, enough for a lifetime behind bars,\" Tang Jin's bright voice came through. \"It's almost the weekend. Do you want to go look at engagement dresses together?\"","Ji Jingchuan agreed.","Leaving his room, he encountered Ji Zhouye, who whistled. \"Fourth Brother looks radiant. Seems you've made up.\"","Duoduo clapped her hands. \"Great! I'll soon have a fourth aunt. Oh, Fourth Uncle, can I be a flower girl at the engagement?\"","Ji Jingchuan picked her up. \"Of course.\"","Ji Zhouye mimicked Duoduo, speaking in a pinched voice. \"Fourth Brother, I want to be a flower girl too. I heard flower girls get a super big red envelope.\"","\"Hearing you, this unlucky child, acting cute first thing in the morning is enough to finish me off!\" Old Master Ji glared at him with feigned annoyance. \"If you can get into Tsinghua or Peking University, I'll reward you a million.\"","Ji Zhouye pouted. \"That's a pie in the sky I can't reach.\"","\"I'll help you,\" Ji Jingchuan said. \"Great-Grandma is going to Hong Kong for the competition next. I'll move to sit next to you. Let's aim for your next monthly exam score to break five hundred.\"","Ji Zhouye felt a chill.","He remembered when Great-Grandma first arrived, he was at the bottom of his class, with a total score under a hundred.","Later, under Great-Grandma's devilish tutoring, his scores climbed step by step through each monthly exam, reaching around 480-490... and then got stuck.","The progress was very obvious at first, but now it was getting harder and harder.","His homeroom teacher said this score should be enough for university, but getting into a good one would be very difficult.","Honestly, his expectations weren't that high. Just getting into any university would be fine. Like Silin—Silin didn't even go to a regular university and was always happy as can be.","But!","In this family, Eldest Brother was a business genius, Second Brother a performance genius, Third Brother a research genius, Fourth Brother... also showed genius potential. Even Duoduo was often praised by her piano teacher for having talent and was about to enter a piano competition.","If he fell too far behind, left in the dust by his family, then the Ji family really would have no place for him in the future.","\"Fourth Brother, I want to get into a first-tier university!\" Ji Zhouye clenched his fist. \"I don't dare dream of Tsinghua or Peking, but I must get into a first-tier one!\"","Ji Jingchuan picked up his schoolbag. \"Then let's go. School.\"","The two brothers left for school.","Rong Yu did not go.","Because she was heading to Hong Kong for the global finals.","Butler Yu had people pack the luggage—two large suitcases.","Before Rong Yu could question it, Old Master Ji puffed out his chest, putting on a serious face. \"I heard a hospital in Hong Kong developed the latest anti-aging drug. An injection can maximally delay organ failure. I need it, and Uncle Tang needs it too. I'll go investigate on-site first. I think Mom won't object, right?\"","Rong Yu: \"...\"","This old rascal had even prepared such a high-sounding reason. What could she say? Naturally, she had to take her old son to Hong Kong.","However, Hong Kong wasn't like Haicheng. The Ji family had few connections there. If something happened, it would be hard to handle. She asked Butler Yu to arrange for a bodyguard and a nurse to accompany them.","Ji Zhiyuan looked up. \"I remember the Ji Group's real estate division has been wanting to buy land in Hong Kong to build a shopping mall. Perfect, I'll go for an on-site inspection too.\"","He really wasn't at ease letting the two elders travel alone. One was too old, not keeping up with the times; the other had traveled from seventy years ago, also not keeping up with the times...","He had to go personally to feel at ease.","Rong Yu was both amused and exasperated. It was just going for a competition, yet several generations were traveling together.","Well, it was the children's filial piety.","After the three finished their meal, they set off for the airport with the bodyguard and nurse.","Pei Yaru was already waiting at the airport. She was in charge of logistics for the two competing students. Also going together were Song Huai's mother, Madame Song, and Rong Wangtian."]},{"number":230,"title":"Chapter 230: It gave her a very strong sense of familiarity.","paragraphs":["As Rong Yu's nominal father, Rong Wangtian indeed ought to accompany her to Harbor City.","Standing beside Pei Yaru, he watched the two prominent figures of the Ji family—one the founder and the other the current helmsman—personally escort Rong Yu here. Even though he had long known that this daughter of his was treated with the utmost respect by the Ji family, he still felt a deep sense of shock every time he witnessed such a scene.","He quickly stepped forward to greet them. Thank you for the trouble, Old Mr. Ji and CEO Ji. You can just hand my daughter's luggage to me. I'll go check her in.","Ji Zhiyuan spoke in a mild tone, We happen to be going to Harbor City on business anyway, so we'll just check it all in together.","He and his bodyguard, each pushing two suitcases, walked toward the check-in counter.","Old Master Ji kept a straight face, an imposing aura radiating from him. He stood right beside Rong Yu, wearing a look that clearly said strangers should keep their distance.","Mrs. Song wanted to go over and strike up a conversation.","This was the founder of the Ji family, after all. Even just exchanging a few words and getting his contact information would be immensely beneficial.","But after taking only two steps, she was pulled back by Song Huai. Mom, I think I lost my earphones. Can you help me find them?","Mrs. Song had no choice but to give up.","The group boarded the plane.","Since Rong Yu's ticket was purchased by her school, Old Master Ji hadn't bought a first-class ticket either, which perfectly allowed them to pick seats next to each other.","Rong Yu sat by the window, Old Master Ji sat in the middle, and Ji Zhiyuan took the aisle seat. His tall, broad frame effectively blocked out any probing gazes from the rest of the cabin.","I haven't been to Harbor City in at least thirty years, Old Master Ji murmured to Rong Yu. I heard there's a highly effective temple there where any wish you make comes true. It's only a twenty-minute drive from the airport. Mom, why don't we go pay our respects first?","Rong Yu asked him, What does Yingbao want to pray for?","Old Master Ji looked out at the layers of white clouds through the window and slowly replied, I want to pray for the gods to bless me with a few more years of life.","Rong Yu's heart tightened.","She reached out and gently stroked his deeply wrinkled face. Alright, Mom will go with you.","Old Master Ji mumbled to himself for a little while before falling asleep on his biological mother's shoulder. Rong Yu asked a flight attendant for a blanket, draped it over her elderly son, and went back to reading her book.","Just as the plane was preparing to land.","Someone in the cabin suddenly screamed in panic. Oh no! Help! Is there a doctor on the plane? Doudou, Doudou, please don't scare Mommy!","A female passenger in the front row was holding a three- or four-year-old child, her face full of terror and helplessness.","The child was coughing violently, his eyes rolling back, and his lips turning blue. His condition looked incredibly dire.","A flight attendant rushed over and was just about to make an announcement.","I am a pediatrician, a deputy chief physician, a woman said, appearing quickly. She pulled out her professional credentials, handed them to the flight attendant, and swiftly laid a blanket on the floor. Please lay the child flat down. I need to examine him.","Ji Zhiyuan paused in surprise.","It was Dr. Wen, Wen Yan.","This woman always gave him a strong sense of familiarity, as if he had met her somewhere before.","He watched her crouch down and use extremely professional techniques to check the child's pupils and throat, while rapidly questioning the parent, Has the child had any cold symptoms over the past three days?","He's had a bit of a runny nose the last few days, the child's mother sobbed. Before getting on the plane this morning, he only had a slight cough...","A barking cough like a seal, supraclavicular retraction, and subglottic edema. It is highly likely to be laryngeal obstruction, Wen Yan said rapidly. Miss, is there a first-aid kit on the plane? I need some medication right now...","The first-aid kit handed over by the flight attendant was much more basic than expected. Wen Yan quickly rummaged through it, her expression turning grave. There's only epinephrine injection, but no nebulizer.","The child's mother nearly broke down. How could it be laryngeal obstruction? Is his life in danger? What should I do? My Doudou...","Wen Yan glanced around, grabbed a plastic water bottle, and quickly emptied out the liquid. After wiping it with a sanitizing wipe, she took a syringe and an oxygen mask from the first-aid kit. She cut off the bottom of the water bottle, injected the diluted medication into it, and connected it to the oxygen mask. A makeshift nebulizer was instantly ready.","Wen Yan placed the device over the boy's nose and mouth, saying softly, Sweetheart, can you hear me? Be a good boy, don't be afraid. Take a deep breath...","The surrounding passengers and flight attendants didn't even dare to breathe too loudly, terrified of distracting the doctor from saving a life.","Ji Zhiyuan's breathing also lightened. His gaze fell involuntarily on Wen Yan. She was so incredibly focused, her voice so gentle. Her calm and effortless composure while hovering on the line between life and death made it impossible to look away.","It wasn't until she confirmed the danger had passed that Wen Yan let out a long sigh of relief. The child is out of immediate danger for now. Once we land, send him to the hospital right away for more specialized treatment.","The child's mother was endlessly grateful, thanking her over and over again.","Wen Yan waved her hand dismissively, not taking the praise to heart.","She suddenly felt an intense gaze resting upon her. Turning her head, she met Ji Zhiyuan's eyes and her entire body instantly stiffened.","She frequently interacted with the fathers of her sick patients, many of whom were social elites, but no one had ever given her such a strong sense of familiarity like Ji Zhiyuan did. This familiarity seemed to be hidden within all her senses, making her want to avoid him at all costs.","Dr. Wen, Ji Zhiyuan spoke up first. What a coincidence. Are you heading to Harbor City as well?","Ripples of emotion surged in Wen Yan's heart, but her face revealed very little. She smiled and replied, I'm going to Harbor City to attend a medical seminar.","So you are Dr. Wen! Old Master Ji said, looking delighted. Our Duoduo talks about you every single day. I've been wanting to invite you to our home as a guest for a long time.","You must be Duoduo's great-grandfather. Miss Rong is here too, Wen Yan said with a smile. Duoduo said she especially loves her great-grandfather because he always plays around and causes mischief with her.","That little brat, ruining my reputation! Old Master Ji blew into his beard and glared playfully. Just watch how I lecture her when I get back.","Wen Yan couldn't help but laugh out loud.","Her seat happened to be right behind Rong Yu's, so Old Master Ji could chat with her just by turning his head. The two of them conversed back and forth, with Rong Yu occasionally chiming in. Even though they only talked about Duoduo, they grew much closer.","When the conversation shifted to Duoduo's upcoming piano competition, Old Master Ji couldn't quite remember the exact title. Ji Zhiyuan chimed in at the right moment, It's the International Youth Piano Open, held at the Sea City Concert Hall.","Wen Yan's mind was completely filled with the sound of Duoduo's voice.","She hadn't seen Duoduo for quite a long time and truly missed the child.","She hesitated for a moment before asking, When is the Open?","Ji Zhiyuan replied, Next weekend. If you have time, Dr. Wen, you are welcome to come to the venue and cheer Duoduo on.","Wen Yan nodded and agreed.","The plane soon arrived at the Harbor City airport.","Wen Yan had someone waiting to pick her up, so she waved goodbye to them.","Rong Yu told Pei Yaru that she needed to go take care of some business first.","Rong Wangtian asked curiously, Little Yu, this is your first time in Harbor City, and you aren't familiar with the area. What kind of business do you have? I'll go with you.","There's no need to trouble CEO Rong, Ji Zhiyuan said, glancing at Rong Wangtian before turning to Pei Yaru. Don't worry, Teacher Pei. I will escort Rong Yu back to the hotel before five o'clock this evening. It won't delay any official business.","Pei Yaru nodded. Be careful on the road.","Rong Wangtian rubbed his temples.","He had canceled all his work and come to Hong Kong for one reason alone: to accompany his eldest daughter to her competition.","However, it seemed like his eldest daughter didn't need him for a single thing.","He truly was a failure of a father."]},{"number":231,"title":"Chapter 231: May Yingbao be safe and sound, may everything go smoothly, and may she live a long life.","paragraphs":["The car drove all the way to Po Lin Monastery.","The majestic architecture blended traditional and modern elements, and the Buddha statues were solemn and sacred.","Looking up at the towering Buddha statue and meeting its eyes, Rong Yu felt a momentary wave of dizziness.","Old Master Ji spoke up, \"Countless people come to Po Lin Monastery every year. As long as you are sincere enough, your wishes will come true. Mom, what do you want to pray for?\"","Rong Yu smiled but did not answer.","What to pray for...","Of course, she wanted to pray for Yingbao to be safe and sound, for everything to go smoothly, and for him to live a long life.","There were too many tourists. The three of them waited in line for quite a while before finally reaching the very front. They knelt down, closed their eyes, and pressed their palms together.","Rong Yu was silently praying in her heart.","Suddenly, she felt a huge shadow looming over her head. She abruptly opened her eyes and met a familiar face. It was actually Sheng Qingyan.","He was bending over, his glassy eyes quietly watching her.","\"Excuse me, who are you?\"","As soon as Old Master Ji opened his eyes, he saw a tall, large man standing condescendingly in front of his mother. That face was almost pressed against his mother's face.","The distance was a bit too close.","The old man reached out and pushed the person away.","When he saw that face, he paused. Wasn't this the young man who came to the Ji family to look for his mother at the beginning of the year?","This young man had left a deep impression on him.","\"Yan'er, where did you go, Yan'er!\" Old Madam Sheng's voice was tinged with panic. \"Yuan'er, hurry and find your older brother. If he's lost, I might as well die with him!\"","Rong Yu immediately turned around and, across a large crowd of tourists, waved her hand. \"Old Madam Sheng, Sheng Qingyan is over here.\"","Sheng Ciyuan supported Old Madam Sheng and dashed over in a single stride.","The old madam checked on Sheng Qingyan, breathed a sigh of relief, and looked at Rong Yu. \"Miss Rong, why are you in Hong Kong City too?\"","\"Grandmother, I mentioned it to you briefly. Miss Rong is with me, representing Hua Xia in the International Physics Competition.\" Sheng Ciyuan looked at the few people beside Rong Yu. \"Hello, Old Master Ji. Hello, President Ji. I am Sheng Ciyuan, this is my grandmother, and this is my older brother.\"","Old Madam Sheng stepped forward and smiled. \"Old Master Ji, this is our first time meeting. It's a pleasure.\"","Old Master Ji shook his head. \"It's not our first time meeting. About twenty years ago, when your Sheng family's eldest young master was born and held his one-month-old celebration banquet, I happened to be on a business trip in Jingcheng and had the honor of attending the banquet. However, there were too many people at the time, so it's normal that Old Madam Sheng doesn't remember this.\"","Old Madam Sheng indeed did not remember. She spoke up, \"Another day, when Old Master Ji visits Jingcheng, please be sure to let us know. Our Sheng family will definitely host you warmly. I won't exchange too many pleasantries today. I still have to take Yan'er to see the Master and let the Master take a good look at him.\"","Old Master Ji glanced at Sheng Qingyan, his gaze carrying a trace of sympathy.","Such a fine person, how could he be abnormal...","His sympathy had just overflowed a little bit when it came to an abrupt halt, because he saw that Sheng Qingyan had actually grabbed his mother's hand.","Ji Zhiyuan cursed inwardly.","Whenever someone sent his great-grandmother roses, the old man would stomp his feet in anger for half the day.","Now, a grown man was holding his great-grandmother's hand in broad daylight and in front of a crowd. The old man was probably going to explode.","The current old man was no longer the calm and measured head of the family he used to be. Under his great-grandmother's doting, he was becoming more and more unreasonable... He was genuinely a bit afraid that the old man would jump up and punch Sheng Qingyan right in the face.","Old Master Ji indeed had that intention.","However, just as he clenched his fists, he met those clear, indifferent, glass-like eyes. He felt as if he was suppressed by some invisible force and was completely unable to move.","\"Yan'er!\" Old Madam Sheng said loudly. \"How many times have I told you? You must be polite. Politeness must come first. Let go, hurry up and let go!\"","Sheng Qingyan understood, and a trace of grievance surfaced on his lips.","He slowly let go of her hand.","Rong Yu felt secretly surprised in her heart.","She actually really disliked any physical contact from people she was unfamiliar with.","Yet, she surprisingly didn't feel the slightest aversion towards Sheng Qingyan.","Moreover, when he looked aggrieved, she actually felt a hint of pity.","She spoke up, \"Forget it, I'll go with you to see the Master. It's a good opportunity for the Master to take a look at me too.\"","Old Madam Sheng laughed. \"Then let's go to the backyard together.\"","This Master had a great reputation in Hong Kong City. Many wealthy businessmen and celebrities might not even be able to book an appointment a month in advance. It was only because Old Madam Sheng had arranged it early on that they were able to meet him so quickly.","Compared to the front courtyard, which was full of tourists, the backyard was much quieter. The group was led into the inner hall.","The light inside the hall was dim, and the scent of sandalwood was so thick it almost felt tangible. A Master sat cross-legged on a futon, his eyes half-closed, a string of ebony prayer beads slowly turning in his hands.","Regardless of whether they believed in these things or not, as soon as they entered this place, a sense of piety naturally arose in their hearts. The group pressed their palms together and bowed to the Master.","Old Madam Sheng led Sheng Qingyan forward. \"Master, do you remember that we came here over ten years ago? At that time, Master said that in the child's zodiac year, his destiny would change. Can you see any changes now?\"","The Master suddenly opened his eyes, his gaze burning like a torch as he looked straight at Sheng Qingyan. \"Of the three ethereal souls and seven corporeal souls, he is missing one ethereal soul, Taiguang, and one corporeal soul, Fushi. He needs a serendipitous encounter to retrieve them. The serendipity has already appeared; it just depends on whether he can grasp it.\"","Old Madam Sheng's face was full of excitement. \"I hope Master can guide us. Where is this serendipity?\"","The Master shook his head. \"The secrets of heaven must not be revealed.\"","As his words fell, he was about to close his eyes.","Suddenly, he turned his head, his wise eyes looking towards Rong Yu. \"You?\"","Old Master Ji shuddered and subconsciously shielded Rong Yu behind him.","In a place like this, he felt an inexplicable sense of panic.","This Master seemed to possess genuine abilities, and he was afraid the Master would see through something... He had crossed seventy years to reunite with his mother, and they had only been together for a few short months...","The Master abruptly stood up and walked straight towards Rong Yu.","Old Master Ji did not yield an inch.","Sheng Qingyan, who had been standing silently beside Old Madam Sheng, also suddenly walked over and blocked the Master's path.","The Master suddenly smiled. \"The relatives of this benefactor must be a family that accumulates good deeds and widely practices hidden virtues... As the saying goes, a family that accumulates good deeds will surely have abundant blessings. This is heaven rewarding diligence, the result of cause and effect.\"","Rong Yu was startled in her heart.","Her biological father and blood brothers had all thrown themselves into the battlefield and died heroic deaths.","Her biological mother was a military doctor who, in order to save the soldiers, was blown away by an explosion, leaving no remains.","Her husband, Ji Zheng, was a soldier who, in order to protect the intellectuals meticulously cultivated by Hua Xia, was shot and fell into the sea to his death...","Her beloved family members had dedicated their entire lives to this country, accumulating hidden virtues. Was this why she had the fortune to be reborn seventy years later?","\"Destiny is determined by heaven, but fortune is created by man.\" The Master sighed and looked at Old Madam Sheng. \"Although destiny is hard to change, performing good deeds and accumulating virtue can change one's fortune. I offer these words to Old Madam Sheng.\"","Old Madam Sheng repeatedly expressed her gratitude. \"Thank you for your guidance, Master.\"","The Master returned to the futon and closed his eyes.","Old Master Ji only then realized that, despite the early spring season, he had broken out in a cold sweat from shock..."]},{"number":232,"title":"Chapter 232: Afraid the Master Might Stick a Talisman on Mom's Forehead","paragraphs":["Smoke curled upward from the incense burner.","Fine beads of sweat broke out on Old Master Ji's forehead.","He had been truly terrified just now, terrified that the master would pull out a talisman and slap it onto his mother's forehead, causing her soul to dissipate...","A tissue was suddenly held out in front of him.","The old man looked up and met Sheng Qingyan's emotionless face.","This child was missing a part of his soul, yet he actually knew to hand him a tissue?","\"Thank you.\"","Old Master Ji took it and wiped his sweat.","Seeing that the old man's collar was also damp with sweat, Ji Zhiyuan spoke up, \"Let's go to the car so you can change your clothes first. Don't catch a cold.\"","From the moment they entered the temple until now, he had barely spoken a word, silently following behind the two elders with an extremely low presence.","The moment his voice rang out.","Sheng Qingyan's gaze involuntarily shifted toward him. Those rippleless, glassy eyes suddenly paused before surging with turbulent waves.","He spun around and began rummaging through Old Madam Sheng's handbag.","\"Yan'er, what's wrong? What are you doing?\" Old Madam Sheng asked hurriedly. \"Do you want to drink some water?\"","Sheng Ciyuan understood immediately. \"What else could make Big Brother so anxious besides the photos? Grandmother, where did you put the photos?\"","From the backpack of the bodyguard standing behind her, Old Madam Sheng took out a box wrapped in soft silk. She slowly uncovered it, revealing a stack of photographs.","Sheng Qingyan flipped through them until he found the photo of the Zhenhua ship that Rong Yu had bought at all costs during the auction. His fingers gently brushed over the man in the photo who was kneeling on the ground, having been shot.","Old Madam Sheng abruptly turned her head and stared at Ji Zhiyuan's overly handsome face.","This face was almost identical to the soldier in the photograph...","It was just that the man in the photo had sharp, chiseled features, exuding the tough, iron-blooded aura of a hardened soldier.","Meanwhile, Ji Zhiyuan looked more refined and elegant.","\"This, this...\" Old Master Ji's nose stung with emotion. Pointing at the photo, he said, \"This is my father, and this is my mother. I was still in my mother's belly...\"","Rong Yu immediately covered his eyes.","Witnessing his mother being hit and killed by a car had already left Yingbao with a lifelong trauma that was hard to overcome.","If he were to see the final moments of his father's sacrifice, she feared Yingbao would suffer an emotional breakdown. At his advanced age, such violent emotional swings would be too damaging to his health.","Sheng Qingyan paid no attention to Old Master Ji.","He took a large stride and stopped right in front of Ji Zhiyuan. Before anyone could react, his hands suddenly reached out and grabbed both sides of Ji Zhiyuan's face, gave it a squeeze, and then pulled, instantly distorting the handsome face.","Ji Zhiyuan was utterly dumbfounded.","As a grown man nearing thirty and the dignified CEO of the Ji Corporation, he was actually having his face pinched like a child by someone with autism.","And it wasn't just his face being pinched...","Sheng Qingyan also squeezed his nose, prodded his lips, and even tugged at his ears and ruffled his hair.","Yet he felt as if he had been struck by an immobilizing spell, completely unable to move.","\"Big Brother!\" Sheng Ciyuan hurriedly rushed over. \"This is impolite, way too impolite! I am so sorry, President Ji. My big brother can be a bit oblivious sometimes. Please be the bigger person, President Ji, and don't hold it against him...\"","Ji Zhiyuan wiped his face and said in a muffled voice, \"It's fine.\"","He quickly stepped back a few paces to dodge, terrified of being manhandled again.","Old Madam Sheng suppressed the emotions in her eyes and said, \"You all must come visit the Sheng family often in the future.\"","Yan'er treated these three people far too specially.","He was uncontrollably drawn to Miss Rong.","Handing a tissue to Old Mr. Ji.","Inexplicably making overly intimate gestures towards Ji Zhiyuan.","These actions were indeed very impolite, but they also showed that Yan'er was no longer someone living in a closed-off world; he could see others and even interact with them.","Were these people the fateful encounter the master had spoken of?","After leaving Baolian Temple, Old Madam Sheng prepared to take Sheng Qingyan back to the capital. She pulled Sheng Ciyuan aside and whispered, \"Yuan'er, you must build a good relationship with this Miss Rong. Do whatever she says and make sure to keep her happy. Whether your older brother can return to normal in his zodiac year all depends on you.\"","Sheng Ciyuan nodded solemnly. \"Yes, Grandmother.\"","Old Madam Sheng led Sheng Qingyan into the car.","Sheng Qingyan looked back with every step he took, glancing at Rong Yu, then at Old Master Ji, and then at Ji Zhiyuan, as if he simply couldn't get enough of looking at them.","After the car drove away.","Old Master Ji pouted. \"That person is too weird. His eyes are weird, his actions are weird. Mom, you should interact less with the Sheng family in the future.\"","Sheng Ciyuan didn't catch that \"Mom.\" Of course, even if he had heard it clearly, he would have assumed he misheard. He only heard the old man say to interact less with the Sheng family.","His heart skipped a beat, and he hurriedly explained, \"You've misunderstood, Old Master. Actually, my older brother isn't usually strange. He rarely stares at people, nor does he do these weird things. He probably, um, probably just likes President Ji too much.\"","Ji Zhiyuan: \"...\"","Being liked by a grown man... he would rather pass on such a blessing.","Rong Yu shook off some inexplicable emotions in her heart and spoke up, \"The team members still need to meet up tonight. Let's head back to the hotel first.\"","Old Master Ji and Ji Zhiyuan were also staying at this hotel. Upon arriving at the entrance, the two groups parted ways. Rong Yu and Sheng Ciyuan went to the meeting room on the first floor for their meeting.","The six members of the China team had all arrived. Along with the two lead teachers, there were eight people in the meeting room.","When Rong Yu walked in, everyone's eyes involuntarily fell on her.","Although she had not yet starred in any movies or TV dramas, nor had she participated in any variety shows, she was always trending on social media. Therefore, everyone present was not unfamiliar with her face. Plus, they had seen her from afar during the national finals.","Perhaps it was because her face was simply too beautiful, which always gave people a feeling that she was extremely unreliable. Several team members kept looking her up and down.","\"Everyone is here,\" Teacher Huang began. \"Let's have all the members introduce themselves first, starting with the captain.\"","Rong Yu: \"Hello everyone, my name is Rong Yu, from Haicheng No. 1 High School.\"","After finishing her introduction, she simply sat down.","The second person to introduce himself was the vice-captain, Su Ronghua.","He stood up. \"My name is Su Ronghua, a sophomore at Sucheng Experimental High School. The awards I have won include... The papers I have published include... The scientific research achievements I have made include...\"","He went on and on, speaking eloquently at length, his eyes filled with arrogance and confidence.","Next, it was Sheng Ciyuan's turn. Just like Rong Yu, he gave a very brief self-introduction. \"Hello everyone, my name is Sheng Ciyuan, from Jingda Affiliated High School.\"","The next one was Song Huai.","Unable to compare to Su Ronghua's honors, he also simply gave a brief introduction of his name and school.","The remaining two followed the crowd, keeping it just as brief.","A look of embarrassment appeared on Su Ronghua's face.","This made him look like an absolute show-off who loved to flaunt his achievements.","His embarrassment lasted only a split second before his gaze locked onto Rong Yu. \"Could we ask our fellow student Rong Yu to share the latest research on the Shi element?\"","Rong Yu's lips curved into a smile. \"It is a classified project, so it is not convenient to share right now. How about we warm up for tomorrow's competition instead?\"","A look of pure mockery crossed Su Ronghua's face.","Was it really inconvenient to share, or was it because a fringe member of the team simply had nothing of value to offer?","Sure enough, capitalists could do whatever they pleased. The fact that someone completely clueless could be shoved into such a massive, national-level project was utterly despicable."]},{"number":233,"title":"Chapter 233: These Proud Sons of Heaven, Each Believes They Are the Most Outstanding","paragraphs":["Rong Yu tapped her fingers on the tabletop.","She had indeed only started to stand out half a year ago, so it was understandable that she was being questioned by a group of the country's most outstanding students.","She raised her eyes and said calmly, \"Apart from Su Ronghua, there must be others who think I shouldn't be the captain of the Huaxia Team, right?\"","\"I don't think so!\" Sheng Ciyuan said loudly. \"Forgive me for being blunt, but out of everyone sitting here, whether in terms of talent or ability, no one can compare to Rong Yu!\"","The whole room fell silent.","Song Huai's face was full of disbelief.","He knew Rong Yu was very impressive, but... why did Sheng Ciyuan think so too?","A member of the Sheng family in the capital, a chosen one, with a top-tier family background and top-tier personal talent. Someone like him was actually kissing Rong Yu's ass?","For some reason, the image of Ji Zhouye popped into his mind.","What was the difference between Sheng Ciyuan's current appearance and Rong Yu's little follower, Ji Zhouye?","Su Ronghua laughed out of anger. \"An 'elderly' eighteen-year-old repeating student, with no achievements and no papers. Besides a gold medal from the domestic physics competition, what else do you have to show for yourself?\"","Rong Yu: \"...\"","An \"elderly\" eighteen-year-old.","It was clearly the prime of youth, but she was being called elderly. She refused to accept it.","But on second thought, Su Ronghua was a high school sophomore, probably only sixteen years old. Eighteen was indeed a bit older to him.","Moreover, questioning only her age and not her gender was pretty good already.","She looked at the leading teacher. \"Since everyone has doubts about my ability, why don't we verify it on the spot? Teacher Huang, please give us a question.\"","Teacher Huang also became interested.","These proud geniuses all thought they were the best, so it was completely normal for them to be unconvinced by someone else being the captain. Giving them a question at this time to let them compete and recognize each other's abilities would be a great thing for enhancing team cohesion.","There was a whiteboard in the meeting room. Teacher Huang picked up a marker, walked over, and started writing the question: \"Calculate under the background of curved spacetime...\"","The meeting room was dead silent.","Song Huai's fingers stiffened. This question was a bit too difficult, somewhat beyond the scope of their usual training.","It required handling the metric of general relativity, calculating the matrix algebra of quantum field theory, as well as the connection coefficients of differential geometry... Not only did it test physics, but it also required profound professional knowledge in mathematics.","Su Ronghua thought intently for a few minutes, immediately opened the laptop he carried with him, and began to calculate.","Sheng Ciyuan was about to start solving the problem when he saw Rong Yu empty-handed without any auxiliary tools. He immediately pushed his laptop over. \"You use it.\"","This warm-up competition was to make the team members wholeheartedly submit to the captain; he didn't necessarily have to participate.","Rong Yu twirled her gel pen and shook her head. \"No need.\"","As a person from the 1970s, she hadn't yet developed the habit of carrying a laptop when going out. For her, as long as she had a pen and a piece of paper, she could construct a massive mathematical and physical world, not to mention she also possessed an excessively young brain.","The question Teacher Huang came up with on the spot didn't have too many complicated components; it could be completely calculated by the human brain.","Sheng Ciyuan met her confident eyes, nodded, and began to calculate diligently.","Su Ronghua's fingers flew across the keyboard extremely fast. He pressed the enter key for the last time. Next, he only needed to wait for the computer to run for about five minutes to get the final result.","He looked up at his teammates beside him.","Song Huai's brows were tightly knit; evidently, he was still stuck at a critical point.","Sheng Ciyuan was progressing smoothly, but he was too slow—a step behind him.","Ding Zhe was still frantically calculating...","His gaze finally landed on Rong Yu, and he immediately let out an unceremonious laugh.","Rong Yu surprisingly didn't even have a computer. In front of her were only a pen and a piece of scratch paper, and the paper was completely blank except for a few numbers and symbols.","Was she unable to even keep up the act anymore?","Could someone like this still be the captain?","In his view, Rong Yu wasn't even fit to be a team member. If this kind of person went onto the battlefield, wouldn't it be a disgrace to the great nation of Huaxia?","He looked at Teacher Huang, conveying the meaning: Look, this is the captain you chose, nothing more than this.","Before long, Su Ronghua's computer program finished, and a string of characters appeared. He strode forward and wrote it on the whiteboard.","Just as he finished writing, Sheng Ciyuan's result also came out. He spoke up, \"My result is the same as Su Ronghua's. Rong Yu, what is your final result?\"","Su Ronghua smiled and looked at Rong Yu.","He wanted to see how she would talk her way out of this.","Rong Yu's face was extremely calm, as if she were just having an ordinary chat. She pushed the scratch paper on the table over. \"The same.\"","\"Wh-what?\"","Su Ronghua was completely stunned.","He dashed forward in a single stride and stared intently at the scratch paper. Indeed, it was exactly the same as what he had calculated.","But!","Rong Yu hadn't used a computer, and the scratch paper was practically blank. She hadn't even calculated it; how could she have arrived at this result?","\"You copied my answer.\"","Su Ronghua didn't say it as a question; his tone was absolutely certain.","Teacher Huang said calmly, \"Fifteen minutes ago, Rong Yu had already written this value on her scratch paper. And at that time, you were still building your model. Of course, if you don't believe me, you can check the surveillance footage.\"","Su Ronghua was rendered speechless. He mumbled, \"Relying purely on the brain, how could it be possible to calculate it?\"","\"Because the human brain is more flexible than a computer and holds more possibilities.\" Rong Yu raised her hand. \"If the human brain and computer are combined, perhaps it would be faster. Bring your model over for me to see.\"","Su Ronghua didn't know what she wanted to do, but he pushed his laptop over.","However, there was still some distance from the middle of the oversized office desk to Rong Yu. She would need to stand up and lean over to reach it.","Sheng Ciyuan immediately stood up, picked up the laptop with both hands, and carefully placed it in front of Rong Yu.","Song Huai frowned.","The Second Young Master of the Sheng family was actually fawning over Rong Yu like this?","Was he pursuing her?","Rong Yu scrolled the mouse and quickly scanned through the model. This model was very mature, which was quite rare for someone of Su Ronghua's age. No wonder he could stand out among the physics geniuses nationwide while only being a high school sophomore.","She slightly modified a few coefficients. \"You made the computer run an extra loop, so it needed five minutes. Changing it here can reduce the time to about two minutes.\"","Su Ronghua's expression froze.","Since stepping into the math and physics competition circle, he had basically never met a rival. Sheng Ciyuan was the first, but later Sheng Ciyuan's focus shifted, and he easily surpassed Sheng Ciyuan, becoming one of the top academic gods among the younger generation in Huaxia...","Now, meeting Rong Yu... being easily surpassed by someone else, to be honest, didn't feel very wonderful.","\"It seems everyone should have recognized the captain's ability.\" Teacher Huang clapped his hands. \"I hope that under Rong Yu's leadership, our Huaxia Team will achieve excellent results in this competition. Meeting adjourned.\""]},{"number":234,"title":"Chapter 234: Are the Talents of the Huaxia Team Here to Embarrass Themselves Again","paragraphs":["After leaving the meeting room.","A group of parents were sitting on the sofas by the door. Rong Wangtian stood up and spoke with a gentle expression, \"I've arranged for two simple tables at this hotel. Parents and children can sit, chat for a while. The adults can share educational experiences, and the kids can get closer, get to know each other. What does everyone think?\"","Mrs. Song responded warmly, \"It's fate that we've all gathered in Hong Kong. Let's all give Father Rong some face and have a meal together. It's also a good chance for us parents and teachers to exchange contact information.\"","The parents, keen to interact more, followed Rong Wangtian towards the dining hall.","Rong Yu did not refuse either.","Upon entering the hall and seeing the dishes on the two tables, the entire group was stunned.","There were at least eighteen dishes on each table, more lavish than a wedding banquet, with king crab, Australian lobster, and sea cucumbers all laid out.","\"Father Rong, this is too extravagant.\" Even Pei Yaru was shocked. \"It's just a casual get-together to chat. So many dishes, it's really...\"","\"No trouble at all.\" Rong Wangtian waved his hand dismissively. \"Destined souls meet across a thousand miles. It's not easy for everyone from all corners of the country to gather here. The children have a big competition tomorrow. It's important they eat well and feel at ease. Please, don't stand on ceremony, have a seat.\"","As he spoke, he exhibited the inherent consideration of a businessman, inviting everyone to sit one by one. He managed to avoid making guests feel pressured while ensuring no one was left out.","Rong Yu thought to herself that this was probably one of the reasons Rong Wangtian could build his business from scratch and grow the Rong Group to its current scale.","The meal was enjoyed by hosts and guests alike.","By the time dinner ended, it was already past eight in the evening. She went upstairs back to her room.","Her room had been upgraded to a presidential suite, with three bedrooms and a living room. She, her old son, and her great-grandson were all staying there.","As soon as she swiped her card and pushed the door open, Old Master Ji said cheerfully, \"I just had dinner with an old friend from Hong Kong. He's five years older than me but looks younger. He said three months ago he received an injection of the latest black-tech product developed by Li's Hospital. He originally just tried it on a whim, but the effects were surprisingly obvious. I'm planning to go check out the hospital tomorrow.\"","Ji Zhiyuan frowned. \"Is it a setup?\"","\"Setup your head!\" Old Master Ji kicked him. \"That friend of mine is the chairman of a Hong Kong bank. His wealth is no less than ours. Why would he set up a trap for an old man like me?\"","He moved closer to Rong Yu. \"This rejuvenation project at Li's Hospital is still in the clinical trial stage and hasn't been publicly released. Only the wealthy class has caught wind of it, and you need an introduction to get a spot. Luckily, I have this friend as a middleman, otherwise I wouldn't even know which door to knock on... Mom, once I use this medicine, I'll look at least ten years younger. That means I can stay with you for ten more years.\"","The pursuit of longevity can be traced back to Qin Shi Huang.","The Chinese have been researching it for thousands of years without any real breakthrough, so Rong Yu was also skeptical.","But, with the rapid advancement of science nowadays—for example, those female celebrities on TV in their fifties and sixties who still look like they're thirty, or that year when rumors swirled in the entertainment industry about a certain hospital developing a 'rejuvenation shot' that made a group of actresses look younger collectively—such things are not entirely impossible.","She spoke up, \"I have the competition tomorrow. A Yuan, cancel all your work and accompany him.\"","Ji Zhiyuan had come to Hong Kong precisely to accompany his elders; work wasn't that important. He immediately nodded in agreement.","Early the next morning, at six-thirty, Rong Yu got up, had a quick breakfast, and went to the first floor to meet up with the teachers and teammates.","At the entrance to the competition venue, the teachers in charge of the team, such as Pei Yaru, and the parents had to stop. Teacher Huang led the six students into the competition hall.","The dome of the International Physics Competition hall was dizzyingly high. Flags from over forty countries and regions were interwoven and hung overhead, like a sea of colorful clouds.","As soon as they entered, their ears were filled with a cacophony of different languages. Even though Rong Yu was proficient in several, she felt momentarily overwhelmed.","The team members present had all participated in international competitions before and weren't too nervous. They followed Teacher Huang inside.","\"Hey! Look who's here.\" An intentionally raised voice speaking American English came from the right. \"The geniuses from Team China here to lose face again?\"","Rong Yu turned and saw six blond teenagers in dark blue suits walking towards them. The boy at the front was nearly 190cm tall, with a US flag pin on his tie, his gray-blue eyes filled with contempt.","A girl beside him frowned. \"Jackson, don't go too far.\"","\"What, am I wrong?\" Jackson crossed his arms. \"Last year, in the experimental round, China placed third from last. Chinese physics, garbage.\"","At his words, the faces of all the teammates beside Rong Yu darkened.","Although over the past decade or so, the physics proficiency of Chinese youth had grown exponentially, there was still a gap compared to the US. They could hold their own in theory, but were often crushed in experiments.","Faced with the mockery from the US team, they were furious but felt helpless.","\"Interesting.\" A smile appeared on Rong Yu's face as she spoke in impeccable American English. \"In last year's finals, the US team mistakenly calculated a Bose-Einstein condensate as a fermionic system. Such a basic error, that's the real garbage.\"","\"Look at you, speaking such beautiful American English. How many years did you spend memorizing it?\" Jackson sneered disdainfully. \"Right, you Chinese are the best at these theoretical systems because you rely entirely on rote memorization. Being useless at physics experiments makes you garbage. Victory in physics belongs to the United States.\"","Sheng Ciyuan, furious, was about to speak when Rong Yu pressed her hand on his arm.","Rong Yu looked towards the nearest team from another country, Japan, and with a smile curling her lips, spoke in Japanese: \"Physics doesn't belong to any single country. Do you agree?\"","Hearing this, the entire Japanese team was stunned.","This Chinese person's Japanese was too fluent. At first listen, she sounded like a native.","Rong Yu turned to another team, the Russian team, and spoke in fluent Russian: \"Half a century ago, Russia was invincible, leading numerous countries forward as the big brother, upholding the belief that physics has no borders.\"","The Russians nodded dumbly.","She switched to French, \"But, dignity has borders. Insulting another country is tantamount to trampling on its dignity. In my book, that is unforgivable.\"","Finally, she looked at Jackson from the US team and said, \"Of course, if you could master five languages through rote memorization, I might consider forgiving you.\"","Jackson didn't understand most of it, but he could see the change in attitude of the people around him. The roots of his ears turned red as if about to bleed. He took a sudden step forward but was stopped by his teammates.","Suddenly, applause broke out around them.","No matter the country, they had all suffered under US dominance for too long—politically suppressed, militarily encroached upon, economically sanctioned, and academically mocked year after year. No one could swallow that anger easily.","And this Chinese girl, effortlessly switching between several languages, had made Jackson feel utterly ashamed. It was deeply satisfying."]},{"number":235,"title":"Chapter 235: When did you learn so many languages","paragraphs":["The entire hall erupted with thunderous applause.","The female teachers from Asia stamped their feet excitedly, the Russian team members whistled, and even the Asian-American member of the American team couldn't help but clap—only to be glared at fiercely by Jackson, who then turned and walked away.","Song Huai's pupils constricted.","He had seen Rong Yu reading original Russian texts before and knew she was proficient in Russian, but he never imagined she was also fluent in Japanese and French.","Her mathematics and science subjects were outstanding, and her language skills were no less impressive. She truly made him realize once again the gap that could exist between people.","Su Ronghua curled his lip.","Showing off language skills in such a serious competition setting was rather ridiculous.","Sheng Ciyuan asked with a face full of admiration, \"Rong Yu, when did you learn so many languages?\"","Rong Yu replied, \"I've been self-studying for a few years.\"","In her era, when the country was being invaded by Japan, anyone who paid even a little attention to national affairs would know a few phrases of Japanese.","As for English, she had studied it since childhood. After studying abroad, she dealt with foreigners every day, becoming almost as fluent as in her native tongue.","Back then, the Soviet Union still existed, and many physics books were in Russian. Through self-study, bit by bit, she learned enough Russian to read professional texts without issue.","And French...","She coughed lightly. Actually, she wasn't that proficient.","She remembered, during her years abroad, a Frenchman had pursued her, chattering away in French by her ear every day, which passively taught her some daily expressions. She wasn't fluent.","But it was enough to bluff that American, Jackson.","The group arrived at the Chinese team's experimental station.","The first day was the preliminary round.","Out of forty-six participating countries and regions, only twelve would advance after the preliminaries—the competition format was quite brutal.","The starting bell rang.","The problem was displayed on the large screen: Determine the quantum confinement effect of electrons in a nanomaterial and establish a model of its relationship with material thickness.","Su Ronghua was indeed capable. The moment he saw the problem, he had a plan in mind. He spoke up, \"Direct observation is the safest approach. Use an atomic force microscope to scan the sample surface and directly measure the electron cloud distribution.\"","Rong Yu thought for a few seconds. \"Direct observation is too time-consuming. I believe we should first establish a theoretical model and use X-ray diffraction data to deduce electron behavior. This could save at least forty minutes.\"","As soon as she finished speaking, Su Ronghua's expression changed.","He had participated in countless competitions, nearly a hundred large and small, and had always been the captain. It was always him proposing the experimental framework, and the team members would simply follow.","This was the first time someone had proposed a completely different plan.","He said coldly, \"Building a model would also take at least half an hour. If it fails, we'll end up in last place directly.\"","Rong Yu said calmly, \"It won't fail.\"","Su Ronghua sneered.","The atmosphere within the team immediately grew tense.","Song Huai looked from one to the other and cautiously suggested, \"Since the captain and vice-captain have a disagreement, should we put it to a vote?\"","Rong Yu nodded. \"Then let's vote. Raise your right hand if you agree with Su Ronghua's plan. Raise your left hand if you agree with mine.\"","Su Ronghua immediately raised his right hand.","Everyone else raised their left hand.","His face turned extremely ugly. Was this intentional exclusion of him, the vice-captain?","\"Begin.\" Rong Yu got into gear, quickly assigning tasks. \"Sheng Ciyuan, calibrate the X-ray instrument. Song Huai, prepare the samples. Ding Zhe, record the data and write clear theoretical support.\"","She looked at Su Ronghua. \"You assist in setting up the—\"","\"I have my own plan.\" Su Ronghua walked straight to the equipment area, stood in front of an atomic force microscope, and began working on his original proposal.","Rong Yu shrugged, not even frowning. She turned to the remaining five members and explained the key points of model construction in detail. Her voice was steady and clear, allowing others to grasp the essentials instantly.","\"Rong Yu,\" Song Huai glanced at Su Ronghua fiddling with the instrument alone in the corner. \"He's talented enough. Having him join would increase our precision... Should I go talk to him?\"","\"Pay attention to your sample quantity.\" Rong Yu didn't look up, pushing the computer towards Ding Zhe. \"Write the theory first. Come to me with any questions.\"","A deliberate clattering sound came from Su Ronghua's side.","This task required multiple people to cooperate, but he was alone now, clumsily connecting the complex microscope wiring. Several operational errors caused the instrument to emit sharp alarms. A referee frowned in their direction. Rong Yu immediately raised her hand to signal, \"Equipment debugging. Apologies.\"","She quickly walked over to Su Ronghua, her voice very low. \"Either join us now, or fail quietly. Your choice.\"","\"How dare you—\"","His words were cut off.","\"A third alarm will result in point deduction.\" Rong Yu glanced at her wristwatch. \"You have ten seconds to decide.\"","Su Ronghua's hand hovered in mid-air, finally slamming down on the table. But after that, he made no more noise.","He didn't believe there was anything wrong with his plan.","He would produce results.","To show everyone that Rong Yu was wrong.","To make everyone realize that Rong Yu was not a qualified captain.","Rong Yu returned to the main experimental area. The team members were nervously awaiting the first batch of data. She checked every step, her fingertip pressing the enter key. A beautiful three-dimensional electron cloud model gradually appeared on the screen.","\"Beautiful!\" Sheng Ciyuan couldn't help but exclaim. This model could provide more dimensional information than direct observation.","In the corner, Su Ronghua's microscope was finally debugged, but most of the competition time had already passed. He stared at the continuously refined model on Rong Yu's team's computer screen, his expression growing increasingly grim.","\"Final phase.\" Rong Yu clapped her hands. \"Prepare for cross-validation.\"","Her fingers flew across the keyboard. The complex model on the screen gradually converged, finally presenting a set of perfect data curves.","\"Model verification complete!\"","Song Huai could hardly believe it. The process had been so smooth, smooth to an almost unbelievable degree.","He glanced at Su Ronghua, who was sweating profusely, still observing and recording. By the looks of it, he needed at least another hour, but now, there were only half an hour left on the countdown.","Rong Yu quickly checked all the data, revised the theoretical framework written by Ding Zhe and another member, and after confirming everything was correct, decisively clicked the submit button.","The large screen instantly refreshed—","\"Team China: Submission successful. Time: 2 hours, 16 minutes.\"","The entire venue fell silent for a second, followed by a wave of low exclamations.","\"What? How are they so fast?\" Jackson from the American team looked up sharply, his face dark as he stared at the screen.","At the judges' table, several referees exchanged looks of surprise. Based on past competitions, an experiment of this difficulty would take at least two and a half hours to complete.","Team China had finished so much earlier.","\"This has broken the competition record!\" a member of the Russian team exclaimed.","Jackson's face completely darkened. He stood up abruptly, pointing at Rong Yu. \"You must have cheated! How is this possible?!\"","Rong Yu didn't even glance at him. \"You can keep your doubts, but time is running out.\"","Jackson looked at the large screen. With just over half an hour left, he hurriedly resumed his verification.","Su Ronghua stood in the corner, his fists clenched so tightly his knuckles turned white.","He had intended to prove his own method was more reliable, but now, before he could even obtain his results, it was all over..."]},{"number":236,"title":"Chapter 236: This is absolutely impossible, the data must be fabricated.","paragraphs":["The countdown timer for the International Physics Olympiad echoed through the hall.","On the massive screen, the submission order for various national teams refreshed one after another:","\"Team USA: Submitted successfully, time taken: 2 hours 31 minutes.\"","\"Team Japan: Submitted successfully, time taken: 2 hours 33 minutes.\"","\"Team Russia: Submitted successfully, time taken: 2 hours 40 minutes.\"","\"...\"","After submitting their own results, the competitors finally relaxed enough to watch the scores on the big screen.","By comparison, the Chinese team stood out like a sore thumb.","A Russian team member pushed up his glasses. \"The Chinese team was actually fifteen minutes faster than the Americans. Did they skip the verification process just to get the bonus points for finishing first?\"","\"Too fast,\" a French competitor said, narrowing his eyes. \"They are either lunatics or geniuses.\"","Jackson from the USA stared at the screen, a cold sneer playing on his lips. He turned to his teammates and announced loudly, \"It seems some people have forgotten the basic rigor of scientific research. In a real physics competition, speed is meaningless. Precision is king!\"","He dragged out the last word, his voice dripping with undisguised mockery.","The captain of the German team adjusted his glasses, his expression steady. \"Our data has undergone triple verification. Our error rate will not exceed 0.5%.\"","The Japanese captain bowed slightly, his voice laced with hidden sharpness. \"Our country’s experimental precision has always been the industry benchmark.\"","Su Ronghua clenched his fingers until his knuckles turned white. He lowered his voice and spoke to his teammate, Song Huai. \"Rong Yu is too conceited... In a competition of this caliber, there’s no point in rushing. Precision is the key. If we are disqualified because of an accuracy error, does she have any idea how severe the consequences will be?\"","Song Huai frowned. He didn't agree with the sentiment, but he didn't speak up to refute it.","Sheng Ciyuan’s cold voice drifted over. \"Student Su, you actually think there will be an error in precision? Or rather, are you hoping for one?\"","Su Ronghua was choked for words. He had always been the core of the team, but now, being isolated like this made his expression turn incredibly unsightly.","Once all countries had submitted their results, the display on the screen suddenly changed. It revealed the theoretical exact values provided by the official committee alongside a comparison of each team’s error rate:","\"Team China: Error Rate, 0.001%.\"","\"Team USA: Error Rate, 0.1%.\"","\"Team Japan: Error Rate, 0.25%.\"","\"Team Germany: Error Rate, 0.43%.\"","\"...\"","\"Oh my God, our error is only zero point one!\" Jackson’s eyes widened. \"This is the lowest error we've had since training began. I knew first place belonged to us...\"","\"No, I say, you're celebrating too early...\" a Russian nearby kindly reminded him. \"If you would just move your eyes and look at the Chinese team’s error rate.\"","\"It’s impossible for anyone to be lower than zero point one, what...\" Jackson stared, counting the zeros. He suddenly slammed his hand on the table and stood up, his chair screeching harshly against the floor. His face turned bright red, and the veins on his temples bulged. \"0.001%? Is that even possible? It’s absolutely impossible! It must be forged data!\"","The German leader’s glasses slid to the tip of his nose, but he didn't even notice. He just stared fixedly at the screen. \"0.001%... this value is terrifying.\"","A girl from the French team covered her mouth, her eyes wide with shock. \"How did they even design their experiment to achieve that?\"","The Japanese captain, his shock fading into a cold tone, said, \"China used to be our inferior; their education was backward and their physics department was pathetic. How could they calculate such a precise value? Either it’s luck, or they cheated.\"","Jackson strongly agreed with the Japanese captain, shouting loudly, \"If the Hong Kong organizers do not investigate this thoroughly, then Hong Kong will lose its qualification to host international academic events in the future!\"","Su Ronghua looked miserable. \"Rong Yu, you actually faked the data? Do you know that if this behavior is proven, the Chinese team will be banned for at least three years? Do you have any idea what kind of devastating blow this will deal to our juniors in the future?\"","Rong Yu spoke calmly. \"Since things have reached this point, I don't think there is any need for you to question my ability anymore.\"","Sheng Ciyuan frowned. \"Student Su, be quiet and listen to the judges.\"","Song Huai pursed his lips and patted Su Ronghua on the shoulder. \"Trust the captain. There won't be a problem.\"","Su Ronghua fell silent.","On the judging panel sat twelve judges from various countries. However, because the competition was held in Hong Kong, the chief judge was a local. He stood up, his face possessing an unquestionable authority.","\"The experimental data of the Chinese team has been re-tested by the committee’s instruments and confirmed to be correct.\"","His voice, resonant as a bell, was broadcast into everyone’s ears. The venue fell deathly silent.","The chief judge paused, his gaze sweeping across the room. \"This is the lowest error record in the experimental segment of the International Physics Olympiad in the last decade.\"","Jackson’s face had turned from bright red to a deathly pale. His lips trembled, but he couldn't make a sound. His mind flashed back to his pre-match mockery of the Chinese team, where he had called Chinese physics \"trash.\" Now, those words felt like a slap delivered directly to his face.","He suddenly turned toward the referee’s bench. \"This... this is simply impossible! It’s ridiculous! I demand a re-test! They must have cheated!\"","The Japanese leader rose slowly and bowed ninety degrees. \"Forgive me, judges. Although it is rude to say so, I also believe...\"","He appeared polite, but his words were extremely offensive. He was halfway through his sentence when he was coldly interrupted by the chief judge. \"If you continue to make groundless accusations, the USA and Japan will be disqualified from the competition.\"","Jackson’s fists clenched until his knuckles cracked, but he couldn't say another word. He felt as if the entire world was spinning. He saw competitors from other countries casting admiring glances at the Chinese team; he saw the appreciation on the judges' faces; and he saw Rong Yu’s calm yet radiant figure...","Beside him, the Japanese captain looked at Jackson, hoping he would cause more of a scene, but unfortunately, Jackson stayed quiet.","The judging panel began to announce the names of the twelve countries advancing to the finals.","Rong Yu turned back to her teammates. \"We advanced in first place.\"","Sheng Ciyuan cheered loudly. \"Great! That’s amazing! Rong Yu, you are literally my goddess!\"","The people who had originally questioned Rong Yu's leadership now spoke up sincerely. \"The entire framework of the plan relied on the captain. Otherwise, it would have been impossible to take first place so smoothly.\"","These words were effectively a kick to Su Ronghua. He turned around and walked out of the arena without saying a word.","Rong Yu and her teammates packed up their equipment and headed out the door, only to run straight into the American team.","Jackson had already regained his composure. He stood with his hands in his pockets, leaning against a pillar with a mocking curl to his lip. \"Congratulations, Team China. Your luck is truly enviable.\""]},{"number":237,"title":"Chapter 237: In Haicheng, Gazing Afar at Jinling, Overwhelmed with Grief","paragraphs":["Jackson's meaning was obvious.","Huaxia's victory was merely based on luck.","Rong Yu smiled.","Losers always found excuses for their failures. It was perfectly normal; no matter how excellent you were, if they thought you were terrible, then in their eyes, you were terrible.","There was nothing to explain.","Because the opinions most people held of her did not even affect her as much as the glass of water she drank in the morning.","She stepped forward to leave.","But in Jackson's eyes, her attitude was pure contempt and disdain.","He grew even more irritated. \"Hey, didn't you hear me? Or do you just not understand? Winning the preliminaries is nothing; the finals are where the real test lies. Don't think your Huaxia country can go far on luck alone. Trash with good luck is still trash.\"","Rong Yu finally looked up.","The lights reflected in her pitch-black eyes like tempered blades.","\"Luck?\" She gave a soft chuckle. \"Mr. Jackson, if an error rate of 0.001% is luck—\" She leaned in slightly, her voice as light as a feather yet cutting to the bone. \"Then what should the 0.1% error rate of your Lighthouse Country be called? Bad luck? People who are too unlucky should stay far away from me.\"","Sheng Ciyuan made a gesture of disgust.","The expressions of the Lighthouse Country team members changed drastically.","Jackson said angrily, \"You Huaxia people have no manners at all!\"","Song Huai was usually a man of few words, but even he could not hold back at this moment. \"Huaxia has five thousand years of civilization, while your Lighthouse Country only has two hundred. You really don't have the right to lecture us about manners.\"","For the first time, Rong Yu agreed with Song Huai.","She wore a smile on her face. \"We Huaxia people do not show courtesy to a group of people who dictate terms about our territorial issues and constantly set restrictions in the field of technology.\"","From the side, members of the Sakura team walked over. \"Rong, academic exchanges should be pure. They shouldn't involve politics...\"","\"Captain Sato.\" Rong Yu suddenly switched to fluent Japanese, her voice turning as cold as ice. \"When the city of Jinling fell in 1937, what were the scholars of your country doing?\"","Sato's expression changed drastically.","Recalling that period of history, a trace of pain surfaced in Rong Yu's cold eyes.","Others only read about this tragic history in textbooks, but she had been twelve years old that year, standing in Haicheng, gazing toward Jinling in utter agony.","Still studying vocal music at the time, she had resolutely given it up.","With the nation torn apart, what good was singing?","Song Huai was a sensitive person. He acutely noticed the shift in Rong Yu's emotions. To think she would have such a massive emotional fluctuation when facing people from the Sakura Country?","To be honest, that part of history had passed for over half a century. The governments of Huaxia and Sakura Country had officially reconciled, and many citizens traveled to Sakura Country almost every year. It was rare for a young person to reveal such deep-seated hatred.","\"Let's put aside the massacre that angered both men and gods for a moment,\" Rong Yu spoke. \"Back then, you were plundering Huaxia's cultural relics and burning Huaxia's ancient texts. Kyoto University still houses tens of thousands of precious documents stolen from Huaxia—\"","The members of the Sakura Country team collectively took a half-step back.","Rong Yu's lip line was as sharp as a knife. \"And now you want to talk to me about academic purity. Do you even deserve to, hmm?\"","Seeing this, Jackson tried to interject, but she shot him a piercing glare. \"And your Lighthouse Country. During the war, you condoned looting, stripping our millennia-old civilization of its cultural artifacts—\"","She raised her head to look at the growing crowd of onlookers, her voice echoing across the square:","\"Standing here today, we are competing not just in physics, but in a nation's reverence for the truth and respect for history!\"","Amidst the dead silence, Rong Yu cast one last glance at Jackson. \"See the real deal in the finals? Alright, I will let all of you know—\"","\"The five thousand years of cultural heritage of the Chinese nation is not something you can easily shake.\"","She took wide strides and walked out of the competition arena.","Teacher Huang looked at her in astonishment. This child had so much national integrity. Outstanding students with such a strong sense of righteousness were becoming increasingly rare. No wonder so many academicians voted for her to be the team leader.","\"Good, good, good! Truly worthy of being a child of the Rong family!\" Rong Wangtian, standing at the door, happened to hear these words. His eyes turned red. \"Little Yu, Dad is so proud of you!\"","He still remembered his college days when he and a group of classmates marched to boycott goods from the Sakura Nation. Whenever they saw imported goods from the Sakura Nation, they would smash and destroy them. Back then, he was just a hot-blooded youth who only knew how to solve problems with violence.","But his daughter was able to stand on the world stage and bend the spines of these foreign powers.","\"But...\" Madam Song frowned. \"Those people from the Sakura Nation looked furious. We've offended them too much. If they cause any trouble, will the children be able to handle it?\"","\"What are you saying, Madam Song,\" Rong Wangtian spoke up. \"This is Hong Kong, the territory of our Hua Xia. If foreigners dare to cause trouble here, aren't they just bringing about their own destruction? Although we Hua Xia people believe that visitors are guests and that harmony brings wealth, when it comes to matters of the nation, we must stick to our principles.\"","Several parents nearby echoed his sentiments.","Teacher Huang said, \"Tomorrow is a rest day, and the finals are the day after. I suggest all parents take their children to get some good rest...\"","Everyone said their goodbyes.","A distance away, Mother Su pulled Su Ronghua aside and said, \"Didn't you say that after the preliminaries, the organizing committee would hold a revote for the team leader? If you're too embarrassed to ask, I'll go say it. This team leader must be you!\"","Su Ronghua's expression was ugly. \"Even if they vote again, they won't choose me.\"","Rong Yu's performance was too perfect; not a single flaw could be picked out. The talent he had once been so proud of was nothing in front of Rong Yu.","Mother Su grew anxious. \"But only by becoming the team leader will your application to Harvard University not be rejected. Your dad and I have lived frugally to pay for your studies, and I quit my job to raise you full-time. The whole family is counting on you. You can't drop the ball at this crucial moment... Let's go talk to Rong Yu. Maybe she'll give the team leader position to you.\"","\"She isn't that generous.\" Su Ronghua looked up. \"I'm only a sophomore in high school. I still have a chance to compete again next year. Don't panic.\"","As long as he didn't run into a monstrous genius like Rong Yu in the next competition, with his abilities, he would definitely be able to become the team leader and get an admission letter from Harvard University.","Rong Yu returned to the hotel.","Old Master Ji had also just returned. \"Mom, Yuan and I went to Li's Hospital today. Director Li arranged for me to have a physical examination tomorrow. If everything goes smoothly, I'll be able to receive the injection soon. When the time comes, I'll bring Uncle Tang over together, so Uncle Tang can also live a few more years.\"","Rong Yu looked at Ji Zhiyuan. \"Did they provide any relevant information about this drug?\"","Ji Zhiyuan picked up the document from the coffee table. \"This is the hospital's internal data. Great-grandmother, please take a look.\"","Rong Yu opened the booklet.","The first half was entirely dedicated to introducing the project's clinical trial subjects. They were all powerful elites from various circles: the founder of Li's Hospital, the chairman of Harbor City Bank, the Zhou family real estate tycoon, the God of Gamblers from Xiangshan City... The participation of so many prominent figures instantly swept away any lingering doubts.","She continued to flip through the pages. The information about the drug itself was confined to a single, brief page.","The concept originally stemmed from the cellular regeneration abilities of the deep-sea immortal jellyfish, as well as the anti-aging mechanisms of tardigrades in extreme environments. The serum could activate human telomerase activity, delaying telomere shortening and increasing the maximum limit of cell division by 300%.","A single injection of the serum cost a staggering thirty million US dollars."]},{"number":238,"title":"Chapter 238: How Could He Bear to Let His Mother Lose Him","paragraphs":["After the physics preliminaries, there was a day off to rest.","Rong Yu decided to accompany her old son to Li's Hospital to take a look. She was mainly worried that this old fellow was so desperate to prolong his life that he might get scammed.","Early in the morning, right after breakfast, Ji Zhiyuan arranged for a car and took the two elders there together.","Li's Hospital was the largest private hospital in Hong Kong. Founded over thirty years ago, it had quickly gained a firm foothold in the city and had been growing stronger day by day.","Walking into the hospital, they headed to the lounge to wait for reception. They happened to pass by a conference room, and a clear English conversation drifted out from the half-open door: \"...I think this gene-editing target must be re-evaluated.\"","The woman's voice was crisp and decisive. Ji Zhiyuan subconsciously turned his head and saw the scene inside the conference room through the glass window.","Seven or eight blonde, blue-eyed foreign experts sat around a long table. An Asian woman stood in front of the projection screen, holding a laser pointer in one hand. A light apricot silk shirt peeked out from under her white lab coat. With a light tap of her finger, the slide switched to a set of chromosome maps.","\"It's Dr. Wen,\" Old Master Ji said. \"To think Dr. Wen is actually holding a medical seminar at Li's Hospital.\"","Ji Zhiyuan's eyes deepened. \"She is very outstanding.\"","At such a young age, she had already reached the position of deputy director of pediatrics. She spoke with ease and remained calm and composed in front of so many medical experts. He really appreciated this kind of woman.","They always say women admire the strong.","The same goes for men.","\"Excuse me, are you Old Master Ji?\"","A young doctor walked over and asked, interrupting Ji Zhiyuan's focus.","Old Master Ji's voice was authoritative: \"That is me.\"","\"This way, please.\" The young doctor led the group into the elevator and went straight to the office on the eighteenth floor. \"Director Li, Old Master Ji has arrived.\"","\"Please have a seat, Old Master Ji.\" Director Li, who was in his sixties, stood up, poured a cup of tea, and set it down. \"If Old Master Ji has thought it through and wants to proceed with this project, we can go ahead and arrange the physical examination.\"","Old Master Ji glanced at Rong Yu.","Whether or not to do this project still had to be decided by his mother. After all, a single injection cost a staggering thirty million dollars, and he didn't have that much money.","Rong Yu spoke up, \"What are the exact ingredients of this Rejuvenation Injection? Is it convenient to disclose?\"","\"It seems Old Master Ji's granddaughter still has some doubts about our project.\" Director Li turned around and took out several stacks of reports from a drawer. \"These are the three most recent elderly patients who received the injection. Their myocardial cells have become ten years younger on average. These numbers are enough to prove the efficacy of this Rejuvenation Injection.\"","Rong Yu flipped through the reports. Looking at all the data, she couldn't see any problems.","Director Li paused for a moment and continued, \"Anyone in this industry knows that telomerase activators can delay aging and increase lifespan. But why is it that only our Li's Hospital has managed to develop it? It's because the Li family established this project twenty years ago. The annual research and development investment is as high as twenty trillion US dollars. Year after year of investment has finally brought about today's success. An asking price of thirty million dollars per injection is really not expensive.\"","\"Moreover,\" he smiled, \"for someone of Old Master Ji's wealth, thirty million dollars should be just a drop in the bucket. Using such a small amount of money to make your body ten years younger is a great deal, isn't it?\"","Old Master Ji's heart raced wildly when he saw those numbers.","He was already seventy-eight years old and could clearly feel that his bodily functions were failing in all aspects. In the past, he figured that getting old was just getting old, and dying was just dying; he didn't care much.","But now.","His mother was so young, only eighteen years old.","And he was old and frail.","How could he accept being separated from his mother.","How could he bear to let his mother lose him.","Meeting her old son's longing gaze, Rong Yu's heart softened.","She closed the report. \"Then let's do the physical examination first.\"","Director Li smiled and said, \"To prevent any accidents during the injection process, we need at least one family member to accompany the patient for a blood test. I wonder which one of you it will be?\"","Rong Yu's brow furrowed. \"Accidents?\"","\"Don't be nervous, miss,\" Director Li said. \"Even ordinary people having babies can encounter accidents. However, with modern medicine, the incidence rate of such medical mishaps has been reduced to a negligible level. The biggest risk when injecting the solution is an allergic reaction. But please rest assured, we have specific countermeasures in place...\"","Only then did Rong Yu nod.","Ji Zhiyuan spoke up, \"I will accompany him for the examination.\"","The group was taken to the examination room. It was just like a regular physical checkup, involving blood tests, X-rays, color ultrasounds, and so on.","Over an hour later, it was finally over.","However, some of the test results wouldn't be available until tomorrow, so the injection was scheduled for the next day.","Old Master Ji was full of anticipation. \"Old Xu from the Hong Kong Bank was able to climb a mountain the day after his injection. Mom, just you wait. From now on, I will accompany you to climb mountains and row boats every week, traveling all over the beautiful mountains and rivers of our motherland.\"","Rong Yu patted his head. \"Alright.\"","\"Well...\" Ji Zhiyuan coughed lightly. \"I've had the bodyguards bring the car around. Great-grandmother and Old Master Ji can return to the hotel first. I still have some things to take care of.\"","Old Master Ji asked curiously, \"What things...\"","But Rong Yu covered his mouth. \"Don't pry into young people's business.\"","Ji Zhiyuan sat near the entrance of the lounge for over half an hour before he saw Wen Yan, still in her white lab coat, getting ready to get off work.","He stood up and walked over. \"Dr. Wen.\"","Wen Yan was pondering over work matters and was startled by his sudden call. \"Mr. Ji, why are you here?\"","\"I accompanied my elders for a physical examination and happened to see Dr. Wen busy at work.\" Ji Zhiyuan glanced at his watch. \"At this hour, Dr. Wen should be off work. Do you have time to grab a meal together?\"","Before Wen Yan could refuse.","He continued, \"Don't misunderstand, Dr. Wen. I wanted to ask for your help in picking out a gift for Duoduo here in Hong Kong. Treating you to a meal is my way of saying thank you.\"","At the mention of Duoduo, Wen Yan's smile became much gentler. \"Alright, wait for me to change my clothes.\"","She took off her white lab coat and put on a black trench coat with flat shoes on her feet. Standing next to Ji Zhiyuan, the top of her head just reached his ear. Her height was considered quite rare among women.","At this moment, Ji Zhiyuan suddenly remembered Duoduo once saying that because she was the tallest in her class, she was always placed at the very back whenever they lined up. The little girl had felt incredibly wronged.","Last month, when he took Duoduo for a physical, the doctor also mentioned that Duoduo had good genes and would grow to be at least 1.7 meters tall in the future.","He was tall.","Duoduo's mother was also tall.","About the same height as this Dr. Wen.","Wen Yan turned to look at him. \"Mr. Ji, what's wrong?\"","Ji Zhiyuan pulled the car door open. \"Get in, let's go eat first.\"","He chose an ordinary Chinese restaurant and simply ordered a few dishes, which made Wen Yan relax a lot.","After the meal, they went to buy a gift for Duoduo.","Ji Zhiyuan subconsciously started heading into those luxurious shopping malls.","Wen Yan reached out and stopped him. \"Little girls don't like these things. They love shiny, fluffy things. Let's go to that street.\"","It was a pedestrian street, and the roadside was full of various creative handmade doll shops, attracting many young girls to browse and choose.","\"What do you think of this one?\" Wen Yan picked up a little toy rabbit. \"It blends right in with the local Harbor City culture and is really unique. Don't you think Duoduo will love it?\"","She had just turned around when a boy suddenly crashed hard into her."]},{"number":239,"title":"Chapter 239: Where does this sense of familiarity come from","paragraphs":["Ji Zhiyuan stood right beside Wen Yan.","He subconsciously reached out and wrapped his arm around her shoulders. Her long hair brushed against the tip of his nose. With a quick turn, she propped herself against the wall and stood up straight, avoiding falling into his embrace.","Feeling a bit awkward, Wen Yan said, \"Thank you, Mr. Ji.\"","Ji Zhiyuan reached out and picked up a sparkling hair clip from the stall. \"How about this one?\"","Wen Yan nodded. \"It is quite nice. It should look very pretty on Duoduo.\"","The two strolled around for a while, buying a whole pile of things that little girls liked. Before they knew it, it was already past ten o'clock at night.","Wen Yan felt a little startled.","She actually instinctively resisted Ji Zhiyuan.","But when they were actually spending time together, she did not seem to mind it. Moreover, there was always a faint sense of familiarity.","Where exactly did this sense of familiarity come from?","Day broke, and a light rain began to fall over the harbor city. The weather was a bit chilly. Rong Yu reminded her youngest son to wear thicker clothes and instructed Ji Zhiyuan, \"When your grandfather is injected with the medicine, you must accompany him the entire time. If anything happens, contact me immediately.\"","Ji Zhiyuan nodded. \"I understand, Great-grandmother.\"","Rong Yu was going to participate in the finals of the Global Physics Competition.","Out of the more than forty countries that initially participated in the preliminaries, only twelve remained for the final battle.","As Rong Yu led her team members into the arena, they bumped right into Jackson from the Lighthouse Country team and Sato from the Sakura Country team.","The moment Jackson saw her, his face instantly darkened. However, he kept his lips tightly sealed, forcefully swallowing the mockery that had reached the tip of his tongue, as the memory of being left speechless by her retorts the day before yesterday was still fresh in his mind.","Sato, on the other hand, gave a slight nod and managed to squeeze out a stiff smile. However, his eyes were darting around, clearly indicating that he did not dare to speak up easily either.","The corners of Rong Yu's lips curled up slightly. She cast a fleeting glance at them and walked straight toward the experimental station of the Huaxia team.","\"Captain,\" Su Ronghua looked up, \"I will completely follow your arrangements.\"","Rong Yu raised her eyebrows, somewhat surprised.","Ever since being slapped in the face during the preliminaries, Su Ronghua had been reticent, keeping a very low profile. She did not expect him to take the initiative to express his stance right before the finals.","Naturally, she would not reject a capable team member, so she nodded.","After all the national team members were in position, the big screen displayed the topic for the finals: \"Micro-satellite Orbit Correction Experiment Based on Hall Thrusters.\"","Countdown: eight hours.","Rong Yu's brain immediately began to work.","Sheng Ciyuan said, \"First, we need to simulate the space environment to determine the thrust efficiency of the plasma plume...\"","Song Huai picked up a pen and said, \"We must build an optimization model to complete the experiment within eight hours...\"","Rong Yu spoke up, \"Su Ronghua, you are in charge of calibrating the vacuum chamber pressure. Sheng Ciyuan, you are responsible for regulating the current parameters. Song Huai, you will collect the plasma data. Ding Zhe, you...\"","The team members had fully recognized her abilities and plunged into the experiment without another word.","Rong Yu needed to model in real-time to calculate the optimal thrust angle.","The judges' seats were also quite lively.","The top figures in this field from various countries were conversing in low voices.","\"The Lighthouse Country's Hall thruster scheme is very mature. Someone won an award using a similar model last year.\"","\"The Sakura Country team's new ion source design also has its highlights, and Germany has adopted an innovative model. This batch of students really has fantastic ideas.\"","\"The Huaxia team achieved impressive results in the preliminaries, making their finals worth looking forward to... Wait a minute, what is going on with their model...\"","\"This is too innovative; it completely ignores the space environment.\"","\"The Huaxia team probably got carried away by winning first place in the preliminaries. This captain is too eager to win an award, which has instead led to a mistake. They messed up right from the first step...\"","Time ticked by, minute by minute, second by second.","Rong Yu's group was making very fast progress.","However, after the experiment had been running for more than three hours, Su Ronghua suddenly cried out in alarm, \"The pressure value has dropped to zero!\"","The vacuum chamber pressure plummeted, the plasma plume instantly became chaotic, and the experimental data fluctuated wildly.","Sheng Ciyuan shoved him aside and quickly checked, \"Rong Yu, the vacuum pump has failed! The pressure cannot be maintained!\"","Several judges on the panel revealed expressions that said they knew this would happen.","\"This is the consequence of being too reckless.\"","\"We are halfway through the competition; it is clearly too late to start over.\"","\"What a pity...\"","Among the judges, a professor from Huaxia said coldly, \"Indeed, there is still half of the competition left. Isn't it a bit too early to jump to conclusions right now?\"","In the Huaxia zone, Rong Yu had forcefully opened the equipment panel. Her pupils shrank abruptly—the screws on the pressure sensor interface had been deliberately loosened by three turns.","Her gaze swept coldly over the several team members.","Sheng Ciyuan was in a panic, Song Huai was frantically calculating data, Su Ronghua looked deeply remorseful, and Ding Zhe along with another team member were trying to figure out how to tighten the screws.","\"The Lighthouse Country must have come in early and tampered with it!\" Ding Zhe cursed. \"This is deliberate retaliation!\"","Song Huai spoke up, \"It could also be the Sakura Country.\"","Sheng Ciyuan gnashed his teeth, \"I am going to report this to the organizing committee...\"","\"With only four hours left, reporting it will affect the progress of the experiment,\" Su Ronghua said. \"We might as well build the model using the traditional method, but it seems it is too late for that too.\"","\"Listen up,\" Rong Yu spoke. \"Sheng Ciyuan, use the acoustic ranging method to estimate the actual pressure. Song Huai, reduce the ion source power to 20%. Su Ronghua, preserve the evidence first. Ding Zhe, prepare for manual overclocking...\"","Her voice carried a certain magic. Everyone instantly found their backbone and quickly got busy.","The more critical the moment, the faster time seemed to fly.","Only the sounds of submissions could be heard echoing through the hall—","\"Lighthouse Team: Submission successful. Time taken: 7 hours and 01 minute.\"","Jackson looked at the big screen. Only seven hours had passed, and their Lighthouse Country had already submitted their data. On the finals stage, the Huaxia Country was being ruthlessly trampled under his feet.","Next, the other countries submitted their data one after another.","\"Germany Team: Submission successful. Time taken: 7 hours and 19 minutes.\"","\"Russia Team: Submission successful. Time taken: 7 hours and 24 minutes.\"","\"Baka!\" Someone from the Sakura Country team suddenly cursed loudly. \"What is going on? It is smoking! Why is it smoking!\"","With only half an hour left until the end of the competition, an equipment failure was like a heavy blow to the head.","Sato stared blankly at the big screen, murmuring, \"It is over, it is over, everything is ruined... How could we be so unlucky?\"","Meanwhile.","Rong Yu checked the data one last time and was just about to submit it.","Su Ronghua spoke up, \"The final results are too important. Let each of us check it over to avoid any omissions. Anyway, we still have half an hour, so there is no rush.\"","Rong Yu said indifferently, \"It is precisely because it is so important that I do not feel at ease letting you all check it.\"","Before Su Ronghua could even retort, her hand swiftly pressed the Enter key. The data was successfully submitted.","\"Huaxia Team: Submission successful. Time taken: 7 hours and 32 minutes.\""]},{"number":240,"title":"Chapter 240: From now on, Haicheng No.1 High School takes pride in you.","paragraphs":["The countdown timer beeped.","The national teams participating in the finals submitted their results one by one.","Only the Sakura Nation team, due to an equipment failure, failed to calculate the final result and was excluded from the final ranking.","Jackson whistled. Sato-kun, decades ago your country could do whatever it wanted on Huaxia soil, but this era belongs to our Lighthouse Nation. Let the light of our Lighthouse Nation illuminate the entire physics world.","The final whistle of the competition blew, and the entire venue fell silent.","The data submitted by the various countries slowly appeared on the large screen, numbers jumping constantly before finally freezing—","Huaxia Team: Orbit Correction Accuracy: 99.7%, Fuel Utilization Rate: 98.9%.","Lighthouse Nation Team: Orbit Correction Accuracy: 93.1%, Fuel Utilization Rate: 86.4%.","Germany Team: Orbit Correction Accuracy: 89.0%, Fuel Utilization Rate: 81.7%.","Russia Team: ...","Under the gaze of the entire audience, the Huaxia team was first, and the Lighthouse Nation team was second.","The smile on Jackson's face didn't even have time to fade. How, how is this possible? Didn't they have a problem halfway through? Why did they still get first place? This is impossible, absolutely impossible! Right! Cheating, they definitely cheated!","His teammates stood silently to the side; no one echoed his sentiments. The Asian female vice-captain glanced at him coldly. Jackson, that's enough.","What do you mean enough! Jackson spun around abruptly, his eyes bloodshot. Didn't you see it? Their vacuum chamber clearly had a problem! How could they—","They just did it, the female vice-captain said in a cold voice. They encountered a problem and solved it in time, and surpassed all teams in both accuracy and utilization rate. This is enough to show that Huaxia's level of physics is not inferior to our Lighthouse Nation. Stop saying ridiculous things and embarrassing us.","The usually confident and composed Jackson's expression instantly twisted, as if he had been stabbed in the chest.","The captain of the Sakura Nation team, Sato, stood at the forefront of his team, his hands hanging by his sides, his fingertips trembling slightly.","The three months of closed training in the laboratory, the noise of the Hall thrusters that he had treated as a lullaby, all turned into ringing in his ears at this moment.","He remembered the battle sword hanging in his great-grandfather's study. Many years ago, his great-grandfather led his comrades on this piece of land, invincible in every battle... But now, on that large screen symbolizing honor, there wasn't even the presence of the Sakura Nation. He could only lead his companions and return in defeat.","We lost thoroughly, Sato said slowly. Pack up the equipment, consider it maintaining our last shred of dignity.","The team members were all stunned.","Sato had always been proud and never bowed his head, yet now...","At this time, the chief judge walked onto the stage. Next, please invite the entire winning teams to the stage to receive their awards. Mr. Ole, the pioneer of international physics, and the International Physics Association... will present the awards to these outstanding students...","The national anthem of Huaxia played in the arena, and the lighting of the entire venue suddenly turned to Huaxia red.","Such a familiar melody made the heart in Rong Yu's chest beat wildly. This was her country, the motherland she was proud of. She was honored to be able to stand here and earn a piece of glory for her country.","She stood in the center of the podium, the gold medal on her chest shining brightly under the lights. She looked up at the dome, where staff members were raising the five-star red flag.","After the award ceremony, the organizers held a celebration banquet.","The students from the twelve countries participating in the finals were all invited to attend this banquet.","Rong Wangtian and a group of parents had been waiting there for a long time. Seeing the children return wearing gold medals, they couldn't close their mouths from smiling so happily.","Pei Yaru was very excited. Rong Yu, Song Huai, you represent the Huaxia Nation, and of course, you also represent Haicheng First High School. From now on, Haicheng First High School is proud of you.","Madam Song hugged her son's shoulders. Next, our Song Huai will also participate in the Global Math Olympiad. When he gets another first place then, he should be the number one honorary alumnus of Haicheng First High School.","When she said this, she gave Rong Yu a faint look.","So what if Rong Yu was excellent? She only gained honors in the single subject of physics.","But her son was excellent in physics and even better in mathematics, developing in both directions, and was the prized pupil of Academician Liu.","Rong Wangtian said neutrally, Then let's wait until Song Huai gets first place in mathematics to talk about it.","Song Huai pursed his lips.","When he participated in the domestic Math Olympiad finals last time, he felt it was very strenuous. It was only out of good luck that he won the gold award.","When it came to the international finals, facing so many outstanding mathematical geniuses from all over the world, he didn't know if he would still have such good luck.","The Huaxia side was jubilant.","Meanwhile, Jackson from the Lighthouse Nation stood in a corner, gripping his champagne glass so tightly that his knuckles turned white. His teammates had long since blended into the banquet; only he stared fixedly in Rong Yu's direction, unwillingness surging in his eyes.","Clearly...","He suddenly smiled and strode toward Rong Yu's direction.","Rong Yu was chatting with Sheng Ciyuan. At first, they were talking about the orange cat Pangpang, but somehow, the topic shifted to Sheng Qingyan.","Sheng Ciyuan said, My grandmother said that when my eldest brother was just born, a Daoist priest passed by our door and asked for a sip of water. The master read my brother's fortune then, saying that my brother suffered a lot in his previous life, and in this life, he reincarnated into our Sheng family to enjoy blessings. He said the family just needed to feed him well and raise him properly, and that we shouldn't force anything. Before, my grandmother didn't understand what it meant to not force anything. Later, when my brother got sick, she realized what it meant...","Halfway through his words.","Jackson's voice rang out. Huaxia Team, first place, congratulations.","Rong Yu raised her glass and smiled brightly. Also congratulations to the Lighthouse Nation for winning second place. Joy to us both, congratulations.","This smile was too blinding for a loser.","Jackson sneered and spoke loudly, Captain Rong, you are too dishonest. I spent so much money to make you have a problem during the experiment phase. In the end, you took the money but didn't do the job, and you actually dared to take first place?","The bustling banquet hall instantly fell dead silent.","All conversation came to an abrupt halt, and countless gazes shot over in unison. The judges frowned, the participating team members from various countries looked at each other in dismay, and even Rong Yu's teammates froze in place.","You son of a bitch, what kind of nonsense are you spouting! Rong Wangtian was the first to react. He quickly rushed forward and shoved Jackson away. Is the character of you Lighthouse Nation people this inferior? You lose the competition, so you start spreading rumors?","He was also someone who had attended university and knew English, but he was not good at it. He stumbled through the sentence, cutting its lethality in half.","Jackson scoffed and pulled a folded piece of paper from the inner pocket of his suit. A transfer record, two hundred thousand US dollars, remitted to an offshore account—don't tell me you don't know who received this money!"]},{"number":241,"title":"Chapter 241: I need to reconsider the marriage between Yaoyao and Song Huai.","paragraphs":["The banquet hall instantly exploded into an uproar.","\"What did I just hear? Jackson bribed the captain of the Chinese team?\"","\"Isn't the Lighthouse Nation supposed to be amazing? To win the championship, they actually bribed Captain Rong to intentionally make the Chinese team lose?\"","\"Well, the Chinese team performed so outstandingly in the preliminaries. The Lighthouse Nation had to resort to some dirty tricks to secure first place, didn't they?\"","\"No wonder the Chinese team had a major mistake halfway through the finals. It turns out it was man-made.\"","\"That Captain Rong doesn't look like that kind of person.\"","\"You can't judge a book by its cover.\"","\"...\"","Rong Wangtian's chest heaved violently from anger.","Although the father-daughter relationship between him and this daughter was very weak, even so, he could be one hundred percent certain that Rong Yu would absolutely never accept such dirty money to do such a dirty deed.","It should be said that any Chinese person with a backbone would never let any personal interest override national honor.","Rong Wangtian said in broken English, \"Mr. Jackson, is it? Fine, just wait to receive a legal summons. I'm going to sue you to death...\"","Halfway through his words, Rong Yu pressed his arm down.","Rong Yu reached out and snatched that piece of paper from Jackson's hand. It really was two hundred thousand US dollars.","She was still wondering... why?","So, someone had been bought off by money.","Two hundred thousand US dollars was equal to over a million RMB. This sum of money was indeed not small, but to betray teammates and betray the country for money, what was the difference between this kind of person and the traitors during the war years?","She held up the piece of paper. \"May I ask Mr. Jackson, did I really receive this money?\"","Jackson's face was full of malice. \"It's the account address you provided. If it's not you, who else could it be?\"","For people from other countries, second place in the global competition would be considered a very good result.","But for the Lighthouse Nation, it was a disgrace.","Moreover, Rong Yu was simply too outstanding. Her data on the field was too terrifying. She was absolutely a genius among geniuses. If such a person joined the Chinese physics industry, it would absolutely be like adding wings to a tiger!","By destroying Rong Yu, he was doing a great service for the Lighthouse Nation!","Jackson said coldly, \"Rong Yu took the money, causing the Chinese team's experiment to malfunction halfway through. I suggest that the Chinese Physics Association ban Rong Yu for life and prohibit Rong Yu from entering any field of physics in any capacity!\"","Various voices echoed around them.","Pei Yaru had already stood in front of Rong Yu in a protective posture.","Sheng Ciyuan gritted his teeth and said, \"A mere two hundred thousand dollars, how is that possible? Rong Yu wouldn't even bat an eye at it.\"","Song Huai was about to speak but was pulled back by Madam Song. \"Does this matter have anything to do with you? Keep your mouth shut and just watch the show.\"","Rong Wangtian stood on the sidelines. Hearing these words, his anger immediately surged.","The Rong family and the Song family were not completely unrelated; they were in-laws.","When a child of the Rong family was in trouble and being slandered, Madam Song actually had such an attitude!","Rong Wangtian spoke coldly, \"Madam Song, I will have to reconsider the marriage between Yaoyao and Song Huai.\"","Madam Song's expression darkened. \"The Rong family's business cannot even compare to half of the Song family's. Back then, it was only because the two elders were old friends that the marriage was arranged. Do you really think our Song family cares? Since CEO Rong wants to reconsider, then let's cancel the engagement. There's no need to discuss it further in the future...\"","Song Huai frowned. \"Mom, can you please stop talking...\"","The chief judge pushed through the crowd and walked over. He picked up the transfer receipt and frowned. \"An offshore anonymous account with an untraceable owner. Jackson, why do you think you can convict Rong Yu with just a transfer receipt? On what grounds can you ban an outstanding physics genius with just one sentence from you? Do you think my country of China is like your Lighthouse Nation, where you can just fabricate evidence and declare war on someone?\"","The chief judge's imposing aura made it hard for Jackson to lift his head. Gritting his teeth, he suddenly looked up, reached out, and pointed at someone in the crowd of onlookers, saying loudly, \"This is physical evidence. I also have a witness. It's Su Ronghua from the Chinese team. He is the witness!\"","Su Ronghua's face was already pale. Suddenly, everyone turned around and looked at him in unison. Beads of sweat the size of beans immediately rolled down his forehead, and he could barely stand steady.","Jackson said loudly, \"Su Ronghua, speak up!\"","Su Ronghua bit his lip tightly, unable to utter a single word.","Sheng Ciyuan said angrily, \"Jackson, isn't it enough for you to throw dirty water on Rong Yu? Now you want to throw dirty water on Su Ronghua as well. Why don't you just throw dirty water on the entire Chinese team? That way, your Lighthouse Nation can take first place by default, right?!\"","\"Su! Rong! Hua!\"","Jackson's eyes turned gloomy, carrying a strong warning.","Rong Yu looked back, her gaze landing lightly on Jackson's head.","She was waiting.","Unfortunately.","He disappointed her.","Unable to withstand the warning, Su Ronghua raised his head and said word by word, \"The night before the finals, I saw Rong Yu and Jackson talking at the corner of the stairs. But the distance was too far, and I didn't hear clearly what they were saying. I never expected that it was actually a private transaction... Fortunately, so many of us team members managed to turn the tide, otherwise, the Chinese team would have missed out on first place...\"","Slap!","Sheng Ciyuan raised his hand and threw a punch.","He was actually not a violent person and usually handled things gently, but right now, he was truly driven mad with anger.","Rong Yu grabbed Sheng Ciyuan.","This kid was too skinny. If the other party recovered and fought back, he would definitely be pinned down and beaten.","Standing in front of Sheng Ciyuan, she sighed and said, \"Originally, I thought that our own family matters should be solved behind closed doors to avoid letting people from other countries watch a joke. But since it involves another country, we can only lay it all out in the open.\"","Su Ronghua's expression changed drastically. \"What, what do you mean?\"","Rong Yu took out her phone and played a few video clips. The footage showed the finals venue, specifically Su Ronghua's experimental area.","While doing the experiment, he kept looking around, clearly absent-minded.","In the first video, he stealthily reached out and crumpled one of Song Huai's scratch papers into a ball to destroy it.","In the second video, he pulled out a wire...","Su Ronghua looked as if someone had grabbed him by the throat. His breathing instantly became rapid as he constantly backed away...","Rong Yu's voice rang out, \"After the pressure cabin had a problem, I guessed that there was probably a traitor on the inside.\"","This was Chinese territory. It would be too difficult for foreigners to personally cause trouble.","Therefore, it could only be a fellow countryman.","Those judge teachers were all accomplished and famous; it was highly unlikely they would ruin their reputations over such a trivial matter.","So, she locked her target on the team members.","During those four hours, besides building the model framework, she had been observing.","Song Huai had been frantically calculating.","Sheng Ciyuan had been taking notes around the console.","Ding Zhe had not slacked off in the slightest either.","Only Su Ronghua seemed to be on a completely different layer from the hardworking team members.","She had set up her phone camera early on and quietly recorded everything.","She originally thought that Su Ronghua was jealous of her captaincy, so he intentionally caused damage.","In her view, this was an internal contradiction that just needed to be resolved internally.","But she never expected that it would actually involve the United States.","This meant that Su Ronghua was not merely jealous of her; she was committing treason and betraying her country!","She simply could not tolerate this kind of person.","After all, if someone was willing to commit betrayal over such a petty matter, they would be completely untrustworthy when it came to anything of real importance."]},{"number":242,"title":"Chapter 242: This time, China has not only won impressively but also delivered an even more impressive verdict.","paragraphs":["As soon as the video was played, the expressions of everyone in the banquet hall changed. Hundreds of pairs of eyes turned to stare at Su Ronghua in unison.","\"Traitor!\" Sheng Ciyuan's face was full of disbelief. \"For a mere two hundred thousand dollars, you sold out your teammates and your country. I was wondering why we kept running into so many problems during the experiment. It turns out we had a mole. Thank goodness Rong Yu was always there to solve them in time, otherwise, the Chinese team would have lost miserably!\"","Song Huai shook his head. \"And you actually tried to team up with Jackson to put the blame on us.\"","Ding Zhe slammed his champagne flute onto the table. \"Su Ronghua, are you even human?\"","\"Outrageous!\" The chief judge was furious. \"The country put so much effort into cultivating you so that you could win glory for the nation and contribute to the country, not so you could betray your teammates and your country at a critical moment! Your actions have severely violated the principles of the physics competition. The Physics Association will take you to court to face judgment from the highest judge.\"","Su Ronghua shook his head violently. \"I didn't, it wasn't me...\"","He was truly desperate for money. Two hundred thousand US dollars could do a lot of things.","Moreover, he also wanted to see Rong Yu fail.","She was too confident, too proud, acting as if she knew how to do everything. He wanted to see if she would come to him to discuss countermeasures if she failed.","But she didn't.","She calmly handled every unexpected situation throughout the entire process.","She took first place.","And it was a landslide victory.","Her excellence made him feel a sense of frustration that even if he lived ten more years, he might not be able to surpass her.","It was his jealousy that had swallowed his reason.","He couldn't even believe that he had actually done such a thing...","\"Su Ronghua, the organizing committee will revoke your gold medal and certificate!\" A judge shot him a cold look before turning their gaze to Jackson.","Jackson muttered several curses under his breath.","That idiot, he couldn't even be careful when doing dirty work, and actually got caught red-handed.","Before the chief judge could speak, he shrugged. \"Do the judges of China still want to punish me? Don't forget, I am from the Lighthouse Nation. In the International Physics Association, people from the Lighthouse Nation make up seventy-five percent. China has no right to punish me, much less ban me from competing. Got it?\"","These words successfully ignited the anger of everyone present.","A German said, \"People from the Lighthouse Nation take drugs at sports events to evade inspections, and now they even cheat in physics competitions?\"","Someone from the Sakura Nation said, \"It makes it hard not to suspect whether our equipment malfunctioned during the finals because the Lighthouse Nation was causing trouble.\"","A Russian said, \"Aha! So freedom and democracy mean tearing up the rules whenever you please?\"","A French person said, \"Look here, this is the world's number one Lighthouse Nation. If they can't win, they resort to sabotage. Tsk tsk, no wonder the Lighthouse Nation is number one in physics. So this is how they got to be number one.\"","Someone from the Kimchi Nation said, \"If even basic fairness cannot be guaranteed, our country will withdraw from international competitions next year.\"","A mix of various languages rang out.","Jackson didn't care at all and laughed. \"Please remember, the rules of this world are made by the strong.\"","He kicked his chair aside and walked out.","The people on his team were going crazy. Although second place wasn't very glorious, being pointed at and having their results questioned was obviously much worse!","The group of people scrambled out of the banquet hall in a panic.","Among the judges, there was also someone from the Lighthouse Nation. His face was flushed red, ashamed that his country had such a young man.","But there was nothing he could do.","Because Jackson's father was a member of the International Physics Association, no one could punish him.","\"The International Physics Competition has never been a game of power.\" The chief judge's voice was unhurried but firm as iron. \"The actions of the Lighthouse Nation's team have severely violated academic ethics and competition fairness. If we tacitly accept the existence of such despicable behavior out of fear of a certain country's power, then what is the point of this competition?\"","The entire hall held its breath.","The chief judge's gaze swept over the judges from various countries and finally landed on the representative judge from the Lighthouse Nation's team.","\"Therefore, by the unanimous decision of the Chinese judging panel—\"","\"The Lighthouse Nation team's results for this competition are hereby voided immediately.\"","The judge from the Lighthouse Nation widened his eyes. \"This, this...\"","The chief judge interrupted him. \"This is China, and we will handle it according to China's rules.\"","\"Good!\" The Russian judge slammed his hand on the table. \"Now that's what you call fairness!\"","The German judge nodded. \"It should have been done long ago. Hah, do they really think the international academic community is their own backyard?\"","\"At the same time, the International Physics Society will officially send a letter to the Lighthouse Nation's Physics Association, demanding an investigation into the individuals involved.\" He paused, his gaze burning like a torch. \"Academia knows no borders, but morality has a bottom line.\"","\"Beautiful! This is the demeanor of a great nation!\"","\"China won beautifully this time, and the ruling was even more beautiful!\"","\"...\"","On the internet, a massive uproar had already been stirred up.","When Rong Yu appeared at the international competition as the team leader, it was already shocking enough.","When she took first place by a landslide, the entire internet boiled over, and Rong Yu's name was immediately pushed to the top of the trending searches.","And the moment the conspiracy was exposed, it could be said that the trending searches on every single platform across the internet exploded.","\"LMAO, the Lighthouse Nation team can't afford to lose so they play dirty? In the end, Goddess Rong exposed them on the spot, their faces must be swollen from the slapping, right?\"","\"How did a moral traitor like Su Ronghua even get into the national team?\"","\"Come and admire the American double standards—when they cheat it's a technical error, when others win the championship it's just good luck.\"","\"...\"","\"Rong Yu debuted in the entertainment industry as a landslide first place, and in the physics world, she's also a landslide first place winning glory for the country. I just want to ask, why doesn't she even have a public social media account?\"","\"My idol separates her work and personal life, there's nothing wrong with that.\"","\"My daughter is a fan of Rong Yu. With Rong Yu as a role model, I hope my daughter can also stand on the international stage in the future.\"","\"Rong Yu is so strong in the physics world, does this mean she won't be in the entertainment industry anymore?\"","\"No way, I still want to keep stanning her. If she leaves the industry, who am I supposed to stan?\"","\"...\"","Rong Yu put down her champagne and went to the restroom. She never expected to bump into a group of girls. The girls looked at their phones, then looked at her, and then swarmed around her.","\"Ahhh, it's Rong Yu!\"","\"Rong Yu is actually attending a banquet at this hotel, we are so lucky!\"","\"Rong Yu, can we take a picture together?\"","\"Rong Yu, can I get an autograph?\"","\"...\"","Facing a group of cute little girls, Rong Yu couldn't bring herself to refuse. She took photos with them one by one. Fortunately, there were only seven or eight people, otherwise, she would have died of exhaustion.","After using the restroom, Rong Yu stayed obediently in the banquet hall and didn't go anywhere else, to avoid being surrounded again.","At this time, she received a message on her phone.","Rong Ruoyao: \"Sister, do you plan to open a Weibo account? Many of your fans have been coming to me to ask.\"","Rong Yu: \"No.\"","Opening a Weibo account was too troublesome, and she would have to interact and manage it. Just thinking about it gave her a headache.","She glanced at the time; the banquet was almost over.","\"Bzz bzz bzz!\"","Her phone vibrated violently. She took a look and saw it was a call from her son.","She answered with a smile: \"Yingbao, it will be over in about ten minutes. Just wait for me in the room...\"","Before the words could even fade, Old Master Ji interrupted, \"Mom, Mom, this is bad! Yuan has gone missing. You have to think of something quickly...\""]},{"number":243,"title":"Chapter 243: A Yuan Has Probably Been Kidnapped","paragraphs":["The banquet hall was buzzing with noise.","Rong Yu couldn't hear clearly. She walked to a quieter spot on the side and asked, \"What do you mean figure something out? What happened, Yingbao?\"","Old Mr. Ji's voice was trembling.","In the past, if a sudden accident occurred, he would handle it calmly.","Perhaps because he now had his mother and a pillar of support in his heart, his first instinct when something major happened was to seek her help.","\"Yuan is missing.\" The old man tried his best to keep his voice clear. \"Early this morning, Yuan accompanied me to Li's Hospital for my injection. Director Li suddenly suggested that Yuan donate a kidney. I angrily refused and dragged Yuan back to the hotel. But when I woke up from my nap and tried to contact Yuan, I couldn't reach him... Yuan is the most filial child. His watch is linked to my phone. Whenever I contact him, no matter what he is doing or where he is, he will always reply to me immediately. But now, four hours have passed, and there is absolutely no news.\"","Rong Yu's pupils suddenly dilated. \"Donate a kidney?\"","When they were at the hospital yesterday, the other party had not brought up this condition.","Old Mr. Ji's voice was hoarse. \"Director Li said that Yuan's blood type and kidneys meet the criteria. If he agreed to donate a kidney, they would waive the thirty million dollar medication fee; otherwise, they would refuse to treat me... Mom, although I really want to live a few more years, how could I possibly do so at the cost of Yuan's health? I'm worried now, could Yuan have gone to donate his kidney on his own?\"","Rong Yu's face was cold and dark, but her voice was very gentle. \"Yingbao, leave this matter to me. Don't panic.\"","She hung up the phone and immediately contacted the bodyguards and caregivers, telling them to stay with her elderly son and make absolutely sure he didn't wander off.","Clenching her phone tightly, several possibilities flashed through her mind.","\"Xiao Yu, what happened?\"","Rong Wangtian had noticed her emotional shift early on. One look and he knew something bad had happened.","Rong Yu shook her head. \"It's nothing.\"","\"Xiao Yu, I am your father,\" Rong Wangtian said firmly. \"I can help you.\"","Rong Yu met his gaze.","No matter what he was thinking in his heart, at least in this moment, he was sincere.","She spoke, \"Come with me to the police station.\"","Rong Wangtian's pupils shrank. \"What's wrong?\"","Rong Yu said quickly, \"The President of the Ji Consortium, Ji Zhiyuan, has gone missing.\"","Rong Wangtian's face was filled with shock.","But not daring to ask too much, he hurriedly arranged for a car and took Rong Yu to the nearest police station.","\"Missing for only four hours?\" The police officer frowned. \"It's very normal for adults to lose contact. Maybe his phone died, or he went out to sea with friends. Just wait a bit longer.\"","Rong Yu already knew the police wouldn't file a case.","If it were a child, even if missing for just an hour, the police would immediately initiate procedures.","She spoke up, \"Before he went missing, Ji Zhiyuan took a large amount of pain-relief medication. The medication contains hallucinogenic ingredients. Being missing for four hours means there is an eighty percent chance his life is in danger.\"","An adult losing contact for four hours wouldn't warrant a case.","But if they had taken hallucinogenic painkillers and couldn't be reached for four hours, it became a very serious case.","The police officer immediately initiated the procedure and applied to view the citywide surveillance footage.","Rong Yu gave Rong Wangtian a look.","Rong Wangtian pulled the officer aside and said, \"I remember now, before he went missing, he seemed to have mentioned where he was going. Right, I think it was the western suburbs. I'm not very familiar with Hong Kong City. Could you bring out a map for me to look at? If I can narrow down the area, it should be easier for you to check the surveillance...\"","The officer's line of sight was blocked by Rong Wangtian.","Rong Yu sat in front of the surveillance monitor and rapidly typed out a string of commands.","A long time ago, when Qiu Sang's son went missing, it was this string of code that locked onto the location within the massive surveillance data system.","The last location where Yuan appeared was an abandoned warehouse in the eastern suburbs.","Ten minutes later, an inconspicuous car drove away. Halfway through the journey, the car was switched. It drove around in a few circles, switched again, and along the way, changed vehicles four times before finally stopping at the back door of Li's Hospital.","Rong Yu drew in a sharp breath.","It was a kidnapping!","Just as she was about to speak.","All the footage she had just found on the computer completely vanished.","Her heart skipped a beat.","\"Hey, what are you doing?\" The police officer finally noticed her. \"How dare you mess with the internal system!\"","Rong Yu said in a deep voice, \"Li's Hospital kidnapped Ji Zhiyuan. Please arrange for officers to search the premises immediately.\"","The officer frowned. \"What nonsense are you talking about? Li's is a famous charity hospital in our city. Every year, they provide free medical quotas, and countless children suffering from illnesses across the country travel from afar to seek treatment here. Both the director and the chairman of Li's Hospital are globally renowned philanthropists. You have no evidence, yet you falsely accuse Li's Hospital of kidnapping?\"","Rong Yu glanced at the computer.","Due to her negligence, her program had alerted the other party, allowing them to delete the surveillance footage one step ahead of her.","In other words, her words were now baseless.","Furthermore, Li's influence in the city was too vast, practically penetrating every industry. Moreover, the big shots in various sectors were all members of Li's Hospital. Invisibly, countless protective walls had been erected around the hospital.","\"I must have seen it wrong,\" Rong Yu stood up. \"There's no need to file a case.\"","She turned and walked out.","Rong Wangtian quickly chased after her. \"Xiao Yu, what do we do?\"","Rong Yu glanced at the pitch-black sky. \"Sorry to have troubled you today, President Rong. The Ji family will visit to express our gratitude another day.\"","Back at the hotel, as soon as Rong Yu entered the room, Old Mr. Ji came forward to greet her. \"Mom, how did it go? Did you find Yuan?\"","Rong Yu originally wanted to hide it from him.","But Yingbao was no longer a child, and she wouldn't be able to keep it hidden.","She said, \"Yuan has likely been kidnapped. He's at Li's Hospital. I will handle it, so don't worry.\"","Old Mr. Ji's eyes widened. \"It must be because Yuan refused to donate his kidney. It must be! I need to report this to the police. I absolutely must report it.\"","Rong Yu shook her head. \"Without evidence, it will be very difficult.\"","The influence they had in Hai City was basically ineffective here in Hong Kong City. Otherwise, Li's Hospital wouldn't have dared to resort to kidnapping.","She made a phone call. \"Secretary Jiang, find out the founding history of Li's Hospital as quickly as possible. I want all the information.\"","Secretary Jiang was the chairman's secretary and possessed exceptional capabilities. However, investigating backgrounds in Hong Kong City was quite difficult. It took over forty minutes before Secretary Jiang sent the documents over.","Rong Yu read through them carefully.","When she saw the information about the founder of Li's Hospital, she was instantly stunned.","Li Chunsheng, the founder of Li's Hospital, was ninety-six years old this year and had already retreated behind the scenes. The current director of Li's Hospital was Li Chunsheng's eldest son.","In Rong Yu's mind, the image of a very thin and small child surfaced. That child was named Li Chunsheng. He was four years younger than her and had gone abroad to study in the same year as her. He was a medical student.","The data showed that Li Chunsheng started suffering from kidney disease at the age of sixty and had already undergone one kidney transplant... His other organs had also developed problems one after another, but he had been saved by black-tech medical treatments, becoming a living signboard for Li's Hospital. That was why so many wealthy people were willing to spend fortunes there."]},{"number":244,"title":"Chapter 244: Ji Zhiyuan, Don't Close Your Eyes, Look at Me","paragraphs":["Six o'clock in the morning.","A knock sounded at the door. Rong Yu, who hadn't slept all night, got up to open it. It was Ji Yanting.","He had dark circles under his eyes, clearly having stayed up all night as well. His voice was incredibly hoarse. \"Great-Grandma, is there any news about my oldest brother?\"","\"We have a lead,\" Rong Yu replied calmly. \"Pack up these documents and come with me to Wangyue Mountain.\"","Old Master Ji dug out an old man's outfit and a hat from his suitcase. \"A-Yan, you have a very high profile here in Hong Kong. It'll be hard to get things done with too many fans around. Cover yourself up well.\"","Ji Yanting nodded.","He put on Old Master Ji's clothes, hunched his back slightly, and put on the old man's hat. He basically no longer looked like a young man, let alone the superstar Best Actor famous all across Asia.","As for Rong Yu, although she was also a public figure, it had only been half a year since her first public appearance. While the news coverage was broad, most people forgot what they saw shortly after.","When she went out, the number of times she was recognized could be counted on one hand.","The two headed directly for Wangyue Mountain.","Wangyue Mountain was the top luxury residential area in Hong Kong. More than a dozen mansions stood halfway up the mountain; this place was a symbol of status, wealth, and prestige.","Their car drove all the way up and stopped in front of a massive estate at 7:30 in the morning.","Almost as soon as they parked, a security guard came over and knocked on the car window.","Rong Yu got out of the car and said, \"I am an old friend of Chairman Li. Give this to Chairman Li, and he will naturally know who I am.\"","The object in her hand was a painting.","The painting depicted a very simple rural landscape: a dilapidated thatched cottage, an old woman sitting under a tree sewing clothes, and a big rooster standing on a branch.","The security guard frowned.","There were many similar paintings on the walls inside the estate, but they were all masterpieces by famous artists from various countries. This picture, however, was too simple, and the brushstrokes were quite hasty.","However, this young girl claimed to be an old friend of the chairman.","The security guard spoke up, \"At this hour, the chairman is still resting...\"","Halfway through his sentence, a stretched ultra-luxury car suddenly drove out from within the estate.","The security guard muttered, \"In all these years, this is the first time the chairman has gone out this early...\"","He ignored Rong Yu, this inexplicable visitor, and hurried over to open the gates.","The massive iron gates of the Li family required the combined effort of four security guards to push open. The car drove out from inside.","Rong Yu looked at the half-lowered car window. The over ninety-year-old Li Chunsheng leaned back in the car seat. Deep wrinkles covered his entire face, and he exuded a heavy aura of old age. In person, he looked much older than his heavily retouched photos on the internet.","\"Chairman Li!\"","She immediately shouted.","However, the person in the car didn't hear her at all, and the car sped down the mountain.","Rong Yu put the painting away, turned around to get into the car, and said in a deep voice, \"A-Yan, go to the Li Family Hospital, quickly.\"","Ji Yanting didn't dare to delay for a moment.","He was young and drove extremely fast. By the time their car reached the hospital entrance, Li Chunsheng had just gotten out of his car.","The nearly centenarian was escorted by over a dozen doctors and over a dozen bodyguards as he walked through the hospital's main doors and headed straight into the elevator.","It was impossible for Rong Yu and Ji Yanting to get close.","\"Miss Rong!\" Wen Yan, who had just arrived at the hospital entrance, saw Rong Yu's solemn expression and hurriedly asked, \"Did something happen?\"","Rong Yu calmed her emotions slightly.","She spoke in a low voice, \"Dr. Wen, how much clearance has this hospital given you?\"","Wen Yan was taken aback. \"What do you want me to do, Miss Rong?\"","\"The founder of the Li Family Hospital, Chairman Li, appeared at the hospital early in the morning to undergo a kidney transplant.\" Rong Yu enunciated every word clearly. \"Can you find a way to get into the operating room?\"","She paused and added, \"The person providing the kidney is Ji Zhiyuan. He was kidnapped.\"","Wen Yan covered her mouth in shock.","Her heart began to race uncontrollably.","She took a sharp breath and said, \"Although I'm only here to attend a seminar, I am a deputy director after all. Even though I'm in pediatrics, I should be able to enter the surgical area. However, the people performing surgery on Chairman Li are probably top experts and professors. I don't know...\"","She babbled a bit incoherently before finally saying, \"I will definitely find a way to get into the operating room. And then? What do I do?\"","Rong Yu grasped her suddenly cold hands. \"Stall for time.\"","Wen Yan squeezed her hands back.","Then she turned around and strode into the hospital.","She was a doctor sent from Haicheng to attend an international seminar at the Li Family Hospital in Hong Kong, and she wasn't involved in outpatient clinics or surgeries. But wearing a hospital lab coat and a mask, she walked toward the surgical preparation room without anyone stopping her. She entered the surgical area very smoothly.","There were dozens of operating rooms here.","Wen Yan pressed her lips together tightly.","Chairman Li should be in the largest operating room, the one with the most advanced equipment that could accommodate the most experts and professors.","In the corridor, a nurse happened to step away to attend to something else. She took the nurse's cart and pushed it straight toward that largest operating room.","There were already four or five doctors inside, all experts brought in overnight by the Li family. They were unfamiliar with the hospital staff, so when she walked in, she didn't attract anyone's attention.","Wen Yan spotted Ji Zhiyuan at a glance. He lay quietly on the operating table, his eyelashes casting fine shadows under the lights, looking as if he were asleep. But the tubes connected to his body and the red marks left by the restraint straps reminded her—","He had been brought here against his will.","The anesthesiologist was adjusting the ventilator parameters, and the chief surgeon was checking the surgical instruments with an assistant.","\"The patient's blood pressure is normal, blood oxygen is normal, and anesthesia injection has started. We can notify the chairman to come to the operating room.\"","Wen Yan's blood instantly froze.","She pretended to organize the instruments, quietly approaching the equipment, and secretly kicked out the power cord of the anesthesia machine. The monitor let out a piercing alarm.","\"What's going on?\"","\"How could we make such a rookie mistake!\"","\"The chairman will be here any minute. Don't waste time, troubleshoot the issue quickly...\"","The doctors and nurses in the operating room quickly began to inspect the equipment.","She quickly grabbed Ji Zhiyuan's hands and pinched them hard, but the man didn't react at all.","Her heart sank. She grabbed a needle from the side and secretly pricked him with force.","Ji Zhiyuan's eyes snapped open.","The operating room lights pierced his clouded consciousness like a sharp sword.","He remembered that he had been kidnapped. Where was this? Why did it look like a hospital operating table?","How did he end up here?","\"Ji Zhiyuan, don't close your eyes. Look at me,\" Wen Yan's throat felt tight. \"As long as you stay awake, the surgery won't start for now. Hold on.\"","Ji Zhiyuan's eyelids felt as heavy as lead, but he still managed to force them open to a slit.","The halo of the surgical lights diffused into a vast white fog in his eyes. Wen Yan's figure flickered faintly within it. Her eyes seemed to carry a magical power that inexplicably gave him the strength to fight to keep his eyelids open.","Meanwhile, the founder of the Li Family Hospital, Li Chunsheng, was preparing for the pre-surgery procedures."]},{"number":245,"title":"Chapter 245: The brother's camera angle seems like he's secretly taking photos","paragraphs":["Li Chunsheng had been tormented by kidney disease for many years.","As someone with top-tier medical resources, he had obtained a perfectly matched kidney through private channels in his sixties, and the surgery had been highly successful.","However, his sixties were more than thirty years ago. The medical standards back then were far inferior to today's. A few years after the surgery, his body began to show chronic rejection, requiring long-term use of immunosuppressants, which led to a weakened immune system and frequent infections.","Over the years, he had been searching for a kidney donor all over the world.","As his life was nearing its end, he finally found one.","Undergoing surgery at this age was extremely dangerous.","But if he didn't get a younger, higher-quality kidney, he wouldn't live for another three months.","Weighing his options, he decided to lie on the operating table.","The doctor was giving him a final physical examination. Once everything was normal, he would head to the operating room.","Just then, his assistant walked in briskly: \"Someone wants to see the chairman.\"","Li Chunsheng waved his hand: \"No.\"","\"But...\" The assistant offered a painting with both hands. \"This is the painting that lady asked me to pass to the chairman. She said she is an old friend of yours.\"","\"An old friend?\"","These two words made Li Chunsheng pause.","When he saw the painting, he was completely stunned. He snatched it over, his eyes fixed on the old woman under the tree in the painting, his eyes suddenly turning red.","This was his grandmother.","\"Quick, invite her in.\"","Li Chunsheng's voice trembled slightly.","Living to this age, people of his generation were long gone, let alone the generation before.","His grandmother had passed away more than seventy years ago. The river of time rolled ever forward, but he never dared to forget her voice and smile.","He had been orphaned at a young age, ignored by his clan, and raised by his grandmother.","Because he had a good memory and excelled in his studies from a young age, his grandmother exhausted her wealth to support his education. Later, due to his outstanding academic performance, he was selected by the government to study abroad.","Although the government covered the tuition and travel expenses, living expenses were a bottomless pit. His grandmother sold their ancestral home and gave him all the money.","But he was careless; the money was stolen by someone on the cruise ship going abroad.","\"Miss, please come in.\"","Li Chunsheng looked up at the person walking in, surprised to see a young girl.","He thought it might be an elderly person from his old village using this painting to identify themselves and seek his help. How could it be such a young child?","He suppressed his emotions and asked, \"What is your elder's surname?\"","Rong Yu replied calmly: \"Surname Rong.\"","She quietly shielded Ji Yanting behind her.","Ji Yanting was disguised as an old man, stooped and hunched, looking entirely inconspicuous.","No one noticed a tiny camera hidden in his collar.","The great film emperor Yan Ting had focused on acting and releasing albums since his debut, rarely appearing on variety shows, let alone hosting live streams.","The moment his account went live, his fans exploded.","\"I can't believe I get to see my idol live-streaming in my lifetime. I'm going to faint from happiness.\"","\"The great film emperor didn't even announce it before going live. And why is the camera angle so weird, shooting the floor?\"","\"Where are his manager and assistant? Why aren't they helping adjust the camera? We want to see his face, not the floor, okay?\"","Just then, a hand suddenly appeared in the frame.","It made a gesture.","\"That's the secret signal he uses at concerts to tell fans to be quiet.\"","\"He wants us to watch the live stream quietly.\"","\"This feels like it's going to be interesting.\"","\"...\"","In the office, Li Chunsheng continued to ask, \"Where did you get this painting?\"","Rong Yu stepped forward, appearing in the camera's view.","\"Oh my god, isn't that Rong Yu?\"","\"Excuse me, why is she in our idol's live stream?\"","\"During the finale of the talent show last time, Yan Ting specially wrote an award speech for her. I thought their relationship was unusual back then.\"","\"Never mind Rong Yu, don't you guys think that old man looks familiar? He looks like the founder of Li's Hospital in Hong Kong?\"","\"The founder of Li's is about to die, how could he be live-streaming!\"","\"Have you guys noticed that the camera angle looks like it's secretly filming?\"","\"...\"","\"I painted this,\" Rong Yu said, looking at the painting. \"This old lady's surname is Xiao. The villagers called her Granny Xiao. She had three sons and two daughters in her life. All three sons died on the battlefield. One daughter was stolen, and the other died of a hemorrhage during childbirth, leaving only a grandson. Granny Xiao lived frugally her whole life to support her grandson's education...\"","Li Chunsheng's eyes were filled with shock.","How did this young girl know that his grandmother's surname was Xiao? Who exactly was she?","The doctor beside him whispered a reminder, \"Chairman, it's time to go to the operating room to prepare for surgery.\"","Li Chunsheng raised his hand: \"Let them wait a bit longer.\"","He didn't know if he would make it off the operating table, so he had to figure this out while he was still alive.","\"Granny Xiao's grandson was very promising and was selected by the government to study abroad,\" Rong Yu said softly. \"The grandson returned to his home country after six years of studying abroad. When he arrived home, this was the scene: his grandmother was making shoe soles under the tree, the rooster was crowing in the tree, and she caught the only rooster to make soup to entertain two classmates who were close to her grandson...\"","Li Chunsheng was extremely shocked: \"Who are you? How do you even know this!\"","Rong Yu's lips tightened.","Because she was one of those classmates.","She and Li Chunsheng went abroad in the same batch. Li Chunsheng was young, and his living expenses had been stolen. She had never lacked money since childhood, and the Rong family had always been involved in charity, supporting countless poor students every year. She naturally began to help Li Chunsheng.","She helped Li Chunsheng for six years.","Li Chunsheng always called her sister.","The pure and kind-hearted boy who went abroad with ideals and ambitions had actually turned into a complete villain.","How could she accept this?","It was hard to accept.","Perhaps her gaze was too direct, and the figure of a girl inexplicably appeared in Li Chunsheng's mind.","That was the person who helped him the most when he was studying abroad.","This young girl's surname is Rong. Could she be a descendant of Rong Yu?","His eyes softened considerably.","However.","Rong Yu's gaze was as sharp as a knife.","\"Your grandmother exhausted her wealth and poured out her heart's blood just so you could rise from poverty and stand upright in the world!\"","\"Your classmate lent a helping hand in your time of need, only hoping that you would live up to your education and one day save the world and its people!\"","\"The country poured its resources into sending you to study abroad, and those martyrs paved the way for you with their blood, only hoping that you would become a pillar of society and serve this great nation of China!\"","\"But what about you?\" Her voice was like a cold blade drawn from its sheath, every word piercing his heart. \"How are you repaying them? How can you face your conscience?\"","\"You are a medical student—your hands were meant to save lives, not to be stained with blood!\"","\"Your knowledge was meant to heal the world, not to become a butcher's knife!\"","\"You've done so many things that betray humanity. Who exactly have you done right by?\""]},{"number":246,"title":"Chapter 246: Do you think you can threaten me with just these documents","paragraphs":["The live stream was boiling over.","\"Is this Rong Yu? What on earth is she talking about?\"","\"The person in front of her should be Li Chunsheng, the founder of the Li Corporation, right? The appearance matches, and so does the background.\"","\"But the founder of Li Hospital is a famous philanthropist. He started doing charity thirty or forty years ago and has saved many sick children and teenagers. A few years ago, when he was in good health, he often participated in various charity donation events. How could such a kind person be the bloodstained villain Rong Yu is talking about!\"","\"Maybe they are filming a movie. Otherwise, how do you explain Yan Ting and Rong Yu appearing in the same place at the same time?\"","\"If they're filming, why isn't my idol showing his face? It's not fair!\"","\"...\"","Yan Ting's account had over a hundred million followers. As soon as the broadcast started, the number of viewers instantly reached a hundred thousand and continued to increase.","Furthermore, this live stream was a bit strange. It was shot from a hidden camera perspective, and the main character was Rong Yu. With her angry reprimands and questioning, the number of viewers climbed steadily, unexpectedly breaking through the one million mark and even making it onto the real-time trending search list.","In the live stream, Li Chunsheng's face was deathly pale.","He was already old and riddled with illnesses. Hit by this continuous questioning, he nearly collapsed and slumped into his chair.","The assistant beside him angrily rebuked, \"The founding purpose of Li Hospital is to practice medicine and help the people. Although it is a private hospital, it spends hundreds of millions on charity every year. Over the past few decades, more than a hundred thousand people have been saved by Li Hospital. What you are saying are baseless accusations; it's rumor-mongering and slander!\"","\"Baseless accusations?\"","Rong Yu smiled.","She raised her hand and threw a stack of documents onto the desk.","\"Director Li, do you still remember that kidney transplant surgery from three months ago?\" Her voice was very light. \"The patient, Zhang Meiling, died under mysterious circumstances three days after the surgery. Her family didn't even get to see her body.\"","Without waiting for Li Chunsheng to speak, she turned a page and continued, \"Four months ago, a young patient, Li Qian, was admitted for treatment. When she was discharged, she was missing a kidney, and at the same time, a certain wealthy man received a kidney donor.\"","\"Five months ago...\"","Rong Yu's words left everyone in the live stream completely stunned.","\"What era is it that such black-hearted hospitals still exist? Is this something that should happen in modern society? Hell is empty, and the devils are here on earth!\"","\"The patients who go to Li Hospital are there to save their lives. I didn't expect them to be targeted for their body parts. That's too terrifying!\"","\"Isn't the founder of Li Hospital a great philanthropist? Why would he do such a thing? It's surreal!\"","\"I vaguely remember that three months ago, Zhang Meiling's family made a fuss on the internet, but they disappeared after two days. At the time, netizens said the family just wanted to extort money. Thinking back now, it's truly terrifying.\"","\"Isn't it too hasty to convict Chairman Li based solely on Rong Yu's one-sided story?\"","\"Hasty my foot! My idol Yan Ting personally went into the field to secretly film and gather evidence. This shows the matter is already set in stone. Otherwise, why would two public figures do something so risky?\"","\"...\"","\"Framing, this is a naked frame-up!\" Li Chunsheng stared intently at the young woman in front of him. \"Where did you get these things? Who exactly are you?\"","Rong Yu lowered her brows.","These things were forged documents she had created based on the recent negative news about Li Hospital on the internet.","Yes, they were forged.","If she had solid evidence, she would have reported it to the police long ago, instead of having A-Yan start a live stream to borrow the power of public opinion.","\"Although these negative news stories about your hospital have all been suppressed,\" she spoke slowly, \"as long as they happened, they will definitely be found out. Did you think you could hide them for a lifetime?\"","\"What a bold young person.\" Li Chunsheng laughed out of anger. \"You even dare to investigate the Li Group, and you dare to come see me single-handedly. No matter whose junior you are, I must praise you for your courage. Men, clean this up!\"","The heavy solid wood door was violently smashed open, and four armed bodyguards in black rushed in. The leader, Scarface, grabbed Rong Yu by the shoulder.","Rong Yu did not struggle. A smile appeared on the corner of her lips. \"Clean me up, just like how you handled those missing patients?\"","Li Chunsheng looked at her coldly. \"Do you think you can threaten me with just these documents? How much tax revenue does Li Hospital generate for Hong Kong City every year? How many wealthy and powerful people has it saved? Do you think that with this painting, I would sit down and negotiate with you, and be threatened by you? You are too naive. Do it!\"","At his command, the four men in black immediately made their move.","The people in the live stream couldn't sit still anymore.","\"This isn't freaking acting; someone is really going to get killed!\"","\"Do you guys remember, about five or six years ago, a reporter went undercover at Li Hospital and ended up missing. Could they have been silenced?\"","\"It wasn't just this doctor who went missing, but also a female nurse who reported Li Hospital's crimes under her real name, but she was quickly dealt with. Who knows if that nurse is still alive now.\"","\"There is actually quite a lot of negative news about Li Hospital, but Li Chunsheng's image is too perfect, and he has indeed saved many people, which covered all of this up.\"","\"Since Rong Yu dared to provoke Li Chunsheng to his face, she's dead for sure. She's definitely going to lose her life here...\"","\"Why is the camera suddenly shaking? I can't see anything clearly...\"","\"Oh my god, it's Yan Ting rushing forward. My idol is so brave...\"","Ji Yan Ting blocked Rong Yu.","The miniature camera fell to the ground, capturing his face perfectly. The four bodyguards punched him right in the face, and his mask was knocked off.","A handsome face filled the entire live stream.","Punch after punch landed, hitting flesh with every blow, and Ji Yan Ting screamed incessantly.","\"Too much, these people are going too far. My idol's face is going to be ruined.\"","\"Are there any fans in Hong Kong City? Can you call the police? If this continues, Yan Ting will die at the hands of these people!\"","\"I called the Hong Kong City police ten minutes ago. I don't know if they will dispatch anyone.\"","\"Eighty percent of the wealthy people in Hong Kong City have had shady medical procedures done at Li Hospital. The Li family has many protective walls. Without evidence, they definitely won't dispatch the police.\"","\"What do we do, what do we do? My idol is throwing up blood, he's dying...\"","\"What's the use of feeling sorry for him? Hurry up and push the trending searches. Once it trends, it will catch the country's attention in a short time. In front of the state, any Li family or Zhou family are just ghosts and monsters. Push the trending searches, hurry up everyone...\"","Yan Ting's fans spanned a huge age range, from their forties and fifties down to teenagers.","Plus Rong Yu's fans.","And a large group of clueless passersby.","Tens of thousands, hundreds of thousands, even hundreds of thousands of people joined in at the same time. The top ten trending searches on all major platforms were entirely occupied...","Ji Yan Ting spat out three mouthfuls of blood in a row, looking extremely miserable.","Rong Yu rested her hands on the desk, speaking word by word: \"Since I dared to charge into the Li headquarters, you should have guessed that I still have something to rely on...\"","Li Chunsheng narrowed his eyes, pulled open a drawer, and pressed a gun against Rong Yu's forehead: \"Whose person are you? Who sent you? Tell the truth, or else—\"","Rong Yu's face was cold and grim.","This gun was the ironclad evidence.","Convicting the Li Family Hospital was proving to be far too difficult. By starting with the illegal possession of firearms and detaining the primary person in charge first, the investigation would become much easier.","Click...","Li Chunsheng pulled the trigger.","Bang!","The office door burst open."]},{"number":247,"title":"Chapter 247: Do you know who I am, to dare give such an order","paragraphs":["Police! Right here!","Old Master Ji, leaning on his cane, led four police officers as they burst through the door.","He originally did not need to use a cane anymore, but with his eldest son in trouble, his second son acting as bait, and his mother facing Li Chunsheng head-on... three of his closest family members were in immense danger. His mind and body were on the verge of collapse, making the cane a necessity to keep his legs from giving out.","Still, when he saw Ji Yanting collapsed on the floor, his heart uncontrollably skipped a beat.","The captain leading the squad stepped forward. So this is Chairman Li's office. May I ask what exactly is going on here?","This patient was emotionally unstable and showed aggressive tendencies. My bodyguards took action, which was indeed our fault. Li Chunsheng had regained his refined demeanor. Medical expenses, nutrition fees, compensation for mental distress, and lost wages—Li's Hospital will take full responsibility for all of it.","The captain looked at Old Master Ji. The other party is willing to take full responsibility. We can close the case like this, assuming neither side has any objections?","Close the case? So hastily? Rong Yu suddenly raised her hand, grabbed Li Chunsheng's right arm, and yanked it upward. She snatched the gun he was trying to hide and slammed it onto the desk. Illegal possession of a firearm. Are the police just going to ignore this?","It is just a toy gun, Li Chunsheng said calmly. You can inspect it right now.","Li Chunsheng sat in his chair, his expression serene.","He had navigated the turbulent waters of Harbor City for decades. Whether in the underworld or legitimate society, among officials or civilians, he had connections everywhere. Trying to convict him over such a little thing was a joke.","With just a single look from him, would these people dare to escalate the matter?","If he said it was a toy gun, then this thing could only be a toy gun.","As for this little girl...","Li Chunsheng's eyes turned icy. No matter who she was, he would dispose of her cleanly before the surgery. He absolutely would not leave any loose ends.","The expressions of the police officers froze.","As professionals, they could tell at a glance that this was the real deal, not a toy gun at all.","But...","Li Chunsheng was a top-tier figure in Harbor City. If he had powerful protectors above...","Just then, the captain's phone suddenly began to vibrate.","He glanced at the caller ID, and his expression drastically changed. He immediately answered, Yes, sir! Understood!","After hanging up, the captain's attitude shifted instantly. He barked an order: Cuff Li Chunsheng!","Li Chunsheng's face stiffened. Do you know who I am? How dare you give such an order?","I just received instructions from my superiors, the captain said coldly. The founder and chairman of Li's Hospital is in illegal possession of a firearm and is suspected of multiple cases of illegal organ trafficking and intentional homicide. Please come down to the station to cooperate with the investigation!","Li Chunsheng outright laughed. Have your Chief Wang come over. Ask him if he dares to arrest me.","His arrogant demeanor infuriated the viewers in the live stream.","Holy shit, this old bastard is so arrogant. Imagine how rampant he is behind the scenes! Truly, a scourge lasts a thousand years!","See that? This is the true face of the upper class!","Weren't people just praising Li's Charity Hospital? I suggest tying Li Chunsheng to an operating table so he can experience what his victims felt.","If Chief Wang really comes, does that mean this great demon will escape investigation?","Is there no one who can do something about this?","...","The captain enunciated every word: It was the Central Government of China that ordered the Harbor City government to arrest you!","Li Chunsheng was suddenly stunned. The Central Government? Why would the Central Government intervene in Harbor City's affairs?","Rong Yu sneered.","This was the reason she had brought A-Yan here.","A-Yan had debuted in his teens and struggled in the entertainment industry for over a decade, accumulating hundreds of millions of fans.","How could these fans tolerate their idol being so violently beaten? Naturally, they would fight tooth and nail to push the incident to the top of the trending topics, drawing official attention.","There is strength in numbers.","As long as the Central Government noticed the live stream, everything else would fall into place.","Everything had gone much smoother than she imagined.","It was just that... A-Yan had suffered quite a bit.","But Yuan was still in the operating room, and his situation was unknown. Compared to that, getting beaten up like this was nothing.","Take him away!","The captain gave a stern order, and silver handcuffs were snapped onto Li Chunsheng's wrists.","The live stream erupted in jubilation.","Thank goodness, the Central Government stepped in. Our brother is saved.","No, it is not just our brother who is saved. It is that all the victims can finally get justice. All the ordinary people targeted by capital have been saved.","I suggest investigating those wealthy tycoons who miraculously recovered. This case absolutely cannot end here!","...","At that moment, Ji Yanting wiped the blood from the corner of his mouth, picked up the camera, faced the millions of viewers, and spoke softly: It is just some superficial wounds. I am fine.","Thank you to my fans, and thank you to every passerby who paid attention to this matter. Because of every soul behind the screen who refused to remain silent, the sound of your typing keyboards converged into the thunderclap of this very moment.","From now on, when the dark hands of capital reach for the weak again, please always remember today—remember how millions of ordinary people wove a net of justice with their attention, leaving evil with nowhere to hide.","Thank you all once again. The live stream ends here.","The live stream was turned off, but the news regarding this incident only intensified on the internet.","Many victims' families stepped forward. Weibo posts containing victims' statements were pushed to the top of the trending lists one by one. The Central Government immediately formed an investigation team and dispatched them to Harbor City...","Li's Hospital was shut down.","The Li family's power began to crumble.","When Rong Yu and Old Master Ji supported Ji Yanting to the doorway, they saw Ji Zhiyuan being wheeled out by Wen Yan and a few staff members.","Wen Yan's face was full of smiles. Do not worry, President Ji was only injected with anesthesia. He will be fine after a good sleep.","The taut strings of Old Master Ji's heart immediately relaxed.","He grabbed Rong Yu's hand, his eyes red, and said in a low voice, Mom, it is all my fault. If I hadn't insisted on getting the injection, Yuan wouldn't have suffered all this, and A-Yan wouldn't have been beaten up like this. It is all my fault...","Rong Yu rubbed his hair. Yingbao, you should think about it this way: if we hadn't happened to get involved in this, who knows how many more ordinary people would have fallen victim to their vicious hands.","Illegal organ trafficking was only one aspect.","The second was that life-extending drug. From the limited information she had found, this drug was highly likely extracted from certain cells in the bodies of minors, dealing a devastating blow to the children's bodies... This also explained why, for so many years, Li's Hospital had treated countless children for free...","Thinking of Li Chunsheng, Rong Yu's lips turned a bit pale.","If she hadn't helped Li Chunsheng financially back then, perhaps so many people wouldn't have been victimized.","But life doesn't allow for so many regrets.","Besides, even if time flowed backward, she probably still would have made the same choice.","It wasn't that she was wrong.","It was Li Chunsheng who had taken the wrong path.","She spoke up, The meaning of life lies not in its length, but in its breadth. Rather than spending thirty million dollars on that drug, it would be better to donate it. What do you think?","Old Master Ji nodded profusely. I will handle this matter personally."]},{"number":248,"title":"Chapter 248: He actually didn't even recognize his own ex-wife.","paragraphs":["Ji Zhiyuan had been trapped in a hazy state of semi-consciousness.","In his subconscious, there seemed to always be a voice encouraging him, telling him not to fall asleep, not to give up.","His eyelids twitched, and he finally opened his eyes.","The blinding white light forced him to close them again.","\"President Ji, are you awake?\"","A gentle female voice sounded, exactly the same as the voice in his subconscious.","Ji Zhiyuan slowly opened his eyes and met Wen Yan's gaze. \"Doctor Wen?\"","Wen Yan smiled and said, \"It is good that you are awake. Old Master Ji and Miss Rong accompanied Second Young Master Ji to get his injuries treated. They will be over in a moment.\"","The memories of the operating room slowly flooded back.","At that time, he was like a fish on a chopping block, entirely at the mercy of others.","If she had not appeared, he probably would have been cut open, his life or death uncertain...","\"Thank you, Doctor Wen,\" Ji Zhiyuan said, his voice hoarse. \"When we return to Haicheng, I will definitely visit you to express my gratitude in person.\"","His dark eyes looked at her quietly.","Perhaps his gaze was too intense, giving Wen Yan a sudden illusion that they had known each other for a long time.","She quickly averted her eyes.","Right then, her phone vibrated. As if to avoid the awkwardness, she quickly answered the video call. \"Brother, what is it?\"","On the screen was the face of a mature man, his brow slightly furrowed. \"I saw the news. Something major happened at Li's Hospital, and many medical staff were arrested. I remember you were attending a seminar there these past few days. You weren't caught up in it, were you?\"","\"I am an outsider, so I won't be involved. Don't worry, brother.\" Wen Yan chatted about a few other things before hanging up.","She turned her head and met Ji Zhiyuan's gaze once again.","She saw that his deep black eyes seemed to be churning with stormy waves, staring at her fixedly and unblinkingly.","\"President Ji, what is wrong?\"","Wen Yan touched her face, thinking there was something on it.","Ji Zhiyuan slowly steadied his breathing, trying his best to maintain a normal tone. \"The person you were just talking to... is he your biological brother, sharing the same father and mother?\"","Wen Yan nodded. \"My parents divorced, and my father started a new family. My mother passed away early. My brother played the role of both father and mother to raise me. He always feels like I am still a child and worries that something might happen to me...\"","Ji Zhiyuan's entire body trembled. He asked softly, \"What is your brother's name?\"","\"Why do you ask, President Ji?\" Wen Yan looked at him. \"My brother's name is Ke Yan. Do you know him?\"","\"Ke Yan...\"","Ji Zhiyuan murmured through his lips.","His ex-wife was named Ke Man.","At his and Ke Man's wedding, Ke Yan had appeared. That was the first time he met Ke Yan. The second time was on the day Duoduo was born.","Ke Man had a difficult labor and suffered a sudden amniotic fluid embolism... Later, the doctor informed him that Ke Man had died.","Ke Yan, acting as her biological brother, took Ke Man's body away and buried her in their hometown cemetery, laying her to rest beside her relatives.","Every year during the Tomb-Sweeping Festival, he would take Duoduo to her hometown so Duoduo could pay respects to her deceased mother.","He thought Ke Man had died long ago.","Why had she changed her name and returned to his and Duoduo's side?","Ji Zhiyuan rubbed his temples.","He always remembered his first meeting with Ke Man. It was at a cocktail party. He had drank too much and was taken to a hotel suite. When he woke up, there was a woman beside him, and that was Ke Man.","Driven by his family's upbringing and his own character, he took on the responsibility a man should bear. He and Ke Man walked down the aisle into marriage.","That night had left Ke Man pregnant.","Ke Man's figure was originally plump, and after getting pregnant, she grew heavier day by day... But the Wen Yan in front of him was very thin, too thin, probably weighing less than ninety pounds.","Although there was a difference in their builds, this face was undeniably Ke Man's face.","No wonder he always found her familiar...","He actually could not even recognize his own ex-wife...","\"President Ji, why are you looking at me like that?\"","Wen Yan felt a chill all over her body and had the urge to run out the door.","\"Doctor Wen, can you help me sit up?\" Ji Zhiyuan's voice was tinged with hoarseness. \"It is a bit tiring to lie down.\"","Wen Yan hesitated for a moment but still walked over, holding his arm and helping him sit up against the hospital bed.","Looking at her from a close distance, Ji Zhiyuan saw a tiny red mole behind her earlobe. He raised his hand, picked two strands of hair off her back, and quietly hid them in his sleeve.","At this moment.","Ji Yanting finished having his injuries treated and came over together with Rong Yu and Old Master Ji.","Wen Yan took a step back, distancing herself a few paces from Ji Zhiyuan. \"Old Master Ji, Miss Rong, I have some personal matters to attend to, so I will take my leave first.\"","\"Doctor Wen, thank you so much,\" Old Master Ji said. \"When we return to Haicheng, please make sure to come to the Ji family for a meal.\"","Wen Yan smiled and agreed.","Rong Yu observed Ji Zhiyuan's condition. Seeing that it wasn't a major issue, she finally breathed a sigh of relief.","Only then did she have the time to take out her phone. It had already blown up with various messages and calls. Just as she was about to check them, a call came in. It was Sheng Ciyuan.","\"Rong Yu, I suddenly couldn't find you at the banquet last night. I thought you had headed back to Haicheng early, so I rushed back to the capital overnight.\" Sheng Ciyuan's voice carried a hint of frustration. \"How are things now? Are you alright? Will you get dragged into this?\"","\"The central authorities are investigating. I won't get involved,\" Rong Yu said. \"I will give my statement in a bit, and then I will be ready to return to Haicheng.\"","\"That is good.\" Sheng Ciyuan said hesitantly, \"My older brother saw the news and insisted on going to find you. Do you think it would be convenient for me to bring my brother to Haicheng to meet you?\"","Rong Yu remained silent for a while before saying, \"That is fine.\"","Not long after, the police arrived and had them each give their statements. This matter was considered temporarily settled for now.","The family set off to return to Haicheng.","As soon as they arrived at the airport, they ran into Rong Wangtian, who was waiting there.","He looked at Rong Yu walking over, feeling a sense of shared pride.","She was so intelligent and so brave.","Once again, his understanding of this daughter had been refreshed.","\"Little Yu!\" Rong Wangtian went up to greet her. \"Are you alright?\"","Old Master Ji grasped his hand. \"Thank you for the help you provided, President Rong. As it happens, the Ji Group has a project. If you are interested, President Rong, you can come to the Ji Group headquarters tomorrow to have a good talk with my eldest grandson.\"","Ji Zhiyuan spoke up, \"We will quietly await your arrival, President Rong.\"","Rong Wangtian was a bit stunned.","This was the very first time the Ji family had been so amiable and pleasant to him.","Was it just because he accompanied Little Yu to the police station to file a report?","But he hadn't done it to secure a collaboration with the Ji family.","However, the collaboration was being delivered right to his doorstep... If he could reach a stable partnership with the Ji Group, the Rong family would reach a new height and truly join the ranks of the wealthy families in Haicheng.","Rong Wangtian opened his mouth, wanting to agree, but he was afraid of appearing too opportunistic.","But such a good opportunity...","He struggled with himself for quite a while before finally saying, \"Then, thank you, President Ji.\"","Rong Yu showed no emotion on her face and boarded the plane along with the flow of passengers.","The Ji family followed her inside.","Rong Wangtian scratched his head.","Why did he feel like he shouldn't have agreed?"]},{"number":249,"title":"Chapter 249: She can travel through time, but what about Ji Zheng","paragraphs":["The plane skimmed across the clouds.","Rong Wangtian originally wanted to invite Rong Yu back to the Rong family for a meal. She was clearly his daughter, his own flesh and blood, yet in front of the Ji family, he felt more like an outsider.","While he hesitated, Rong Yu had already gotten into the Ji family's car.","The person who came to pick her up was Ji Jingchuan.","As he drove, he said, \"Old Master, Great-grandmother, we have guests at home. It's the Sheng family from the capital. They arrived not too long ago.\"","Old Master Ji's wrinkled face showed his displeasure.","That eldest young master of the Sheng family was too impolite. He always stared straight at his mother, which made him very unhappy.","As for the previous Mr. Min Jianshen, although he also looked down on him, at least the man was normal. If his mother were to date Min Jianshen, he could force himself to accept it.","But this Eldest Young Master Sheng... to put it nicely, he was autistic; to put it harshly, he just wasn't normal... Impolite, ignorant, and always getting handsy. Just looking at him was annoying.","Old Master Ji twitched his mouth, wanting to voice his opinion.","But thinking about the massive disaster he had caused, almost getting A-Yuan killed... a person who made a mistake had to be well-behaved for a few days before acting up again.","He obediently shut his mouth.","The car soon arrived at the Furong Manor.","Before Rong Yu could get out, Ji Zhouye quickly came over to open the door, bending down to whisper, \"Great-grandmother, this guy surnamed Sheng is too weird...\"","He was extremely displeased with this Eldest Young Master Sheng.","From the moment he entered the Ji family's gates until now, that man had been walking around with his big, dark eyes wide open, looking everywhere. One moment he was touching a big tree, the next he was touching the wall, and just now, he even touched his face.","In all his life, it was the first time an irrelevant man had touched his face.","This feeling was truly uncomfortable.","Fortunately, the man didn't stare at him for too long. He turned around and started playing with Duoduo, lifting Duoduo high in the air and giving her a piggyback ride, instantly capturing Duoduo's heart.","Rong Yu got out of the car and looked toward the lawn.","Under the setting sun, Sheng Qingyan picked up Duoduo, tossed her forcefully into the air, and then caught her accurately. Duoduo giggled, but the bystanders were so scared their hearts almost jumped out of their throats.","Especially Old Master Ji, the old man cried out, \"Hey you, put Duoduo down, don't drop the child!\"","Sheng Ciyuan, who was recording a video, put away his phone and walked over. \"Don't worry, Old Mr. Ji. My eldest brother knows what he's doing. He used to attend a military academy, and his physical fitness was ranked first every year—first by a wide margin, at that. Duoduo's weight is nothing to him.\"","Rong Yu asked, \"He went to a military academy?\"","\"Although my brother has autism, his learning ability is not low. He taught himself from a young age, got into middle school, high school, and successfully enrolled in the Capital Military Academy.\" Sheng Ciyuan's face carried a look of pride. \"If his communication skills weren't limited, he would be an excellent military officer by now.\"","Ji Zhouye's face was full of disbelief. \"Him? He got into the Capital Military Academy?\"","That was a prestigious university, with an admission score around 650 points.","Could such an abnormal person get such a high score on the college entrance exam?","Sheng Qingyan noticed that Rong Yu had returned. He put Duoduo down and quickly jogged over. He probably wanted to stand close to Rong Yu.","But Old Master Ji was on Rong Yu's left, and Ji Zhouye was on her right. There was no empty space.","So he rubbed up against Ji Zhouye.","Ji Zhouye's scalp instantly went numb, and goosebumps rose on his skin. He rubbed his arms and quickly ran away.","\"A-Yu.\"","Sheng Qingyan nudged closer to Rong Yu and called out softly.","Old Master Ji immediately bristled. \"A-Yu my foot! Is that a name you can call her? Either call her Miss Rong, or respectfully call her by her full name!\"","Only people of Uncle Tang's generation could call her A-Yu.","\"A-Yu.\"","Sheng Qingyan called out again.","As if deliberately going against Old Master Ji.","Old Master Ji glared at him. \"Are you provoking me? You, a junior, actually dare to provoke an old man like me?\"","\"Alright, Yingbao,\" Rong Yu said, feeling very helpless. \"I'm hungry. Go tell the butler to set the table.\"","Old Master Ji walked away in a huff.","Sheng Ciyuan looked embarrassed. He pulled Sheng Qingyan and whispered, \"Brother, you've seen Rong Yu now. We should go home, okay?\"","Sheng Qingyan's thin lips were pressed tightly together.","He widened his eyes, looking at Rong Yu. The emotion in his gaze could be easily read by anyone.","Rong Yu spoke up, \"Since you're here, have a simple meal with us first.\"","The group sat down in the dining room.","Because there were guests and many people, they switched to the Western-style dining room with a long table. Rong Yu always sat at the head of the table. Old Master Ji and Ji Zhiyuan sat below her, and the other juniors sat further down one by one.","Sheng Ciyuan was terrified that his brother would be impolite again and face rejection, so he gripped Sheng Qingyan's arm tightly with both hands.","Until Old Master Ji spoke up: \"Why are you still standing there like idiots? Do I have to beg you to sit?\"","Sheng Ciyuan hurriedly pulled his brother down to sit.","\"Student Sheng, don't be so constrained,\" Rong Yu said. \"I know about your brother's condition. You shouldn't always feel embarrassed or apologetic.\"","Sheng Ciyuan actually had many question marks in his heart.","For example, this was the Ji family, so why did Rong Yu live here year-round?","For example, why did Rong Yu sit in the elder's seat at the Ji family's dining table?","Or, for example, why did everyone else in the Ji family wait for Rong Yu to pick up her chopsticks before they started eating...","However, every place had its own customs, and it wasn't his place to ask about other people's family matters. He just silently lowered his head to eat, occasionally picking up some food for Sheng Qingyan.","Fortunately, the meal went very smoothly.","After the meal, Old Master Ji asked calmly, \"Second Young Master Sheng, do you need me to arrange a driver to take you back?\"","The intention to see the guests off was very obvious.","Sheng Ciyuan also planned to take his leave.","Although his brother seemed more and more like a normal person here, this was ultimately not the Sheng family. Staying too long would cause resentment, and it would be difficult to come back in the future.","But at this moment, Rong Yu suddenly spoke up: \"Student Sheng, you and your brother sit for a little while. I'm going to get something for your brother to look at.\"","She went upstairs to her vanity and took out a small box. Inside were all her past belongings, mainly photos and letters. After thinking for a moment, she took out an excellently preserved pocket watch from the drawer and brought it downstairs with her.","As soon as he saw the photos in her hand, Sheng Qingyan's expression changed.","Especially when he saw the scene of her and Ji Zheng holding hands and walking into the church to get married, his breathing suddenly became rapid.","Rong Yu's eyes trembled with shock.","This person, from the time he was sensible enough to understand things, had been collecting the belongings of those overseas students. Especially the photos and anecdotes about her, he had kept every single one.","She wondered if, somewhere in the unseen world, a subconscious force was telling him that he was connected to these overseas students, making him collect them out of pure instinct...","His instinct wasn't just limited to collecting photos.","It was also in his inexplicable affection for her.","And in his natural closeness to everyone in the Ji family...","She could time-travel here.","Then, what about Ji Zheng?","Rong Yu picked up the pocket watch and handed it over: \"Take a look at this too?\"","The pocket watch, adorned with an intertwining peony motif, remained perfectly intact even after nearly a century. Its hands still ticked steadily. When opened, the upper lid revealed an engraving made by a military saber: Ji Zheng, Rong Yu.","This was the token of love Ji Zheng had given her all those years ago.","There had been two identical pocket watches—one for her, and one for Ji Zheng.","\"Ji... Ji Zheng...\"","Sheng Qingyan's voice was terribly hoarse, grating like a stone scraping against glass.","His fingers traced the pocket watch. Suddenly, his eyes rolled back in his head, and he collapsed straight to the ground."]},{"number":250,"title":"Chapter 250: I May Die, But There Will Be Thousands More Like Me","paragraphs":["Thump—","Before anyone could react, Sheng Qingyan unexpectedly collapsed to the ground.","Old Master Ji was stunned for a moment, his mouth moving faster than his brain: \"Could he be faking a fall just to stay at our Ji family home for the night?\"","\"Brother, brother, don't scare me.\" Sheng Ciyuan's face instantly turned pale. \"Brother, wake up, wake up...\"","Judging by his voice, he was on the verge of tears.","\"A-Yuan, quickly call the private doctor over,\" Rong Yu said rapidly. \"A-Yan, A-Ye, you two help get Sheng Qingyan onto a bed.\"","Old Master Ji did not actually hate Sheng Qingyan.","He just did not quite like how clingy this guy was to his mother.","At this moment, the clingy person was lying there motionless, looking extremely pitiful.","He subconsciously spoke up, \"Put him on my bed. My room is fully equipped with medical devices, so it will be more convenient to examine him.\"","Old Master Ji's bedroom was on the first floor. It was very spacious, with many medical instruments placed by the bedside.","The private doctor quickly arrived and examined Sheng Qingyan. \"All his vitals are normal. It's nothing serious; he's probably just too exhausted. A good night's sleep will fix it.\"","Rong Yu asked Sheng Ciyuan, \"Has your brother ever had a situation like this before?\"","\"Yes.\" Sheng Ciyuan scratched his head. \"When he was studying, my brother would sometimes stay up for three days and nights reading, eventually passing out in the study...\"","Rong Yu nodded. \"Then you two can stay the night at the Ji house.\"","Sheng Ciyuan did not dare to agree immediately and glanced at Old Master Ji.","Old Master Ji curled his lips. \"The Ji family home is huge. If you want to stay, then stay. But agreed, just for one night.\"","\"Thank you, Old Mr. Ji, and thank you, Rong Yu,\" Sheng Ciyuan said. \"I'll go call my grandmother first to let her know, so she won't worry.\"","He went out to make the call.","Rong Yu turned to look at her elderly son. \"Has anyone else ever lain on this bed of yours besides Sheng Qingyan?\"","Old Master Ji's face suddenly turned red. \"Mom, why are you asking this? It's quite embarrassing... This was the bridal chamber for me and my wife. What do you think?\"","Rong Yu: \"...\"","She really was... inexplicably force-fed a mouthful of expired romantic sweetness.","She was just thinking that a bed, for the vast majority of people, was a very private item. Most people would not let an outsider lie in the bed they slept in.","Yet Yingbao naturally offered to let Sheng Qingyan, who was practically a stranger, sleep in his bed.","Did this mean that deep down, Yingbao was actually not averse to Sheng Qingyan?","Just like she was?","Could he be that person?","Rong Yu harbored a glimmer of hope.","However, his situation was completely different from hers.","Was she overthinking it?","That night, braving Old Master Ji's murderous glare, Sheng Ciyuan insisted on sleeping in the same bed as his older brother...","Old Master Ji could only huffily sleep in the guest room.","Perhaps what one thinks about by day becomes one's dreams by night. That evening, as soon as Rong Yu fell into a deep slumber, the man she yearned for day and night appeared before her eyes.","\"A-Yu.\" His gaze was so gentle. \"I am going on a mission. If I do not return in a year's time, I will probably never come back. Do not wait for me.\"","He took out two pocket watches.","One for her, engraved with: Ji Zheng, Rong Yu.","One for him, engraved with: Rong Yu, Ji Zheng.","This time, he came back safely from his mission.","But on the cruise ship returning to their home country, he sacrificed his life.","The moment he died, he was clutching the pocket watch in his hand.","\"A-Yu, I'm sorry.\" His voice was very light. \"A-Yu, I know the journey home is difficult, but you are a military spouse. From now on, it all depends on you... Cough, cough. Please take our child, take these intellectuals, and make sure you safely return to our country to strengthen our China...\"","\"Though I die, there will be millions more like me. Our motherland will surely grow strong. Only the motherland can be the greatest shelter for you and our child...\"","\"Ji Zheng...\"","Rong Yu murmured aloud in her dream and suddenly opened her eyes.","The sky was already growing faintly light.","She saw a person standing by the bed. It was Sheng Qingyan.","When did this person sneak into her room without her realizing it at all?","Rong Yu sat up. \"What are you doing in my room?\"","Sheng Qingyan bent down, bringing his face a bit closer to hers. He spoke, \"Looking, at you.\"","Rong Yu met his gaze. \"Why are you looking at me?\"","\"Dream...\" He probably did not know how to express it. His lips parted and closed, closed and parted, before he managed with difficulty, \"Dreamt, of you.\"","Rong Yu was startled.","He had a dream too?","Was it the same dream as hers?","She asked him, \"Was there a ship in your dream, a very, very big ship?\"","Sheng Qingyan shook his head.","Just as he did, Sheng Ciyuan's panicked shouts suddenly came from outside the door: \"Oh no, my brother is missing! Brother, where are you? Brother, where did you go?\"","\"So noisy first thing in the morning.\" Old Master Ji's voice immediately followed. \"He's a grown man, it's not like he could just vanish. Old Yu, quickly arrange for people to search around.\"","A servant whispered, \"Old Master, I saw the eldest young master of the Sheng family go upstairs. It seemed, it seemed like he went... went to Miss Rong's room.\"","Old Master Ji's eyes suddenly widened. \"Damn it, why didn't you say so earlier? Why didn't you say so earlier!\"","He dashed up to the second floor in one breath and, using his octogenarian body, burst open the door to Rong Yu's room.","Inside, he saw his mother sitting on the bed and Sheng Qingyan standing beside it. The faint morning light from the window spilled in, coating their figures in a soft, beautiful glow. This scene felt like a dream, incredibly unreal and illusory, leaving Old Master Ji frozen in place.","He was actually afraid of shattering this dreamlike scene.","\"Brother!\"","Sheng Ciyuan felt his head splitting with a headache.","God knows how devastated he felt the moment he woke up in the morning and saw his brother was not beside him.","He was afraid his brother had gone missing.","He was also afraid his brother would wander around the Ji family home.","Sure enough...","\"Brother, brother, what are you doing here?\" Sheng Ciyuan hurriedly rushed in. \"This, this, this is a girl's room. Men and women should keep their distance. You can't just casually enter someone else's room. It's impolite, truly very impolite...\"","He bowed to Rong Yu. \"I'm sorry, I'm truly sorry. My brother doesn't understand these things. I will slowly teach him, and this definitely won't happen again in the future...\"","Rong Yu smiled and spoke, \"Student Sheng, why are you always apologizing?\"","Sheng Ciyuan lowered his head.","Actually, before meeting Rong Yu, his brother was very normal. When he took him out to attend classes, eat, or shop, his brother would stay by his side very obediently, and he never had to worry about anything else.","But now...","Truly, he was only surviving on thick skin; otherwise, he would have loved to dig a hole and hide in it.","Rong Yu stood up. \"It's fine, I don't mind.\"","\"How can you not mind!\" Old Master Ji said huffily. \"A grown man entering a girl's room early in the morning is a huge deal. Although it's excusable since he's sick, we can't encourage his arrogance, otherwise...\"","He was halfway through his sentence.","Sheng Qingyan suddenly took something out of his pocket and handed it to Old Master Ji, his voice raspy: \"For you. Don't be angry anymore.\"","It was a grasshopper woven from grass leaves, brightly colored and incredibly lifelike."]},{"number":251,"title":"Chapter 251: Sheng Qingyan, That Is Ji Zheng","paragraphs":["Old Master Ji froze for a moment.","This person actually gave him a small woven grass trinket. Wasn't this something used to coax children?","He was already in his seventies or eighties; he had absolutely no interest in such things.","Just as he was about to speak, he froze again.","This thing looked a bit familiar... His memory was instantly pulled back to seventy years ago. At that time, he was only eight years old. His mother was busy with work, and whenever he threw a childish tantrum, she would pluck a few blades of grass and weave a little trinket to coax him. Flowers, birds, fish, insects—his mother could make anything.","He seemed to remember his mother saying that his father had taught her.","How did this Eldest Young Master Sheng know how to do it too?","While he was still deep in thought, Rong Yu's hand had already picked up the lifelike grasshopper.","She directly dismantled it.","The three people in the room had no idea what she was doing, but they all watched obediently without saying a word.","Rong Yu's fingers traced the familiar creases and patterns. That was a weaving technique uniquely created by Ji Zheng. A tremor went through the tip of her heart.","...Sheng Qingyan was Ji Zheng.","It wasn't time travel; it should be reincarnation. He was missing a piece of his soul, which was why he had become like this now.","Mom, Mom...","Seeing her eyes glaze over and her fingers tremble, Old Master Ji hurriedly called out to her in a low voice and shook her shoulder.","Rong Yu snapped back to reality.","She knew this idea was absurd.","However, even she existed, so why couldn't Ji Zheng?","She spoke, Ciyuan.","Sheng Ciyuan subconsciously stood up straight. I'm here.","He remembered that Rong Yu used to call him Classmate Sheng. Why had it suddenly changed to Ciyuan?","Whatever, it made them seem closer anyway. In the future, when he troubled Rong Yu again, he wouldn't feel so embarrassed.","Rong Yu asked him, You should have already been recommended for admission to Huaqing University, right? Does the school still require you to attend classes normally?","Sheng Ciyuan replied, I'm participating in a major national project, so the school teachers don't manage my attendance. What's wrong?","She said slowly, If it's convenient, could you stay at the Ji family home for a few days?","Sheng Ciyuan froze.","Stay at the Ji family home for a few days?","This... this wouldn't be appropriate, right?","Setting aside whether his grandmother would agree, just looking at the way Old Master Ji was acting, he worried that his older brother would eventually be dragged into a corner and beaten up...","Old Master Ji was completely dumbfounded.","His mother was actually taking the initiative to ask someone to stay for a few days?","Could it be that his mother had really taken a fancy to the Eldest Young Master of the Sheng family!","It wasn't that he looked down on people, but from head to toe, there wasn't a single thing about Eldest Young Master Sheng that was worthy of his mother, okay!","Just because of this grasshopper?","A few blades of grass had captured his mother's heart?","Ridiculous!","Absolutely ridiculous!","Ji Shunying.","Rong Yu spoke faintly, calling him directly by his full name.","Old Master Ji seemed to have been hit by a freezing spell and reluctantly shut his mouth.","What are you all doing here? Ji Zhouye's head popped in from the doorway. Come downstairs and eat breakfast.","The group of people went downstairs.","It was still the long Western-style dining table.","Ji Zhiyuan, Ji Yanting, Ji Jingchuan, Ji Zhouye, and Duoduo were just about to take their seats.","Rong Yu spoke up, Yuan, move back one seat. Sheng Qingyan, you come sit here.","Old Master Ji was completely stunned.","The seat meant for the heir of the Ji family, his mother was actually letting an outsider sit there. What did this mean?","No way, did she really take a fancy to Eldest Young Master Sheng?!","But he didn't dare to utter a word of complaint.","Since even the old man didn't ask why, Ji Zhiyuan didn't dare to ask either. He looked at the few people beside him. All of you, move back a bit.","The several good grandsons moved back one by one. Although they were full of questions, none of them opened their mouths to raise any doubts...","Sheng Ciyuan: ...","Wait, what was going on here?","In his home, the seat Rong Yu was taking was where his grandmother sat.","The seat Old Master Ji was taking was where his old man sat.","The seat Ji Zhiyuan had, which was the seat his older brother was about to sit in, was where his mom sat.","He didn't understand why his older brother had managed to snag a senior's seat.","What kind of situation was this?","However, the members of the Ji family all lowered their heads and earnestly ate their breakfast without asking any questions. Fine, then he wouldn't ask either.","Sheng Ciyuan sat down next to Ji Zhouye.","Ji Zhouye winked at Ji Jingchuan and muttered in a low voice, Fourth Brother, aren't you quite smart? Did you figure out what's going on?","Ji Jingchuan took a sip of soy milk and said, It probably means we're going to have another senior elder.","Ji Yanting nodded. Great-Grandma is only eighteen, it's very normal.","Ji Zhiyuan thought about having his face rubbed back then and looked uncomfortable. But the other party isn't normal...","Slap—","Old Master Ji slapped his hand on the table. What are you all muttering about? It's so noisy! Even eating can't shut your mouths, right!","The dining room instantly fell silent.","At this moment, Butler Yu hurried in. Miss Rong, there is a Mr. Min outside the door who wants to see you. Should I invite him in or...?","Before Rong Yu had time to speak.","Old Master Ji abruptly stood up. Invite him, quickly invite him in. It's so early, he probably hasn't eaten breakfast yet. Bring him to the dining room to eat together.","When Min Jianshen walked in, he saw a room full of people.","He actually wasn't socially anxious, but seeing such a large group of people here, it was inevitably a bit awkward. Um, it seems I've come at a bad time...","It's the perfect time. Old Master Ji walked over. I've finished eating, Mr. Min can sit right here and have some breakfast.","If he had to choose a man to date his mother.","He chose Min Jianshen.","He was normal, polite, had a job within the government system, and could be considered to have common ground with his mother.","He pressed down on Min Jianshen's shoulders, forcing him to sit down.","Rong Yu: ...","This old boy really knew how to stir up trouble.","She treated Sheng Qingyan differently because Sheng Qingyan was highly likely to be Ji Zheng, the old patriarch of the Ji family.","However, before this matter was confirmed, it wasn't suitable to tell Yingbao.","This old boy was too blustery and kept causing mischief.","Mr. Min, just sit down and eat, Rong Yu spoke up. We can talk after you finish.","Min Jianshen revealed a professional fake smile. Then I won't be polite.","The several grandsons of the Ji family looked curiously at Sheng Qingyan, then curiously at Min Jianshen. Their heads couldn't help but lean together as they whispered.","Ji Zhouye: This Mr. Min's looks are lacking.","Ji Jingchuan: Having regular features is already good enough.","Ji Yanting: But Great-Grandma doesn't have that kind of interest in him. The old man is really playing matchmaker blindly.","Ji Zhiyuan: Let's all say a few words less.","Min Jianshen: ...","He could hear all this muttering, okay? Even though he couldn't hear it clearly, he could guess they were talking about him.","He was really crazy. Why did he visit at this hour?","Sheng Ciyuan silently looked up.","He felt that his older brother and Rong Yu really looked like a perfect match, very ship-worthy.","But his grandmother and old man had said that given his older brother's condition, he wasn't suited for marriage. First, they were afraid of holding back the girl. Second, they were afraid of producing offspring with genetic defects..."]},{"number":252,"title":"Chapter 252: Martyrs' Remains on the Zhenhua Ship in 01947","paragraphs":["It happened to be the weekend.","Breakfast was over. Those who usually went to school didn't have to go, and those who worked were temporarily off duty. A group of good grandsons sat quietly on the sofa in what seemed like a picture of peaceful days.","But—","Ji Zhiyuan hadn't turned a page of his project file for ages.","Ji Yanting's phone screen looped boring news on repeat.","Ji Jingchuan silently read an English essay over and over, but nothing registered in his brain.","Ji Zhouye had written the word \"Solution\" on his math problem, and that was it...","The group of grandsons occasionally glanced at Sheng Qingyan and then at Min Jianshen, the gleam of gossip and amusement in their eyes growing brighter and brighter.","Min Jianshen felt like he was sitting on pins and needles.","He didn't know how he had inexplicably stumbled into such an atmosphere.","Avoiding their messy gazes, he turned his head and said, Um, Miss Rong, I came today because I have something very important to share with you.","Old Master Ji nodded.","A person who is good at sharing will definitely be able to manage intimate relationships well.","Back in the day, after he met his wife, even someone as taciturn as him developed a strong desire to share. In his view, the desire to share was the most fundamental factor in determining whether two people could end up together.","As for Sheng Qingyan... better not to mention him.","Being looked at with such an appreciative gaze by Old Master Ji made Min Jianshen's hair stand on end.","He clearly remembered that the first time he came to the Ji family, Old Master Ji had a terrible attitude towards him. Why was he suddenly so enthusiastic?","It's like this... he began, biting the bullet. Last time at the auction, you bought that precious photo of the Zhenhua at a high price. Can I assume that you are very interested in this part of history?","Rong Yu replied, Yes, what about it?","Take a look at this. Min Jianshen took out his phone and tapped open a few photos. These are more than a dozen remains excavated three days ago by a Sakura Country archaeological team in a fishing village near the coast. The location is close to a volcano, and these remains, which drifted over from the ocean, were wrapped in a special volcanic material and perfectly preserved. According to the analysis of Hua Xia archaeologists in Sakura Country, these remains are very likely the soldiers who heroically sacrificed themselves to protect the overseas students on the Zhenhua over seventy years ago, in 1947...","Wh-what...","Old Master Ji suddenly stood up.","The gleam of gossip in the eyes of the Ji family members instantly vanished, replaced by disbelief.","Even Sheng Qingyan and Sheng Ciyuan, who were building blocks with Duoduo, stopped what they were doing, strode over, and sat down beside Rong Yu.","Min Jianshen's expression was heavy.","He had specially checked the list of these soldiers, so he knew very well that Great-grandfather Ji was one of the martyrs.","He said slowly, Because these remains were discovered on Sakura Country's territory by their archaeological team, they are temporarily kept by Sakura Country. However, the Hua Xia Ministry of Foreign Affairs has already stepped in to negotiate. If nothing unexpected happens, in about three days, these remains will be transported back to our country and handed over to our archaeological team. They will only notify the families one by one after the archaeological team finishes their identification... Miss Rong, if you want to see them as soon as possible, you can come to the capital the day after tomorrow. I have the clearance to take you in for a look.","Rong Yu's heart pounded rhythmically.","It took about three or four minutes for her to slowly calm down.","She asked softly, How many people do you have the clearance to bring?","Min Jianshen didn't know why she asked that, but he still thought for a moment and replied, My position in the domestic archaeological team is not low. Bringing four or five people shouldn't be a problem.","Old Master Ji's voice was urgent. I want to go.","Ji Zhiyuan quickly spoke up, I will accompany you.","Ji Yanting, Ji Jingchuan, and Ji Zhouye had just stood up when they were stopped by Rong Yu's sharp glare. We don't need you guys.","She turned her head to look at Sheng Qingyan. You, come with me, are you willing?","He's willing, of course my older brother is willing! Sheng Ciyuan answered on his behalf. Then we'll stay at the Ji family's house for two days and return to the capital together the day after tomorrow.","Min Jianshen stood up. Then it's settled. I'll take my leave first. Contact me on WeChat if you need anything.","He hurried out the door.","If he stayed any longer, he was afraid the Ji family's probing gazes would burn a few holes through him.","Once he left, the hall remained quiet for a good while.","Old Master Ji had pools of tears in his eyes and choked out, I have never met my dad, never. I really didn't expect that at this age, I would go to see his remains. I feel terrible, so terrible...","Ji Zhiyuan: ...","The old man was really acting more and more like a child, crying as easily as a child.","But he could understand this kind of emotion.","Back when both of his parents perished in an accident, he had been the same, crying until he broke down and fainting from crying in the old man's arms.","At that time, the old man, having lost his son in middle age, didn't even have red rims around his eyes. He stood steady as a mountain in front of the brothers.","It turned out that the old man wasn't unsorrowful.","Rather, when there is no one standing in front of you to shield you, you can only suppress your grief.","When the spirit has something to rely on, naturally there is no need to force yourself to hold on.","Old Master Ji wailed loudly.","Sheng Ciyuan was dumbfounded.","The helmsman of one of the four major families in Haicheng, a prominent figure in the business world, an iron-willed octogenarian, was right at this moment crying like a baby with his head on Rong Yu's lap.","Ji Jingchuan spoke up at the right time. Second Young Master Sheng is good at studying. Could you come upstairs and teach me a few math problems?","Sheng Ciyuan was dragged upstairs.","Old Master Ji, no longer having any reservations, cried even louder. Mom, Mom, boohoo...","What are you crying for? Rong Yu sighed and gently wiped away his tears. Hasn't Mom come back? Perhaps your dad will come back too; it's just a matter of time. Alright, stop crying. Today is Saturday. How about we go out and play?","Old Master Ji immediately sat up straight. Where are we going?","Rong Yu glanced at Sheng Qingyan sitting beside her. To the place we went last time, to go fishing.","Old Master Ji's eyes lit up.","Although he didn't know how to fish.","But Mom did.","Old Master Ji called his two old buddies, Old Master Hai and Old Master Si. Do you want to eat some wild fish? If you do, let's go fishing together, and let you witness Rong Yu's fishing skills again!","Old Master Hai and Old Master Si were both retired and had nothing to do all day. Naturally, they accepted the invitation.","Old Master Ji had just hung up the phone when he saw Sheng Qingyan helping the servants bring fishing gear out of the storage room. The old man narrowed his eyes. What is he doing going with us?","He's coming along, Rong Yu rubbed his head. His fishing skills should be better than mine.","Old Master Ji frowned. Mom, how do you know so much? Have you gone fishing together before? Why didn't you take me with you?","Rong Yu couldn't help but laugh.","She had wanted to bring him, but at that time, Yingbao hadn't even been born yet.","However...","Her smile paused for a moment.","Just what did she have to do to make Ji Zheng's missing soul and spirit return to their rightful place?","Forget it, she would just take it one step at a time.","Ji Zhiyuan drove, accompanying the two elders to the suburbs of Haicheng to go fishing."]},{"number":253,"title":"Chapter 253: Forever Bidding Farewell, Departing, and Waiting","paragraphs":["There were many people by the river over the weekend.","The three old guys gathered together, either bragging or showing mutual disdain, bickering back and forth in a lively manner.","Ji Zhiyuan had long been accustomed to this scene. He took a tent from the trunk of the car, propped it up and secured it, laid out a ground mat, set up a folding table, and finally arranged the fruits and snacks prepared by Butler Yu on the table one by one.","He also took a bouquet of flowers from the car and placed it on the table.","Old Master Hai: \"We're just fishing, there's no need for all these fancy things.\"","Old Master Ji: \"Don't you understand ambiance? It's so comfortable this way.\"","Old Master Si: \"Zhiyuan is a great CEO after all. You really have the nerve to make him do all this manual labor.\"","Old Master Ji: \"My Zhiyuan is showing filial piety. Look at those disappointing brats in your families, which one of them can compare to Zhiyuan's devotion?\"","Old Master Hai shut his mouth.","Old Master Si fell silent.","After a good while, Old Master Si sighed, \"Among my grandchildren, that little bastard Si Lin is the most disgraceful. It's bad enough he got into a trashy university, but he's also dating every day. I mean, if you secretly date a few girls, no one would say anything. But good heavens, every time he dates, it's a public figure, either a celebrity or a model. He's on the tabloid news every day, leaving me with nowhere to hide my old face...\"","Old Master Ji scolded in annoyance, \"He even dared to set his sights on Rong Yu, completely turning the world upside down. I suggest you publicly sever ties with that brat to save yourself from further embarrassment.\"","Old Master Si choked back a response, \"He's just dating, not committing any crimes. Striking him from the family register is a bit too severe...\"","Old Master Hai pursed his lips, \"What's the use of asking Old Ji? You might as well ask Miss Rong.\"","The grandsons of the Ji family used to be more ignorant than the last, but ever since Miss Rong arrived, they had become increasingly obedient, sensible, and filial.","Just as they were speaking.","Suddenly, there was a splash.","A fish was pulled ashore.","Old Master Ji was just about to flatter his mother.","Only to see that the person who caught the fish was Sheng Qingyan.","While the old guys were chatting, Sheng Qingyan had baited all the fishing rods and cast them into the river. Controlling four rods by himself, he pulled them up one by one. The fishing lines instantly went taut, and huge splashes churned the surface of the water.","\"Steady! Reel it in slowly!\" Old Master Hai stood up excitedly to direct, as if he were the one who had hooked the fish.","Sheng Qingyan's movements, however, were surprisingly steady. In a short while, four large grass carp, each weighing over ten pounds, were pulled ashore, flopping wildly on the ground.","Rong Yu's long eyelashes trembled.","Back then, when studying abroad, there was a period when he was on leave, and they would go fishing every weekend.","He knew how to fish, catch fish, clean fish, and make fish soup... That time was truly happy, so happy that it seemed to make one forget all worries.","But he had not forgotten his military uniform.","And she, too, dared not forget the heavy responsibility on her shoulders.","The fleeting happiness was exchanged for long periods of separation. It was always about seeing each other off, leaving, waiting, and rarely reuniting...","\"Splash—\"","A few more fish were pulled ashore.","This scene made the three old masters gasp at the same time.","Old Master Hai's dentures almost fell out: \"It's only been a few minutes, and he's already caught several?\"","Old Master Si's eyes widened like brass bells: \"Kid, did you... did you use some special bait?\"","This fishing skill was even more impressive than Rong Yu's.","Old Master Ji snorted coldly: \"It's just good luck. You two old fogeys are just making a fuss over nothing.\"","\"Yingbao, it's not luck,\" Rong Yu spoke up. \"Go sit next to Sheng Qingyan and learn how to fish from him.\"","Old Master Ji crossed his arms: \"I won't—!\"","Before his words even faded.","Old Master Hai and Old Master Si, with lightning speed, took the spots to the left and right of Sheng Qingyan, sitting down before anyone else.","Old Master Ji: \"...\"","These two idiots were actually learning to fish from a greenhorn. Did they have any image left as the helmsmen of major families?!","Anyway, he had his mother, and his mother knew how to fish. He didn't need to learn!","The old boy sat huffily on the mat: \"Zhiyuan, I want some watermelon. Zhiyuan, I want water. Zhiyuan, there are mosquitoes...\"","Ji Zhiyuan: \"...\"","The term \"old child\" was truly fitting.","He bore the burden of being ordered around without complaint.","But Old Master Ji grew increasingly dissatisfied, his expression worsening by the minute.","Because Old Master Hai had caught two fish, and Old Master Si had caught four... Since when did fishing become so easy?","He already regretted not learning.","But going over there on his own initiative now would seem beneath his dignity.","More importantly, there was no space left next to Sheng Qingyan.","At this moment.","Sheng Qingyan suddenly stood up.","He walked toward Old Master Ji.","\"I'll teach you.\"","He rarely spoke; his voice was raspy and his tone heavy, but his words carried sincerity.","Old Master Ji put on airs: \"Who needs your teaching? You really think you're something...\"","Old Master Hai: \"Qingyan, ignore him. He's just a stubborn mule.\"","Old Master Si: \"Qingyan, come back here quickly...\"","Old Master Ji: \"...\"","Tsk tsk, they were even calling him Qingyan now. Who were they being so affectionate for!","Sheng Qingyan automatically tuned out the other two.","He crouched down, took Old Master Ji's hand, and spoke again: \"Come here, I'll teach you.\"","An indescribable tremor ran like an electric current from his palm through his entire body. The grumpy old boy instantly froze.","Surprisingly, he felt no aversion at all to having his hand held by Sheng Qingyan.","How could this be...","\"Click—\"","Rong Yu pressed the shutter on her phone, snapping a picture of this moment.","Her Yingbao, at the age of seventy-eight, finally had both his parents.","She clicked away, taking a barrage of photos of the two of them.","Old Master Ji sighed.","Forget it, he would just treat it as coaxing his mother to make her happy.","As long as his mother liked it, he wasn't entirely unable to accept Sheng Qingyan.","He bumped Old Master Si out of the way with his hip and sat obediently next to Sheng Qingyan.","Ji Zhiyuan breathed a sigh of relief.","He could finally spare a moment to handle some company business.","He had just sat down and taken out his phone when he saw a new email in his inbox: \"... Paternity test results... Please review.\"","Ji Zhiyuan's brow darkened.","The moment he returned from Hong Kong, he had someone send two samples to a paternity testing facility: one of Wen Yan's hairs and one of Duoduo's.","Although he was almost certain, he still needed proof.","He opened the email, skimming through it rapidly, and scrolled to the last page. His chest instantly tightened in suffocation.","Sure enough.","She was indeed Duoduo's biological mother.","She was Ke Man.","She was his ex-wife.","That taciturn, dull, insecure, and lackluster Ke Man was actually Wen Yan.","Was she a doctor before?","Did she have a career before?","Was she ever this radiant before?","He didn't remember, didn't remember at all.","He remained silent for a long time before dialing Wen Yan's number: \"Dr. Wen, at three o'clock tomorrow afternoon, Duoduo has a piano competition. Can you make it to the venue?\"","Wen Yan's voice came through: \"I have a surgery at two o'clock, so I might be a few minutes late. Can I still enter if I'm late?\"","Ji Zhiyuan replied, \"It's fine. Duoduo and I will wait for you.\""]},{"number":254,"title":"Chapter 254: Dad is no longer the father he used to be.","paragraphs":["As the only junior of the Ji family's fifth generation participating in the competition, the whole family wanted to go.","However, after being beaten up in Harbor City, Ji Yanting still had injuries on his face. He couldn't go out for fear of ruining his image.","Ji Jingchuan and Ji Zhouye were high school seniors and were ordered to stay home to do their homework.","Finally, it was Ji Zhiyuan who took the two elders, held Duoduo's hand, and of course, along with Sheng Qingyan, who was temporarily staying at the Ji family's house, to the concert hall. Sheng Ciyuan, the top student, stayed at home to tutor the boys with their homework.","The children participating in the piano competition were at most eight or nine years old, and the youngest were only four or five. They were all escorted by their entire families, making the backstage preparation area extremely bustling.","Rong Yu went in to help Duoduo change into her performance dress.","It was a sparkling dress. When worn, the gemstones scattered like stars, reflecting the lights from the ceiling in a dazzling display. Many children backstage looked at it with deep envy.","Duoduo leaned close to Rong Yu, feeling a little shy.","Suddenly, she felt a strong gaze—a very familiar, repulsive, and uncomfortable stare.","She turned her head and saw an old acquaintance, Lan Yue.","Lan Yue was also participating in the piano competition.","Standing beside Lan Rouxue, her eyes were glued to the dress on Duoduo. Such a beautiful dress, why couldn't it belong to her?","Lan Rouxue squeezed out a smile, \"Miss Rong, what a coincidence.\"","Rong Yu reached out to adjust Duoduo's collar and said indifferently, \"Not really a coincidence. After all, back then, Lan Yue only clamored to learn the piano because she saw Duoduo learning it, and the Ji family even paid the tuition.\"","\"That's ancient history, what's there to talk about?\" Lan Rouxue looked disdainful. \"Miss Rong must have reaped quite a few benefits during your time with the Ji family, right? Look at your outfit, how many people in Sea City could compare?\"","Rong Yu shook her head. \"When the heart is dirty, everything one sees is dirty.\"","Lan Rouxue's face stiffened.","Recently, she had scrolled past news about Rong Yu countless times.","Rong Yu had become the spokesperson for China's aerospace industry.","Rong Yu represented the country and won a global gold medal in physics.","Rong Yu risked her life to expose the dark secrets of Li Medical...","Each and every one of these achievements was not something an ordinary person could do.","She seemed to faintly understand why Old Master Ji valued Rong Yu so much.","But even so, she couldn't stand Rong Yu appearing before her with such a lofty posture; it made her feel incredibly uncomfortable.","\"Children, the competition is about to start,\" a staff member walked in. \"Parents can go to the audience seats now. Please come back here to pick up your children after the performance.\"","Rong Yu squatted down and instructed, \"Duoduo, stick closely to the teacher, and don't talk to Lan Yue alone. If anything happens, use your smartwatch to call Auntie.\"","Duoduo nodded obediently. \"I'm not afraid of Lan Yue anymore, Auntie, don't worry.\"","In the past, her father favored Lan Yue, and she was afraid of making him unhappy, so she feared being alone with Lan Yue.","But now, her father was no longer the same father he used to be.","With her family unconditionally spoiling and protecting her, she had nothing to fear.","Rong Yu waited until Lan Rouxue left the backstage before stepping out herself, making sure to ask the teacher to pay extra attention to Duoduo.","Lan Rouxue's gaze swept quickly across the audience.","But she only saw Old Master Ji, not Ji Zhiyuan.","The corners of her lips curled into a mocking smile.","Even without Little Yue, Ji Zhiyuan still didn't value his daughter, Duoduo.","And here she thought their father-daughter bond was so deep...","Just as she was thinking this.","A figure walked in through the entrance of the auditorium. Even against the light, she could recognize that it was Ji Zhiyuan.","Only this man possessed such a tall stature and such handsome contours.","After breaking up with him, her days had grown worse by the day. She wanted to get back together so badly, but she couldn't even get into the Ji Corporation building.","It just so happened there was a piano competition, and knowing Duoduo met the requirements, she signed Little Yue up too, all for the sake of a chance encounter.","However, Lan Rouxue had barely taken a step forward when she saw there was actually a woman beside Ji Zhiyuan.","The woman was dressed sharply, with a gentle face and a spark in her eyes, looking very much like the woman who had walked down the aisle with Ji Zhiyuan all those years ago.","But didn't Ji Zhiyuan dislike Ke Man?","Why would he be with a woman who looked so much like Ke Man?","While Lan Rouxue's thoughts were running wild.","Ji Zhiyuan had already taken his seat with Wen Yan, right next to Rong Yu, Old Master Ji, and Sheng Qingyan.","Sheng Qingyan had probably never been in an enclosed space with so many people before and seemed a bit uneasy. He instinctively tightened his grip on Rong Yu's hand.","Rong Yu squeezed his hand back. \"Don't be afraid.\"","Old Master Ji's eyebrow twitched.","He then pinched the bridge of his nose. Forget it, let it be, he accepted it.","Piano music soon rang out in the concert hall as the participating children took the stage one by one.","\"Duoduo is on stage,\" Old Master Ji beamed. \"Our little girl is dressed so beautifully today, she will definitely win first place!\"","Ji Zhiyuan spoke up, \"It's the participation that counts. What place she gets doesn't matter.\"","Wen Yan stared intently at the sparkling little figure on the stage, her eyes full of tenderness. She took out her phone, found the right angles, and snapped photos.","Under the soft stage lights, Duoduo, wearing her little white dress, walked gracefully to the piano. She took a deep breath, gently placed her small hands on the keys, and began to play her piece.","As her tiny fingers pressed the first key, it was like a star quietly lighting up the night sky. The single notes in the high register danced crisply, while the occasional chords in the lower register sounded just like a mother's gentle voice.","Wen Yan's hand suddenly paused.","She could hear Duoduo's longing for a mother in this melody.","A child who grew up without a mother, who didn't know what having a mother felt like, could still play this piece with such profound emotion.","Wen Yan's eyes instantly turned red.","A tissue was handed to her from the side. She took it and said in a hoarse voice, \"Thank you, President Ji.\"","Rong Yu was also handing a tissue to her old son. \"Look at you, what are you crying for?\"","Such a cheerful tune, yet this old boy was crying along. He was really becoming more and more of a crybaby.","Old Master Ji said in a muffled voice, \"My heart aches for Duoduo. This child has been without a mother since she was little, and her father always took an outsider's side. It's too pitiful.\"","Rong Yu didn't know what to say, so she gently patted his back to comfort him.","Before long, Duoduo's performance ended, and next up was Lan Yue.","Old Master Ji frowned. \"I'm not watching anymore. Let's go to the backstage to pick up Duoduo.\"","Rong Yu helped him up. \"Move quietly, don't disturb the others.\"","At the same time, she pulled up Sheng Qingyan on the other side. \"Let's go.\"","Ji Zhiyuan also felt there was no point in staying and asked for Wen Yan's opinion.","The one thing Wen Yan wanted to do most right now was to give little Duoduo a tight hug, so naturally, she left the audience seats with them.","The group walked to the backstage area.","A group of children who had finished their performances were playing games there.","Ji Zhiyuan stepped forward. \"Teacher, please ask Ji Zhiyi to come out.\"","The person in charge was taken aback for a moment and said, \"Ji Zhiyi was just picked up by her family, barely three minutes ago.\"","A bad premonition arose in Ji Zhiyuan's heart, and his face darkened. \"Who picked her up?\""]},{"number":255,"title":"Chapter 255: Haven't you corrected the bad habit of randomly calling people \"daddy\" yet","paragraphs":["The person in charge realized the gravity of the situation.","But there were too many children and parents at the scene. With people coming and going, he couldn't recall exactly who had picked up Duoduo.","\"Please don't worry,\" the staff member said. \"I remember it was someone Ji Zhiyi knew, otherwise we wouldn't have allowed her to leave with them. Please wait a moment, I'll go check the security footage.\"","\"Daddy!\"","A crisp, sweet voice rang out. It was Lan Yue, who had finished her performance. Lifting her skirt, she threw herself toward Ji Zhiyuan.","She hadn't seen her father in a very, very long time.","Ji Zhiyuan coldly sidestepped her. \"Haven't you kicked the bad habit of calling random people your father yet?\"","Lan Yue froze in place. Blinking, large tears rolled down her cheeks. \"You are my daddy, I'm not calling you that randomly. I really missed you so much, Daddy. It was Mommy who did something wrong, I'm innocent. Why are you treating me like this...\"","\"Yes, Zhiyuan,\" Lan Rouxue said, having appeared at some unknown point. Biting her lip, she added, \"Yue dreams about you, her father, every single day. Just out of pity...\"","Ji Zhiyuan's voice was frigid. \"It has nothing to do with me.\"","This mother and daughter had exhausted all his patience. He wouldn't waste another second on them.","\"It's been so long since it happened,\" Lan Rouxue softened her voice. \"We shouldn't always dwell on the unpleasant past. We should look forward. Zhiyuan, let's start over.\"","Ji Zhiyuan's face suddenly darkened. \"Do you even hear what you're saying?\"","His intimidating aura radiated outward.","Terrified, Lan Yue hid behind Lan Rouxue.","At that moment, the staff member came out holding a tablet with the security footage. \"I just checked. Ji Zhiyi was picked up by her fourth uncle. Here, that's her fourth uncle, right?\"","Ji Zhiyuan took the tablet.","When he saw the face on the screen, his heart plunged into an ice cellar.","It was Ji Liuguang... no, He Liuguang!","Back when his true identity hadn't been exposed, He Liuguang had never been very friendly to Duoduo.","Later, He Liuguang was kicked out of the Ji family. Rumor had it that he got into a conflict with his biological father, pushed him into a river, and nearly drowned him. The He family called the police, and he was arrested.","To think he was released so quickly.","He Liuguang picking up Duoduo definitely meant no good.","Ji Zhiyuan's heart began to pound uncontrollably.","At the same time.","At the back entrance of the concert hall.","Duoduo was led to a white van. Seeing several strange men inside, she backed away in fear. \"Uncle He, did Great-Grandpa really fall ill? Why didn't my daddy come to take me to the hospital? Why did he send you?\"","The corners of He Liuguang's mouth curled up. \"Your daddy is the great CEO of the Ji Corporation. He's very busy, how would he have time for you? Hurry up and get in, don't waste time.\"","He grabbed the back of Duoduo's neck and gave her a hard shove, completely ignoring the fact that the little girl was wearing a long dress. The hem caught on the car door, and a sparkling gemstone fell to the ground.","He Liuguang bent down to pick it up. \"This gem doesn't look cheap. There must be at least a few hundred of them on this dress. Heh, the Ji family is so rich, why couldn't they just afford to raise me too? Why did they have to be so heartless to me...\"","The car door slammed shut.","The cramped space was filled with the terrible stench of cigarette smoke.","Duoduo's eyes immediately turned red.","She knew struggling was useless because she was just a child, and there were four grown men.","Her hands quietly moved behind her back. She tapped her smartwatch and dialed a number...","However, the moment she made a slight move, He Liuguang pinned her arm down, roughly snatched the watch, rolled down the window, and threw it straight out.","Meeting He Liuguang's gloomy eyes, Duoduo shrank her neck. \"Uncle He, I'll be good. I won't cry or make a fuss, please don't hit me...\"","He Liuguang sneered. \"At least you know what's good for you!\"","If Ji Jingchuan were here, he would definitely recognize that the man sitting next to Duoduo was his adoptive father, He Cheng.","The man driving and the one in the passenger seat were gamblers who often hung out with He Cheng. They were the kind of lowlifes who would abandon their wives and children and commit any evil deed just to gamble.","He Cheng frowned. \"Liuguang, are you sure this little girl alone can make the Ji family willingly cough up a hundred million?\"","He Liuguang twitched his lips. \"She's the only granddaughter of this generation in the Ji family. The old man protects her like the apple of his eye. Asking for a hundred million isn't excessive. It's settled: I take fifty million, and the rest of you split the other fifty million.\"","\"Who said it's settled?\" Scarface, who was driving, spat out some saliva. \"I'm providing the car and doing the heavy lifting, and I'm responsible for contacting the people at the docks to smuggle us out of the country. I should get the lion's share. That fifty million belongs to me!\"","He Liuguang laughed out of anger. \"If it weren't for me, could you have smoothly tricked the eldest miss of the Ji family into getting in the car?\"","\"Shut up!\" He Cheng said angrily. \"The job isn't even done yet and you're already dividing the spoils. Drive faster. We'll contact the Ji family for the money once we're on the boat!\"","He Liuguang glanced at the innocent Duoduo.","The group's plan was to smuggle Duoduo out of the country and then have the Ji family wire a hundred million into a foreign account.","After receiving the money, they would put a bullet in Duoduo.","His eyes held a trace of pity.","Since the Ji family was so cruel to him, then the child would just have to bear the consequences.","\"Uncle He...\" Duoduo whispered. \"Do you just want money? You could have just told me directly. I'm very rich, didn't you know?\"","He Liuguang narrowed his eyes.","\"I'll give my money only to you, Fourth Uncle.\" Duoduo leaned closer to him. \"That new fourth uncle stole all the family's attention, I hate him. I still like you better. Fourth Uncle, it's too stuffy in the car. Can you open the window and let me get some fresh air?\"","She took a necklace out of her pocket. \"Great-Grandpa gave me this gift yesterday. It auctioned for a high price of thirty million. I'll give it to you, Fourth Uncle.\"","He Liuguang's expression softened a bit. He let her sit by the window and rolled it down.","Duoduo secretly tore the gemstones off her dress and threw them out.","That necklace was actually a fake one she had beaded herself.","And this dress was a custom-made performance outfit from her aunt. The blue sapphires on it were extremely rare. As long as her family saw these sapphires, they would know where she had been taken.","The car sped along and soon arrived at the Haicheng docks. This area was a massive cargo distribution center, bustling with ships and people everywhere.","Duoduo was dragged out of the car.","He Liuguang's gaze swept over her bare hemline, and his eyes instantly darkened. \"You brat, how dare you play tricks on me? See if I don't kill you!\"","Since she was discovered, Duoduo stopped pretending to be good. She shouted loudly, \"Help! These men are human traffickers! Misters and misses, help me... Mmph!\"","He Cheng offered an apologetic smile to the passersby. \"My granddaughter is sick. She's just speaking nonsense!\"","This group of four grown men looked like people you shouldn't mess with. Especially Scarface, just standing there was enough to keep the passersby from saying anything.","Just as the group was about to head to the hidden docks, He Liuguang's expression suddenly changed. \"They've caught up to us!\""]},{"number":256,"title":"Chapter 256: After All, She Called You Fourth Uncle for Several Years","paragraphs":["The sea breeze, carrying a salty and fishy scent, poured into the pier. The rusty shipping containers looked like the teeth of a giant beast.","Duoduo was tucked under Scarface's arm. Her small face was deathly pale, and tears welled up in her eyes, but she bit her lip, not daring to cry out loud.","\"Hurry up,\" He Cheng urged. \"Stuff this wretched brat inside, and as soon as the ship arrives, we'll ship her out.\"","The door to a container was pulled open. Inside, it was pitch black, emitting the smell of mildew and engine oil.","Duoduo finally couldn't help but let out a sob. He Liuguang immediately covered her mouth and said viciously, \"Make another sound and I'll throw you into the sea to feed the fish!\"","Right at that moment—","\"Bang—!\"","The iron gate on the side of the pier was kicked open, and four figures rushed in against the glare of the searchlights.","It was Rong Yu, Ji Zhiyuan, Wen Yan, and Sheng Qingyan. As for Old Master Ji, he had been sent to the police station to report the crime.","Rong Yu's face was extremely gloomy.","He Liuguang had grown up eating the Ji family's food, living a pampered life in the Ji family for over twenty years. The education he received there was enough to benefit him for a lifetime. Yet, he had found a bunch of scumbags to kidnap Duoduo.","This gang was very experienced. They had been avoiding the surveillance cameras all along, and the car they drove was the most common white van on the road. When she tried to lock onto it in the surveillance system, tens of thousands of them appeared, heading in different directions, making it difficult to distinguish for a while.","Just when she was at her wits' end, she saw in the surveillance footage the gemstones reflecting light under the sun.","These gemstones were collectibles Yingbao had bought for her. She had little interest in them, so she gave them all to a designer to make a sparkling dress for Duoduo.","Duoduo had thrown the gemstones all along the road.","Therefore, they were able to successfully track them here. Fortunately, they were still in time.","\"Let go of Duoduo,\" Ji Zhiyuan's voice was extremely hoarse.","His cold, heavy eyes stared intently at He Liuguang. \"No matter what, you shouldn't have laid a hand on Duoduo. She called you Fourth Uncle for years.\"","\"Cut the crap.\" Scarface sneered and pulled out a pistol, pressing it against Duoduo's temple. \"Take one more step, and I'll kill her right now.\"","Ji Zhiyuan's eyes darkened.","The kidnappers were actually carrying firearms. The situation was trickier than he had imagined.","Wen Yan covered her lips in fright.","Logically speaking, as an outsider, she shouldn't have come to such a scene, but she couldn't control herself.","Seeing Duoduo trying so hard to hold back her tears, she almost cried too.","Rong Yu said in a low voice, \"Dr. Wen, go guard the door. When the police arrive, bring them in to surround this place. Sorry to trouble you.\"","She turned her eyes to Sheng Qingyan, who had a very low presence, and pursed her lips. \"Watch for the right moment and grab the gun. Do you understand?\"","Sheng Qingyan's glass-like eyes showed a slight fluctuation when he looked at the black gun. His finger subconsciously made the motion of pulling a trigger.","Rong Yu felt a sense of relief in her chest.","Although he had lost a piece of his soul, his instincts were still there. He could fish, and he could use a gun.","She could use a gun too, of course, but after all, she wasn't a professional soldier, and her accuracy wasn't high.","And Ji Zheng, who had been in the military camp, was known as a sharpshooter, especially skilled at shooting moving targets, which was why he was always assigned special missions.","\"Liuguang, you guys are just doing this for money. There's no need to take a life.\" Ji Zhiyuan raised his hands in a gesture of surrender. \"Compared to Duoduo, I'm much more valuable. Swapping hostages would be more beneficial to you.\"","\"Bullshit!\" He Cheng spat out some saliva. \"You're a grown man, we wouldn't be able to control you. Stop your fucking nonsense and transfer the money. Hurry up and transfer it! One hundred million, not a penny less!\"","Ji Zhiyuan reached his hand toward his pocket.","The gun in Scarface's hand immediately changed direction, pointing at him: \"Put your hands up! Don't reach into your pocket. Take off your clothes! Take them off now, or I'll shoot!\"","\"Do you think guns are that easy to get, that everyone can have one?\" Ji Zhiyuan took out his phone from his pocket. \"Don't you want money? Fine, I'll transfer it to you. But don't you dare touch Duoduo. If Duoduo loses even a single hair, I won't let any of you off!\"","Scarface stared intently at his movements, afraid that the phone in his hand would suddenly turn into a weapon.","He Liuguang kept refreshing his overseas account. Soon, a massive sum of money arrived, and he hastily counted how many zeros there were.","\"Step aside.\" He Cheng snatched the phone away. \"Let me see if it's really one hundred million.\"","One hundred million was a massive fortune for anyone, even for He Liuguang, who was once the Fourth Young Master of the Ji family.","The four men were momentarily distracted.","Now's the chance—","Rong Yu suddenly hurled a fire axe at the oil drum to the left of the kidnappers. Amidst the loud crash, the kidnappers instinctively turned their heads toward the source of the sound.","Before Scarface could recover his wits, Rong Yu had already picked up a steel pipe and smashed it hard against his elbow. The pistol in his hand traced a parabola in the air and fell to the ground.","He Liuguang bent down to pick it up.","He was kicked away by Rong Yu.","Before the harsh sound of metal hitting the ground could dissipate, Sheng Qingyan had already moved.","Like a hunting cheetah, he lowered his body and sprinted forward. In the instant before He Liuguang's fingers could touch the gun handle, he snatched the pistol first. His movements were smooth and flowing, without a single wasted motion.","He Liuguang abruptly looked up, meeting Sheng Qingyan's cold eyes—pitch-black, indifferent, yet carrying a chilling sense of oppression.","\"Don't move!\" He Liuguang yanked Duoduo from Scarface's arms and held her in front of him as a shield, his hand gripping Duoduo's throat. \"Throw the gun over! Or I'll snap her neck!\"","The muzzle of Sheng Qingyan's gun remained perfectly still, his calm gaze landing on He Liuguang.","Ji Zhiyuan's heart skipped a beat.","He knew that the eldest young master of the Sheng family had autism and had difficulty communicating with others. Often, when someone spoke ten sentences, he could only process one.","He was afraid that Sheng Qingyan would enrage the utterly inhumane He Liuguang.","\"Throw the gun over! Now!\" He Liuguang tightly pinched Duoduo's tender neck, his whole body shifting wildly as he spoke. \"I'll kill her, I swear I'll kill her! Don't force me to commit murder!\"","However—","Sheng Qingyan couldn't hear these voices at all.","The kidnapper's movement trajectory, the amplitude of the hostage's struggles, the speed of the bullet—all these variables were rapidly calculated in his mind, forming a clear trajectory.","The next second—","As the gunshot rang out, the bullet accurately brushed past Duoduo's ear and directly hit He Liuguang's shoulder. The impact of the bullet made He Liuguang stagger backward, and the hand gripping Duoduo suddenly let go.","Scarface cursed loudly and lunged forward to grab Duoduo.","\"Bang!\"","A bullet exploded on the ground, stopping Scarface in his tracks.","Scarface roared furiously, \"There are only two bullets left! Since it's already come to this, let's go all out! Everyone, get them!\"","Moving faster than he ever had in his life, Ji Zhiyuan reached out, pulled Duoduo toward him, and then pushed her toward the main gate. \"Duoduo, run! Get out of here and hide...\"","He Liuguang still tried to grab Duoduo.","But Rong Yu picked up the steel pipe and brought it down heavily onto his arm.","With a loud crack, He Liuguang heard his own bone seemingly shatter..."]},{"number":257,"title":"Chapter 257: So, Wen Yan is Ke Man","paragraphs":["Wen Yan stood anxiously by the road, waiting for the police to arrive.","As she heard the sirens, she also saw Little Duoduo rushing out from the gate of the pier.","Instinct drove her to run in Duoduo's direction. She only wanted to go faster, even faster, to pull that tiny body into her arms.","\"Auntie...\"","Duoduo broke down and threw herself into Wen Yan's arms, sobbing uncontrollably.","She hadn't cried when those people tied her up, nor had she cried when a gun was pressed against her temple. But the moment she saw Auntie Wen, all her suppressed fear came crashing down like a tidal wave. She buried her face in Wen Yan's embrace and cried without any restraint.","\"Good girl, Duoduo, it's okay. Auntie is here, don't be afraid...\"","She stood up with Duoduo in her arms and shouted to the dozens of police officers who had just arrived, \"Right there! They have guns!\"","The police split into four teams and swiftly surrounded the shipping container at the pier.","Before the police could even call out, He Liuguang was kicked out by Rong Yu. With seven or eight broken bones all over his body, he curled up like a shrimp, screaming in despair, \"Help, save me—\"","Ji Zhiyuan dragged Scarface by the back of his collar and threw him in front of the police.","Meanwhile, Sheng Qingyan still wore a detached expression, but his actions were ruthless. He grabbed He Cheng by the neck and hurled him heavily onto the ground, knocking him out cold instantly.","Rong Yu frowned and said, \"There were four of them in total. One got away. I'll have to trouble the police to do a thorough search.\"","Crouching in the shadows near the side of the pier was the one who got away from the four-man gang, the Thin-faced man. His face was covered in blood, and his eyes were filled with madness.","He stared coldly at Wen Yan and Duoduo in the distance. Before anyone could notice, a cold glint flashed in his hand as he thrust a dagger straight at Wen Yan's back.","Wen Yan only heard a sharp gust of wind approaching and dodged instinctively. Seizing the opportunity, the Thin-faced man grabbed Duoduo's ankle—","Wen Yan held onto Duoduo tightly, stumbling backward as the kidnapper dragged them.","\"Splash!\"","The two of them plunged into the deep water by the pier together.","The murky seawater instantly swallowed their mouths and noses. The Thin-faced man was still frantically pulling at Duoduo. Holding her breath, Wen Yan kicked him hard in the throat. The Thin-faced man let go in pain, but then he grabbed Wen Yan by the hair, smashed her head violently against the stone steps on the bank, and shoved her under the water—","The intense pain and lack of oxygen began to blur her vision.","She heard Ji Zhiyuan's voice. Struggling to open her eyes, she saw the man through the surface of the water.","Her hands were still pushing Duoduo with all her might, helping the child float to the surface.","Wen Yan's consciousness began to fade.","She vaguely saw Ji Zhiyuan swimming toward her, but her body sank like it was filled with lead. The last thing she remembered was the strength of the man's grip on her wrist, and Duoduo's heart-wrenching cries as they surfaced.","Her vision went black, and she lost consciousness.","Until she heard the cries of a child—a baby crying.","Where was the baby coming from?","Wen Yan looked around and saw a woman lying on an operating table, covered in blood. The woman was very plump, her face covered in freckles, her stomach lined with stretch marks, and blood continuously gushing from her lower body...","\"Oh no, the mother is hemorrhaging!\"","\"Quick, notify the family to sign the consent form!\"","\"Excuse me, where is the patient's family... You are the patient's husband, right? Quick, sign this, we need to operate!\"","Wen Yan froze.","Wasn't this man Duoduo's father, Ji Zhiyuan?","Was she dreaming about the scene of Duoduo's birth?","The next moment, a man ran over from the end of the corridor. \"I am the patient's biological brother, it's more appropriate for me to sign!\"","She froze again.","This was her eldest brother, Ke Yan.","Her brother only had one sister—her.","Then, the person lying on the delivery bed... was her?","A sudden, agonizing pain pierced her brain. Countless images flashed rapidly through her mind like a movie playing on fast forward...","Ji Zhiyuan stood by the bedside. \"Doctor, how is the patient?\"","The doctor checked Wen Yan's condition and said, \"Her head suffered a severe impact, resulting in a serious concussion. It will probably take some time for her to wake up. But please rest assured, the patient is not in any immediate life-threatening danger.\"","\"Wuwu, Auntie Wen...\" Duoduo lay on the bed, clutching Wen Yan's hand tightly as large teardrops fell. \"It's all because I was foolish, because I was too stupid and got tricked away, that Auntie Wen ended up like this. Auntie Wen, you have to wake up...\"","Rong Yu hugged the little girl. \"He Liuguang had his eyes on you; no matter how careful you were, it wouldn't have mattered... It's not your fault, don't blame yourself. Doctor Wen likes you very much. The best thing you can do is stay in the hospital and keep her company.\"","Duoduo wiped her tears and opened a book. \"Auntie Wen, I'll tell you a story, okay? I'll tell you the story of the little tadpole looking for its mommy...\"","Rong Yu left the space to the two of them, gesturing for Ji Zhiyuan to step outside. She asked in a low voice, \"Doctor Wen's concern for Duoduo goes far beyond the norm, and Duoduo seems overly attached to her as well. Have you looked into what's going on?\"","Ji Zhiyuan was just about to speak.","Just then, a flurry of hurried footsteps echoed down the corridor.","A tall figure in a suit strode over rapidly, raised his hand, and threw a vicious punch right into Ji Zhiyuan's face. \"Every time my sister is near you, she nearly loses half her life. I wish I could kill you!\"","Ji Zhiyuan's head snapped to the side from the blow. He slowly and methodically wiped the corner of his lips and said evenly, \"She really is your sister. So, Wen Yan is Ke Man?\"","Ke Yan had just arrived in China a couple of days ago. First, to handle company business, and second, because he wanted to forcibly take Wen Yan back to Los Angeles.","The city of Haicheng brought him nothing but bad luck.","But before he could even finish his business, he received a call from the hospital saying his sister had been in an accident, was in a coma, and needed a family member present.","He rushed over without stopping, and the moment he saw Ji Zhiyuan, his heart sank to rock bottom.","Five years ago, his sister had hemorrhaged during childbirth and walked right up to death's door, all because of Ji Zhiyuan.","Five years later, his sister was in a coma in the hospital, and once again, it was because of Ji Zhiyuan.","Why did this man have to haunt them like a lingering ghost!","Filled with rage, Ke Yan raised his hand and threw another vicious punch.","Ji Zhiyuan didn't dodge.","Rong Yu didn't try to stop him either; she was a bit stunned.","If she hadn't misheard, Wen Yan's real name was Ke Man. She had heard the name Ke Man from Yingbao—it was the name of Duoduo's biological mother.","But!","Didn't Duoduo's biological mother pass away from an amniotic fluid embolism?","If Wen Yan was Ke Man, that meant Duoduo's mother was still alive. What on earth was going on?","Rong Yu still hadn't fully processed it.","Ke Yan's gaze fell on her. \"Ji Zhiyuan, you already have a girlfriend. Why are you still messing with my sister?\"","\"She is not my girlfriend,\" Ji Zhiyuan said, staring intently at him, enunciating every word. \"Regarding Wen Yan, shouldn't you be the one giving me an explanation?\""]},{"number":258,"title":"Chapter 258: You Have No Right to Know Anything About My Sister","paragraphs":["\"Explain?\" Ke Yan laughed out of sheer anger. \"What the hell gives you the right to demand an explanation from me?\"","When he was fifteen, his parents divorced. His father married his mistress, and his mother passed away from illness. He took over his mother's family business.","Ke Man was ten years younger than him. Back then, she was just a kindergartener. He raised her with his own hands. He would rather suffer himself than let his sister suffer the slightest grievance.","As Ke Man grew up, she was pursued by an increasing number of men.","Despite his reluctance to let her go, he carefully selected and asked around everywhere, finally choosing a brother-in-law who was perfect in every way, and arranged the marriage for Ke Man and that man.","However, on the night of her engagement, Ke Man disappeared. To be precise, she didn't just disappear; she ran away from her wedding. She left home, left Los Angeles, and returned to her mother's homeland, Haicheng.","By the time he found her in Haicheng, Ke Man told him that she had chosen a husband for herself—the CEO of Haicheng's Ji Group, Ji Zhiyuan.","He strongly opposed it, but his sister disregarded everything and got the marriage certificate. It was only at the wedding that he met this brother-in-law for the first time.","The Ji family's status was too high, and Ji Zhiyuan's appearance was too outstanding, making it hard for people to trust him.","Sure enough—","After marriage, Ji Zhiyuan subjected Ke Man to long-term emotional abuse, and it was rumored he still had a first love on the outside.","His perfectly fine sister, married into the Ji family, had been tortured into what state?","\"Let me tell you, you have no right to know anything about my sister!\" Ke Yan's anger boiled over. \"Get out of the way, I'm taking my sister home!\"","He shoved Ji Zhiyuan aside.","Suddenly, a little girl appeared, spreading her arms wide and standing in front of Ji Zhiyuan. \"You're not allowed to bully my daddy!\"","Ji Zhiyuan's heart softened.","He had neglected Duoduo for nearly five years and had only started to love her properly in the last six months, but she had always loved him earnestly.","His Duoduo, he owed her too much.","Meanwhile, Ke Yan stood frozen in place.","This girl looked almost exactly like Ke Man did when she was little—the same eyes, the same nose, the same mouth. Even her angry expression was carved from the exact same mold.","Was this the child his sister had narrowly escaped death to give birth to?","He despised Ji Zhiyuan, so over the years, he had never actively looked into anything regarding Duoduo. This was the first time he, her biological uncle, had ever seen Duoduo.","Ke Yan's lips pressed into a tight, straight line.","Without a word, he entered the hospital room, sat beside Ke Man, and whispered something.","Duoduo asked in a low voice, \"Daddy, who is that man? Why is he so weird, and what is his relationship with Aunt Wen?\"","Ji Zhiyuan paused. \"Don't call him that.\"","Duoduo nodded immediately. \"Right, he's a bad guy. He actually bullied my daddy.\"","\"He's not a bad guy,\" Ji Zhiyuan said, his voice hoarse. \"He just loves your mommy too much. He's your mommy's biological brother. He's your uncle.\"","\"What...\" Duoduo's eyes widened. \"I actually have an uncle? Why did Daddy never tell me?\"","Ji Zhiyuan didn't know how to answer.","Back then, when Ke Man suffered a massive hemorrhage during childbirth and was pronounced dead, Ke Yan beat him ruthlessly and took Ke Man's body away for burial. Since then, the two sides had no further contact.","Ke Yan refused to acknowledge this niece.","And naturally, Duoduo didn't need an extra uncle.","Rong Yu rubbed Duoduo's little head. \"Go inside and pour your uncle a glass of water.\"","Duoduo was still in a daze, but obediently walked inside.","Rong Yu looked at Ji Zhiyuan. \"Regardless of the truth back then, you were indeed too derelict in your duties as a husband. During the late stages of Duoduo's mother's pregnancy, Lan Yue happened to be born. You must have spent a lot of effort on Lan Yue, neglecting your pregnant wife. You can't blame Duoduo's uncle for being so furious.\"","Ji Zhiyuan said, \"At that time, Lan Rouxue and I didn't engage in any behavior that crossed the line. I absolutely did not forsake my marriage or betray my wife, I...\"","\"You don't need to explain these things to me,\" Rong Yu interrupted him. \"If you only want to give Duoduo a complete family, I don't recommend you have any emotional entanglement with Duoduo's mother. If you hope to start over, then however long you neglected her back then, you must spend double or even triple the time loving her to have the right to stand by her side. Think it over carefully.\"","She turned her head to look into the hospital room.","Little Duoduo poured a glass of water and handed it to Ke Yan. \"Uncle, drink some water.\"","Ke Yan had originally kept his face taut, but this single word \"Uncle\" directly broke his defenses. His throat trembled, and his eyes instantly turned red.","\"Huh, are you going to cry?\" Duoduo tilted her head to look at him. \"You're such a fierce person, can someone bully you too? Look at me, I'm so little, only five years old. I was kidnapped today and fell into the sea and almost died, but I didn't even cry...\"","At this point, she stuck her tongue out guiltily.","She had only cried for a little while, so it could probably be ignored.","Ke Yan's heart instantly melted. He raised his hand, lowered it, raised it again, and finally placed it on top of Duoduo's head, rubbing it gently. He sighed, \"How are you so cute?\"","Duoduo wasn't quite used to having her head patted by strangers. She quickly dodged and changed the subject, \"What is your relationship with Aunt Wen?\"","Ke Yan looked at his empty palm and smiled bitterly. \"I'm her biological brother.\"","Duoduo froze. \"Do you have a lot of sisters?\"","Ke Yan looked at her. \"Just this one.\"","Duoduo felt as if she had been struck by lightning.","Just now, Daddy had said that this person was her mother's biological brother.","And this person only had Aunt Wen as his sister.","So—","Duoduo's pupils shrank sharply. She whipped her head to look at the person lying on the bed and spoke in disbelief, \"Aunt Wen is my mommy?\"","Ke Yan's heart suddenly constricted.","His voice was hoarse. \"Yes, she is your mommy. Your biological mommy.\"","\"Mommy, mommy... So Aunt Wen really is my mommy...\"","Duoduo covered her lips.","Ke Yan thought she would ask why, or thought she would cry.","Instead, he saw the little girl run out of the hospital room, shouting loudly, \"Daddy, Auntie, I have a mommy! This is great! I have a mommy! It turns out I also have a mommy, I must be the happiest kid in the world...\"","Rong Yu gently wiped away a tear from the corner of her eye.","She thought of her own mother, an outstanding military doctor who was blown up by a shell while trying to save an injured soldier.","She missed her mommy too.","A tissue was suddenly handed to her from the side. She looked up and saw Sheng Qingyan.","From beginning to end, he had stayed by her side. Those glassy eyes of his seemed to only be able to see her.","\"Tomorrow, we go to the capital,\" she said. \"Maybe we can get back your lost soul and spirit.\"","When science didn't work, they could only try the metaphysical. Perhaps, after seeing his remains from his previous life, his soul might return to his body."]},{"number":259,"title":"Chapter 259: You Hired a Hypnotist to Seal My Memories","paragraphs":["Wen Yan's eyelids twitched as she lay in a coma.","Hearing the repeated cries of \"Mommy,\" her heartbeat involuntarily quickened.","Fragmented images in her mind slowly merged into a complete picture, and deeply buried memories began to surface.","She was Wen Yan, but she was also Ke Man.","When she was twenty-three, her eldest brother had arranged an engagement for her.","Her brother was too overbearing, completely disregarding her wishes. Knowing that resistance was futile, she ran away on the night of her engagement and fled to Haicheng.","On her second day in Haicheng, a classmate took her to a business reception. Her original intention was to find a job there, but because she drank too much, she entered the wrong room. By the time she woke up the next morning, she knew everything was ruined.","However, when she saw the man's face, she felt that perhaps heaven was looking out for her. It was actually her long-time crush.","She had first seen Ji Zhiyuan at an outstanding alumni speech in Los Angeles. Of course, she only knew him; he had no idea who she was. She had fallen in love at first sight and wrote about him in her diary.","He was a responsible man and immediately proposed marriage.","No one could refuse a proposal from the man of their dreams.","He was indeed a good husband. He would accompany her to prenatal checkups, remind her to take her medicine, and occasionally take walks with her... until Lan Rouxue got divorced and returned to the country heavily pregnant. Then, everything changed.","Ji Zhiyuan became incredibly busy.","He was always keeping Lan Rouxue company. Even though she knew he and Lan Rouxue had not crossed any lines, it was still hard for her to accept.","Later, when Lan Rouxue gave birth to a daughter, Ji Zhiyuan grew even busier...","As for her, she grew more silent and gained weight day by day. She cried every day and every night. She was in pain, miserable, and had no outlet for her emotions...","On the day she went into labor, she was taking a walk alone in the courtyard when her water suddenly broke. It was Old Master Ji who shouted for the servants to take her to the hospital.","She still remembered that the baby she gave birth to was fair, chubby, and incredibly cute. She had even kissed the baby's face. Then, suddenly, there was a massive hemorrhage... All her memories after that became chaotic and blurry...","Later on, she transformed from Ke Man into Wen Yan.","Mommy...","Mommy...","The repeated calls made Wen Yan snap her eyes open.","She felt a heavy weight on her chest. Looking down, she saw Duoduo asleep, resting against her.","You are finally awake. Ke Yan looked at her with great joy. Little sister, we will process your discharge tomorrow, and I will take you back home to Los Angeles.","Wen Yan gently stroked Duoduo's face. She couldn't get enough of looking at her, no matter how long she stared.","Her expression made Ke Yan's heart skip a beat. Little sister, you...","Brother, I remember now. Wen Yan's voice was very soft. Duoduo is my daughter, my biological daughter. I missed the most important five years of Duoduo's life.","Ke Yan was left speechless.","If he had never met Duoduo, he could have said all sorts of bad things about the child.","However, in the short half-day he had spent with Duoduo, he didn't even realize when he had grown fond of the little girl.","The thought that Duoduo had been without a mother for five whole years because of him made him feel a bit suffocated.","Brother, six years ago, you ignored my wishes and forced me to get engaged, so I ran away. Wen Yan's voice was hoarse. Five years ago, I suffered a massive hemorrhage during a difficult labor, but it wasn't life-threatening. Yet, to force me to leave the Ji family, you spun a massive lie. By the time I was out of danger, I was already in Los Angeles. You forbade me from returning to the country to see my daughter. You ordered me to forget Ji Zhiyuan and the baby, but I couldn't forget. So what did you do next?","She smiled bitterly. You hired a hypnotist to selectively seal away my memories and sent me for cosmetic micro-adjustments.","Ke Yan pressed his lips tightly together.","Hiring the hypnotist was an act of desperation because his little sister was in too much pain and couldn't forget her past in Haicheng.","After the hypnosis cleared her memories, everything went exactly as he had hoped.","But looking into Wen Yan's pained eyes, he couldn't help but reflect. Did he really do the wrong thing back then?","You always say it is for my own good. You always use your own way of thinking to control my life, never allowing me to have a single thought of my own. Wen Yan said softly. Back then, no matter where Ji Zhiyuan and I ended up, whether we continued the marriage or chose to divorce, whatever the outcome, it should have been a choice I made after careful consideration, not something you forcibly changed, brother.","Ke Yan's lips began to tremble. Little sister, I...","You care so much about me, brother, so why couldn't you spare a little sympathy for my daughter? Wen Yan's tears fell onto Duoduo's face. She was so tiny, yet she lost her mother. For five whole years, my daughter had no mother to accompany her. How envious she must have been of others... Brother, tell me, how am I supposed to forgive you?","Ke Yan couldn't utter a single word.","Wen Yan looked up and saw the man standing in the doorway.","Ji Zhiyuan had been standing there for a while. He stepped inside, his voice husky. Doctor Wen... no, Ke Man. I must apologize to you for my actions five years ago. It was because I failed in my duties as a husband and lost your trust that Mr. Ke made such a decision. Don't blame Mr. Ke. Blame me.","Lying in Wen Yan's arms, Duoduo rubbed her eyes and opened them. Upon seeing Wen Yan, she instantly became overjoyed. Wow, Mommy, you're awake! Oh, right, Mommy, let me tell you a secret. It turns out you really are my mommy! Daddy said so. You are my mommy, my real mommy. You are not allowed to leave me behind ever again, okay? Let's pinky promise...","Wen Yan smiled tenderly. Okay, pinky promise.","Ke Yan let out a defeated sigh.","He knew his little sister would never leave Haicheng now.","He stood up. Ji Zhiyuan, I will leave my sister in your care for now. I...","Before he could finish, Wen Yan interrupted him. Brother, I am Duoduo's mother, and I am an independent individual. I do not need you to hand me over to anyone.","Ke Yan paused, looking away. Since you have a stable job in Haicheng, I won't force you to return to Los Angeles. I will be leaving now.","If he didn't leave soon, he was afraid he wouldn't be able to control himself from forcibly taking his sister away.","The room suddenly fell quiet.","Ji Zhiyuan cleared his throat. Duoduo, it's already past eleven at night. Daddy will take you home to rest.","No! Duoduo hugged Wen Yan's neck tightly. I want to sleep here with Mommy. The mommies and daddies of my friends at kindergarten all sleep in the same bed. Daddy, you should come lie down too.","Ji Zhiyuan's face darkened. Stop this nonsense.","Deep down, Duoduo was still a little afraid of him. She immediately shrank into Wen Yan's embrace. Perhaps having her mother there made her braver, because she even secretly made a funny face at Ji Zhiyuan.","Ji Zhiyuan felt helpless. Then I will have to trouble Doctor Wen to look after Duoduo. I will come back tomorrow morning.","Wen Yan couldn't have asked for anything more. Don't worry, I will take good care of Duoduo.","The next morning, after staying at the hospital for a little while, Ji Zhiyuan went to see the elders off at the airport.","Rong Yu, Sheng Qingyan, Sheng Ciyuan, and Old Master Ji, who had insisted on tagging along, boarded a flight to Beijing.","During the three days he had stayed at the Ji family residence, Sheng Ciyuan had clearly noticed that his eldest brother was acting more and more like a normal person.","His brother would communicate normally with Rong Yu.","His brother would have staring contests with Old Master Ji.","His brother would teach Ji Zhouye how to do math problems.","His brother would lift Duoduo up high in the air.","He believed the master's words that his older brother would definitely recover during his zodiac year.","Perhaps going to pay his respects to the remains of the fallen heroes aboard the Zhenhua would be the turning point..."]},{"number":260,"title":"Chapter 260: Old Master Ji Sandwiched Between Rong Yu and Sheng Qingyan","paragraphs":["The plane arrived at the Beijing airport.","The Sheng family's driver was already waiting at the entrance.","Sheng Ciyuan spoke up, \"The Beijing Archaeological Center isn't far from the Sheng family residence. Rong Yu, why don't you stay at my house for the night?\"","\"Stay, stay, stay, what's there to stay for!\" Old Master Ji said grumpily. \"Our Ji family has a massive business and multiple properties in Beijing. We don't need to stay at someone else's house. It's not very con...\"","\"It is convenient,\" Rong Yu smiled and rubbed her old son's head. \"We're staying at the Sheng family's house. Be good.\"","The last time she went to the Sheng residence was for a banquet, so she knew very little about everything there.","Now that she had confirmed Sheng Qingyan's identity, she wanted to understand the Sheng family on a deeper level. She wanted to know what kind of family he lived in during this lifetime.","Old Master Ji had absolutely no resistance and obediently nodded.","Having stayed at the Ji family's house for three days, Sheng Ciyuan saw scenes like this almost every day. Even so, it still made his eyes hurt.","He really couldn't understand why Old Master Ji acted like a child in front of Miss Rong. Could it be that Old Master Ji was suffering from Alzheimer's disease?","But Old Master Ji was full of energy every day, bouncing up and down without the slightest sign of being ill.","Unable to figure it out, Sheng Ciyuan stopped thinking about it. He immediately sent a message to his family, informing them that distinguished guests were arriving soon.","Old Madam Sheng was drinking tea. Seeing the message from her youngest grandson, she stood up abruptly in excitement, \"Miss Rong and Old Master Ji are coming to our Sheng family as guests, and they even agreed to stay the night! This is wonderful, truly wonderful...\"","For the past two days, she had been watching the videos Yuan'er sent from Haicheng with her meals every day.","Her Yan'er seemed like a completely different person at the Ji family's house in Haicheng. Apart from speaking a bit less, he was absolutely no different from a normal person.","The Ji family must be the serendipity the master had spoken of.","\"Butler, hurry, go hire a state banquet chef.\" Old Madam Sheng eagerly began making arrangements. \"The decoration in the largest guest room is too stiff. Have someone redecorate it in a style that an eighteen-year-old girl would like. Prepare another sunny room for Old Master Ji to stay in. I don't know what he likes, so go look it up online...\"","Sheng Dian was inspecting a construction site.","Madam Sheng, Xu Lu, was accompanying him.","The two received a call from the Old Madam and rushed home without stopping. As soon as they stepped through the door, they were shoved brand-new evening wear, \"Hurry up and change. Don't let them think our Sheng family doesn't value our distinguished guests.\"","Sheng Dian looked bewildered, \"Who is coming? The Party Secretary?\"","Madam Sheng, Xu Lu, spoke up, \"Why would the Secretary suddenly visit? Did something happen?\"","\"It's none of that,\" Old Madam Sheng waved her hand. \"It's Rong Yu and Old Master Ji. They are coming to stay at our Sheng house for the night. Yan'er and Yuan'er stayed at the Ji family's house for three days and received high-standard hospitality, which is why Yan'er's condition has improved. Our Sheng family must host these distinguished guests properly; we must treat this as a top priority!\"","The car parked at the entrance of the Sheng family mansion.","When the main gates opened, Rong Yu was almost scared off by the grand display before her.","Even Sheng Ciyuan was stunned.","What on earth was wrong with his family? Why were they wearing such formal evening gowns at home?","Not only that, but even the household servants had all changed into neat formal attire. Standing in a row, they chorused, \"Welcome, Old Master Ji. Welcome, Miss Rong.\"","\"Old Master Ji, Miss Rong, welcome, welcome!\" Old Madam Sheng greeted them. \"Are you tired from the journey? Are you thirsty? Are you hungry...\"","Sheng Dian stepped aside, \"Please come inside.\"","Xu Lu instructed the butler, \"You may start serving the dishes.\"","Rong Yu asked in a low voice, \"Ciyuan, does your family always put on such a huge display for guests?\"","Sheng Ciyuan covered his face, \"Of course not. It's only like this for you.\"","In the dining room, Rong Yu looked at the table full of dishes comparable to an imperial feast and fell deep into thought.","Old Master Ji snorted coldly and whispered to Rong Yu, \"Mom, these are all sugar-coated bullets. It's superficial enthusiasm just to trick you into becoming their daughter-in-law. I don't have any objections to you dating, but if it comes to marriage, I think you should consider it carefully. After all, you have a huge burden like me...\"","\"Alright, say less,\" Rong Yu patted his arm. \"If you keep grumbling, I won't bring you along when I go out anymore.\"","Old Master Ji instantly behaved.","\"This is scallion braised sea cucumber, using wild sea cucumber from the Bohai Bay. It's exceptionally fresh.\" Old Madam Sheng was full of enthusiasm. \"This is truffle foie gras, air-freighted from France. You top scholars use your brains a lot, so you need nourishment. Come, try this bowl... Old Master Ji, don't be polite, please eat too.\"","During the meal, the Old Madam continuously served food to Rong Yu, piling her bowl into a small mountain.","Halfway through the meal, Madam Sheng, Xu Lu, asked curiously, \"Miss Rong, I heard that you are also fluent in five languages?\"","Rong Yu smiled, \"I only know a little, I wouldn't call it fluent.\"","\"Miss Rong is too modest,\" Sheng Dian spoke up. \"I've seen the live video. Miss Rong converses fluently with standard pronunciation. You can definitely be called fluent. To be able to learn the languages of so many countries while doing scientific research is worthy of praise.\"","\"Of course,\" Old Master Ji couldn't help but say. \"These past two days, the diplomacy professors from Jingbei University even went to Haicheng No. 1 High School to recruit her...\"","His mom became famous overnight after that battle in Hong Kong.","Not to mention how famous she was in the entertainment industry.","In the academic circle, physics, mathematics, engineering, diplomacy... major universities and major departments all extended olive branches.","It was a pity that his mom had long decided to go to Huaqing University for aerospace engineering, making him miss the chance to see those professors fight over his mom...","After dinner ended.","Rong Yu was pulled into a room by Old Madam Sheng, \"Miss Rong, these are my collections from decades of my life. Do you like this bracelet? These gemstone earrings are treasures from the Qing Dynasty royal family, try them on. How about this pearl pendant, you...\"","\"Old Madam, there's no need for this,\" Rong Yu quickly stood up. \"The moonlight is quite nice tonight. Um, I'll go out to admire the moon first.\"","Sheng Qingyan followed behind her like a shadow, completely inseparable.","Old Master Ji suddenly felt a bit jealous because he was, after all, the head of a family and cared about his face. So, in the Sheng family, he couldn't act like a child.","Meanwhile, because Sheng Qingyan had autism, nothing he did seemed strange.","There was an open-air pavilion in the Sheng family's courtyard, a perfect spot to sit and admire the moon. As soon as Rong Yu sat down, Sheng Qingyan followed suit.","Old Master Ji stood on the side, curling his lips.","Rong Yu waved, \"Yingbao, come over and admire the moon together.\"","Old Master Ji glanced around him. Seeing no one, he immediately started acting up, curling his lips and saying, \"It's just a bare moon, what's there to admire?\"","Sheng Qingyan suddenly stood up, giving up his seat, and said clearly, \"Yingbao, you sit.\"","\"What did you call me?\" The old man instantly flared up. \"How old are you, and how old am I? In my eyes, you're just a little brat. Who allowed you to call me by my childhood name? It's impolite, disrespectful to your elders, dis...\"","Halfway through his words, Rong Yu gave him a pull, dragging him to the middle seat.","Old Master Ji was sandwiched between Rong Yu and Sheng Qingyan, unable to move.","\"Smile.\"","Rong Yu took out her phone and snapped a group photo of the three of them."]},{"number":261,"title":"Chapter 261: This pocket watch is the token of love between my parents.","paragraphs":["The Sheng family's tearoom faced the pavilion perfectly.","Old Madam Sheng's face was full of excitement: Look, Yan'er smiled. Our Yan'er actually knows how to smile. Who said he was a block of wood? He can smile. How could someone who smiles be a block of wood? Thank heavens...","Xu Lu wiped away her tears and said, Yan'er is completely different in front of Miss Rong. Miss Rong must be Yan'er's destined match. Why don't the Sheng family prepare a bit and propose marriage to the Rong family?","Sheng Dian's face immediately darkened: Miss Rong is a great benefactor to the Sheng family. Your action would be biting the hand that feeds us, understand?","It's a bit too much for you to say that. No matter what, Yan'er is still our biological son, Xu Lu said. If it's as the master said, Yan'er will return to normal in his zodiac year. Even so, is he still not good enough for Miss Rong?","Sheng Dian fell silent for a moment.","Naturally, he isn't good enough, Old Madam Sheng spoke up. Miss Rong is a gold medalist in the global physics competition, a genius admitted early to Huaqing University, and a key research project leader at the Aerospace Institute... What does Yan'er have? He only has the Sheng family. His title is the eldest young master of the Sheng family, but without the Sheng family, he is nothing. He needs to have his own career, his own field, before he can be qualified to stand beside Miss Rong.","The old lady delivered a strong wave of opinions, then suddenly froze.","She used to pray to the Bodhisattva every day, just hoping that Yan'er could be like a normal person. But now, she was actually starting to fantasize about Yan'er having his own career... She was really going crazy.","The moonlight was cold and clear, and the night slowly passed.","Rong Yu had a good night's sleep at the Sheng family home.","After breakfast in the morning, they had to head to the archaeological center. Old Madam Sheng wanted to go, but Sheng Dian stopped her: When you were young, you loved attending various state banquets and grand occasions, and you were often on TV. Too many people in the capital recognize you. It's better if you don't go to that kind of place and cause trouble. Just let Yuan'er tag along.","Sheng Ciyuan immediately said, With eldest brother following me, you guys can rest assured.","Sheng Dian drove, personally escorting the group over.","Min Jianshen was waiting at the main entrance of the archaeological center: Because they are remains, they are kept underground after being transported back to the country. Put on these clothes first and follow me in.","Rong Yu and her group put on protective suits and followed Min Jianshen, slowly descending the metal stairs.","Under the dim lights, the walls of the corridor were mottled with bullet holes. Rusted guns and shattered steel helmets lay quietly in glass display cases. Walking into the special identification room, thirteen remains covered with the national flag were neatly arranged on a constant-temperature platform. The air was filled with the scent of dust and time, so heavy that it made it hard to breathe.","As soon as she entered this space, Rong Yu's mood instantly hit rock bottom, filled with an inexplicable sense of grief and indignation.","She held her son's hand and said softly, Yingbao, I originally didn't want you to come, but you really should see your father once. Don't be too sad, keep a calm mind.","Old Master Ji's voice trembled slightly: I know, don't worry about me.","Rong Yu noticed that since entering this place, Sheng Qingyan's mood had become a bit restless.","She could understand.","But, she didn't know how to handle it either.","She gently held his fingers, giving him strength, hoping that he could find his origin here...","Now we will begin confirming the list of martyrs, Min Jianshen picked up a booklet and said. The soldiers who escorted this group of overseas students back to the country that year totaled thirty-eight, and thirteen remains have been recovered... According to preserved historical data and analysis of the remains' characteristics, the first one from the left is the captain of the third squad of the Navy's special escort team that escorted the third batch of overseas students back, Chen Zhiyuan.","His white-gloved hand carefully turned over the carbonized identification tag. This is the ID found in the volcanic soil layer. There should be no dispute about the identity of the first remains.","The staff beside him immediately recorded it.","Rong Yu's nose tingled with sorrow.","Memories of the past instantly flooded back, and her tears rolled down in large drops.","On the cruise ship back home, Chen Zhiyuan had said that what he missed the most was the chirping of cicadas in his hometown. He even planned to go back and catch cicada pupae after this mission ended, to bring them over for them to taste.","However, he drove a small escort boat and blocked a torpedo for the cruise ship.","He died a heroic death at the age of twenty-three.","Don't cry.","Sheng Qingyan's hoarse voice sounded.","He clumsily raised his hand and wiped away Rong Yu's tears.","Rong Yu suppressed her emotions and listened carefully as Min Jianshen continued to confirm the identities of the martyrs: The second from the left is...","At this moment, her gaze was suddenly attracted by an object on the chest of the seventh set of remains.","It was a pocket watch half-buried in the uniform fibers. The watch chain was rusted and broken, but the intertwined peony pattern on the gilded cover was still clearly visible under the light.","Rong Yu uncontrollably reached out her hand, her fingers touching that pocket watch.","Stop. A young archaeological team member shouted sternly. Do not touch the remains! This is a great disrespect to the heroic spirits!","As soon as the words fell, Old Master Ji suddenly began to tremble violently. The old man's wrinkled hand took out a pocket watch from his inner jacket pocket, the intertwined peony pattern showing the exact same texture under the light.","The gazes of everyone present instantly swept over.","Min Jianshen's gaze was heavy, and he spoke slowly: These remains belong to Ji Zheng, the commander of the Navy's special escort team temporarily established during the Republic of China era.","He is my father. Old Master Ji's voice choked with sobs. This pocket watch is a token of love between my parents. My mother's pocket watch is still here, but my father's has already...","The old man's hand gently stroked the pocket watch, stroking the remaining gold threads on the epaulets of the remains. Those were marks that had not faded even after being buried underground for over seventy years; they were the glory belonging to a warrior.","Dad... Old Master Ji's tears flowed freely. The students you escorted back then all returned home safely. The Zhang family's child became a bridge expert, the Zhao family's child built the first tractor, and my mother became one of China's first-generation mathematicians. There are many, many others who devoted themselves to building the nation, making our China stronger day by day, finally standing at the pinnacle of the world...","It was unknown who raised their hand first, but the staff wearing white coats in the entire identification room stood at attention and saluted one by one.","Rong Yu gently stroked her son's back, afraid that he would faint from being too emotional.","She wasn't paying attention for a moment.","Sheng Qingyan, who was beside her, strode forward and walked to the very front.","The archaeologists thought he was also a descendant of the martyr Ji Zheng, so they didn't do much to stop him.","He first picked up that rust-spotted pocket watch.","Immediately after, he looked at the remains lying there. His glass-like eyes seemed to be injected with something, surging wildly.","His hand suddenly grasped the hand of the remains.","This pair of hands! That pair of hands! Grasping tightly pair by pair, letting go, and grasping tightly again...","No! You can't do this! Min Jianshen hurriedly went to stop him. You can't touch them, it will damage the remains. Rong Yu, quickly hold him back...","Before he could finish his sentence.","Suddenly.","Sheng Qingyan let out a sound and spat out a mouthful of black blood.","Sheng Ciyuan was shocked: Eldest brother! What's wrong with you, eldest brother!"]},{"number":262,"title":"Chapter 262: He Didn't Know What He Was Expecting","paragraphs":["Capital Military Region Hospital.","Sheng Qingyan was rushed into the emergency room. His heart rate was dangerously high, nearly threatening his life, and he was currently undergoing emergency resuscitation.","Old Madam Sheng collapsed into Sheng Dian's arms, weeping bitterly.","Xu Lu leaned against Sheng Ciyuan, crying silently.","Sheng Dian spoke up, \"Yan'er just has a rapid heart rate, it's a minor issue. Don't cry so hard that you actually make yourselves sick.\"","Old Master Ji turned his head and looked at Rong Yu, who was standing in the shadows.","The old man sighed, truly unable to understand why his mother was so worried about this kid, Sheng Qingyan.","Perhaps because his mother was worried, and due to the telepathic connection between mother and son, he actually found himself fearing that something might happen to Sheng Qingyan too.","\"How could he go to a place like that!\" A man in his thirties rushed into the hospital. \"That kind of place, to put it nicely, is a memorial hall for martyrs' remains. To put it bluntly, how is it any different from a funeral parlor, a crematorium, or a graveyard? If you ask me, Yan'er was possessed by something unclean, which is why...\"","\"Nonsense!\"","Old Madam Sheng was furious. She raised her hand and slapped him.","This was her youngest son, Sheng Yun.","With trembling lips, the old woman scolded, \"Your father was a martyr. Your words insult the martyrs and insult your own father. It is highly disrespectful! Besides, aren't you a soldier yourself? Is it appropriate for you to say such things?\"","Sheng Yun quickly hid behind Sheng Dian. \"Mom, I'm just worried about Yan'er. He's your lifeblood. If something happens to him, wouldn't our Sheng family be thrown into chaos?\"","Just then, the doctor came out of the emergency room, and a large group of people immediately swarmed him.","The doctor took off his mask and said, \"The patient is out of danger, but we are not sure exactly when he will wake up.\"","\"Thank goodness, thank goodness.\" Old Madam Sheng breathed a sigh of relief and pressed, \"Have you found the cause of the attack?\"","The doctor frowned. \"The current results show that extreme emotional agitation caused the rapid heart rate. However, under normal circumstances, it wouldn't lead to such severe consequences, let alone in a patient this young. We ask the family to observe him closely moving forward. If there are any abnormalities, bring him in for treatment immediately.\"","Old Madam Sheng committed his words to memory.","Sheng Qingyan was wheeled out of the emergency room by the nurses.","His face was completely devoid of color, lying there like a blank sheet of paper. It was as if a wall had been erected around him; even when Old Madam Sheng rushed over, it felt as though she and he were not in the same dimension.","Rong Yu's lips were pressed tightly together.","She just looked at him like that. Her mind suddenly went blank—thinking about everything, yet thinking about nothing at all.","\"Mom...\"","Old Master Ji quietly held her hand.","Rong Yu squeezed his hand in return.","Suddenly, she saw the eyelashes of the person on the bed flutter. She quickly walked to the bedside and called out softly, \"Sheng Qingyan, I am Rong Yu, you...\"","Halfway through her sentence, she was pushed aside by Sheng Yun. \"No, who are you?\"","Smack—","Old Madam Sheng slapped the back of his hand.","She frowned. \"Who told you to come to the hospital? You haven't helped at all, only caused trouble. This is Miss Rong, Yan'er's savior and an honored guest of the Sheng family. If you keep up this attitude, get out.\"","Sheng Yun narrowed his eyes, sizing up Rong Yu.","His gaze was too brazen, earning him another heavy blow from Old Madam Sheng.","\"He's awake, Yan'er is awake!\" Xu Lu's voice rang out. \"Yan'er, how do you feel? Are you uncomfortable anywhere?\"","Sheng Yun facepalmed. \"How would he know what being uncomfortable means? Asking him is pointless.\"","On the bed, Sheng Qingyan slowly opened his eyes. His pitch-black pupils were like a night sky washed by rain, incredibly clear. They were no longer the glassy eyes of the past, which had seemed covered by a layer of gauze.","Those eyes first looked at Xu Lu, who was closest.","\"Mom.\"","The man's thin lips slowly uttered this single word.","The moment the word fell, the entire ward plunged into a dead silence.","Xu Lu covered her mouth as tears streamed down her face. \"Yan'er, what... what did you just call me?\"","She knew Yan'er could speak now.","But—","It had been limited to only when he was in front of Miss Rong.","Furthermore, it was usually Miss Rong asking questions and him answering.","He never spoke on his own initiative, much less voluntarily addressed anyone.","In the twenty-four years Yan'er had been alive, this was the very first time he had opened his mouth to call her 'Mom'.","\"Dad.\"","Sheng Qingyan then called out again.","Sheng Dian's eyes widened abruptly. \"Yan'er, you, you, you...\"","\"Move aside.\" Old Madam Sheng shoved him away and rushed to the bed. \"Yan'er, do you recognize me? I'm your grandmother. I'm your grandmother.\"","\"Grandmother,\" Sheng Qingyan spoke softly. \"Grandmother's hair has gone completely white. I'm sorry, I've made Grandmother worry.\"","How could Old Madam Sheng handle this? Her tears flowed down like a running faucet. \"It doesn't matter if my hair is white, it doesn't matter at all. As long as you can get better, Yan'er, Grandmother would even give up her life. Yan'er, quickly tell Grandmother, you...\"","\"Ah, there's me too!\" Sheng Yun eagerly leaned his head in. \"Yan'er, do you recognize me?\"","Sheng Qingyan said, \"Uncle.\"","\"It seems you've really returned to normal!\" Sheng Yun was overjoyed. \"The Sheng family's ancestors were in the military, and the old lady insisted that I inherit the family legacy. But I don't have the talent! I've been in the military region all these years and I'm still just muddling along, losing face for the Sheng family. I haven't wanted to do it for a long time. Now that Yan'er has become a normal person, let's leave the Sheng family's legacy to him to inherit and glorify!\"","\"Uncle, it's way too early for you to be saying this.\" Sheng Ciyuan stepped forward and scratched his head, saying, \"Big Brother.\"","Sheng Qingyan looked at him and said, \"These past few years, it's been hard on you cleaning up my messes.\"","\"It hasn't been hard, not hard at all.\" Sheng Ciyuan felt a bit embarrassed and quickly pulled Rong Yu over. \"Big Brother's illness getting better is all thanks to Miss Rong.\"","It was as if Sheng Qingyan had only just noticed Rong Yu.","His eyes were no longer hazy like before, but clear as a freezing pool, reflecting Rong Yu's figure—unfamiliar and lucid.","His gaze slid down from her eyes and brows, swept past her tightly pressed lips, and finally rested on the hand she used to hold a pocket watch.","His expression suddenly grew complex.","He had memories regarding the pocket watch in his mind.","At the Ji family home.","At the remains memorial hall.","As for anything more, there was nothing.","But recalling it now, these matters felt very unfamiliar, yet he carried an almost instinctive desire to investigate them.","He clearly knew her.","But it felt like it shouldn't be this kind of knowing.","Where had things gone wrong?","Sheng Qingyan looked at her for a long time before finally speaking, \"Miss Rong.\"","Then he looked at the person beside her, \"Old Mr. Ji.\"","His voice was hoarse. \"Recently, I've been a bother to Miss Rong and Old Mr. Ji.\"","Old Master Ji couldn't help but frown.","For some reason, he felt that Sheng Qingyan shouldn't have this attitude. Something seemed off.","He didn't know what he had been expecting.","He only knew that his expectations had fallen through.","But Rong Yu knew.","Her voice was steady: \"Do you know Ji Zheng?\"","\"I know of him,\" Sheng Qingyan replied. \"He was the commander of the Navy's Special Escort Team. He died a heroic death and is a martyr.\"","He paused for a moment and looked up at the Sheng family. \"Dad, Mom, please help donate all the historical artifacts in our family's collection gallery to the National History Museum.\""]},{"number":263,"title":"Chapter 263: Let's Reintroduce Ourselves: My Name is Rong Yu","paragraphs":["The ward was completely silent.","The Sheng family exchanged glances.","Ever since Sheng Qingyan was four years old, he had subconsciously begun collecting those historical artifacts. A photograph, a piece of clothing, a scroll... These were all the objects that sustained Sheng Qingyan's life. Relying on these things, he built a massive historical world in his heart, absorbing nutrients from within it.","He never allowed anyone to touch those things.","Those in the Sheng family who were a bit distant from him, such as his young uncle Sheng Yun, did not even have the right to enter the collection room, let alone the servants.","Even the dusting and cleaning of the collection room were done entirely by Sheng Qingyan himself.","He was incredibly careful, treating those artifacts as precious treasures.","In the past, Old Madam Sheng disliked her eldest grandson being obsessed with these things every day, because being too immersed in the historical world caused his autism to worsen.","Now, when her eldest grandson proposed donating all his precious treasures, she subconsciously felt a bit reluctant.","What if one day her eldest grandson relapsed? These artifacts were his life-saving medicine.","\"Yan'er, are you serious?\" Xu Lu's face was full of disbelief. \"Are you sure you want to donate them all?\"","Sheng Qingyan spoke slowly, \"Museums have temperature and humidity-controlled display cabinets, and molecular-level restoration technology. Only experts can perfectly replicate that history, a history that proves even in this nation's darkest moments, there were still people willing to protect knowledge and civilization with their lives.\"","\"Well said!\"","Sheng Dian was overjoyed. These words, spoken so clearly and logically, were enough to prove that his eldest son was indeed no different from a normal person.","Rong Yu watched him quietly.","Although he had recovered a piece of his soul, he had not regained the memories of his past life.","Because she had expectations.","So, it was inevitable that she felt a bit disappointed.","However, didn't this fit scientific logic better?","If everyone in this world remembered their relatives from their past lives after reincarnating, wouldn't it be total chaos?","From another perspective, perhaps this was for the best.","He would no longer remember his biological mother being held down tightly in the muddy water by the Japanese invaders, her hair scattered like broken duckweed. Her fingers had dug into the mud of the riverbank, yet she never called out his or his comrades' names. It wasn't until the last bubble disappeared from the water's surface that the enemy smirked and released their foot...","He would no longer remember his squad leader, at the dawn when they ran out of ammunition and food, stuffing a blood-stained party ID into his arms. To protect him and his comrades, the squad leader had carried a satchel charge and charged into the enemy camp, while he carried his unconscious comrade on his back, breaking through the encirclement over a ground littered with severed limbs...","He would no longer remember when over a dozen young lives rushed toward the machine gun nest arm in arm, those familiar figures disappearing one by one in the hail of bullets, until finally, he was pushed into a bomb crater, his face covered in blood...","He had awakened from nightmares countless times.","He had slashed his wrists with a military knife countless times.","He often sat in the dark night until dawn...","But history had not given him the right to break down. There were always new teammates, always losses, always healing, always walking on an endless revolutionary path...","Rong Yu smiled and gently wiped the corner of her eye.","He had lost his painful memories.","He now had a family that loved him.","She so hoped—","That those heroic souls who never got to hear the horn of victory could experience this peaceful, bustling world.","That those young faces forever frozen in black-and-white photos could reincarnate into this beautiful land they had exchanged their lives for.","\"Miss Rong, what's wrong?\"","Old Madam Sheng noticed her emotional state and, temporarily ignoring her eldest grandson, quickly handed her a tissue.","Rong Yu shook her head and said, \"I'm fine.\"","To be able to reunite in this prosperous era.","How could this not be a gift from God?","She looked at Sheng Qingyan, \"Let's get to know each other again. My name is Rong Yu.\"","Sheng Qingyan sat up, \"My name is Sheng Qingyan.\"","He was very proper and exceptionally serious.","Rong Yu suddenly wanted to laugh.","So when he and she first met, he was this aloof. Compared to the person who was super clingy every time they met later, it was like night and day.","Sheng Qingyan watched her smile.","A massive surge of unfamiliar emotion inexplicably rose and fermented in his chest, completely beyond his control... It was as if a few small sprouts had instantly grown into a towering tree, its lush branches and leaves forcefully occupying his entire heart.","\"Buzz, buzz!\"","Old Master Ji's phone began to vibrate.","\"Hello, are you a descendant of Ji Zheng? Ji Zheng's remains have been... Please come to the Capital Martyrs' Square tomorrow at 3:00 PM to attend the posthumous award ceremony.\"","Old Master Ji immediately replied, \"Alright.\"","He instantly called all his grandsons. For such a major event, the entire Ji family had to be present.","Rong Yu took one last look at Sheng Qingyan, \"Goodbye.\"","In her era, goodbye most likely meant never seeing each other again.","But in this prosperous era, goodbye simply meant see you again. She looked forward to their next meeting.","Old Madam Sheng stood up to see them out and strongly invited the two of them to come as guests to the Sheng family again next time.","Rong Yu smiled and agreed.","Ji Mohan's car was waiting at the hospital entrance. He respectfully carried the bags for the two elders and drove to Ji Yanting's large flat in the capital.","By nightfall, all the descendants of the Ji family had arrived.","Ji Zhiyuan, Ji Yanting, Ji Mohan, Ji Jingchuan, Ji Zhouye, and the youngest generation's Duoduo.","Old Master Ji said, \"This flat is still a bit too small. Yuan, didn't you buy a few villas in the capital a few years ago? Get someone to tidy up the largest one, and have the garden designed too. When your great-grandmother comes to the capital to attend university in a while, she'll have a place to stay.\"","Ji Zhiyuan couldn't help but ask, \"If great-grandmother comes to the capital for university, are you going to move in too, Old Master?\"","\"Of course.\" Old Master Ji looked entirely justified. \"If a child doesn't follow their mother, then tell me, who should they follow?\"","Ji Zhiyuan rubbed his forehead.","A seventy-eight-year-old child, only the Old Master was thick-skinned enough to say such a thing out loud.","Old Master Ji, afraid of being rejected by his own mother, hurriedly spoke up, \"Yan has a studio in the capital, Mo is at the materials institute here, and later Chuan and Ye will also apply for universities in the capital. It's perfect for us to look out for each other, right, Mom?\"","Duoduo felt wronged, \"What about me, Great-Grandpa? Are you going to leave me all alone in Haicheng?\"","\"You silly girl, how are you alone?\" Old Master Ji gently tapped her nose. \"You have a father, and now you have a mother too. You are the happiest child in our Ji family.\"","For the past few generations of the Ji family, they were either orphans or raised by single parents. Every one of them grew up soaked in bitterness.","Duoduo had suffered for a few years, but now she finally had both her parents.","Duoduo pursed her lips and smiled.","Actually, her family treated her very well, and her aunt treated her even better, but it still wasn't the same as having a mother.","A mother is a mother, an existence in this world that no one else can replace.","The next day.","Everyone in the Ji family changed into solemn black attire and drove to the Capital Martyrs' Square.","At six o'clock in the morning at the Martyrs' Square, the white marble monument loomed in the morning light, like an unsheathed sword.","Thirty-six honor guards were slowly approaching, carrying a coffin draped in the national flag. The sunlight pierced through the clouds, illuminating the mottled dents on the coffin.","The Ji family group converged with the other relatives.","However, for many of the martyrs, no descendants could be traced at all. They had never married and left no children behind...","The families walked inside, and the posthumous awarding ceremony officially began.","On the street across from the Martyrs' Square sat a parked car. The driver, Sheng Yun, the youngest uncle of the Sheng family, looked at the person in the passenger seat and said, \"Yan'er, these martyrs belong to a period of history you were once obsessed with. If you wish to attend the ceremony, with the Sheng family's status in the capital, you'd only need to say the word to get inside.\"","Sheng Qingyan clutched his chest.","He didn't understand why his heart was pounding so violently, as if resonating with something unseen.","He sat there for a long moment until his racing heart gradually settled. In a quiet voice, he said, \"Uncle, let's go to the military district.\"","His life was only just beginning at twenty-four, far later than anyone else's. He needed to spend more time to bridge the gap and catch up."]},{"number":264,"title":"Chapter 264: Tang Jin Officially Becomes the Heir of the Tang Family","paragraphs":["After flying back to Haicheng from the capital, Rong Yu once again threw herself into her scientific research.","In the blink of an eye, the day of Ji Jingchuan and Tang Jin's engagement arrived.","The engagement banquet was scheduled for Saturday. On Friday, Ji Jingchuan and Ji Zhouye still had to participate in the monthly exam at Haicheng First High School, taking tests until nine o'clock in the evening before returning home.","\"Today's exam papers were too easy; I can definitely make the top ten in my class!\" Ji Zhouye sat down smugly next to Rong Yu. \"Great-grandma, if I make the top ten, what do you say?\"","Rong Yu: \"What do you want?\"","As long as she didn't mention extra study materials like the Huanggang mock exams, Ji Zhouye was excited. He rubbed his hands together: \"How about increasing my allowance a bit? Or, buy me the latest gaming console. It's not expensive, just over a hundred thousand.\"","Old Master Ji rolled his eyes at him: \"That's not a lot? Do you think our family's money grows on trees?\"","Right now, he didn't even have ten thousand yuan of pocket money to his name.","\"How is a hundred thousand a lot!\" Ji Zhouye protested. \"Then please tell me, Old Master, between our Ji family and the Si family, who is more powerful?\"","Old Master Ji scoffed: \"Nonsense, of course it's the Ji family. That old dog Si only managed to squeeze into the four great families by relying on his ancestors' coat-tails.\"","Ji Zhouye pursed his lips in grievance: \"But the Si family's young master, Si Lin, spent five million customizing a smart robot dog just a couple of days ago to support his girlfriend's career. And me? I can't even get a hundred thousand.\"","\"What dog costs five million?\" Old Master Ji's eyes widened. \"This world has finally gone crazy in ways I can't even recognize!\"","\"Smart dogs have been popular for a while now. Yingbao, you should watch the news more often in your spare time so you don't fall behind the times.\" Rong Yu frowned. \"However, even the most cutting-edge customized smart dog wouldn't cost more than a million. Si Lin got scammed.\"","Old Master Ji chuckled: \"Old Si's little bit of family fortune will sooner or later be squandered by these prodigal sons.\"","Rong Yu cast a glance at him.","This old guy still had the nerve to talk about others. If she hadn't been lucky enough to transmigrate here, the Ji family would probably have gone bankrupt before the Si family.","She changed the subject. \"Chuan, come and take a look at tomorrow's engagement schedule. The process is quite tedious, and you'll have to change into three different outfits. Take a look at this...\"","Hearing this, Ji Zhouye knew that his reward was out of the question.","Forget it. Once the monthly exam results were out, he would take his report card to her, and he refused to believe his great-grandma wouldn't buy him that gaming console.","The engagement banquet was held on a small island.","Ji Jingchuan and Tang Jin, along with Hai Chang'an and Tang Mi, were getting engaged on the same day. Three of Haicheng's four great families were involved. The entire island had been completely redecorated, radiating a festive atmosphere everywhere.","When Rong Yu and her old son arrived, many people were already there. Tang Che was sitting in a wheelchair, watching her from afar.","Recently, Tang Che's health had been failing more and more. She would frequently bring Yingbao to the Tang family home to sit with him for a while. At first, Tang Che could chat with her for half a day and even play a few games of chess, but these past few days, he had been growing increasingly drowsy.","However, Tang Che was in very good spirits today.","\"A'Yu,\" Tang Che said with a smile. \"Come sit.\"","Rong Yu sat down beside him.","As soon as she sat down, she heard her old son actually arguing with Hai Dadun and Sima Gang. The three old buddies were going back and forth, bickering with each other.","Elder Si: \"Tsk tsk, young people's weddings these days are so flashy. Back when I married my wife, I carried her on my back for ten miles, and that was considered crossing the threshold!\"","Elder Hai: \"That's because your parents found it too troublesome. Back in my day, I at least borrowed a donkey.\"","Old Master Ji: \"When I got married, I picked up my bride on a bicycle! A brand new twenty-eight-inch frame! Sponsored by Uncle Tang!\"","Elder Si: \"What's so great about a bicycle? My Si Lin is currently driving a globally limited edition car. There are only five of them in the world, and he managed to snag one. Do you guys have that?\"","Elder Hai: \"Tsk, no wonder that brat Si Lin dares to be so wasteful. It turns out he has you, you old geezer, helping him swipe the card.\"","Old Master Ji: \"When the Si family goes bankrupt, don't come crying to us.\"","Elder Si said angrily: \"You guys are just jealous!\"","Elder Hai: \"Stop your whining. Look, the new couples are coming out. My family's Chang'an is truly handsome.\"","Old Master Ji narrowed his eyes: \"Not even half as good-looking as Chuan.\"","Elder Hai: \"Bullshit! Chang'an is clearly more handsome.\"","Old Master Ji scoffed: \"Old Si, you tell us, who is more handsome?\"","Elder Si: \"They're both ugly, terribly ugly... Ugh, what are you two doing? They're hitting me! Help! Miss Rong, Uncle Tang, hurry up and control these two old geezers!\"","Rong Yu and Tang Che exchanged a glance and couldn't help but laugh.","The engagement ceremony proceeded smoothly.","The host held the microphone, speaking with great passion: \"Today, we are gathered to witness the happy moments of these two perfect couples. Now, please invite the two grooms-to-be to put the engagement rings on their beautiful fiancées—\"","Ji Jingchuan and Hai Chang'an both pulled out the engagement rings at the same time.","Just at this moment—","\"Woof woof!\"","Before everyone could react, a shiny silver smart mechanical dog suddenly darted out from the bushes. Its four mechanical legs transformed with a click-clack sound, instantly turning into a small carrier robot that charged straight toward the four newly engaged individuals.","Ji Jingchuan reached out, wrapping his arm around Tang Jin's waist, and pulled her to the side, narrowly dodging it.","Hai Chang'an was dumbfounded: \"No, Si Lin, why did you let the dog up here? Hurry up and get it down!\"","Si Lin laughed mischievously: \"There's a surprise!\"","The next second.","Hai Chang'an was completely lifted up by the mechanical dog. In a perfect parabolic arc, he was tossed straight into the nearby swimming pool. Water splashed everywhere, guests screamed, his suit was instantly soaked, and his carefully styled hair became a messy tangle.","Ji Zhouye roared with laughter.","Hai Chang'an emerged from the pool, cursing angrily: \"Si Lin! You'd better not tell me when you get engaged, otherwise, I'll show you what it really means to lose face.\"","Si Lin didn't care about that and rushed to rescue his smart dog.","But he was a step too late.","\"Water ingress... detected. System... shutting down...\"","Si Lin wailed: \"The high-end smart dog I spent five million to customize just sacrificed itself for your engagement! Is there a better brother than me in this world?\"","Elder Hai: \"Spending a fortune on a dog that isn't even waterproof. You got scammed.\"","Elder Ji: \"Too much money with nowhere to spend it, huh? What a waste.\"","Elder Si felt guilty: \"Si Lin meant well...\"","Hai Chang'an changed his clothes, and the ceremony continued.","After the two couples exchanged rings, the host proceeded to the final segment: \"Next, we invite the elders to offer their blessings to the newly engaged couples.\"","Tang Youyi pushed the wheelchair, bringing Tang Che onto the stage.","Tang Che was getting on in years and found walking extremely difficult, which was why he used a wheelchair. After getting on stage, he leaned on Tang Youyi's arm to stand up, presenting himself in the most upright posture before all the guests.","Tang Youyi's right hand silently supported the old man's lower back, providing him with ample strength.","\"Thank you to all the guests for taking time out of your busy schedules to attend this engagement banquet,\" Tang Che spoke into the microphone. \"Today is a wonderful day, except for a certain blind smart dog. Si Lin, it's time you grew up a bit.\"","Si Lin held the corpse of his smart dog, wanting to cry but having no tears left.","Tang Che then shifted the topic, \"There is another important matter today. I announce that starting from today, Tang Jin will officially become the next head of the Tang family!\""]},{"number":265,"title":"Chapter 265: Tang Che Has Gone to Another World","paragraphs":["As soon as Tang Che said this, all the guests were in an uproar.","\"What? The heir to the Tang family?\"","\"Isn't Tang Jin the granddaughter of the Tang family? A girl can be the head of the family?\"","\"She is neither the eldest daughter nor a male heir. Why can she inherit the Tang family? Has Old Master Tang gone senile?\"","\"Will the rest of the Tang family accept this?\"","\"...\"","Tang Mi, dressed in her wedding gown, froze.","Tang Jin was marrying into the Ji family, and she was marrying into the Hai family. The Hai family was no worse than the Ji family. Why was Tang Jin the heir and not her?","Before she could voice her doubts, Madam Tang spoke up first: \"Uncle, this is against the rules.\"","\"Rules?\" Tang Che said indifferently. \"The rules of the Tang family are set by me. Regardless of gender, the most capable person takes the position. Why don't you tell me, among the younger generation of the Tang family, who is more outstanding than Tang Jin?\"","Madam Tang was immediately stumped.","In her eyes, no matter who was chosen, the heir should never be a girl.","Once a girl married out and became a daughter-in-law of another family, wouldn't the massive assets of the Tang family be merged into the Ji family?","Tang Youyi said coldly, \"Since Uncle has chosen Tang Jin, then it is Tang Jin.\"","He looked at the audience. \"Little Jin, come up to the stage.\"","Tang Jin had long guessed this outcome and was not too surprised.","Lifting her skirt, she walked up calmly and stood beside Tang Che.","Tang Che picked up the share transfer agreement that had been prepared in advance and handed it over. She raised both hands and accepted it solemnly.","She saw the elders of the clan standing below, each showing dissatisfaction on their faces, which was also expected.","First, she was too young.","Second, and most importantly, she was a girl.","Technology was changing rapidly, and times were rolling forward, but when it came to whether a man or a woman should inherit a family business, people still held an almost unanimous view.","Holding the microphone, she spoke: \"Hello everyone, I am Tang Jin.\"","She picked up the necklace pendant on her chest. \"This is a jade court bead necklace that I won at an auction three years ago for twenty-three million.\"","\"At the time, the news said that the Tang family's daughter threw money around like water and was a true spendthrift. My grandmother accused me of squandering the family fortune.\"","\"In fact, that twenty-three million was the total profit from the jewelry I designed during my college years. I did not squander my ancestors' estate.\"","\"It was exactly this auction that led me to discover the lost secret recipe of the Yanjing Eight Imperial Handicrafts' Tian-tsui. Now, this intangible cultural heritage technique generates over a hundred million in revenue for Tang's Jewelry every year.\"","\"As a designer, my mission is not to break tradition, but to let tradition continue to shine in a new era.\"","\"From today on, I will use the vision of a designer and the wisdom of a chairman to lead the Tang Group to create a better future.\"","Standing offstage, Ji Jingchuan looked up at her.","He liked this sparkling girl.","She was confident, calm, bright, and open-minded... She was his exact opposite.","Being with her, it was as if the dark side of his heart dissipated little by little.","He also had to work hard to be worthy of her.","Below the stage, Old Master Ji, Old Master Hai, and Old Master Si, the three old men took the lead in applauding. Immediately after, all the guests applauded one after another. Amidst the enthusiastic applause, Tang Che suddenly began to cough violently.","\"Great-grandfather!\" Tang Jin hurriedly supported him. Seeing the blood he coughed up, she was terrified out of her wits but still maintained her composure. \"Great-grandfather, let me help you down to rest first.\"","Every few months, reporters from the outside world would spread rumors that Old Master Tang had died of illness.","On such an occasion, with people everywhere, they had to be careful.","Tang Che, sitting in a wheelchair, was pushed off the stage. As soon as he was pushed to a secluded spot, he suddenly spat out a mouthful of blood, staining the ground red, a shocking sight.","\"Tang Che!\"","Rong Yu was greatly alarmed.","She spoke quickly, \"Hurry and arrange a private car to go to the hospital!\"","She gripped Tang Che's hand tightly. \"Hold on a little longer. Don't fall asleep, Tang Che. I'm here. I'm right here...\"","This was the first time Rong Yu had called the helmsman of the Tang family by his first name in front of so many people.","Old Master Hai and Old Master Si exchanged a glance, and the two silently blocked Madam Tang, who was walking over.","Tang Youyi looked at Madam Tang: \"The banquet has just begun. You stay here to receive the guests. I will take Uncle to the hospital. Be careful not to leak the news.\"","The private car arrived quickly.","Tang Che, who was coughing up blood, was helped into the car.","Rong Yu followed him into the car, holding his hand tightly the entire time.","Tang Che struggled to open his eyes and looked at her: \"A-Yu, it's so good... so good to see you again... cough, cough, cough!\"","\"Stop talking.\" Rong Yu's throat felt tight. \"We can talk slowly once you get better.\"","\"There's no chance. I know my own body best. I've just been pushing through these past few months, cough, cough!\" Tang Che's eyes held a smile. \"A-Yu, I'm so jealous of you, jealous that you could become so young again, but... cough, cough, cough... but it's okay, I... I'm going to start my life over again too...\"","The car sped along the road and arrived at the hospital in less than five minutes.","Tang Che was rushed inside.","A large group of people waited outside.","No one knew what to say. They were very silent, quietly watching the light of the emergency room.","About twenty minutes later, the door opened.","Tang Youyi dashed forward: \"How is it? Is my uncle alright?\"","The doctor's voice was heavy and slow: \"Patient Tang Che, male, one hundred years old, passed away due to multiple organ failure. Resuscitation efforts were unsuccessful, and he has been declared clinically dead.\"","Tang Youyi staggered and almost fell to the ground.","Rong Yu choked back a sob, her eyes turning red.","\"Uncle Tang...\" Old Master Ji wailed, \"Uncle Tang!\"","He rushed into the emergency room, and Old Master Hai and Old Master Si followed him inside.","On the hospital bed, Tang Che looked as if he had fallen asleep. His wrinkles had smoothed out, and there was even a faint smile on the corners of his mouth. However, his chest, which used to rise and fall slightly with his breathing, was now completely still.","The doctor said softly, \"The old gentleman passed away very peacefully. In his final moments, his blood pressure and blood oxygen dropped slowly, and he showed no signs of pain.\"","Tang Youyi suddenly knelt in front of the hospital bed, tightly grasping Tang Che's gradually cooling hand, and pressed his forehead against the back of the hand covered in age spots. His whimpers were muffled in the white sheets, and his whole back heaved violently.","The other three old men were also crying loudly.","Old Master Si: \"When Uncle Tang left, he must have still been thinking of us.\"","Old Master Hai: \"Our elder is gone, and soon it will be our turn. We agreed, no matter who leaves, we are not allowed to cry like this.\"","Old Master Ji choked up: \"I still want to live for a few more decades. Don't drag me into this...\"","Rong Yu stood quietly.","She saw the plane trees rustling outside the window. A withered yellow leaf stuck to the glass and slowly slid down. The sound of a rolling cart echoed in the corridor, drawing near and then gradually fading away.","At this moment, a loud, clear baby's cry from afar suddenly pierced the hospital's gloomy atmosphere.","A child had been born. Every cry demonstrated the most primitive vitality of life.","Rong Yu suddenly felt an unprecedented sense of lightness.","What death took away, new life brought back, just like the ebb and flow of the tide, never ceasing.","Tang Che, I hope that in your next life, you will be born into a loving family and grow up surrounded by joy. May you meet someone you truly love, and have a beautiful child together...","Please, do not ever wait around so foolishly for someone again, and do not ever cling so stubbornly to someone you shouldn't love..."]},{"number":266,"title":"Chapter 266: How to Strike Hard, How to Attack","paragraphs":["The death of the helmsman of one of Haicheng's four major families caused a massive uproar.","The news broadcasted detailed reports on Tang Che's life, made predictions about the future development of the Tang Group, and conducted comprehensive evaluations of the Tang family's new head, Tang Jin...","Back then, when Ji Zheng sacrificed his life, Rong Yu only allowed herself to be depressed for two minutes, because the overall situation didn't permit it.","Now, with Tang Che's passing, she allowed herself to grieve for two days.","She received a call from the Fourth Aerospace Institute, saying they had received a massive anonymous donation intended to boost the development of the aerospace industry.","She smiled bitterly. Tang Che, oh Tang Che, even when leaving this world, he hadn't forgotten her...","Rong Yu composed herself, opened her door, and walked out, only to see her old son getting ready to head out downstairs.","\"Yingbao, where are you going?\"","Old Master Ji sighed, \"Tang Youyi is sick, quite seriously, and has been hospitalized. Although my relationship with him isn't great, we are all juniors protected by Uncle Tang. Now that Uncle Tang is gone, it stands to reason that I should go see him. I also called Old Si and Old Hai to go together. Mom, are you going?\"","Rong Yu nodded, \"Let's go.\"","She was a little worried that when these old boys got together, they would hold each other and cry bitterly. They had finally moved on; it would not be worth it if they ruined their health from crying.","But it seemed she had overthought things.","As soon as they entered Tang Youyi's hospital room, a strong smell of alcohol hit them.","They saw Hai Dadun and Sima Gang, these two fools, had actually brought several bottles of white liquor along with a few dishes of snacks, and were setting up a spread right in the hospital room.","\"Five chiefs! Six, six, six!\"","\"Old Si, you're cheating! I clearly won!\"","Elder Hai and Elder Si were having a blast, while Tang Youyi, leaning against the head of the hospital bed, had a face as black as thunder. \"If you two want to drink, go outside. Don't be a nuisance here.\"","\"Tang Youyi, we came out of the goodness of our hearts to visit you. Is this how you kick people out?\" Old Master Hai handed him a glass of liquor. \"Have a drink. One should enjoy life to the fullest when they can. Uncle Tang is gone, and you placed all his favorite braised pork in front of his memorial hall, but unfortunately, he couldn't even taste a bite. It's better to thoroughly enjoy things while you're still alive.\"","Old Master Si nodded, \"Exactly, this is called enjoying the moment.\"","\"Ahem, ahem, ahem!\"","Old Master Ji coughed loudly to remind the two to take it easy.","Old Master Hai turned his head, just about to invite Old Master Ji to join them, but then noticed Rong Yu was also there. He instantly jolted in fright and quickly raised his glass, saying, \"Um, this isn't liquor, it's just plain water. We're just trying to create an atmosphere.\"","To prove it, he downed a glass in one gulp, only to choke and start coughing violently.","Elder Si immediately distanced himself, \"It was Old Hai's idea. I was forced.\"","Elder Hai: \"...\"","What a mess, actually getting stabbed in the back by a brother.","Tang Youyi frowned.","These old geezers were actually this afraid of Miss Rong?","It was truly a bit absurd.","But then he remembered that when his uncle was alive, his favorite person was Rong Yu.","Perhaps these three old guys were just showing respect for his uncle's sake.","Thinking of this, Tang Youyi's expression softened considerably, and he said, \"Miss Rong is so busy with her studies, why did you come to the hospital personally?\"","Rong Yu placed the fruits on the bedside table. \"Tang Jin just took over as the chairman of the Tang Group, and you've fallen ill and can't attend to things. The Tang family must be going through a turbulent time. If you need any help, just say the word. I think Old Ji, Old Hai, and Old Si wouldn't refuse.\"","\"Thank you for your kindness, Miss Rong,\" Tang Youyi said. \"But it's unnecessary. This is exactly the right time to test Tang Jin. I believe she can handle it well.\"","\"That girl Jin is smart, she'll definitely be fine.\" Old Master Si sighed. \"Speaking of which, it's that worthless brat of mine, Si Lin, who is getting increasingly out of hand. Last night, he actually swiped my card to inject eighty million into his girlfriend's company. Then, first thing this morning, his girlfriend vanished with the money. I'm so furious I could die.\"","Old Master Ji patted his shoulder. \"I told you earlier, cut ties with him sooner rather than later, and you wouldn't have to deal with this crap.\"","Elder Hai looked at Rong Yu. \"Miss Rong, tell us, how should a prodigal son like this be disciplined?\"","Rong Yu sat down and slowly peeled an apple. \"As long as Old Si is always there to bail him out, Si Lin will never grow up. You have to hit him hard.\"","Old Master Si leaned in. \"How do we hit him hard? Please instruct us, Miss Rong.\"","\"I have an idea,\" Elder Hai spoke up. \"A few years ago, wasn't there a popular reality show where rich kids went to the countryside to experience life and came back to the city all grown up? I think Ji Entertainment could take the lead in producing a show like that, with the Hai and Si families investing. We could have Miss Rong act as an observer and send Si Lin over to experience some hardship. How about that?\"","Old Master Si chimed in, \"It's a great show. Miss Rong, would you consider it?\"","Seeing the two of them echoing each other, Rong Yu immediately understood.","It turned out these two had planned this all along, hoping to find a reasonable excuse for her to step in and discipline their two worthless grandsons.","But... a transformation program?","For the rich kids, this kind of program might just be a unique coming-of-age experience. But for the poor children, it was almost a cruel psychological baptism; when the glamour in front of the cameras faded, they were forced to retreat back to their original lives.","A lucky few might transform that shock into upward motivation, striving to chase the world they had caught a fleeting glimpse of.","But most of the children would simply be left with a torn perception, wandering for the rest of their lives in the gap between reality and illusion.","She thought for a moment before saying, \"Tang Che invested some funds in the Aerospace Institute. This money is about to be put into a rocket launch base. In the coming days, I need to go over there and stay for about a month. Whichever of your grandsons is misbehaving, let him come with me to do hard labor. If they can survive a month in a place like that, I guarantee they'll return to Haicheng completely transformed. If even that doesn't change them, then they're hopeless. Just publicly sever ties with them; there's no need to hesitate.\"","Old Master Si hesitated. \"That's in the desert region, right? Si Lin has never left my side since he was little. I'm worried...\"","\"That's enough from you!\" Old Master Ji glared at him. \"Just keep spoiling, coddling, and indulging him like this. One day, when he commits murder or arson and gets thrown in jail, you'll be the one crying!\"","Old Master Hai quickly said, \"My Hai Chang'an, although a bit more promising than Si Lin, still isn't quite up to par. He's about to get married, but he still can't shoulder major responsibilities. Let him follow Miss Rong!\"","Since he had put it that way, Old Master Si could only agree. \"I just hope that brat cooperates a bit.\"","Tang Youyi lay on his hospital bed.","He thought of the younger generation in the Tang family. Tang Tang was sent abroad, Tang Jiaquan was locked up... It seemed he really didn't know how to raise children.","He didn't quite believe that Rong Yu had such immense power to completely transform a person.","But since these three older brothers all trusted Rong Yu, it wouldn't hurt to give it a try.","He said slowly, \"Since Hai Chang'an is going, then Tang Mi, as his fiancée, should go too. It'll be good for them to look out for each other.\"","As soon as they stepped out of the hospital room.","Elder Hai pulled Elder Si aside and said, \"Uncle Tang donated money to the Aerospace Institute, so let's donate some too. After all, the kids are going over there for training, and we can't be a burden to them.\"","\"I will match whatever you donate,\" Old Master Si said.","Old Master Hai thought for a moment before replying, \"Let's both donate fifty million, then.\"","The Si family was poor, so fifty million was enough for them. The Hai family was wealthy, so he figured he would casually donate two hundred million. If the kid showed great promise, he would add more later.","Old Master Si curled his lip.","The money his own Si Lin had squandered was already more than that amount. Old Master Hai was being far too stingy.","He discreetly sent a text message to his secretary, instructing them to donate two hundred million."]},{"number":267,"title":"Chapter 267: Grandma Began to Scheme About Her Heir's Identity","paragraphs":["Tang Mi had no idea that she had been set up.","She was sitting in the Tang family's main hall, slowly sipping tea, waiting to watch the drama unfold.","Before long, Tang Jin rushed back hurriedly.","The butler had called her to say that her grandmother was ill. She had dropped her work and driven back, only to find a large group of people sitting in the living room.","The elderly clan elder of the Tang family, her eldest uncle, another uncle, and a bunch of cousins—these people all had a look of intrigue in their eyes, clearly targeting her.","Tang Jin had initially been worried about her grandmother's illness, but now, that worry dissipated, replaced by composure.","She was now the person in power in the Tang family, the chairman of the Tang Group, and the head of the family. She had no need to fear such an occasion.","\"Why is Third Granduncle here too? Is Grandmother terribly ill?\" Tang Jin stepped forward. \"What illness has Grandmother contracted? Why hasn't she gone to the hospital?\"","\"My health has been acting up frequently lately, so I plan to go to Switzerland for convalescence next week.\" Madam Tang took a sip of tea and said slowly, \"Xiao Jin, put aside your work and accompany me abroad for a while.\"","All eyes instantly swept over to her.","Tang Jin pursed her lips tightly.","Her great-grandfather's body wasn't even cold yet, and her grandmother was already scheming against her position as the heir.","Who did her grandmother want to give the heir position to?","Her eldest male cousin was already in prison, so it had to be her second male cousin.","But her second cousin was a drunkard who drank every day after getting married and committed domestic violence against his wife and children. Could such a person bear the heavy responsibility of the Tang Group?","Tang Jin's expression was indifferent. \"Grandmother, the Tang Group is in a crucial period these few days. I'll have the butler accompany you to recuperate. He took care of Great-grandfather for over a decade and has more experience than I do.\"","\"Do I lack servants? I don't have a daughter, so I want you, my granddaughter, to accompany me.\" Madam Tang's chest heaved violently. \"What, now that you've become the head of the Tang family, you no longer put me, your grandmother, in your eyes, is that it?\"","Tang Jin's eldest uncle said coldly, \"Xiao Jin, even though you are the head, she is still your elder. Your grandmother is ill and asked you to accompany her to the sanatorium. What's wrong, are you feeling wronged? You even dare to refuse?\"","\"Why is Eldest Uncle in such a hurry to send me abroad?\" Tang Jin was completely unafraid, meeting his gaze. \"For my shares? For my position as heir? Are you hoping I never return to the country?\"","\"Insolent!\" Madam Tang said angrily. \"Filial piety is the most important of all virtues. If you can't even respect your elders, what right do you have to be the heir!\"","Tang Mi pretended to persuade her, \"Third Sister, it's too exhausting for a girl to manage the group. Just give it up. You can collect a large dividend every year and live comfortably.\"","\"If you truly thought that way, you wouldn't have agreed to a marriage alliance with Hai Chang'an.\" Tang Jin smiled. \"You lost, so you hope I lose too. It's perfectly normal for a loser to have such thoughts.\"","\"You!\"","Tang Mi flung her hand down.","Death is imminent, yet she's still so arrogant.","Now that Great-grandfather had passed away and Grandfather was lying in the hospital, Grandmother had the final say in the Tang family.","\"Xiao Jin,\" Third Granduncle spoke up. \"Look at the ancestors of the Tang family. When has there ever been a precedent of a daughter taking power? The old master was confused on his deathbed. Are you going to be ignorant too?\"","Eldest Aunt sneered, \"A girl will eventually marry. You are hogging the family business now; are you going to take it all to the Ji family in the future?\"","Tang Jin smiled.","She first looked at the clan elder: \"Third Granduncle, your branch indeed has a male in power, but more than half of your family fortune has been squandered away. That's why, despite your old age, you are always coming to my great-grandfather for handouts... Great-grandfather used to say that we shouldn't judge people by their gender, only by whether they are useful or not. Sure enough, some men really have nothing to show for themselves except boasting about their gender.\"","Third Granduncle's face turned livid.","Tang Mi was dumbfounded.","Even when Great-grandfather was alive, he wouldn't speak to Third Granduncle like that. Tang Jin was far too bold.","Did she not want to survive in the Tang family anymore?","Tang Jin then looked at her eldest aunt: \"Eldest Aunt indeed gave birth to two outstanding sons. What a pity, though. The eldest male cousin has been arrested, and the second male cousin commits domestic violence against his wife every day. It's only a matter of time before things blow up and he gets detained. Giving birth to two such trashes who aren't even worthy of being human, and you still have the nerve to compare genders with me?\"","She said indifferently, \"The company is busy, so I won't keep you all company for tea.\"","She turned around and walked away.","A teacup was violently swept onto the floor, sending porcelain shards flying.","Third Granduncle rose in anger: \"If you dare walk out this door today, your name will be removed from the genealogy book! We'll make your father's branch die out! Offending the entire Tang family, let's see who will back you up in the future! Would the Ji family want a daughter-in-law who disowns her own relatives?\"","\"What a lively scene.\"","A cold, clear male voice came from the doorway. Ji Jingchuan strode in, still wearing his school uniform, twirling a car key in his hand.","\"Pardon the intrusion. I'm here to pick up my fiancée for a meal.\"","Madam Tang's expression changed slightly. \"This is our Tang family's private matter.\"","\"What a coincidence, I'm practically half a member of the Tang family, aren't I?\" Ji Jingchuan suddenly glanced at a document placed by the sofa and smiled. \"Oh? An election for a temporary chairman? Old Master Tang's body isn't even cold yet, and the ink on his will hasn't even dried.\"","\"A'Chuan,\" Tang Jin said softly. \"I can handle this matter well...\"","Ji Jingchuan gently squeezed her fingers and pulled a document out of his briefcase. \"Grandmother, did you just say you don't have a daughter?\"","The temperature in the room seemed to drop by ten degrees.","Madam Tang's face instantly turned deathly pale. \"What, what do you mean?\"","Ji Jingchuan curled his lips. \"Before marrying into the Tang family, Madam Tang had a passionate romance, but in the end, she was arranged by her family to marry into the Tang family. And three months before the wedding, you gave birth to a baby girl in the hospital. That baby girl from back then is now in her forties. With her accompanying you to Switzerland to recuperate, I suppose you won't be lonely.\"","These words were undoubtedly a massive bombshell dropped on the Tang family.","The expressions of everyone present changed completely.","Even Tang Jin had a look of astonishment on her face.","\"Nonsense!\" Madam Tang's lips trembled with anger. \"Fourth Master Ji, if you dare spout one more word of nonsense, I will definitely slap you across the face!\"","Ji Jingchuan held up the document. \"The evidence is conclusive. Do you all want to see if it's nonsense?\"","Ever since Tang Jiaquan made a move against Tang Jin, he had started investigating these demons and monsters of the Tang family.","He truly hadn't expected Madam Tang to be hiding such a massive secret.","He originally hadn't wanted to destroy the peace of the Tang family.","But Madam Tang insisted on constantly causing trouble.","Making trouble for Tang Jin meant making trouble for him. Naturally, he didn't mind tearing off this fig leaf.","He took a step forward, approaching Madam Tang, and spoke in a low voice, \"Grandmother, do you want all the Tang family members to examine the evidence, or do you want to announce that you will voluntarily take Second Young Master Tang and the Third Young Master abroad to recuperate with you?\"","That very night, Madam Tang took her two grandsons and left Haicheng."]},{"number":268,"title":"Chapter 268: Conduct a One-Month Base Support Plan","paragraphs":["As the Tang family slowly returned to peace, Rong Yu was preparing to head to the Aerospace No. 4 Launch Base. The Fourth Aerospace Institute had assigned her an assistant, Dr. Wang Xiaoli.","Having witnessed what a true young genius was, Wang Xiaoli was more than willing to serve as Rong Yu's assistant.","The two left the Fourth Aerospace Institute and headed straight for the airport.","At this moment, the airport VIP lounge was bustling.","Si Lin leaned back on the sofa, his slender fingers swiping across his phone screen, a cynical, playboy smile playing on his lips.","On the screen was a photo of him with his arms around two models at a nightclub last night; the likes had already surpassed ten thousand.","He had originally made plans to take a newly acquainted internet celebrity to the Maldives, but his old man had called him bright and early, ordering him to come to the airport for some important arrangement.","Growing a bit impatient with the wait, he was just about to get up and leave.","Just then, the lounge door was suddenly pushed open. He looked up to see not only his own old man, but also Old Master Ji, Old Master Hai, and Tang Youyi, who had just recovered from a severe illness.","Alarm bells instantly went off in Si Lin's head. These active old men gathering together could mean nothing good.","He was just thinking about making a run for it.","When he saw Tang Mi and Hai Chang'an walk in.","Tang Mi pouted, Grandpa, what are we doing at the airport so early in the morning? I still have to go shopping with my bestie.","Hai Chang'an rubbed his eyes, So many people. Are we going somewhere to attend a banquet?","We called you all here today to announce an important decision, Old Master Hai spoke up. Starting today...","Halfway through his sentence, another old man burst into the lounge. Wait, there is also my granddaughter! Although the Zhou family is not one of the four great families, we also donated a sum of funds to the Fourth Institute. Take us along too.","Old Master Zhou dragged in a young girl with flowing curly hair.","The girl was fashionably dressed with exquisite makeup. Holding up a selfie stick, she spoke to her phone screen, Babies, I just arrived at the airport. I was supposed to go to Paris for Fashion Week today, but my grandpa made some last-minute arrangements. I have to go now, catch you later.","She turned off the livestream and asked curiously, Such a grand lineup, what on earth are we doing?","All you know is streaming this mindless nonsense all day, Old Master Zhou scolded angrily. Go stand over there in a line with the rest of them.","Under the strict glares of the old masters, Si Lin, Hai Chang'an, Tang Mi, and Zhou Shiyu obediently stood in a row. However, they all slouched carelessly, their faces full of indifference, looking thoroughly exasperating.","Old Master Hai took four flight tickets out of his briefcase and slapped them onto the table. Starting today, you four will be sent to the Aerospace No. 4 Launch Base. You will be assigned to the base special support team for a one-month base support program.","What?","The four of them exclaimed in unison.","Si Lin was the first to jump up. Are you kidding me! I am not going to some base. I have a ton of things to do. Whoever wants to go can go.","Tang Mi shrieked, A launch base? Isn't that in the desert? I am absolutely not going to a place like that!","Zhou Shiyu's hand trembled. Don't tell me that place doesn't even have internet? How am I supposed to livestream? I am not going either.","Hai Chang'an spoke up quietly, If they aren't going, I am not going either.","You don't have to go, Old Master Si said coldly. However, every single one of your bank cards, personal accounts, and assets under your names have already been...","These words didn't threaten Si Lin in the slightest.","After all, Old Master Si had frozen his accounts many times before. He would just play the fool and act spoiled, and the old man would always let him off lightly. He had long since figured out exactly how to handle the old man.","But then he heard Old Master Si say coldly, \"All of your assets have been transferred to Old Ji for safekeeping until you return. Old Ji is highly experienced in this regard. If you don't believe it, go ask Ji Zhiyuan and Ji Zhouye if they aren't still suffering under economic sanctions to this day.\"","The four of them were horrified.","Back then, Ji Zhiyuan was already a powerful CEO who had taken over the Ji Group, yet he was still subjected to these controls. Rumor had it that he looked utterly disgraced during that time, running around borrowing money from everyone...","They would rather go to whatever crappy base this was than face economic sanctions!","Instantly, every single one of them fell into line.","Old Master Ji cleared his throat and said, \"Don't worry, you're just going for a month of practical training. It's no big deal.\"","Tang Youyi shot a glance at the bodyguards beside him.","The bodyguards stepped forward and began to search them. They confiscated their luxury items first, then snatched their phones and emptied their account balances.","The four didn't dare to resist, much less think about what was going to happen next.","Just then, Old Master Ji's eyes lit up. \"She's here.\"","Everyone's gaze snapped uniformly toward the door.","Rong Yu was dressed in a simple white button-down and khaki pants, her black hair tied up in a neat ponytail. She wore no delicate makeup and lacked any luxury accessories, yet she inexplicably exuded an aura that demanded attention.","She glanced at the four standing off to the side. \"Are you sure it's them?\"","\"Yes,\" Old Master Hai said hurriedly. \"We are leaving them in your capable hands, Miss Rong.\"","Tang Youyi added, \"Please prioritize your work, Miss Rong. There's no need to go easy on them.\"","Old Master Si chimed in, \"Beat them or scold them as you see fit. If anyone dares to resist, we'll strike them from the family register.\"","Old Master Zhou harbored some doubts about trusting such a young girl. However, since the other four major families were handing their children over to Rong Yu, he decided to just follow suit. Who knew, maybe one day they could expand to become the Five Great Families of Haicheng.","Tang Mi looked utterly incredulous. \"What do you mean, you're handing us over to Rong Yu?\"","Si Lin suddenly burst into laughter. \"If the old man had told me earlier that I'd be following Rong Yu, I wouldn't have been so resistant. I couldn't ask for anything better...\"","Before he could finish his sentence, Old Master Ji smacked him. \"Put away your playboy thoughts, or I'll freeze your bank cards permanently.\"","Rong Yu looked at Old Master Ji. \"The conditions out there are harsh. You shouldn't go. Just stay here and rest well in Haicheng.\"","Old Master Ji quickly and obediently nodded.","Rong Yu checked her watch. \"It's time. Don't worry, everyone. Just come back here in a month to pick them up.\"","She made a hand gesture.","The bodyguards immediately herded the four of them toward the boarding gate.","Si Lin glanced back and noticed the old masters standing together. Their faces bore a mixture of worry, anticipation, and a hint of... relief.","He quickened his pace and caught up to Rong Yu. \"Miss Rong, we still haven't exchanged contact information. How about we add each other on WeChat?\"","Rong Yu replied indifferently, \"I don't add useless trash to my friends list.\"","Si Lin was speechless. \"...\"","Her tongue was far too venomous.","Refusing to give up, he pressed on, \"You added Ji Zhouye, so why can't you add me? Am I really more useless than him?\"","Rong Yu smiled. \"Barring any accidents, he'll be able to get into a top-tier university. Can you?\"","She paused for a moment before adding, \"I suggest you save your energy. Otherwise, you're going to have a very hard time adapting to what comes next.\"","At that moment, Si Lin didn't quite understand what she meant by that.","But he would understand very soon.","For the first time in his life, he realized that a person's knees could actually press right up against the seat in front of them. With his six-foot frame, he looked exceptionally cramped in the narrow space, and his expensive suit pants were already wrinkled beyond recognition.","Are these seats even meant for humans? Tang Mi was on the verge of tears. Flight attendant! I want to upgrade my seat!","The flight attendant, who was currently handing out meals, maintained her professional smile. I am sorry, ma'am, but this flight is completely full.","Zhou Shiyu looked at her meal box in absolute despair. Wait, why is this in-flight meal so pathetic? Is this yellow lump supposed to be curry or what?","Hai Chang'an had already given up the struggle, slumping entirely into his seat. I would honestly rather go to prison.","Sitting on the other side of the aisle, Rong Yu was calmly eating the food from her meal box.","Si Lin noticed that even her eating movements were meticulous. Holding a cheap plastic fork with her slender fingers, she somehow managed to eat with the refined elegance of someone dining in a high-end restaurant.","He could not help but lean closer to her. Is this the kind of treatment you scientific researchers get for serving the country?","Rong Yu could not be bothered to pay him any attention.","Wang Xiaoli looked up and said, This meal is perfectly fine. Once we arrive at the base, you are all going to deeply miss this in-flight food."]},{"number":269,"title":"Chapter 269: This is a rare month to spend with Rong Yu.","paragraphs":["The airplane's engine noise gradually faded. The moment the cabin door opened, a scorching, sandy wind rushed against their faces.","Si Lin couldn't help but curse, swearing, Is this a fucking sauna or an airport?","Tang Mi complained, My makeup is ruined, I need to touch it up. Where is my suitcase? Why didn't the old men pack suitcases for us?","Zhou Shiyu had already raised her phone and started adjusting the filters. Hey family, I'm starting my livestream. Look where I am... wait, why is the internet so bad? The screen is so laggy, how am I supposed to stream?","Hai Chang'an stood dumbfounded on the boarding stairs. In his twenty-three years of life, he had never seen such a sight; as far as the eye could see, there were only rolling heat waves and grayish-yellow sand dunes.","Rong Yu's cold voice sounded: Let's go. We are transferring to a bus next.","Hai Chang'an widened his clear, foolish eyes. What is a bus?","When that vintage 1990s coach appeared before them, the six faded characters for Fourth Aerospace Base on its mottled body made the four of them grimace in absolute shock.","Before anyone could protest, Rong Yu spoke in an indifferent tone, You only have two choices right now. First, follow me to the base for a one-month support program. Second, turn around, get on the plane, and go home—in which case, you will be publicly expelled from your family registers.","She turned around and boarded the bus directly.","Dr. Wang Xiaoli gave them a sympathetic look and followed her onto the bus.","Si Lin gave himself a mental pep talk and chuckled, Look on the bright side, this is a rare chance to spend a month with Rong Yu. What if I actually manage to win her over, right?","He quickly dashed onto the bus.","Stupid hopeless romantic, you are a lost cause! Tang Mi cursed as she also got on. She had no choice; her grandfather was too ruthless. In her generation, Tang Jiaquan had been personally sent to prison by their grandfather, and Tang Tang had been exiled abroad. If she didn't behave, she would definitely be kicked out of the family.","A person had to read the room to survive.","Hai Chang'an was Tang Mi's fiancé. Although they had a weak emotional foundation, they were still considered a small group. He sighed and boarded as well.","Hey, you guys, what the fuck... whatever, I will risk my life to accompany you! As soon as Zhou Shiyu got on the bus, she covered her nose. Was this vehicle used to transport livestock?","The bus's leather seats had long cracked, exposing the yellowed foam inside, and every crevice hid years of accumulated sand and gravel.","Wang Xiaoli reminded them, Please fasten your seatbelts.","However, the four of them looked disgusted and turned a deaf ear. The vehicle soon started up.","When the wheels rolled over the first sand pit, the bus swayed violently like a ship in a storm.","Zhou Shiyu's forehead slammed against the back of the seat in front of her with a thud.","Si Lin tried to take the opportunity to lean closer to Rong Yu, but a sharp turn threw him into the aisle.","Hai Chang'an's face turned green. He grabbed Tang Mi's handbag next to him, opened it, and threw up into it...","You idiot, you... Tang Mi got halfway through her sentence when her stomach churned. She snatched the handbag back and threw up along with him...","Two hours later, the bus finally stopped. The four of them practically tumbled out of the vehicle, collapsing by the roadside and dry-heaving.","We should... be here, right? Hai Chang'an was completely drained of energy.","Rong Yu pointed into the distance. Change vehicles. We are entering the base.","Following the direction of her finger, four military off-road vehicles were waiting for them. The bodies of the cars were covered in dirt and sand, and the tires were thicker than their waists.","Is there no end to this! Si Lin's face was pale. I want a private car, do you hear me? I want a private car!","Rong Yu finally looked up and smiled faintly. There are no private cars. Of course, you can choose to walk yourself. See that? Walk in this direction for about four hours, and you will arrive.","Wang Xiaoli said, Just a reminder, you must reach the base before nightfall, because wolves roam some areas at night.","Si Lin's anger, which had just rushed to his head, was instantly extinguished.","Like a frostbitten eggplant, he reluctantly climbed into the off-road vehicle.","The off-road vehicle bounced wildly among the sand dunes, and the next forty minutes became the longest time of their lives.","Hai Chang'an's temple smashed against the car window three times.","Tang Mi's expensive silk scarf fluttered away into the depths of the desert like a white flag of surrender.","When Zhou Shiyu felt like her ribs were almost snapped by the seatbelt, she finally broke down crying, Waaah, I want to go home!","Rong Yu wasn't feeling great either.","In her past life, she had ridden in all sorts of vehicles in poor condition, but never an off-roader. The violent jolting made her face look terrible as well.","But she could handle it.","We are here.","Wang Xiaoli's voice sounded like heavenly music.","The four collapsed limply onto the sand like four dehydrated fish. In their blurred vision, a massive rocket launch pad pierced the sky, its silver-white metallic shell leaving them in awe.","Welcome everyone to the Fourth Rocket Launch Base!","A few staff members stood there, holding a simple welcome ceremony.","Hello, I am the project engineering consultant sent by the Fourth Aerospace Institute. Just call me Engineer Rong. Rong Yu stepped forward and shook hands with the leader. This person beside me is Dr. Wang from the Fourth Aerospace Institute, my assistant, and these four here...","She gestured over with her hand.","Those four immediately stood up straight.","Although they were very dissatisfied with the current situation, their upbringing told them that they must maintain their composure in front of others, even though they currently had no composure to speak of.","These four are the temporary logistics team mentioned before, Rong Yu said. Please make arrangements for them here.","The person in charge nodded, asked someone next to him to take care of the four people, and turned to smile at Rong Yu. The Chief Engineer is in the office. Engineer Rong, Dr. Wang, please come this way with me.","The two followed him toward the other side.","Si Lin couldn't help but shout, Hey, Rong Yu, are you just going to leave us alone like this? Rong Yu...","Quiet. Logistics team leader Lao Ma picked up the roster. Si Lin, Tang Mi, Hai Chang'an, Zhou Shiyu, that is the four of you, right? Come here first to collect your standard base equipment.","Equipment? Si Lin's eyes lit up. Could it be high-tech communicators? Sand-proof goggles?","The four quickly opened the boxes, only to see two sets of orange overalls, a hard hat, a pair of shoes, and a work badge for each person.","Lao Ma said sternly, You belong to the logistics team. You are temporary workers, to be moved wherever you are needed. These are your passes for moving around the base from now on.","Tang Mi stared blankly. The fabric of this work uniform is way too rough!","Zhou Shiyu was horrified. Are these clothes meant for human beings to wear?","Hai Chang'an spoke with difficulty, Why are we temporary workers? Temporary workers have no human rights.","Si Lin put up a final struggle. Um, look, the four of us have good images—handsome guys and beautiful girls. Can we change to a different position? For example, base image ambassadors?","Lao Ma: ...","Did this kid even hear what he was saying? With their sickly complexions, messy bird's-nest hair, sluggish expressions, and scrawny frames, they called this a good image?","There are no arrangements for today, Lao Ma said. Let's go. First, we will head to the cafeteria to eat, and then you can go to the dormitories to get a good night's rest.","The four dragged their exhausted bodies into the cafeteria.","\"We're... just eating this?\" Hai Chang'an stared at the potato and camel meat stew, steamed buns, and pickled vegetables on his tray, his eyes wide with shock.","Tang Mi was starving. She took a bite of the meat and was instantly dumbfounded. \"Is this meat a fossil? I can't even chew it, how am I supposed to swallow?\"","Zhou Shiyu looked on the verge of tears. \"Isn't there any light salad? All these carbs will make me gain three pounds, and my fans won't love me anymore.\"","Finally, Tang Mi snapped. \"I'm not eating! This isn't fit for human consumption!\"","Si Lin slammed his chopsticks down too. \"I'm going on a hunger strike to protest!\"","Lao Ma simply took their meals away, smiling cheerfully. \"Just a reminder, there are no late-night snacks. The next meal is at six tomorrow morning.\"","The four of them: \"...\""]},{"number":270,"title":"Chapter 270: Ronggong has the highest authority on this project.","paragraphs":["Rong Yu was the chief designer of the Hawkeye space debris collection project, but her true identity was only known to the core team members.","Naturally, Cui Xiao, the chief engineer of the rocket launch base, was also informed.","In his fifties, Cui Xiao looked exactly as his name suggested—gentle, refined, and every bit the highly educated intellectual. Wearing thick-lensed glasses, he was deeply immersed in reading orbital data.","Hearing a knock on the door, Cui Xiao immediately looked up.","He knew Rong Yu was young, but he had not expected her to be this young. She looked like she was not even twenty.","But then he smiled. Back in the day, at the age of eighteen, he too had been entrusted with a heavy responsibility by the country, coming to this land to build a rocket launch base right in the middle of the desert.","Every generation produces its own talents. There was him, and now there were newcomers.","Cui Xiao stood up, walked over, and shook her hand with a firm grip. Engineer Rong, you have had a long journey. I am Cui Xiao, the chief engineer of the base. Welcome to Rocket Launch Base Four.","Rong Yu returned the handshake. You are too polite, Chief Engineer Cui. I am here to learn.","Last night, I read the aerospace institute's internal report on the application of the element Shi, Cui Xiao motioned for her to sit down, smiling. I really did not expect the person who broke through this technical bottleneck to be so young.","Rong Yu replied, Actually, I really admire your early research on suppressing the coupled vibration of liquid rocket engines. That was truly groundbreaking work.","Cui Xiao shifted to the main topic. The national aerospace industry is developing rapidly, and the funding gap is growing. Most of the state budget is allocated to the first and second bases. Our fourth base is like an unloved child, relying entirely on our own thick skin to beg for funds... Fortunately, someone anonymously donated a huge sum of money this time, enough to update the base's equipment and carry out the orbital calculations for the Hawkeye project...","Rong Yu nodded.","Updating the equipment was the base's business. Her mission was to complete the orbital simulation calculations for the Hawkeye project ahead of schedule, which was the key step to shortening the entire project cycle.","Cui Xiao raised his voice and called two people in.","Let me introduce you. This is Rong Yu, Engineer Rong, and this is Dr. Wang Xiaoli, he said. These two are the base's senior engineers. This is Zhao Mingzhe, and this is Jiang Si. They will assist and cooperate with you to complete the main tasks this time.","Zhao Mingzhe, who was in his forties, frowned. Did the aerospace institute just send a young girl to be a consultant? She probably just graduated from college, right?","Jiang Si pushed up his glasses and said, If I am not mistaken, Engineer Rong should be that highly popular celebrity on the internet. If that is true, Engineer Rong has not even graduated from high school. How can a high school student bear the title of Engineer Rong?","Cui Xiao frowned and was about to speak.","Then Rong Yu smiled and said, I have not graduated from high school, yet the Fourth Aerospace Institute made an exception to recruit me. Engineer Jiang, what were you doing when you were in high school?","Engineer Jiang froze instantly.","Rong Yu continued, Chief Engineer Cui, I would like to first see the raw data from the most recent failed launch.","Zhao Mingzhe and Jiang Si exchanged a glance.","On what grounds did this high school girl demand to see the most core launch data the moment she arrived?","Cui Xiao spoke in a calm voice, Please remember, Engineer Rong has the highest authority on this project. Execute the order immediately.","Twenty minutes later, dense streams of data scrolled across the large screen in the base's data center. Over a dozen engineers gathered around, curiously watching this new, overly young Engineer Rong.","Rong Yu stood before the screen, her fingers typing rapidly on the virtual keyboard. She brought up a three-dimensional coordinate system, which plotted the deflection angles of various control surfaces during the rocket's flight.","Here. She suddenly stopped and pointed to an almost imperceptible fluctuation. 0.8 seconds before the separation of the second-stage rocket, the right servo response was delayed by 12 milliseconds.","Zhao Mingzhe was stunned.","Such a tiny error, and she was able to find it so accurately in such a short time?","In the entire base, the only person with such strong abilities was Chief Engineer Cui.","After pondering for a moment, Rong Yu said, Actually, this variance is within the allowable range, but the problem is that this delay is not random. Look at this peak; it is exactly a quarter of the control system's sampling frequency. This is not a mechanical delay, but a phase lag caused by the accumulation of numerical integration errors in the software algorithm...","The solution is not actually that difficult. Just add a feedforward compensation term to the control algorithm. She picked up an electronic pen and quickly wrote down a series of differential equations on the screen. This compensation function can offset the phase lag caused by the numerical integration, but the exact values will require a massive amount of calculation...","Jiang Si stared at the string of equations, his face gradually changing. This... this is almost identical to the solution Chief Engineer Cui proposed at last week's meeting.","Cui Xiao was full of admiration. The solution I proposed was an integration of all the engineers' suggestions. But for Engineer Rong, it is the result of her independent thinking.","Indeed, young minds work best.","If only he could be a dozen years younger, he could probably break through many more major difficulties and make even greater contributions to the aerospace industry.","Zhao Mingzhe reached out his hand. Engineer Rong, looking forward to working with you.","Jiang Si also reached out. I am very much looking forward to doing the orbital simulation calculations with Engineer Rong. It should be very interesting.","Rong Yu shook hands with them one by one. I look forward to it too.","Cui Xiao smiled and said, Let's go, let's grab a meal first to get to know each other. It will make working together easier.","Having witnessed Rong Yu's abilities, Zhao Mingzhe and Jiang Si had put away their contempt. Over a simple meal, the group ate very happily.","Next, the staff led Rong Yu and Wang Xiaoli to the dormitory building.","The dormitory building was built twenty or thirty years ago and was very old. However, since Rong Yu was an old antique from seventy years ago, she did not find it backward at all.","On the other hand, a group of four almost went crazy after entering their dormitory.","The room was very small, with two iron-framed beds. The mattresses were as thin as paper, covered with washed-out military bedsheets. In the corner was a wooden table with peeling paint and a missing piece on one of its legs.","Can people even live here? Zhou Shiyu picked at the peeling wall paint in a breakdown. The walls are crumbling!","Seeing a gecko actually clinging to the window, Tang Mi screamed in terror and jumped onto Hai Chang'an.","Si Lin took a deep breath, trying to maintain his composure, but when he discovered there was not even a private bathroom, his last shred of sanity collapsed.","There was only a rust-stained sign with an arrow pointing to the end of the corridor, reading: Public Toilets and Showers.","The four of them were about to lose their minds.","Zhou Shiyu squatted on the ground and burst into tears. There is not even internet here. I want to go home; I want to go home right now...","Si Lin gritted his teeth. I refuse to believe Rong Yu would live in a place like this...","As soon as his voice fell, Rong Yu's figure appeared in the corridor."]},{"number":271,"title":"Chapter 271: You, the love-struck one, have finally come to your senses.","paragraphs":["The four of them looked up and saw Rong Yu walking over from the other end of the corridor.","The light shone on her face, revealing a calm and composed expression. Without a trace of dishevelment or distress, she made them look like absolute clowns.","Tang Mi was the first to rush forward. Rong Yu, I know you have some say around here. Please, change my accommodation. Once we return to Haicheng, I will give you a blank check. You can fill in whatever amount you want.","Si Lin scratched his messy, bird's-nest hair. Miss Rong, as long as you nod, I will have a friend fly a helicopter over to pick us up, and you can leave with us.","Hai Chang'an said with a hoarse voice, The old man sent us here just to make us grow up. We have learned our lesson now, really. Let us go.","Zhou Shiyu's eyes were brimming with tears. Miss Rong, please have mercy and let me go home. Boohoo...","You think this place isn't worthy of your noble statuses? Rong Yu chuckled. The staff at the rocket launch base have lived here for decades, yet you can't even stand it for a few hours?","She had been busy all day and was genuinely exhausted.","She said coldly, If you don't want to stay here, you don't have to. The moonlight is quite nice tonight. Sleeping outside has a certain romantic charm to it. Go ahead.","She turned around and walked into the dormitory next door.","Wang Xiaoli added, The temperature difference in the desert is huge. It gets very cold at night, so don't freeze to death.","The door to the next dormitory closed.","No, what does she mean by that! Si Lin angrily kicked the wall. Does she think just because I am pursuing her, she can walk all over me? Damn it!","Since he was young, he got whatever he wanted. Women threw themselves at him with just a wave of his hand. But Rong Yu? She didn't even spare him a glance, called him trash, and made him suffer in a place like this!","Your love-struck brain has finally sobered up! Tang Mi gritted her teeth. She is only eighteen, younger than all of us. Why should we be bossed around by her? I refuse to accept this.","Zhou Shiyu cried, What can we do even if we don't accept it? We still have to obediently stay here. I didn't even have dinner tonight, I am so hungry... Boohoo.","All you know is how to cry, it is so annoying. Hai Chang'an looked outside. I can't stay in a place like this for even one night. How about we secretly run away?","He wasn't like Tang Jiaquan, who spent his time drinking and partying, nor was he like Si Lin, who had a different woman every day, and he certainly wasn't like that one guy who loved gambling and horse racing... His biggest flaw was being extravagant and loving top-tier luxury goods... Could it be that just because of this, the old man was going to kick him out of the family?","He didn't believe it.","Zhou Shiyu quickly raised her hand. I... I want to run away too.","Her family's old man had sent her here to suffer just to forcefully blend into the circle of the four major families.","Boohoo, what did she do wrong? Was it wrong for her to love live streaming? Was it wrong to love showing off her wealth? Was it wrong to expose the internal gossip of the Zhou family to satisfy netizens' curiosity?","Si Lin slammed the door shut. Chang'an, what is your plan? Tell me quickly, I will execute it.","Tang Mi hesitated. Is... is this a good idea?","She was a bit afraid of being expelled from the family, and she added, Do you have a car? Do you have a map? Do you know the right route?","There are cars at the base entrance. I saw the keys hanging on the wall in the duty room. Hai Chang'an waved his hand.","The four heads huddled together, whispering and plotting for over an hour.","At one o'clock in the morning, they quietly got up and packed their things by the moonlight, although there wasn't much to pack. Tang Mi and Zhou Shiyu carried their high heels in their hands, walking barefoot on the ground as they sneaked out.","Hai Chang'an peeked through the crack of the door. The corridor was pitch black, with only a faint light shining from the duty room at the end.","No one is there.","Like four ghosts, they hugged the walls and slipped out.","The base's parking lot was just behind the dormitories, where a few off-road vehicles were parked quietly. Si Lin sneaked into the duty room; the keys were indeed hanging on the wall. He grabbed them, his heart almost leaping out of his throat.","Hai Chang'an slid into the driver's seat and frantically started the ignition. The moment the engine roared, all four of them stiffened simultaneously, terrified of waking anyone up.","The tires rolled over the sandy ground, making a muffled grinding sound.","Zhou Shiyu clung to the car window and looked back. The outline of the base faded further away in the night. She finally let out a sigh of relief, a relaxed smile appearing on her lips.","As miserable as they were when they arrived, they were equally thrilled now. Even their motion sickness had vanished.","But soon...","They got lost.","Didn't you say we would hit the highway if we drove north?","My... my sense of direction is great! It must be a sandstorm interfering with the magnetic field!","What sandstorm? There isn't even a single cloud in the sky!","Stop arguing. Hai Chang'an yanked the steering wheel hard. The wheels slipped on the sand, the front of the car suddenly dipped, and the front right tire sank into a sand pit.","The arguing came to an abrupt halt.","Push the car! Push hard!","I will count to three, and we will push together.","It won't budge, it completely won't budge, boohoo...","The four collapsed on the sand, panting like four stranded fish.","Just then, they heard a howl.","Awooo—","The sound was long, eerie, and... getting closer.","Hai Chang'an's eyes widened. What was that sound?","Tang Mi's hair stood on end. Oh my god, it is a wolf! It is a wolf! That female doctor said there were wolf packs in the desert!","Zhou Shiyu gave Si Lin a shove. Aren't you good at fighting? Hurry up and get them!","Si Lin: ...I fight nightclub thugs, not wild wolves, okay?","Just as the four huddled together, trembling in fear, the roar of an engine suddenly came from the distance.","Two blinding headlights pierced the darkness. A military off-road vehicle sped toward them, a searchlight mounted on the roof shining so brightly that the four couldn't keep their eyes open.","Help! Help! Tang Mi waved her arms, so excited she was almost in tears. We are over here!","The car braked sharply, kicking up a cloud of dust. The doors opened, and two tall, upright figures walked over.","The desert moonlight was brilliant, illuminating the two men.","Zhou Shiyu was instantly dumbfounded. Holy crap, handsome guys, absolutely top-tier handsome guys. Wearing military uniforms... uniform temptation...","A gaze as sharp as a blade landed on her. It felt so tangible that her voice cut off abruptly, and she shrank behind Tang Mi in fear.","The two men who stepped out of the military vehicle were Sheng Yun and Sheng Qingyan.","Sheng Qingyan had graduated from the capital's military academy. For the past few years, his health hadn't allowed it, so he had been confined at home since graduation. Now, after passing a comprehensive physical examination by the military district, he was finally allowed to join the army.","To have Sheng Yun look after him, Old Madam Sheng had cast aside her pride and asked an old friend to assign Sheng Qingyan to Base Four, where Sheng Yun was stationed, to start from the very bottom.","Sheng Yun had specifically driven out to pick up his eldest nephew.","Who could have expected that they would encounter a group of suspicious-looking individuals halfway there?","Get down! Sheng Yun drew the weapon from his waist and turned to Sheng Qingyan behind him. There has been spy activity in this area recently. Qingyan, quickly take some photos and check who these people are.","The four were terrified and immediately started explaining over one another.","I... I am an influencer, Shiyu Feifei. You can find me if you search it. I have three million followers, I am not a spy.","I am the biological grandson of Hai Dadun from the four major families of Haicheng, my name is Hai Chang'an!","Seeing the expressions of the two soldiers in front of her grow increasingly grim, Tang Mi hurriedly explained, \"W-we are logistics support personnel from the rocket launch base.\"","\"ID?\" Sheng Yun demanded coldly.","Tang Mi looked embarrassed. \"I-I don't have it on me...\"","Sheng Yun frowned. \"Tell me then, which base number, which logistics unit, and what are your employee ID numbers?\"","The four of them froze.","Which base was this again? Base Four, or Base Fourteen? They actually couldn't remember. As for the logistics unit, they had no idea either, let alone their employee ID numbers...","\"Get down! Hands in the air!\" Sheng Yun ordered coldly. \"Tie up these suspicious individuals and hand them over for interrogation!\""]},{"number":272,"title":"Chapter 272: Indeed, Flirting Is a Man's Innate Skill","paragraphs":["In the backseat of the military vehicle, the four people were tied up like crabs.","Zhou Shiyu sobbed loudly, \"We really aren't spies, my wrists hurt so much...\"","Tang Mi cried and shook her head, \"I won't run, I will definitely cooperate with the investigation. Can you untie us first?\"","Sheng Yun coldly scolded, \"Keep arguing and I'll throw you out to feed the wolves.\"","The four of them instantly went as quiet as mice.","Right at that moment—","The piercing sound of brakes rang out as an off-road vehicle blocked their path. Its headlights blazed, so blindingly bright that people couldn't open their eyes.","The car door was pushed open, and a young woman appeared on the sandy ground.","\"Miss Rong, save us!\" Si Lin was so excited he nearly bounced out of his seat. \"This is illegal detention!\"","Zhou Shiyu's eyes welled with tears. \"Rong Yu, quickly explain to them, we really are employees of the support team!\"","Tang Mi pleaded, \"Rong Yu, my grandfather thought so highly of you. He has barely been laid to rest, you can't just leave me...\"","Rong Yu was just about to speak.","When she saw the person sitting in the passenger seat, she froze.","It was Sheng Qingyan.","After parting ways in the capital, they hadn't seen each other for a while. He was completely different from before; he had lost the pampered air of a wealthy young master and gained a tough, iron-blooded aura.","Sheng Qingyan saw her too.","He immediately pushed the door open and stepped out. Under the moonlight, his tall figure looked like an unsheathed military knife.","He wore a crisp military uniform with sharp shoulder lines and a narrow, lean waist. His sleeves were rolled up to his elbows, revealing well-defined forearms with veins faintly bulging beneath the skin.","She stared blankly for a moment before slowly breaking into a smile. \"Sheng Qingyan, do you still remember me?\"","Sheng Qingyan nodded. \"Miss Rong.\"","His serious demeanor made Rong Yu want to laugh.","Who could have imagined that the clingy, obedient large wolf-dog from her past life would now have such an unapproachable expression.","She suddenly wanted to tease him a little.","It would probably be very interesting.","But suddenly, seeing another person step out of the car, she realized there was someone else. She recognized him as the younger uncle of the Sheng family's previous generation, Sheng Yun.","She immediately restrained her expression and spoke calmly, \"This must be Lieutenant Sheng from the Base 4 Military District, right?\"","Upon hearing the words 'Lieutenant Sheng', Sheng Yun's face turned green.","When he first joined the unit, he was a second lieutenant and quickly got promoted to first lieutenant. However, he had been stuck at the rank of lieutenant for over a decade. Those in the military who disliked him would deliberately emphasize the word 'Lieutenant' to humiliate him.","But this Miss Rong probably wasn't humiliating him on purpose, right?","\"So it's Miss Rong, my eldest nephew's benefactor,\" Sheng Yun said. \"This is a military zone. What brings Miss Rong here?\"","Rong Yu looked at the four unlucky souls in the backseat of the car. \"Those are my people, temporary members of the support team. Here is their identification. Lieutenant Sheng, sorry for the trouble.\"","Sheng Yun was just about to reach out and take it.","Sheng Qingyan, standing beside him, suddenly spoke up, \"Lieutenant Sheng, let me handle it.\"","Without waiting for Sheng Yun's agreement, he walked up to Rong Yu and took the ID badges.","With a serious face, he went through the routine with utmost diligence, checking the four messy faces one by one. He verified one and let one go. After finishing, he handed the four ID badges back to Rong Yu. Just as he was about to speak.","Suddenly!","He pulled Rong Yu into his arms.","Rong Yu: \"...\"","She was truly stunned.","In her past life, Ji Zheng had been well-behaved and honest. It was only after they had been together for a long time that he dared to carefully hold her hand.","In this life, Sheng Qingyan was actually this bold. It was truly...","Sheng Yun: \"...\"","Damn it.","This eldest nephew had just returned to normal, could he have already learned how to flirt with girls?","Sure enough, picking up girls was a man's innate skill.","Meanwhile, the four people who had just been untied widened their eyes in shock, their pupils quaking.","Hai Chang'an: \"Holy crap, this guy is taking advantage of Miss Rong. Old Master Ji will kill him.\"","Tang Mi: \"No, what is going on? Are they a couple?\"","Zhou Shiyu: \"Damn it, I had my eye on this handsome guy first. Rong Yu is actually fighting me for him?\"","Si Lin: \"Hey, don't think I'm afraid of you just because you're wearing a military uniform. Is Miss Rong someone you can take advantage of...\"","He stopped mid-sentence, suddenly choking on his words.","He stared intently behind Rong Yu, his eyes almost popping out of his head. His voice got stuck in his throat, \"There's, there's, there's...\"","Before he could get the word out.","\"Whoosh!\"","A dark shadow swept up, lunging toward Rong Yu's back. Sheng Qingyan hugged her, spun around to switch their positions, and then raised his hand. He grabbed the creature by its weak point and slammed it onto the hood of the military vehicle with a loud smack.","Everyone's gazes simultaneously shot over. They saw that it was a sand python over a meter long. Its black and yellow scales gleamed coldly in the moonlight, its tongue hissed, and venom dripped from its fangs.","Immediately after, screams erupted.","Tang Mi passed out from sheer terror, Zhou Shiyu frantically backed away, and Si Lin and Hai Chang'an hugged each other, jumping up and down wildly. \"A snake! Oh my god, there's a snake ahhh!\"","Sheng Qingyan protected Rong Yu with one hand and drew his military knife with the other. With a swift \"swish,\" he threw it. The tip of the blade accurately pinned the snake's head down. The sand python thrashed wildly a couple of times and then stopped moving.","Rong Yu's eyes lit up.","His combat skills were still so clean and efficient.","Curving her lips, she asked, \"Sheng Qingyan, how long will you be staying here?\"","Sheng Yun whistled and intentionally asked with a wicked grin, \"What's wrong, Miss Rong? Do you like my eldest nephew?\"","Rong Yu sized up the two of them with her eyes and said unhurriedly, \"Compared to Lieutenant Sheng, his appearance is more outstanding and his physique is taller. It's hard for me not to like him.\"","She hadn't forgotten that during their first meeting at the hospital, Sheng Yun had shoved her. For a gentlewoman's revenge, ten years is not too late.","From the corner of her eye, she kept staring at Sheng Qingyan.","Under the moonlight, she saw that his face had actually turned red.","Compared to his thick skin after their marriage, this blushing version of him made her incredibly nostalgic.","Sheng Yun puffed in anger, \"Miss Rong only looks at the exterior and ignores the interior. That's a bit superficial, huh.\"","\"Sheng Qingyan graduated from the Capital Military Academy. What about you, Lieutenant Sheng?\" Rong Yu smiled. \"Sheng Qingyan can kill a sand python barehanded. What about you, Lieutenant Sheng?\"","Sheng Yun: \"...\"","Fine, fine, fine. In the end, he was the clown.","He kicked the damn sand python away and got into the car.","The sand python was kicked right to the feet of the four people. Scared out of their wits, they scrambled and crawled toward Rong Yu's car.","The man in front of her was blushing so hard his face was practically dripping blood, which put Rong Yu in an excellent mood. She stopped teasing him and smiled, \"Sheng Qingyan, it's getting late. I'll take these four away first.\"","Sheng Qingyan stood in place, watching the taillights of Rong Yu's car disappear behind the sand dunes before he got into his own vehicle.","Inside Rong Yu's car, the four people huddled in the backseat, still recovering from the shock.","She glanced at them through the rearview mirror. \"Still going to run?\"","The four of them shook their heads frantically.","\"In the desert, aside from sand pythons, there are also venomous scorpions, wolf packs, quicksand... You guys got lucky today.\" Rong Yu's voice was icy. \"Making everyone work in the middle of the night to search for you—tomorrow's breakfast is canceled. Hurry up and get back to the dormitory area. If you cause any more trouble, you'll face the consequences!\"","The four of them didn't even dare to breathe too loudly.","After a whole day of torment, the four were exhausted beyond belief. They no longer complained about the hard bed boards, nor did they mind the rough blankets. They made do with a cold shower and fell asleep the moment their heads hit the pillows."]},{"number":273,"title":"Chapter 273: This is physical labor; girls are naturally not good at it.","paragraphs":["At five in the morning, the group of four was brutally dragged from their dreams by a piercing whistle.","\"Get up! Assemble!\"","Tang Mi shot up from her bed, her hair looking as if it had been struck by lightning. Before she could even fully open her eyes, her stomach began to rumble in protest.","\"I... I'm going to starve to death...\" she clung weakly to the edge of the bed, looking as though she might breathe her last at any second.","Zhou Shiyu curled up under her quilt. \"Just five more minutes... just five minutes.\"","Si Lin and Hai Chang'an were not faring any better. The two of them had been dreaming about gnawing on chicken drumsticks all night, and now their stomachs were so empty you could hear an echo.","However, when they rushed to the cafeteria, they were greeted only by empty food trays and the cold, stern face of the person in charge, Lao Ma.","\"Where's the breakfast?\" Si Lin's voice cracked.","Lao Ma, a cigarette dangling from his lips, slowly blew a smoke ring. \"You stole a car to run away last night, violating discipline, so your breakfast was docked. What, didn't Engineer Rong tell you?\"","The four of them were speechless.","Rong Yu had certainly told them, but they thought she was just joking around.","They had barely eaten their lunch on the plane yesterday and even threw up. After arriving at the base, they couldn't stomach dinner, and now they had no breakfast. Were they being tortured?","Tang Mi clutched her stomach. \"This is abuse! I'm going to sue you!\"","Zhou Shiyu held onto her last shred of dignity and sneered, \"Heh, I'd rather not eat this lousy breakfast anyway! It looks terrible at a glance!\"","Si Lin stared at the meat buns in the bowls of the researchers at the next table, his Adam's apple bobbing as he swallowed hard. \"Indeed, it looks far too greasy.\"","Hai Chang'an's stomach growled again. He weakly supported himself against the table. \"I'm actually... not that hungry either...\"","Lao Ma crushed out his cigarette. \"Get in the car with me, time to start work over there.\"","The four dragged their famished bodies and followed him to the base's nursery area. Rows of tender green saplings were neatly stacked on the sandy ground, with hill-like piles of nutrient soil and tools nearby.","Lao Ma said strictly, \"Your morning task is for each person to move two hundred saplings to the designated area.\"","\"What?\" Tang Mi's eyes widened. \"Why don't you just say two thousand, or twenty thousand! We're humans, not camels!\"","Zhou Shiyu immediately raised her hand. \"Besides, we are girls. The boys should do more of the physical labor.\"","Before Lao Ma could speak, Rong Yu's cold voice came from behind. \"Don't you shout about gender equality and advocate for women's rights in your livestreams every day?\"","Zhou Shiyu stiffened. She turned around to see Rong Yu standing not far away with her arms crossed. Dressed in a neat and crisp work uniform, she exuded an overwhelming aura.","She stammered, parting her lips, \"How is that the same? This is physical labor, and girls naturally aren't good at physical labor.\"","\"Moving a few saplings is considered physical labor?\" Rong Yu chuckled. \"When the female engineers on the research team carry equipment alone for miles and work back-to-back night shifts, why doesn't anyone say that it's physical labor and men should do it?\"","Zhou Shiyu choked on her words. \"I...\"","Rong Yu's voice was light. \"You're full of righteous indignation when demanding privileges, but you hide in the back when it comes to taking responsibility. Is this the gender equality you want?\"","Zhou Shiyu's face flushed red, unable to squeeze out a single word.","Si Lin and Hai Chang'an stood to the side, wanting to chime in but not daring to. After all, they couldn't even save themselves, starving as they were.","Lao Ma said coldly, \"If you don't finish, your lunch will be docked too.\"","The four of them were speechless.","Ruthless, truly too ruthless!","Half an hour later, with the desert sun beating down, the four of them swayed like zombies as they carried the saplings.","Tang Mi cursed with every step she took. \"Why are such small saplings so heavy? There are so many people in the Tang family, why did it have to be me sent here to suffer? It's unfair, so unfair!\"","Zhou Shiyu cried as she moved her load. \"My face is going to get sunburned, how am I supposed to livestream in the future, boo hoo hoo...\"","Hai Chang'an muttered, \"Just carry them, hurry up and finish. I'm really starving to death.\"","Si Lin gritted his teeth. \"Hang in there, we can't let Rong Yu look down on us.\"","Although Hai Chang'an and Si Lin were also raised pampered and spoiled, they worked out in their free time and often got into fights, so they naturally had more strength. By almost eleven-thirty, they finally huffed and puffed their way to completing the assigned task.","The two quickly found a shaded spot to lie down.","In the distance, Tang Mi and Zhou Shiyu were still struggling in the sand.","\"Hahaha, look at them.\" Si Lin laughed loudly. \"Aren't they usually so talkative? Now they can't even figure out how to carry a tree.\"","Hai Chang'an rubbed his sore shoulders. \"So slow. At their pace, they can forget about having dinner too.\"","\"It seems you are very satisfied with your own performance.\"","Rong Yu had just stepped out of the car and overheard this conversation.","Her face was expressionless as she walked over coldly. This demeanor made Hai Chang'an a little scared, and Si Lin didn't dare to laugh anymore.","\"Do you know why they are slower than the two of you?\" she asked coldly. \"The saplings you two carried are all damaged to some extent. Either the roots are damaged, or the leaves have fallen off. This will reduce the survival rate of the saplings by at least twenty percent.\"","She pointed into the distance. \"Take a good look at how Tang Mi and Zhou Shiyu are completing the task!\"","The two followed her gaze.","Tang Mi held a few saplings, squatted down first, and then carefully set them down. The entire process was very slow.","Zhou Shiyu even picked up a watering can nearby and sprinkled water on the leaves before starting her next trip.","\"They are taking their work seriously, which is why they are slow,\" Rong Yu sneered. \"Rather than half-assing the job and then hiding in the shade to mock their companions.\"","\"The four of you are a team.\" Rong Yu's voice wasn't loud, but every word struck the two men's hearts. \"Here, there is no such thing as your task or my task. There is only our task.\"","Si Lin and Hai Chang'an stood stunned for a long moment.","Hai Chang'an was the first to recover. He strode over, snatched the three saplings from Tang Mi's arms, and hoisted them onto his own shoulder.","Tang Mi stared at him blankly. \"W-what are you doing?\"","\"Teamwork.\" Hai Chang'an marched forward. \"Don't just stand there looking dumb, hurry up and keep going.\"","Si Lin also walked over and said to Zhou Shiyu, \"Don't you advocate for gender equality? I'll carry them, and you take charge of receiving them and spraying water to ensure the saplings' survival rate. Can you do that?\"","Zhou Shiyu smiled. \"Of course.\"","The shadows of the four gradually overlapped under the scorching sun. Their sweat mixed together, and sand covered everyone's pant legs, but no one complained anymore.","Rong Yu stood watching from a distance, the corners of her lips turning up imperceptibly.","When the last sapling was transported to the planting area, Lao Ma walked over to inspect it. He gave a rare nod. \"Barely passable.\"","The four let out a massive sigh of relief, collapsing onto the ground in exhaustion.","\"What are you still slumped there for!\" Rong Yu honked the car horn. \"If you dawdle any longer, there won't even be soup left in the cafeteria!\""]},{"number":274,"title":"Chapter 274: Where Should Your Talents Be Put to Use","paragraphs":["Inside the core zone.","Complex orbit calculation models were projected onto the massive electronic screen.","Rong Yu was conducting an orbit analysis.","Wang Xiaoli was assisting her by her side. Next to them were Zhao Mingzhe and Jiang Si, both senior engineers with exceptional capabilities in this field. Meanwhile, seven or eight researchers specializing in mathematics, physics, materials, thermal energy, and mechanical engineering were working together with them.","\"If we use these parameters, the orbit insertion accuracy will drop by 0.3 percent,\" Zhao Mingzhe frowned. \"But fuel consumption has already reached its limit.\"","Rong Yu stood in front of the screen, resting her chin in her hand, and said, \"What if we adjust the separation angle of the third-stage rocket to 42.7 degrees and use the Earth's rotational inertia for compensation? What would happen then?\"","Jiang Si frantically ran the calculations, his pupils dilating slightly. \"This... this would save about 2 percent of the fuel.\"","Everyone in the room looked shocked.","This young Engineer Rong was simply too outstanding. In the entire base, there was probably only one other person as brilliant as her, and that was Chief Engineer Cui Xiao.","They couldn't even imagine how far this Engineer Rong would go, standing on the shoulders of Chief Engineer Pei's years of experience.","Rong Yu spent the whole day calculating in the office area. It wasn't until after seven in the evening that she and Wang Xiaoli got off work and walked out of the office building.","As soon as they reached the main gate, they saw four people leaning over the railing. From left to right, they were Si Lin, Hai Chang'an, Tang Mi, and Zhou Shiyu.","The four of them had been busy in the desert all day. After eating the ordinary meals they would have previously looked down upon, they were instantly revived and started wandering around aimlessly. Because they were temporary workers with insufficient clearance, they couldn't get in anywhere. This spot was the closest place they could get to observe the rocket.","Not far away stood the carrier rocket. Its silvery-white body gleamed with a warm orange glow under the setting sun, towering into the clouds and delivering a powerful visual impact.","\"So cool!\" Si Lin marvelled. \"This is way more exciting than clubbing!\"","\"A rocket! It's a real rocket!\" Zhou Shiyu really wanted to take a picture but didn't dare to, so she could only stare at it intently.","Just then, the door to the work area opened. The group turned around and saw Rong Yu there. They immediately grew excited and quickly gathered around her.","Hai Chang'an was the first to speak: \"Miss Rong, I graduated from a renowned overseas college. I want to apply for a job change, preferably something related to rockets. I love rockets so much.\"","Tang Mi quickly followed, \"I... I also studied abroad. I majored in economic management, so I should be able to help you with data analysis.\"","Zhou Shiyu was not to be outdone: \"I also went to a top-tier university. Doing some clerical work should be more than enough for me.\"","Si Lin: \"...\"","He was only a sophomore in college; he wasn't anything yet.","Oh right, he was still a college student. Why wasn't he studying at school instead of coming to this wretched place to suffer?","Rong Yu's gaze swept over their sunburned, peeling cheeks and their scraped fingers. She said mildly, \"Are you sure you can handle the tasks I assign you?\"","The four of them nodded in unison.","As long as they could work in an office, they would do anything. It was bound to be more comfortable than baking in the desert sun.","Rong Yu said, \"Gather here tomorrow morning.\"","The four were overjoyed.","Early the next morning, the four of them ate breakfast and waited there.","After passing through layers of security checks, they stepped inside. There was air conditioning. This was the first time the four of them had felt air conditioning since arriving at the base, and they greedily took a deep breath.","Rong Yu led them into a small public conference room and pushed a document toward them. \"Work together and calculate this: what is the total cost of successfully planting and growing a single saxaul tree in the desert?\"","Tang Mi opened the file, her smile freezing.","The unit price of soil conditioners, manual labor costs, the depreciation rate of the irrigation system... The densely packed spreadsheets turned her brain to mush.","\"This...\" Zhou Shiyu opened her pretty, bewildered eyes wide. \"How am I supposed to know how to calculate the amortization period for irrigation pipes?\"","Hai Chang'an was stunned. \"What is carbon sequestration benefit?\"","Si Lin was even more clueless.","Two hours later, Rong Yu pushed open the door to the small conference room and saw that the four were still frowning in distress.","She walked over and said calmly, \"One saxaul tree, over an 18-year life cycle, requires a total investment of 327 yuan. Its carbon sequestration value is 1,420 yuan, and its windbreak and sand-fixation benefit is 8,940 yuan.\"","She looked at Tang Mi. \"How much did that pair of high heels of yours cost?\"","\"Thirty... thirty-eight thousand.\"","She turned to Si Lin. \"How much was your watch?\"","\"Two point six million.\"","Rong Yu looked at the group. \"Your pair of shoes and one watch are enough to plant approximately 7,938 saxaul trees, which can stabilize half a football field's worth of quicksand.\"","Her gaze moved from the scratch paper to their faces, her fingertips tapping lightly on the table. \"Do you know what that many saxaul trees means?\"","The wind outside the window suddenly picked up, causing the glass of the observation deck to buzz and vibrate.","\"It means the probability of exposed equipment outside being damaged by wind and sand is reduced by at least three percent. It also means that the people living on this land might suffer one less sandstorm.\" She pulled out a satellite map, her fingertip pointing at the yellow erosion zone on it. \"At the same time, it means that by this time next year, the base's perimeter will have two fewer tons of sand and dust to clear away...\"","All four of them were deeply shaken.","They were born into wealthy, prestigious families with silver spoons in their mouths. Normally, a piece of clothing they wore cost tens of thousands, a bag hundreds of thousands, a car millions, and a villa tens of millions...","When that money was squandered, nothing was left.","But here, it could actually create such immense value.","\"But that's not the issue here.\" Rong Yu suddenly gathered all the documents and neatly tucked them into the folder. \"Can you solve partial differential equations? Can you read remote sensing imagery?\"","The four remained silent.","\"So,\" she pushed back her chair and stood up, \"when you're moving the saplings, think carefully about where your talents should actually be used.\"","Hai Chang'an's Adam's apple bobbed. \"We...\"","Rong Yu pulled open the door to the work area, and a heatwave laced with sand and dust rushed in. \"Now, go and finish moving the new batch of saxaul saplings that just arrived in the East District.\"","No matter how reluctant they were to leave the air conditioning, they didn't have the audacity to ask to stay.","One by one, they hung their heads, stood up, and trudged dejectedly out into the scorching sun to resume the same work as yesterday.","They had just left.","Suddenly, an alarm blared from the core zone.","Rong Yu turned around and sprinted swiftly toward the core zone.","The main screen, along with all the computer monitors, simultaneously flashed blood-red warning boxes.","\"The database has been breached!\" an engineer's voice trembled. \"The intruders have broken through the first firewall and are attempting to copy core data!\"","Rong Yu's gaze sharpened.","The base's database contained at least one-third of Hua Xia's top-secret aerospace data. If it were leaked, the consequences would be unimaginable...","Cui Xiao also rushed over, speaking rapidly, \"Everyone, assist the Chief Engineer of Data Security in protecting the database. You must act fast!\"","Rong Yu was just about to approach a computer when Cui Xiao pulled her back. \"You are a mathematical and physical genius, but when it comes to data engineering, it's better left to the professionals.\"","The chief engineer in charge of this area was a man in his thirties. He squeezed past Rong Yu, his hands operating the keyboard rapidly."]},{"number":275,"title":"Chapter 275: In Consideration of You Being My Elder Nephew's Lifesaver","paragraphs":["Every day, every hour, every minute, and even down to the exact second since Rong Yu arrived seventy years in the future, she had been absorbing knowledge like a sponge.","Previous studies had shown that with the right learning methods, any ordinary person could reach a relatively high level of proficiency in a subject after sixty hours of intense, focused study. Let alone a study god like Rong Yu. As long as she set her mind to learning a subject, she would relentlessly push herself, sleeping only three or four hours a day. Within a week, she could easily reach an average level of proficiency.","If she was particularly interested in a field, she would spend even more time on detailed study and research.","Computer programming, especially the subject of hacking, happened to be one of her interests. During her first month in this era, she had consciously begun to study it.","After less than half a month of learning, she breached the Ji Group's firewall.","Later, after more specialized research, her skills in this area could be considered quite masterful, though she rarely had the opportunity for practical application.","Rong Yu didn't act rashly.","However, the blaring alarms grew increasingly urgent. On the large screen, the rate of data loss was shocking. With every jump of the bright red numbers, the faces of everyone in the room grew a shade paler.","\"The second firewall has been breached!\"","\"The third firewall is collapsing...\"","The chief programming engineer was sweating profusely. He spoke rapidly, \"We don't have enough people! We're short-handed! Hurry, get support from the military district, fast!\"","Cui Xiao wasn't an expert in this field, but he understood enough. His face was pale. \"It's too late. It'll be too late even if the people from the military district rush over. Engineer Rong, Engineer Zhao... you guys, use the fastest speed...\"","Before he could finish his sentence.","Rong Yu walked up to the main control panel, reached out, and began to operate it.","\"What are you doing?!\" the chief programming engineer shouted harshly. \"This isn't something an amateur like you can handle!\"","Cui Xiao pulled him back. \"Let Engineer Rong give it a try.\"","When he was young and full of energy, he had also studied many extra subjects and ranked first in all of them.","Now, in the age of the information explosion, acquiring knowledge was even easier. A genius like Rong Yu couldn't possibly be proficient in only one field.","Rong Yu directly hacked into the core system and began writing defense codes.","The chief programming engineer froze the moment he caught a glimpse of her screen. Her code structure was incredibly exquisite. That line of code was actually self-replicating, automatically patching system vulnerabilities like living vines.","\"This...\" His pupils shrank slightly. \"Dynamic neural topological encryption? This technology only started being put into practical use this year... How can you use it so proficiently?\"","\"It is that technology, but I improved it a bit.\" Rong Yu didn't even look up, her fingers flying rapidly across the keyboard.","The main screen suddenly split into twelve sections, each displaying breathtaking operations. The five sections on the left were building virtual honeypots in real-time, the three in the middle were rewriting the system kernel, and the four on the far right were actually reverse-compiling the attacker's hardware characteristics.","The onlookers were all dumbfounded.","Too strong, this was just too strong!","Such a talent should be in their Engineering Data Department!","Rong Yu took a brief moment to say, \"I can only block this wave, but the next wave of attacks will require real-time countermeasures. I'm not very familiar with this part of the operation.\"","The chief programming engineer immediately issued orders. \"Engineer Li, lead a team to handle counter-tracking! Engineer Wang, reinforce the secondary firewall! Xiao Zhou, transfer all the computing power from the backup servers over here...\"","The entire main control room instantly turned into a boiling battlefield. Twenty-three engineers worked frantically under the defense framework built by Rong Yu.","These codes were like a sharp sword, severing the intruder's data links, while the base's team erected layers of defenses like a sturdy shield. Ten minutes later, when the last firewall node lit up green, someone started it, and the entire main control room erupted into tsunami-like cheers.","Rong Yu, however, was still operating at the main console.","Cui Xiao asked in a low voice, \"What's wrong?\"","\"There's an abnormal data stream that needs to be tracked.\" Rong Yu's talking didn't delay her operations; her fingers moved faster and faster.","Suddenly, the data stream on the screen stopped, and a red warning box popped up, occupying the entire display.","\"Encrypted signal detected. Danger level: Extremely High.\"","The chief programming engineer's face changed instantly. \"This is the first time in all the years the system has been running that it has automatically determined a danger signal to be extremely high.\"","Cui Xiao's expression was grave. He took out his communicator and immediately contacted the security department of the troops stationed at the base.","It was more appropriate to hand this kind of thing over to the decryption experts in the security department.","Seventy years ago, Rong Yu had participated in decryption work.","In that unstable era, the country had too few talents, so she was often borrowed for such tasks. All things considered, she had some experience.","She sat there, frowning in deep thought.","But after thinking for more than twenty minutes, she still didn't have a clue.","At this time, the military's decryption experts arrived. In this base, there were a total of two experts and eight related personnel, escorted in by more than twenty soldiers.","As soon as she looked up, she saw Sheng Qingyan.","Sheng Qingyan had just joined the base troops and was at the lowest level. Dressed in a military uniform, his figure was tall and straight as he stood by the main gate, guarding the exit.","Him standing there made Rong Yu feel exceptionally at ease.","She withdrew her gaze, shook hands with the approaching experts, and got straight to the point: \"...This isn't a traditional encryption method, but a new type of cipher based on quantum computing principles. It cannot be cracked using conventional algorithms...\"","The leading expert looked at her and frowned. \"And this is?\"","\"Let me introduce her,\" Cui Xiao spoke up. \"This is Engineer Rong, the technical consultant sent by the Fourth Aerospace Institute. She is a rare genius in our Hua Xia country...\"","At this point, his voice dropped very low. \"For that groundbreaking project at the Fourth Institute, she is the chief designer. She's only eighteen, a high school student. Her future is unimaginable...\"","The expert understood immediately, his eyes filled with appreciation. \"Then please, Engineer Rong, explain it in more detail.\"","Rong Yu invited the experts to sit down, and both sides began to study it carefully.","However, this cipher had multiple layers of encryption, and the technique used for each layer was different. The entire team stayed up for two days and one night, but they couldn't even decrypt one percent of it.","The higher the level of the cipher, the higher the danger. No one dared to slack off in the slightest.","But, they had to rest eventually.","Rong Yu was ordered by the experts to go back to her dorm and lie down first, and come back to take over the shift tomorrow morning.","She walked out yawning and saw that the guards standing by the door had changed to a new batch. After walking out the main gate, she didn't see Sheng Qingyan either.","\"Tsk, looking for my eldest nephew?\"","A highly punchable voice came from the side.","Rong Yu turned her head to look and smiled. \"Hiding here to smoke while on duty. No wonder Lieutenant Sheng is still in the position of a lieutenant in his thirties.\"","Sheng Yun: \"...\"","He shouldn't have provoked her; her mouth was truly toxic.","He snorted, \"Seeing as you're my eldest nephew's lifesaver, I won't bother arguing with you.\"","\"Sheng Yun!\"","At this moment, a car stopped at the entrance of the office building. A woman in professional attire got out of the car and walked straight up to Sheng Yun.","Sheng Yun frowned. \"Why are you here?\"","\"Base Four overcame a technical difficulty, so the station specially sent me to do a feature report.\" The woman turned her eyes to look at Rong Yu. \"Sheng Yun, who is this?\"","Sheng Yun stubbed out his cigarette and shrugged. \"There's no need for introductions.\"","The woman looked rather awkward. \"Sheng Yun, I am your girlfriend, after all.\"","Sheng Yun's attitude grew even more indifferent. \"We can just break up, then.\"","Rong Yu: \"...\"","She was dead on her feet and had no energy to stick around for the gossip. All she wanted was to hurry back to her dorm and get some sleep."]},{"number":276,"title":"Chapter 276: She must be jealous of our business acumen.","paragraphs":["Rong Yu slept soundly until early the next morning.","She went to the cafeteria for breakfast first. As soon as she walked in, she was surrounded by the foursome, who were chattering away non-stop.","\"Miss Rong, where have you been these past two days!\"","\"Didn't you ask where our talents should be used? We thought about it all night and finally know how to put our skills to good use!\"","Rong Yu swallowed her bite of steamed bun and said leisurely, \"Let's hear it.\"","Hai Chang'an: \"My college major was art. I think I can redesign a much cooler exterior for the rocket.\"","Zhou Shiyu: \"We can modify the rocket into a space livestreaming room and broadcast the whole journey. If fans send 'rocket' virtual gifts, they can make the astronauts do backflips.\"","Tang Mi: \"We can also let fans vote to decide which astronaut gets to go up in the rocket next time. The ratings would definitely go through the roof.\"","Si Lin: \"We can cover the outside of the rocket with advertising space, with bidding starting at least at a hundred million!\"","Rong Yu almost laughed out loud.","She finished her last bite of breakfast and looked up.","\"The outer coating of a rocket has to withstand high temperatures of 2000 degrees. Hai Chang'an, how much heat can your fluorescent paints take?\"","\"Livestreaming inside a rocket... Zhou Shiyu, you really have quite the imagination. Do you want to look up why the base restricts internet access for you temporary workers?\"","\"Choosing an astronaut requires comprehensive consideration of various factors. But to you, Tang Mi, a simple vote is enough?\"","\"The surface temperature of a rocket can reach two thousand degrees when it passes through the atmosphere. Si Lin, who are you planning to burn your advertisements for?\"","The four of them: \"...\"","Rong Yu stood up. \"Use your brilliance and think it over again.\"","She stepped away and left the cafeteria.","The four deflated instantly, like balloons pricked by a needle.","Si Lin was unconvinced. \"She's definitely just jealous of our business acumen!\"","\"Exactly, what's wrong with livestreaming?\" Zhou Shiyu rolled her eyes. \"Other astronauts have livestreamed before, haven't they? What's the big deal, honestly!\"","Tang Mi scoffed coldly. \"Why do we have to listen to her anyway? She's younger than us. Why should we do whatever she says?\"","Hai Chang'an sighed. \"Who asked our old men to blindly trust her...\"","The four headed to the work area.","The task of moving trees was over. Starting today, they were learning to plant trees.","Under the scorching sun, the foursome squatted in the sandy ground, clutching saxaul saplings. Their expressions were even more withered than the saplings. The trees they planted were leaning every which way, looking like drunks that would collectively lie flat the moment a strong wind blew.","Lao Ma strolled over with his hands behind his back. With just one glance, his face turned as black as the bottom of a pot.","\"Are you planting trees or burying corpses?\" He bent down and pulled out a leaning sapling, the dirt falling off its roots. \"The roots aren't even packed tight. They'll fall over with a gust of wind. What the hell kind of planting is this!\"","Tang Mi felt wronged. \"We aren't farmers, how are we supposed to know how to do this!\"","Lao Ma sneered. \"If you don't know, then learn! The four of you will stand guard here tonight. You can go back to sleep when you've planted them properly!\"","\"On what grounds?\" Zhou Shiyu's eyes widened. \"I refuse!\"","Lao Ma walked away without looking back, tossing out a single sentence: \"If you refuse, then get out.\"","\"Damn it!\" Si Lin threw down his shovel. \"It's good enough that I'm willing to obediently plant trees. Why so many damn demands? So annoying!\"","Hai Chang'an gave a sinister smile. \"How about we give Lao Ma a little surprise?\"","As soon as doing something bad was mentioned, the four seemed to be instantly injected with endless energy and immediately started putting their plan into action.","Tang Mi coated the handle of Lao Ma's usual shovel with lubricating oil so he'd slip and fall the moment he grabbed it.","Zhou Shiyu strung a thin rope across the warehouse door at the perfect height to trip someone.","Si Lin secretly rubbed chili pepper into Lao Ma's water bottle.","Hai Chang'an dug a pit, loosely covered it with dead branches, and placed an empty bucket at the bottom. Falling into it in public would definitely be super humiliating.","Imagining Lao Ma making a fool of himself gave the four of them the motivation to work. They didn't return to their dorms until two in the morning. The next morning, they were woken up by the whistle again, entering the cafeteria with huge dark circles under their eyes.","As soon as they entered, they saw Lao Ma walking toward them.","The foursome's sleepiness instantly vanished, replaced by a bit of fear. Could it be that Lao Ma had discovered their masterpieces early?","\"That corsac fox has finally been caught.\" Lao Ma's gruff voice echoed through the cafeteria. \"You four are the great heroes!\"","The four looked completely bewildered.","Shouldn't he be scolding them? Why did it seem like he was praising them?","Lao Ma showed a rare expression of approval. \"That beast ruined several saplings recently. I staked it out for three days and couldn't catch it. It's you young people who have quick minds, knowing how to set traps.\"","Hai Chang'an: \"...\"","He had indeed dug that, but it wasn't to catch a fox, it was for...","Lao Ma suddenly sighed. \"I was also at fault for what happened yesterday. Planting trees requires technique. I shouldn't have let you figure it out blindly on your own. After breakfast, go to the nursery area, and I will teach you step by step.\"","Watching his slightly hunched back, the four suddenly felt the steamed buns in their mouths were a bit hard to swallow.","After breakfast, the four sprinted toward the nursery area at the speed of a hundred-meter dash, but not to learn—they went to destroy the evidence.","Tang Mi frantically wiped the oil-covered shovel handle.","Zhou Shiyu hurriedly untied the tripping rope.","Just as Si Lin was about to secretly switch Lao Ma's water bottle back, he suddenly heard footsteps behind him.","\"Oh, so early?\" A forest ranger walked in, his eyes lighting up. \"Are you guys fixing the tools?\"","\"Ah... yes!\" Tang Mi braced herself and held up the freshly wiped shovel. \"Just doing some maintenance, haha.\"","Several people passing by praised them one after another.","\"Lao Ma said you guys were spoiled, but you're actually quite reliable!\"","\"You guys have improved so much. If my son were this worry-free, I'd eat two extra bowls of rice.\"","\"These days, there aren't many kids as hardworking as you.\"","\"...\"","Amidst the praise, the four gradually lost themselves. Turning over a new leaf, they huffed and puffed, working with all their might.","Meanwhile, Rong Yu had already arrived at the core area.","The two experts had worked until their faces were dark with exhaustion, but they still hadn't cracked the code.","Rong Yu printed out all the current hypotheses, found a corner, and earnestly began to study them.","The experts had already tried over eight hundred combination algorithms, but none matched this encryption pattern.","She lightly chewed on the end of her pen, frowning deep in thought.","Were they too fixated on the technical aspect, which was why they had no clues?","What if she changed her line of thinking?","Rong Yu's eyes suddenly widened.","Cui Xiao, who was right next to her, quickly asked, \"Did you find something?\"","\"I suspect this is a cultural-level key,\" Rong Yu said slowly. \"Although these characters seem random, a slight variation appears after every seven characters. It reminded me of Go... the ancient Chinese manual recording method, where variations start from the seventh move, corresponding to the opening moves of the Tengen layout...\"","She practically lunged at her computer, her fingers flying across the keyboard. On the screen, the password characters were rearranged and converted according to the rules she had just described.","\"Give me three minutes.\" Rong Yu's voice was as taut as a bowstring.","The conference room was completely silent; everyone held their breath and stared at her screen.","\"Got it!\" Rong Yu suddenly understood it all, almost jumping out of her chair. \"This isn't a regular encrypted message. This is a secret route report!\"","She swiftly projected the decoded results onto the main screen.","The once-jumbled characters had now transformed into lines of clear Chinese text:","\"Target's daily schedule: wakes up at 5:00 AM, morning workout at 5:30 AM, breakfast at 6:30 AM...\""]},{"number":277,"title":"Chapter 277: Secret Report Leaked, They Chose to Act Directly","paragraphs":["A dead silence filled the conference room.","Everyone's eyes shifted from the screen to Cui Xiao, because every detail on this itinerary matched Cui Xiao's daily habits perfectly.","Cui Xiao spoke slowly, \"I'm being targeted.\"","The two guards beside him quickly said, \"Chief Engineer Cui, please follow us to evacuate immediately.\"","\"To know my daily habits like the back of their hand means the enemy has been lurking for a long time.\" Cui Xiao's voice was cold. \"I suspect...\"","He only said half of what was on his mind.","But everyone present was smart. They understood immediately: there was a traitor in the base.","Moreover, this person was highly likely someone deeply trusted by Cui Xiao.","In other words, under these circumstances, no matter where he was transferred, his personal safety could not be guaranteed.","\"Using Go as a secret code, it's obvious they are those bastards from the Sakura Country!\" an engineer cursed angrily. \"They can't compete fairly, so they resort to these dirty assassination tactics!\"","\"Those scumbags have never had good intentions!\" another person said through gritted teeth. \"They failed to steal our high-speed rail technology back then, and now they actually come to assassinate Chief Engineer Cui in a vain attempt to destroy our country's aerospace industry!\"","\"Everyone, calm down,\" Cui Xiao said. \"Contact the military immediately to secretly send more personnel. At the same time, conduct an internal investigation. I will go about my daily routine as usual. Only by luring the snake out of its hole can we catch the turtle in the jar.\"","Everyone present grew extremely anxious.","Chief Engineer Cui was the soul and leading figure of Base Four. If anything happened to Chief Engineer Cui, Base Four would effectively be destroyed...","However, before anyone could react.","Suddenly, a sharp alarm sounded from outside the building.","Rong Yu's expression changed. \"The secret report was leaked. They've decided to strike directly.\"","\"Quick, cover Chief Engineer Cui's evacuation!\"","But it was too late.","The enemy was too familiar with the base. It was exactly shift change. Taking advantage of the three-minute window during the soldiers' handover, the group directly threw explosives. Stun grenades exploded loudly outside the multi-layered doors, and the blinding white light and high-decibel noise crashed into them like a physical force.","Rong Yu's vision went completely white, leaving only a sharp ringing in her ears, but relying on muscle memory, she tackled Cui Xiao to the ground.","Bang!","A bullet grazed the ends of her hair and embedded itself into the wall.","The enemy's target was Cui Xiao.","Cui Xiao was no ordinary engineer.","When he was exceptionally recruited into the satellite launch center at the age of eighteen, he was already a legend in the Chinese Academy of Sciences' youth class. In an era when computers were still a rarity, he manually calculated and derived the rocket's fuel ratio formula, solving the combustion oscillation problem that had plagued the team for half a year.","Nearly forty years had passed. The genius youth of the past now carried three gleaming aerospace merit medals on his shoulders. He was a national treasure.","And now, this national treasure had been tackled to the ground by her, his glasses shattered.","Cui Xiao was severely nearsighted. Without his glasses, he was virtually blind. He spoke very quickly, \"I still have three unreleased design blueprints in my drawer. Even if I...\"","Rong Yu pushed him toward the corridor. \"I'll hold them off here. Go!\"","She snatched up a steel chair frame by her feet and hurled it with all her might at the two charging enemies.","One enemy's head was busted open on the spot.","The other man pressed the gun in his hand against Rong Yu's chest.","Rat-tat-tat-tat!","A burst of bullets suddenly swept in from behind. The armed enemy in front of Rong Yu fell as if struck by lightning, and the other enemies in the conference room also collapsed one after another.","Rong Yu looked up and saw seven or eight figures in Chinese military uniforms standing at the doorway, where the smoke had yet to clear.","The leading young officer was none other than Sheng Yun. He shouted, \"The military has arrived to provide backup. This area is now under the control of me, Sheng Yun...\"","Before Rong Yu could even breathe a sigh of relief, she saw the person behind Sheng Yun, Sheng Qingyan, suddenly lunge forward and pin Sheng Yun to the ground.","Almost simultaneously, a spray of bullets flew right past where Sheng Yun's scalp had just been.","Sheng Yun lay flat on the ground, his face deathly pale.","He had thought clearing out the enemies in the conference room was enough. To think there was actually a second wave of attacks...","Sheng Qingyan snatched the squad communicator from Sheng Yun's waist and ordered coldly, \"Team A, lock down entrance 3. Team B, establish crossfire. Lieutenant Sheng, you will personally lead Team C to cover Chief Engineer Cui's evacuation!\"","His commands were concise and powerful, forming a stark contrast to Sheng Yun's earlier panic.","Sheng Yun nodded repeatedly.","Rong Yu helped Cui Xiao up and handed him over to Sheng Yun. At the same time, she reached out and took the gun from Sheng Yun's hand.","\"You!\"","Sheng Yun was about to lash out, but he was frozen by Rong Yu's icy glare.","She cocked the gun with a sharp click. \"Protect Chief Engineer Cui.\"","She had noticed just now that Sheng Yun's shooting accuracy was worse than hers.","Back then, when she was only fourteen, she had killed enemy invaders with her own hands.","Now, doing it all over again, she had nothing to fear.","Sheng Qingyan had already moved behind cover, forming a crossfire angle with Rong Yu.","For some reason, deep down he trusted her unconditionally, as if at some point they had experienced life and death together... He held up three fingers toward Rong Yu. The moment the countdown ended, they both opened fire simultaneously.","Rong Yu's precise burst fire suppressed the enemies on the left, while Sheng Qingyan did a combat roll to approach the right, taking out two killers with three bullets.","Suddenly!","Sheng Qingyan's gaze hardened. He lunged at Rong Yu, executing a side roll to hide behind an electrical box. Almost at the same time, another bullet pierced through the exact spot where Rong Yu had just been standing, leaving a bowl-sized bullet hole in the wall.","The man's voice was low. \"There's a sniper.\"","Cold sweat seeped from Rong Yu's forehead.","She was only slightly better than Sheng Yun, but on a life-and-death battlefield, her meager abilities were simply not enough. One careless move and she would die right here.","She looked in the direction the man was pointing.","She saw a tiny flash of reflection from a dark spot on the distant glass curtain wall, something an ordinary person like her would never have noticed.","As she was panting heavily, she saw Sheng Qingyan uncharacteristically step three paces to the right.","His entire body was completely exposed in the open area!","\"Watch out!\"","She cried out in alarm.","Time seemed to freeze.","Rong Yu saw Sheng Qingyan's movements break down into a series of flawless tactical postures.","While moving, his body suddenly twisted and turned. This ergonomically impossible movement caused him to lean back as if he were broken in half. Almost simultaneously, a sniper bullet grazed his throat and shot into the wall. The flying debris from the wall carved a thin line of blood across the side of his neck.","As he leaned back until he was almost parallel to the ground, his gun-wielding hand remained as steady as a rock. There was no aiming, no hesitation, and not even a complete line of sight. It was purely a perfect combination of muscle memory and battlefield intuition.","Bang, bang!","Two consecutive gunshots rang out, making eardrums ache in the enclosed space. A mist of blood exploded in the distant ventilation duct, and two heavy bodies tumbled limply from the gap in the duct, one after the other, landing with dull thuds.","Only then did Sheng Qingyan allow himself to fall to the ground, tucking into a roll the moment he made contact to absorb the impact.","He neatly holstered his gun, a wisp of blue smoke still floating from the muzzle. His expression was terrifyingly calm. \"Two snipers, neutralized.\""]},{"number":278,"title":"Chapter 278: If I could get your contact info, I'd be over the moon.","paragraphs":["The battlefield was still being cleared.","Sheng Yun led Cui Xiao outside to retreat.","\"Boss, I'm late!\" A tall man rushed over quickly. \"Boss, leave Chief Engineer Cui's safety to me from here on out.\"","Cui Xiao hurriedly said, \"I lost my glasses. Take me to the dormitory building to get my spare pair first.\"","The tall man took the order, \"Yes, sir!\"","He reached out, preparing to take Cui Xiao from him.","\"Wait!\"","Sheng Yun's temples suddenly throbbed violently.","Remembering something, he stared at the tall man in front of him and said coldly, \"Yan Zhuo, Sheng Qingyan and a few of the brothers are still inside. Go in and support them first.\"","Yan Zhuo paused.","He looked up at the office building ahead, then glanced to both sides. Suddenly, his right hand pressed against his waist.","This series of movements was incredibly fast.","Before his gun could be drawn, Sheng Yun shoved Cui Xiao away and lunged at Yan Zhuo to grab the weapon. \"You son of a bitch! Conspiring with the Sakura Country to murder a national treasure of Huaxia? I'll kill you...\"","As soon as the words left his mouth, he took a bullet to the calf, the pain sending him rolling to the ground.","\"Trash.\"","Yan Zhuo shot him a cold look but didn't fire a finishing shot.","The organization's target was Cui Xiao.","However, just as he pulled the trigger, a strong gust of wind struck. Before his gun could go off, a bullet pierced right through his arm, forcing him to stumble back several steps.","The very next second, the muzzle of Sheng Qingyan's gun was pressed against his temple.","\"Yan, you came just in time. I was almost a goner...\" Sheng Yun began to wail. \"I got shot in the thigh! It hurts, I'm dying of pain!\"","Rong Yu was speechless.","This guy was truly too useless. No wonder he had been in the military for over a decade and was still only a lieutenant.","She walked over and helped Cui Xiao up.","Sheng Qingyan stepped on Yan Zhuo's face and reported, \"Lieutenant Sheng, all enemy forces have been captured, and the two snipers have been killed. As for the mole, we'll need to interrogate him thoroughly.\"","\"Sheng Yun!\"","A woman rushed in frantically.","Seeing Sheng Yun's calf bleeding, she was so frightened she burst into tears.","\"Alright, it's no big deal.\" Sheng Yun, who had just been wailing, suddenly toughened up. \"An Nuo, help me to the infirmary to get this wound treated.\"","Rong Yu recognized her; this was the female journalist they had met last night, Sheng Yun's girlfriend.","An Nuo supported Sheng Yun as they walked toward the infirmary, saying through her tears, \"Didn't I tell you not to participate in this operation? Why didn't you listen?\"","Sheng Yun looked at her. \"How did you know there was something wrong with Yan Zhuo?\"","Yan Zhuo had been in the army for five or six years. He was his right-hand man, a subordinate, a good comrade, and a good brother.","If An Nuo hadn't warned him in advance to be wary of Yan Zhuo, he definitely would have handed Chief Engineer Cui over to him... In that case, the consequences would have been unimaginable.","\"Because he's your brother, yet he looked at me with a very uncomfortable gaze. It's the kind of look only a woman can detect,\" An Nuo said. \"So it's perfectly reasonable for me to suspect him, right?\"","Sheng Yun said softly, \"Thank you for the warning.\"","An Nuo wiped her tears. \"Let's hurry up and treat your wound so it doesn't leave any lingering issues.\"","The biggest loss from the attack on Base Four was the bombing of the core office area, which resulted in seven minor injuries, zero severe injuries, and zero deaths. They killed eighteen enemy combatants and captured eight, including two Sakura Country intelligence receivers, and eliminated two snipers.","At the same time, pulling up the radish brought out the mud—an entire chain of operatives was rooted out...","To the military command, this was a massive achievement. A celebration banquet was held that very night, and the base personnel along with the troops threw a bonfire party together.","The night sky was dyed red by the roaring bonfire, with sparks crackling and flying into the air.","Rong Yu sat by the bonfire, surrounded by the foursome.","Si Lin and the others had spent the whole day planting trees in the nursery area. They only found out about the surprise attack on the base when they returned in the evening, and it scared them half to death.","In all their years of living, it was their first time experiencing such a thing.","The group couldn't resist going over to join in the fun.","Sheng Qingyan was currently surrounded by a group of military officers. Field officers with gleaming epaulets patted his shoulders, their laughter shaking the sky.","\"Kid Sheng, did you practice your marksmanship in the womb?\" A heavily stubbled officer grinned widely, holding half a bottle of white liquor in his hand. \"Those two snipers were S-rank on the international black list. The number of big shots who died at their hands is in the double digits at least. But what happened? You took them out with one shot each, like you were just doing target practice!\"","Sheng Qingyan's expression remained calm, not showing the slightest bit of arrogance from the flattery. He took a sip of liquor, the firelight reflecting on the side of his face and tracing his sharp, handsome features.","\"Isn't that the truth?\" a private nearby chimed in. \"I heard those two snipers had a 100 percent success rate and never missed. Today, they both met their end right here at our Base Four!\"","\"You guys didn't see it!\" another private who had been at the scene said excitedly. \"Brother Sheng didn't even aim that shot, it was pure instinct! The moment that sniper poked his head out, he just raised his hand and fired—an instant headshot! So satisfying!\"","\"Really?\" Someone was skeptical. \"The snipers were at least two or three hundred meters away. Can a new recruit shoot that accurately?\"","\"Qingyan!\" someone cheered. \"Show us what you've got! Let everyone broaden their horizons!\"","Sheng Qingyan wasn't one to show off.","He instinctively wanted to refuse, but when he looked up, his eyes met Rong Yu's sparkling gaze from not too far away.","He suddenly changed his mind and asked, \"How should I show you?\"","\"Over there!\" Someone pointed at the searchlight on the base's distant tower. \"I'll go hang an empty liquor bottle over there. Can you hit it?\"","Everyone looked up. The bottle swayed slightly in the night breeze, at least a hundred meters away. The lighting was dim, making it so they could barely see its blurry outline.","Rong Yu narrowed her eyes. This difficulty level was actually quite high.","Sheng Qingyan, however, merely chuckled softly. He drew his sidearm from his waist and didn't even stand up. Just sitting there, he raised his hand.","Bang!","In the distance, the crisp sound of shattering glass rang out as the liquor bottle exploded, sending shards flying everywhere.","The entire venue fell silent for a second before erupting into deafening cheers.","Si Lin widened his eyes. \"Holy crap! He actually hit it?\"","Zhou Shiyu had stars in her eyes. \"So handsome, this man is too handsome. If I could get his contact info, I would die of happiness.\"","Tang Mi nodded. \"If I get the chance, I'll add him too.\"","Hai Chang'an was dissatisfied. \"Hey, you already have a fiancé.\"","Tang Mi rolled her eyes. \"It's just an arranged family marriage. You didn't actually take it seriously, did you?\"","Hai Chang'an was speechless.","Sheng Qingyan holstered his gun, his expression as calm as usual, as if he had merely swatted a mosquito.","But his gaze lightly swept over in Rong Yu's direction.","Rong Yu couldn't help but purse her lips into a smile.","This guy was even better at showing off than in his past life.","She smiled at him, then stood up and walked toward the distant sand dunes.","Sheng Qingyan's eyes darkened slightly.","He had just stood up.","When he was held down by a few young guys. \"Hey, don't leave! Show us another trick, teach us a bit.\"","Sheng Qingyan said indifferently, \"It's an innate talent. You guys can't learn it.\"","He walked briskly in the direction Rong Yu had gone."]},{"number":279,"title":"Chapter 279: Encounter Sheng Qingyan, Give a Kiss","paragraphs":["The night breeze was slightly cool. A sky full of stars poured down, laying a layer of silver light over the grains of sand.","Rong Yu sat on the sand dune, looking up at the moon.","Resting her chin on her hand, she said to the man beside her, \"Sit down and chat for a while?\"","Sheng Qingyan sat down, his posture perfectly straight.","He clearly remembered that before he had regained his senses, he had an abnormal dependence on her. He defined this behavior as turning to anyone in a moment of desperation.","He thought that after becoming a normal person again, he wouldn't do baffling things anymore.","But now...","There was a lively bonfire in the distance, yet he was here admiring the moon with her.","His heart was inexplicably pounding.","It seemed as if it was meant to be this way.","Why?","\"Sheng Qingyan,\" Rong Yu spoke softly, \"do you find tonight's moonlight familiar?\"","Hearing this, he looked up at the moon.","A bright moon hung in the indigo night sky, with countless stars twinkling. This was a moonlight commonly seen in the desert. For some reason, a feeling of deja vu suddenly flashed in his mind.","It was as if, one year, on the ocean, aboard a cruise ship, he had also admired a moon like this.","A sudden stab of pain hit his temples.","\"I shouldn't have brought that up. Don't think about it anymore.\"","Suddenly, Rong Yu held his hand.","Sheng Qingyan froze.","Her movement of holding his hand was so natural, so natural that he didn't even think it was something that shouldn't happen.","Perhaps.","Was it because when he was ill, he often took the initiative to hold her hand, so she had gotten used to it?","Sheng Qingyan's fingers twitched. After a moment of thought, he didn't pull away. Instead, he couldn't help but hold her back, clasping her hand tightly.","Rong Yu's lips curved into a smile.","The moonlight flowed down like a stream, falling softly and lightly upon her, making her exude an incredibly surreal beauty, as if she had suddenly fallen into a dream...","Behind the sand dune.","Four people poked their heads out.","Tang Mi: \"No way, Rong Yu is actually involved with this soldier.\"","Zhou Shiyu: \"Oh my god, their silhouettes together are too cute! Boohoo, lock them up together forever, I've swallowed the key!\"","Hai Chang'an: \"Didn't you just say you had your eye on this man?\"","Zhou Shiyu: \"I'm not worthy.\"","Si Lin's face looked terrible: \"A greenhorn recruit, how is he worthy of Miss Rong?\"","Tang Mi rolled her eyes at him: \"He might be a greenhorn, but he's a crack shot. Given time, he'll definitely become a major general. How is he not worthy?\"","The few of them spoke louder and louder.","Sheng Qingyan picked up a small stone and, without looking back, tossed it behind him.","\"Damn, who hit me?\" Si Lin roared, clutching his head. Looking up, he met Rong Yu's eyes. He inexplicably shrank back and said dryly, \"We... we came to admire the moon.\"","Hai Chang'an chuckled: \"Right, and to inspect the desert environment while we're at it.\"","Rong Yu said faintly, \"It seems your workload is still too light if you have the energy to stalk me.\"","The four of them: \"...\"","Steeling herself, Tang Mi said fearlessly, \"The moonlight is so beautiful. Shouldn't you two be doing something romantic?\"","Zhou Shiyu shouted loudly, \"Kiss! Kiss! Hurry, kiss!\"","Rong Yu: \"...\"","Sheng Qingyan: \"...\"","Zhou Shiyu smirked and gave Tang Mi and Hai Chang'an a push: \"You two are an engaged couple. Hurry up, give a live demonstration of how to kiss, so Rong Yu and Captain Sheng can learn.\"","Tang Mi: \"...\"","Hai Chang'an: \"...\"","Wait, what did this have to do with them, please?","Do engaged couples have to be forced to perform in public?","In the distance, silhouettes of people were faintly moving; it seemed everyone else was about to be drawn over too. Sheng Qingyan kept a straight, slightly reddened face, his voice cold and deep: \"I have something to do.\"","He turned around and left quickly.","His back was extremely stiff, and his footsteps looked somewhat like he was fleeing in panic.","Before Rong Yu could reprimand them.","Si Lin spoke up: \"Miss Rong, the four of us came up with a new proposal that suits our talents. Do you want to hear it?\"","Hai Chang'an took a crumpled notebook out of his pocket and offered it with both hands.","Rong Yu took it and opened it.","Although the handwriting was a bit ugly, the ideas were not bad.","\"We want to organize a charity event,\" Zhou Shiyu said. \"Using social media for promotion to attract volunteers. This way, we can improve the desert environment and relieve the local manpower shortage.\"","Tang Mi added, \"I know a few friends in environmental organizations. I think they'd be very willing to provide technical guidance.\"","Her tone was uncharacteristically devoid of any spoiled attitude.","Hai Chang'an cleared his throat: \"Promotion won't be a problem. My family... I mean, the Hai Corporation can fully support it.\"","Rong Yu flipped through the proposal page by page, her brows gradually relaxing. The plan was unexpectedly detailed. From volunteer recruitment to safety guarantees, from sapling selection to subsequent maintenance, it covered almost all potential issues.","Finally, she looked up: \"Whose idea was this?\"","Si Lin: \"It was my idea!\"","Zhou Shiyu: \"What do you mean your idea? I clearly brought it up first!\"","Hai Chang'an: \"I wrote this proposal stroke by stroke!\"","Tang Mi: \"Hey, I sorted out the most critical processes, okay!\"","The few of them argued back and forth until they realized Rong Yu had fallen silent.","Si Lin scratched his head: \"Alright, it was actually the result of us discussing it together.\"","Rong Yu handed the notebook back: \"The idea has merit. Take it back and revise your proposal, especially the cost accounting and professional technical support sections. I will give you ten days to implement it.\"","The four of them could hardly believe their ears.","\"What?\" Tang Mi covered her mouth. \"Let us execute it? Are you serious? Do you believe we can get this done?\"","Si Lin's eyes widened: \"Miss Rong, you're not making fun of us, are you?\"","Rong Yu smiled: \"If you can use internet celebrity traffic, business planning, corporate resources, and interpersonal networks to actually accomplish something, it's far more meaningful than being locked up here doing hard labor.\"","She stepped toward the crowd.","The four of them looked at each other and then erupted into deafening cheers.","Since coming to this dump, it was the first time they had been acknowledged by Rong Yu. How could they not be ecstatic?","The four of them stayed up all night and went to find Rong Yu the next day with the new proposal. But Rong Yu was busy, truly too busy. For this proposal, she asked the base's propaganda department to help coordinate with them.","With professionals stepping in, the four people's efficiency increased even more.","On the third day, they drove to the city nearest to the base and began deploying the plan.","Online promotion, live stream hype, guiding registrations, gathering points...","On the fourth day, the first batch of over a hundred registered volunteers safely arrived in the desert. In the distance, a cloud of dust rose on the horizon, it was a convoy of dozens of off-road vehicles.","When the midday sun reached its highest point, the desert had transformed into an orderly and bustling ocean. Under the guidance of professionals, volunteers moved trees, dug holes, planted saplings, and watered them.","In the evening, when the final sapling was planted, everyone erupted into thunderous cheers."]},{"number":280,"title":"Chapter 280: That is why generation after generation must stay here.","paragraphs":["The charity volunteering had been going on for a week.","A large designated area of the desert was now planted with saxaul saplings. Their tender green leaves swayed gently in the wind, displaying an astonishing vitality.","An irreplaceable sense of accomplishment swelled in the hearts of the four of them.","Just then, a strange buzzing sound came from the distance, like millions of bees flapping their wings at the same time. Si Lin looked up and saw the western skyline suddenly darken.","\"What is that?\" Zhou Shiyu squinted her eyes.","Tang Mi followed her gaze, her face suddenly changing. \"My God, it looks like a sandstorm! But the weather forecast didn't say there would be one today...\"","Her words were scattered by a sudden gust of fierce wind.","In almost an instant.","The mild sunset in the distance was swallowed by a rolling wall of sand. The sky turned a muddy brownish-yellow, and the sky full of yellow sand rushed toward them like a tsunami.","\"Everyone evacuate immediately!\" Hai Chang'an was the quickest to react. He grabbed a megaphone and shouted, \"Volunteers, get in the vehicles according to your assigned groups! Do not panic!\"","Everyone was terrified, and the scene instantly descended into chaos.","Volunteers dropped their tools and ran toward the vehicles. The fierce wind blew over the registration tent, sending papers flying wildly in the air. Tang Mi and Zhou Shiyu ran across the sand, using their walkie-talkies to call the group leaders to do a headcount.","\"Group three is missing two people!\" Hai Chang'an roared in the wind, sand filling his mouth.","Si Lin climbed onto the roof of an off-road vehicle against the wind and sand, shouting loudly, \"Women and the elderly get in the cars with the staff first!\"","Soon, the off-road vehicles fully loaded with volunteers drove away from the camp.","The vanguard of the sandstorm had arrived. Fine grains of sand hit the vehicles like bullets, making a terrifying crackling sound.","\"We need to leave too!\" Si Lin pulled open the car door, but Hai Chang'an grabbed him.","Hai Chang'an pointed to the other side. \"Look...\"","Following his finger, the four saw a team of staff members in base uniforms walking against the flow of the crowd. Holding windbreak cloths and securing ropes, they struggled in the sandstorm with less than five meters of visibility to build protective barriers for the newly planted saplings.","Lao Ma led a group of sand control workers, their backs hunched, almost being pushed along by the wind, yet they still clung tightly to the securing stakes.","\"Are they crazy?\" Zhou Shiyu exclaimed. \"People could die!\"","Si Lin's hand froze on the car door handle.","Through the sky full of yellow sand, he saw Rong Yu's figure. She had appeared here at some unknown time, and along with the sand control workers, she was using her body to press down the windbreak cloth that the wind was trying to lift.","\"I have the volunteer roster,\" Tang Mi suddenly said. \"Everyone has been confirmed to be safely evacuated, so?\"","\"It's time to make sure these saplings are safe.\" Zhou Shiyu looked up. \"I'm staying. What about you?\"","Hai Chang'an rolled his shoulders. \"I'm strong. I can drive in the securing stakes.\"","Si Lin said nothing. He simply tore off his inner lining, ripped it into four strips, and handed them to everyone to cover their mouths and noses.","When the four rushed toward the sapling area against the wind and sand.","Rong Yu was kneeling on the ground securing a rope. She looked up and saw four blurry figures coming through the curtain of sand, thinking they were volunteers scattered by the wind.","She quickly spoke, \"Leave here immediately! It's dangerous!\"","Si Lin was the first to rush over, taking the rope from her hands that was dancing wildly in the wind. \"Miss Rong, we are also staff members of the base!\"","Tang Mi snorted, \"Who says temporary workers aren't staff members?\"","Hai Chang'an wiped the sand off his face. \"The base's sand control workers are experienced. Since they can stay, it means the sandstorm is within a controllable range.\"","Zhou Shiyu and Tang Mi started tying windbreak cloths to the outermost saplings. Their previously exquisite curly hair was casually tied into ponytails, their beautiful manicures were long gone, and their hands tied professional knots extremely nimbly.","Si Lin and Hai Chang'an did the heavy lifting, protecting the seedlings together with Lao Ma.","Rong Yu couldn't help but smile.","These kids had grown up faster than she had imagined.","However!","At this moment, Lao Ma's voice rang out: \"The sand dunes are moving! Hurry! Everyone, fall back! If we don't leave now, we'll all be buried here!\"","Rong Yu looked up, her heart almost skipping a beat. In the distance, a three-story-high wave of sand was pressing down on them at a visible speed. That was no ordinary wind and sand; it was the desert breathing, devouring.","She stood up decisively. \"Don't just stand there, go!\"","Tang Mi was still holding tightly to the securing rope of a small sapling.","Hai Chang'an wanted to help her, but was knocked to the ground by a fierce gust of wind.","Zhou Shiyu was crying and shouting something incomprehensible.","Si Lin was still charging into the sand.","Lao Ma kicked him and pulled Si Lin up like grabbing a kitten. \"Stop being so stubborn, get in the car, hurry up!\"","Rong Yu said coldly, \"Only if you stay alive can you plant more trees!\"","As the four stumbled toward the windproof warehouse, the wave of sand behind them had already swallowed the edge of the sapling area.","Rong Yu was the last to enter. In the moment she looked back, she saw the large patch of saxaul saplings they had just planted being uprooted like matchsticks, disappearing into the dim, yellow curtain of sand.","The moment the warehouse door closed.","Tang Mi cried.","Zhou Shiyu broke down and sobbed loudly.","The wind and sand struck outside, sand crackling against the exterior walls of the warehouse, drowning out the crying inside.","Rong Yu went in and rummaged for a medical kit, bringing it out. \"Tang Mi, give me your hand.\"","Tang Mi finally noticed that the back of her hand had been slashed by something unknown. It was a very deep cut, bleeding profusely, yet she hadn't felt any pain.","She stammered a little, \"Rong Yu... no, Miss Rong, I'm not crying because of this...\"","\"I know.\" Rong Yu poured alcohol to clean her wound. \"It's going to hurt a little, bear with it.\"","After treating Tang Mi, she went on to clean the wounds of Zhou Shiyu, Hai Chang'an, and Si Lin, one by one.","Holding Rong Yu's hand, Si Lin didn't feel any romantic tension at all. He opened his mouth blankly, \"Is... is it all gone?\"","Sitting to the side, Lao Ma blew a smoke ring. \"The sandstorm moved from that end to this end. Yeah, it's all gone.\"","Hai Chang'an punched the wall. \"Then what was the point of all our hard work these past few days?\"","\"The point is,\" Rong Yu closed the medical kit, \"tomorrow, after the sandstorm passes, we can start over.\"","Tang Mi's tears welled up again. \"We gathered so many people and spent so many days just to plant those saplings, and now we have to start all over again?\"","\"My first year here, I planted three thousand saplings. One sandstorm, and overnight, less than ten were left.\" Lao Ma's voice rang out.","Zhou Shiyu looked up. \"And then?\"","\"I was only sixteen at the time. Of course, just like you guys, I cried.\" Lao Ma shrugged. \"After crying, I kept planting trees. Just like that, I persisted for over thirty years... Over these years, countless saplings have died, and there are also people who were buried in the sand. My master gave his life to the desert...\"","Lao Ma's nose was a little stuffed; he couldn't go on speaking and lit another cigarette.","Rong Yu took over the conversation. \"The desert is just like this. You just plant it, and it might take it away. That's why it takes generation after generation of people, advancing wave upon wave, to guard this place.\"","She looked at the four kids. \"You all did very well today.\"","At such a simple sentence, Si Lin suddenly felt his eyes grow hot with tears.","Hai Chang'an hastily tilted his head back to stare at the ceiling, pretending that something up there had caught his attention.","\"Tomorrow...\" Tang Mi began, her voice still thick from crying. \"Will we still be able to get new saplings tomorrow?\"","Rong Yu met the gaze of four pairs of eyes looking back at her. They were red and swollen, brimming with tears, yet filled with a resolute and burning eagerness.","A smile graced her lips as she replied, \"Of course.\""]},{"number":281,"title":"Chapter 281: Sheng Qingyan's Application to Become Rong Yu's Boyfriend","paragraphs":["Over the remaining half month or so, the four of them completely blended into life at the base.","Rong Yu's work here was also gradually drawing to a close.","\"Engineer Rong, this is the final task.\" Cui Xiao took out a file. \"I'll have to trouble Engineer Rong to make a trip and deliver this to the military department.\"","Rong Yu smiled. \"Chief Engineer Cui, what is the meaning of this?\"","Usually, there were dedicated personnel for delivering documents; she wouldn't normally be asked to do it.","Cui Xiao coughed lightly and said, \"There is an awards ceremony at the military department today. That new recruit, Sheng Qingyan, is being awarded a First-Class Merit for taking down two top-tier snipers. You can go and join in the excitement.\"","A hint of awkwardness appeared on Rong Yu's usually calm face.","Lately, she and Sheng Qingyan had been occasionally taking walks together in the evenings. It wasn't frequent, only once every two or three days, and they would part ways after chatting for half an hour.","She thought they had been very discreet.","How did even someone like Cui Xiao, who usually paid no attention to gossip, know about it?","If she had known, she wouldn't have been so cautious.","Cui Xiao smiled and said, \"It's not easy for researchers and soldiers to date. You two don't get many opportunities to see each other every day, so hurry up and go.\"","Rong Yu cleared her throat. \"We aren't dating, at least not yet.\"","She took the file and drove an off-road vehicle to the military district.","The military district was heavily guarded. After passing through layers of security checks, she arrived at the grand auditorium. A large crowd was gathered there, clapping enthusiastically in a very lively atmosphere.","Rong Yu stepped inside.","Just in time, she saw Sheng Qingyan standing on the stage in a crisp, tailored military uniform.","A colonel was pinning a gleaming gold First-Class Merit medal onto his chest.","\"...During the defense of Base Four, Comrade Sheng Qingyan used extraordinary tactical prowess and astonishing marksmanship to eliminate foreign reactionary forces...\"","Sheng Qingyan stood there with an indifferent expression.","Despite receiving such a great honor, he didn't even crack a smile.","Suddenly, his gaze swept over the audience, cutting through the crowd, and landed straight on Rong Yu, who was standing at the entrance of the auditorium.","He was the center of attention at that moment.","Because he looked in her direction, everyone else's eyes uniformly followed his gaze.","\"Brother Sheng, your family is here!\"","\"Not family, it's his girlfriend!\"","\"Look, Brother Sheng is blushing, hahahaha...\"","Someone boldly took the lead in teasing him, and soon, a wave of whistling echoed throughout the auditorium.","Sheng Yun, whose injuries had not yet healed, picked up his cane and started tapping people on the head one by one. \"Shut up, all of you shut up! Will it kill you to tease him a little less?!\"","His eldest nephew had just recovered from a serious illness and had a reserved personality. If this teasing made him back down, his future niece-in-law would be gone for good.","Sheng Qingyan's ears turned from a light pink to tomato red at a visible speed, but he still maintained his aloof demeanor as he strode over to Rong Yu in quick, long steps.","The teasing grew louder.","Sheng Qingyan said, \"They are just like that, they like to joke around. Don't take it to heart.\"","\"I won't,\" Rong Yu said with a smile. \"Congratulations on being awarded the First-Class Merit.\"","Sheng Qingyan's face turned even redder.","Rong Yu shook her head.","How was this guy even more easily embarrassed than she was?","She turned and walked out, and Sheng Qingyan quickly followed, leaving the waves of teasing cheers behind them.","The two walked to a secluded spot where no one else was around.","Rong Yu looked up at him. \"They all say I'm your girlfriend, and even the people back at the base think so. Tell me, how am I supposed to find a boyfriend in the future?\"","Sheng Qingyan's face was tense. \"I will explain it clearly to them one by one, don't worry.\"","\"Explain?\" Rong Yu held back her laughter and said in a serious tone, \"How do you plan to explain? Are you going to say that admiring the moon together on the sand dunes was purely a work exchange? Say that our daily walks are arranged by the organization? And say that you blushing every time you see me is just an accident?\"","Sheng Qingyan's Adam's apple bobbed heavily.","He knew his face was burning hot.","Was it really that red too?","Was it obvious?","Rong Yu took a step forward and suddenly adjusted his medal for him. She curled her lips into a smile. \"You asked Tang Mi about my work schedule, which is why it was always such a coincidence that we would run into each other downstairs for a walk every day, right?\"","Sheng Qingyan turned his head away.","He hadn't asked Tang Mi; it was Tang Mi and Zhou Shiyu who had blabbered and volunteered the information to him. He just had a good memory and remembered it, that was all.","He didn't dare look into Rong Yu's eyes.","But Rong Yu forcefully turned his face back to face her.","He met her sparkling gaze. In those eyes, his own face was reflected so clearly.","Within his chest, the towering tree that had grown because of her swayed violently. Every leaf rustled, just like his heart, pounding wildly.","Uncontrollable emotions poured out.","He slowly exhaled and said softly, \"Rong Yu, I am twenty-four years old this year, and I have just joined the military. I think I need to have the strength and confidence to protect you before I am qualified to stand by your side.\"","He had lived his twenty-four years in a daze.","Having just recovered from a serious illness, just stepped into the military, and with his career only just beginning, what did he have to promise her a future?","As if making a major decision, he suddenly took a half-step back.","Under Rong Yu's astonished gaze.","He stood at attention and saluted.","\"Report!\" His voice was loud and clear. \"Private Sheng Qingyan requests permission in advance to become Comrade Rong Yu's boyfriend after she graduates from university, which is in four years. Please instruct!\"","Rong Yu couldn't help but laugh. \"Four years? I don't need four years to finish university.\"","Sheng Qingyan heard the deafening sound of his own heartbeat in his chest.","Unable to control his surging emotions, he placed his hands on Rong Yu's shoulders, his gaze firm. \"One year. Give me one year.\"","\"Hey, what are you doing? Let go immediately!\"","Suddenly, a familiar explosive shout pierced their eardrums.","Rong Yu was startled.","She turned her head to look.","In the distance, five elderly men were rushing toward them.","The one leading the charge was her good son Ji Shunying, followed by Hai Dadun, Sima Gang, Tang Youyi, and Old Master Zhou.","The five of them looked travel-worn and exhausted, yet their eyes gleamed with the light of gossip. They surrounded the couple with lightning speed, looking eager to watch the drama unfold.","Only Old Master Ji had his eyes wide open in anger. \"You brat from the Sheng family, how dare you take advantage of a young girl! Where is a cane? Tang Youyi, lend me your cane for a second!\"","Ignoring how colorful Tang Youyi's expression was, he snatched the cane and swung it at Sheng Qingyan.","Elder Hai and Elder Sima hastily stepped aside to watch the drama from a distance.","However, when Sheng Qingyan shot him a faint, sweeping glance, the raised cane froze in mid-air. For some unknown reason, he simply couldn't bring himself to strike.","\"The young folks are just dating, why is an old man like you joining in on the fuss...\" Tang Youyi spoke up. \"Forget it, forget it. It's not easy for anyone.\""]},{"number":282,"title":"Chapter 282: Special Recognition for the Outstanding Performance of Four Young People","paragraphs":["Rong Yu told Sheng Qingyan to go ahead with his work.","Having just received a first-class merit award, Sheng Qingyan indeed had some follow-up arrangements to attend to. He greeted the elderly gentlemen before taking his leave.","\"What brings you all here?\" Rong Yu asked. \"The journey must have been exhausting. Are you tired?\"","Tang Youyi replied, \"The base is holding an awards ceremony and specifically invited us donors to present the awards, so we decided to come together.\"","Old Master Hai rubbed his hands together. \"Miss Rong, that boy of mine hasn't made you angry, has he?\"","Old Master Si asked nervously, \"Has Si Lin done anything morally reprehensible?\"","Old Master Zhou sighed. \"My Shiyu is the most spoiled of them all. I don't expect her to have made much progress; as long as she hasn't caused any trouble, I'll be satisfied.\"","Rong Yu smiled. \"The four kids don't know you've arrived yet. Let's keep it a secret for now. Come, I'll take you to the rest area to freshen up first. The awards ceremony starts tomorrow morning.\"","The base was bustling with preparations for the awards ceremony.","Si Lin and the others had been in this desert for a whole month. On their final day, they thought they would be planting more trees, but instead, Lao Ma led them into the main auditorium.","It was their first time attending such an awards ceremony.","\"Why do we have to attend this kind of ceremony?\" Zhou Shiyu muttered softly. \"It's not like we're qualified to win anything.\"","Tang Mi nudged her with an elbow. \"Rong Yu said it's a show of respect to all the staff at the base.\"","Si Lin's gaze swept over Rong Yu, who was seated in the front row.","She was still wearing her work uniform, her ponytail resting against her perfectly straight back. Just that posture alone was something he would have to practice for years to achieve.","Various leaders took turns going on stage to give speeches.","Soon, the host's voice rang out: \"Our Base Four started in the desert, was born in the desert, and grew in the desert... Today, we are not only paying tribute to scientific research achievements, but also to the unwavering perseverance of our grassroots personnel in moving these sands... Next, I will present the awards for outstanding employees.\"","\"The Outstanding Contribution Award...\"","\"The Best Innovation Award...\"","One award after another was announced, and the base's researchers took turns going on stage.","When Rong Yu went up to receive her award, the quartet nearly went crazy. They clapped so hard their hands turned red, excitedly shouting her name.","The elderly men sitting in the back row were brimming with suspicion.","Old Master Hai: \"Didn't they say we were invited to present the awards? Why didn't they let us go up and present the award to Miss Rong?\"","Old Master Si: \"Didn't you see that the person presenting the award to Miss Rong was the chief engineer of the base? You're not qualified enough.\"","Old Master Zhou: \"Perhaps we're supposed to present awards to our own brats?\"","Mr. Ji: \"What kind of daydream are you having? It's a miracle those little rascals of yours weren't kicked out of the base, and you actually think they could win an award?\"","Tang Youyi: \"Indeed.\"","\"Lastly, we will be presenting a special award.\" The host's voice suddenly turned mysterious. \"This award is not on the program; it was a last-minute addition by the base.\"","Curious murmurs rippled through the venue.","\"The New Pioneer Award for Desertification Control goes to—\" The host deliberately dragged out his words before slowly announcing, \"Si Lin, Tang Mi, Zhou Shiyu, and Hai Chang'an! Will the four of you please come up to the stage to receive your award!\"","Enthusiastic applause erupted across the entire hall.","Meanwhile, the quartet stood frozen at their seats as if struck by lightning.","Hai Chang'an's mouth hung wide open. \"What did I just hear? The New Pioneer Award for Desertification Control goes to the four of us?\"","Si Lin swallowed hard. \"Could it be people with the exact same names?\"","Tang Mi struggled to part her lips. \"One identical name is plausible, but four identical names is a bit ridiculous.\"","Zhou Shiyu abruptly stood up. \"Look at the big screen! It's us!\"","On the large screen in the auditorium, footage of the four of them at the base was playing.","Si Lin demonstrating how to dig holes for volunteers under the scorching sun, the skin on his back peeling from sunburn.","Tang Mi kneeling in the nursery taking notes, completely oblivious to the sand and dirt.","Hai Chang'an walking across a sand dune with two bags of fertilizer slung over his shoulder.","Zhou Shiyu explaining desertification control knowledge to volunteers.","Rong Yu turned around and called out loudly with a smile, \"What are you four still standing there for? Hurry up and get your award.\"","The four stood up like sleepwalkers, supporting each other as they made their way toward the stage.","Standing before the microphone, the blinding lights prevented them from seeing the audience below. Their ears were ringing, and the host's congratulatory words sounded muffled, as if coming through a layer of water.","\"...specially commending these four young people for their outstanding performance, as well as their heroic actions in the face of the sandstorm...\"","\"Now, please welcome our award presenters!\"","The spotlight hit the floor below the stage, and four vigorous elderly men slowly walked out with steady steps.","The moment they clearly saw the faces of the approaching men, Tang Mi and Zhou Shiyu gasped and covered their mouths, while Hai Chang'an nearly dropped to his knees.","\"Grand... Grandpa?\" Si Lin's voice caught in his throat. \"Why are you here?\"","The four elderly gentlemen were dressed in elegant Mao suits, their silvery sideburns combed meticulously. None of them could hide the proud smiles tugging at the corners of their mouths.","\"What, don't recognize me?\" Old Master Hai shoved the certificate into his grandson's hands. \"You little brat, you did well.\"","Old Master Si gave a thumbs up. \"I knew you were a teachable kid. You've really done me proud.\"","Old Master Zhou beamed with shared honor. \"My Shiyu can control the desert now too. She didn't bring any shame to the Zhou family.\"","Tang Youyi patted Tang Mi's shoulder. \"Sending you here was indeed the right choice. In this generation of the Tang family, only Tang Jin was presentable before. From now on, we have you too. Good job.\"","The eyes of all four youths turned red.","It turned out that they, too, could become the pride of their elders.","The host handed over the microphone. \"Will a representative of the award winners please say a few words?\"","The four nudged each other for a long time until Si Lin was finally pushed to the front. He looked out at the dense crowd below the stage, then glanced at his three equally bewildered companions beside him, and suddenly smiled.","\"A month ago, we were problem teenagers exiled to this base by our families,\" his voice echoed through the hall. \"Today, standing here, we still don't know what we did to deserve this award...\"","Rong Yu couldn't help but smile.","\"But I do know that without Researcher Rong Yu's strict demands, without the guidance of seniors like Lao Ma, and without the example set by all the staff who held their ground during that sandstorm...\" He paused and looked at the four elders. \"...and without our families' unwavering love that never gave up on us, we couldn't possibly be standing here.\"","Tang Mi suddenly grabbed the microphone. \"I want to add something! Those saplings were actually all replanted the very next day, and they achieved a survival rate of at least fifty percent.\"","Her voice trembled with excitement and nerves, completely stripped of her usual arrogance.","Hai Chang'an, his face flushed red, managed to squeeze out a sentence: \"I will keep working hard!\"","Then he quickly shoved the microphone over to Zhou Shiyu.","Zhou Shiyu blinked her large eyes and bowed deeply to the audience. \"Thank you to everyone here. Even after we leave this base, we will come back to visit often, because you all taught us what it means to put down roots.\"","Thunderous applause echoed endlessly."]},{"number":283,"title":"Chapter 283: When should we tell Yingbao about this","paragraphs":["The award ceremony ended.","The lives of the four people here had come to a close.","This place they once wanted to escape so desperately now evoked a strong sense of reluctance to leave, filling them with an inexplicable melancholy.","Just as they were about to get in the car to leave, Old Master Ji spoke up with a sour tone, \"Mom, aren't you going to say goodbye to that kid from the Sheng family? After all, one is a soldier and the other is a researcher. It won't be too easy to see each other again, huh.\"","Rong Yu poked his head. \"Yingbao, why do I feel like you're gloating?\"","Old Master Ji gave a proud, cold snort.","Rong Yu shook her head with a laugh.","It was a pity that Sheng Qingyan didn't have the memories of his past life, otherwise he would definitely let this old boy experience a complete childhood.","She was wondering, when should she tell Yingbao about this?","Given Yingbao's personality, he would probably blow his top.","Wait, just wait a bit.","The group got into the off-road vehicle, slowly driving away from the desert.","Si Lin and the others were full of reluctance to part.","But for Rong Yu and Wang Xiaoli, it wasn't a big deal. Because Base No. 4 and the Fourth Aerospace Institute belonged to the same system, the two of them would definitely come back here.","The off-road vehicle drove straight to the private jet parking apron.","When they came, the group had suffered a lot. Now, taking a private jet on the way back, they actually felt a bit unaccustomed to it.","At the base, there was mostly no internet, and even if there was, it was a local area network, making it hard to contact the outside world. As soon as they boarded the plane, the four of them connected to the private jet's Wi-Fi at the speed of light. Their first order of business was to take a perfectly angled photo of their certificates and post it to their WeChat Moments.","Old Master Hai stole the picture and followed suit, posting it to his Moments.","Old Master Si and Old Master Zhou were not to be outdone.","Tang Youyi, someone who hadn't posted on his Moments in ten thousand years, also subtly showed off a bit.","\"So many people are liking my post.\"","\"My likes have broken a hundred.\"","\"Old Ji, what about you? Why aren't you liking our posts?\"","Old Master Ji: \"...\"","Show off, show off, what the hell are they showing off.","He had so many outstanding grandsons, and he hadn't shown off a single one, alright?","These old fogeys were too impatient. He was still the most composed one.","\"Only a few people see a Moments post. When I start a live stream, tens of thousands of people tune in.\" Zhou Shiyu opened her live-streaming app. \"Hello babies, long time no see! It's been a month, you all missed me, right? I am Shiyu Feifei.\"","\"Wait, why did Shiyu get so tanned?\"","\"Hahaha, she forgot to turn on the beauty filter and revealed her true colors. So dark, how does she dare call herself a great beauty?\"","\"Too dark, I don't want to be a fan anymore.\"","Zhou Shiyu smiled and said, \"Babies, let me show you this certificate. This month, I was planting trees in the desert to control the sand, and I was awarded the title of Emerging Sand Control Pioneer. The sunburns on my face are all medals of honor. Isn't that awesome?\"","\"Aha, an internet celebrity actually sneaked into a sand control organization?\"","\"Nowadays, internet celebrities will do anything for fame.\"","A bunch of people in the comment section started cursing.","Zhou Shiyu was used to being scolded and didn't care. She continued to share interesting stories from the base: \"Don't be fooled by my delicate skin, I can do great things too, okay? Have you ever seen a sandstorm? No, right? Hey, I experienced one firsthand, but I didn't run away. This lady has plenty of strength to fight against a sandstorm...\"","\"Tsk, the more she talks, the more it sounds real.\"","\"Hilarious, anyone can be a sand control pioneer these days.\"","\"A sandstorm, heh. Why doesn't she say she experienced a giant tsunami? She doesn't even know how to make up a story.\"","\"First, there was the big star Rong Yu faking her scientific research, and now the big influencer Zhou Shiyu is gilding her resume with sand control. This circle is too messy.\"","Zhou Shiyu was originally smiling and showing off her certificate, but seeing these comments, her face immediately dropped. \"Bullshit! Rong Yu's scientific research results are truer than real gold! It was cleared up eight hundred years ago, and you're still bringing it up to babble about it. Did none of you pay your internet bills? It's fine if your family is poor, but coming out here to blindly attack people is just wrong!\"","Tang Mi rolled her eyes at the live stream. \"While Rong Yu is contributing to the aerospace industry, you keyboard warriors are probably still playing in the mud somewhere!\"","Hai Chang'an twitched the corners of his lips. \"You people don't deserve to know how outstanding Rong Yu is, let alone mention her name!\"","Si Lin laughed out of anger. \"Zhou Shiyu, why did you start this crappy live stream? It's one thing for you to get scolded, but you even dragged Miss Rong down with you...\"","Zhou Shiyu quickly turned off the live stream.","Looking like she had made a mistake, she stammered, \"Miss Rong, I didn't know this would happen. I'm sorry.\"","Tang Mi pursed her lips and said, \"Miss Rong, I also want to apologize for my previous rude behavior towards you.\"","Before going to the base, her opinion of Rong Yu was similar to that of the netizens.","At that time, she simply refused to believe that someone could be this outstanding at the age of eighteen.","One month's time completely changed the prejudice in her heart.","She was truly convinced by Rong Yu.","Si Lin coughed and said, \"Miss Rong, about before, well, I was young and ignorant. Please just forget about it.\"","Hai Chang'an rolled his eyes at him. \"You should have realized this sooner.\"","The plane flew through the clouds and soon arrived in Haicheng.","After getting off the plane, everyone went their separate ways home. Rong Yu and Wang Xiaoli had to carry a large bag of documents and go to the Fourth Aerospace Institute first to report on their work over the past month.","Just as they reached the entrance, they ran into Song Huai.","\"Rong Yu!\"","Seeing her, Song Huai's eyes lit up, and he quickly called out.","Wang Xiaoli knew they were classmates and said, \"I'll go in first. Take your time, it's fine.\"","Song Huai looked surprised and said, \"Where did you go on a business trip this past month? How did you get so tanned?\"","Rong Yu looked unwilling to talk much about it. \"Is there something you need?\"","\"I...\" Song Huai hesitated for a moment and said, \"After I finish my work today, I won't be coming to the Fourth Institute anymore. My teacher, Academician Liu, recommended me to go to the First Aerospace Institute.\"","Rong Yu nodded. \"Congratulations.\"","\"If... if you want to go, I can ask my teacher to write a recommendation letter,\" Song Huai said with difficulty. As if knowing she would refuse, he immediately added, \"You can think about it for a few months. I'll wait for your news.\"","After saying that, he quickly walked away.","Rong Yu's work report went very smoothly.","Just as she left the Fourth Aerospace Institute, she received a message on her phone. It was from Sheng Qingyan.","\"Next, I'm going on a mission. I will be temporarily out of contact for this week. See you when it's over.\"","Rong Yu smiled and replied, \"Okay.\"","Romance had never been the sole focus of her life. As long as she knew that person was out there somewhere, it was enough.","Returning to the Ji family home, her group of good grandsons were all there.","Ji Zhiyuan was managing the Ji Group in perfect order.","Ji Yanting's new movie was released to unprecedented popularity, and his stage name, Yan Ting, continuously dominated the trending charts.","Ji Mohan finally shed the title of junior researcher and was promoted to intermediate.","Ji Jingchuan placed first in the school, district, and city in every monthly joint examination.","Ji Zhouye's grades had improved rapidly, with his total score reaching a peak of five hundred and fifty points.","Duoduo successfully advanced in her piano competition, and next, she could go to an even bigger stage."]},{"number":284,"title":"Chapter 284: The First Birthday Spent with Mom","paragraphs":["A sweltering summer.","The annual college entrance examination arrived as scheduled.","Rong Yu had been admitted in advance and did not need to take the exam, but there were still two candidates in the house.","Early in the morning, the Ji family was in a frenzy.","Old Master Ji brought up a pot of dark soup: \"Chuan, Aye, come here, each of you drink a bowl.\"","Rong Yu's eyebrow twitched: \"What is this?\"","\"This is called the Top Scholar Soup,\" Old Master Ji said. \"When Yuan, A-Yan, and Mo took the college entrance exam, I also prepared this. All three of them became top scholars. Hurry up and drink it.\"","Ji Zhouye chuckled: \"With my level, even if I drink the soup, I can't be a top scholar. Fourth Brother, you should drink more.\"","Ji Jingchuan said lightly: \"My strength is right here; I will be the top scholar even without drinking it.\"","\"No, you must drink it.\" Old Master Ji kept a straight face. \"If you don't drink it, I'll pour it down your throats.\"","\"Ji Shunying.\"","Rong Yu's voice sounded, and Old Master Ji instantly behaved, saying aggrievedly: \"Aren't I doing this for their own good?\"","Ji Zhiyuan spoke up: \"This Top Scholar Soup is actually a calming herbal packet. It doesn't do any harm to drink and can relieve exam anxiety.\"","Ji Jingchuan immediately picked up a bowl and gulped it down.","Ji Zhouye, with a bitter face, had no choice but to follow suit.","\"That's good.\" Old Master Ji beamed. \"Hurry up and check your admission tickets, ID cards, and so on. Also, pay attention during the exam, don't be careless...\"","Ji Zhouye covered his ears and quickly ran out.","Ji Jingchuan listened patiently before getting in the car.","The youngest fourth and fifth went to take the exam, leaving Rong Yu with free time, so she sat in the courtyard playing chess with her old son.","A gentle breeze blew, and the grapevines in the courtyard hung down. The green grapes were not yet ripe, and the grown-up pinecone ran around at their feet. The mother and son enjoyed this leisurely and contented time.","After playing three games, Steward Yu came over and said: \"Old Master, Miss Rong, President Rong and Madame Rong are here to visit.\"","Old Master Ji didn't speak, looking at Rong Yu.","Rong Yu put down her chess piece. Since she moved into the Ji family, Rong Wangtian had only visited once, which was considered quite measured. Coming to the door at this time, perhaps there was really something going on. She nodded: \"Let them in.\"","It was Rong Wangtian's second time at the Ji family, and Shen Lin's first.","After the two came in, they couldn't help but lower their posture because this manor was too large, revealing the heritage of a century-old aristocratic family everywhere.","Entering the reception room, after the servants served tea, Rong Yu walked in with her old son.","Rong Wangtian and Shen Lin had just sat down. Seeing the two of them come in, they immediately stood up again and hurriedly said: \"Old Master Ji, please forgive us for visiting abruptly. My wife and I have something we want to give to Xiao Yu.\"","\"Don't be formal, sit.\" Old Master Ji exuded the aura of a superior. \"You guys chat, don't mind me.\"","Shen Lin silently grumbled in her heart.","With such a big chairman sitting here, how could she not mind?","Fortunately, she was a university teacher and had seen many big shots. Although she was a bit apprehensive in her heart, she could still remain as calm as water on the surface.","She took a document bag from her handbag, placed it on the coffee table, and smiled: \"Xiao Yu, because of you, our Rong family was able to reach a cooperation with the Ji Corporation. A small case for the Ji Corporation has allowed the Rong Group to take a big step forward. Your father and I discussed it and took out all the profits from this quarter to buy you an apartment in the capital, right next to Huaqing University, so it will be convenient for you to go to school in the future.\"","Old Master Ji snorted.","Apartments near Huaqing University were not cheap. Even the smallest layout was a huge expense. The Rong family really invested heavily this time.","His snort made Shen Lin freeze a bit.","She didn't know what it meant.","\"No need.\" Rong Yu's tone was relatively gentle. \"I have a place to live when studying in the capital; I don't need it.\"","Rong Wangtian said dryly: \"Whether you need it or not, this apartment is under your name. It's your property. I'll just leave the real estate certificate here.\"","\"Also,\" he continued, \"You were admitted to Huaqing University in advance. I was thinking of holding a college acceptance banquet for you. What do you think?\"","Old Master Ji looked unhappy.","Shouldn't the college acceptance banquet be hosted by him, her biological son?","Rong Yu said: \"I don't plan to have a college acceptance banquet.\"","Rong Wangtian was very embarrassed.","Shen Lin kept her smile.","The couple had made ample preparations for today's visit. They had rehearsed at home what to say and who would say it, but coming here, they still met with a rebuff.","The two stood up, ready to take their leave.","Rong Yu's voice suddenly sounded: \"Next Sunday is Old Master Ji's birthday. If you two are free, you can come and attend.\"","Rong Wangtian's face was full of disbelief.","In the past, in order to attend the banquets of the four major families, he would start pulling strings long in advance and spend a high price to buy an invitation.","And now, with just one word from his eldest daughter, he could attend?","He looked at Old Master Ji.","Old Master Ji nodded faintly: \"When the time comes, someone will be sent to deliver the invitation to the Rong family.\"","The couple left with great joy.","After they left, the majesty on Old Master Ji instantly disappeared. He approached Rong Yu: \"Mom, how come I didn't know I was having a birthday banquet? Even the Rong family is invited. Are we doing it grandly? But I'm turning seventy-nine this year, not a round number. Should we still do it grandly?\"","Rong Yu looked at his head full of silver hair and said softly: \"This is your first birthday spent with Mom after seventy years. It should be grand.\"","The Rong couple walked outside the Ji family's door. Shen Lin looked back at the huge manor and said: \"Since Xiao Yu isn't having a college acceptance banquet, then Yaoyao won't have one either.\"","Rong Wangtian couldn't help asking: \"Why?\"","Both of his daughters were so excellent, they should hold grand banquets. If Xiao Yu didn't have one, fine, but why couldn't Yaoyao have one?","\"Everyone knows that Xiao Yu and Yaoyao are biological sisters. If we only hold it for the younger sister and not the older sister, how will outsiders view our Rong family?\" Shen Lin said slowly. \"In the next few days, carefully pick a birthday gift for Old Master Ji. It doesn't need to be too expensive, mainly the thought counts. For a family of that status, sincerity is always the most important.\"","Rong Wangtian nodded in agreement.","The two consecutive days of the college entrance examination quickly ended.","As soon as Ji Zhouye came back, he threw all his high school books and test papers from his room off the third-floor balcony, scattering them all over the courtyard.","He shouted: \"Liberated! I'm liberated! I can finally play games! Where is Duoduo? Quick, turn on the game console for your young uncle!\"","Duoduo stood with her hands on her hips and glared at him: \"Throwing trash everywhere, Young Uncle is the naughtiest.\"","Ji Zhouye turned his head and met Rong Yu's indifferent, water-like eyes. He immediately chickened out: \"I'll pick them up right now. Fourth Brother, help me out.\"","Ji Jingchuan smiled and nodded.","After cleaning up the books in the courtyard, Ji Jingchuan sat beside Rong Yu and said: \"For the two months of summer vacation, I want to sign up for a few language classes. Does Great-Grandma have any suggestions?\"","Rong Yu asked him: \"What major are you planning to apply for in college?\"","Ji Jingchuan had already thought about this question: \"I like dealing with flowers and plants, so I'll probably apply to the agricultural college.\"","Rong Yu asked, \"Your major doesn't really have high language requirements. Why are you learning so many different languages?\"","Ji Jingchuan's face suddenly flushed red. \"Ever since Tang Jin took over as the chairman of the Tang Group, she frequently travels abroad for business. She is only fluent in English, and a translator can't be by her side twenty-four seven, so...\"","\"Stop right there,\" Ji Zhouye interrupted, looking thoroughly annoyed as he played a video game nearby. \"I am already choking to death on all this PDA every single day. Have some pity on us single guys, Fourth Brother!\""]},{"number":285,"title":"Chapter 285: Why Are There So Many Overachievers in My Family","paragraphs":["Rong Yu had gained some insights into learning foreign languages.","She found some foreign language learning materials online and discussed them back and forth with Ji Jingchuan.","By the time Ji Zhouye finished a few rounds of his game, the two people beside him had gone from discussing foreign language learning to talking about becoming diplomats...","Meanwhile, Duoduo was nestled in Old Master Ji's arms, and the old and young pair were reading an English picture book together.","Suddenly, the game console in his hands lost its appeal.","Ji Zhouye felt like crying.","He had clearly planned to play games day and night after finishing his college entrance exams.","Why were there so many overachievers in his family!","Smack—","He slammed his game controller onto the coffee table.","Old Master Ji shot him a cold glance: What's gotten into you?","Ji Zhouye stood on the sofa and declared loudly, I've decided! For the two months of summer vacation, I'm going to start a gaming company!","Old Master Ji grabbed a throw pillow and tossed it at him: Wash up and go to sleep. Start a company? Do you even have the brains to run one?","Great-grandmother, the old man is bullying me! Ji Zhouye pouted aggrievedly. Oldest brother tried starting a studio when he was sixteen, second brother entered the entertainment industry at sixteen, and third brother joined a research institute before high school even ended. What about me? Why can't I!","You don't even know your own... Old Master Ji was cut off halfway by Rong Yu.","She looked up at Ji Zhouye: Sit down properly. I have a few questions for you.","Ji Zhouye instantly turned into a well-behaved child, placing his hands on his knees and saying respectfully, Ask away, Great-grandmother.","Rong Yu: Tell me why?","Ji Zhouye immediately replied, Because current games are too boring. They're all just pay-to-win reskins. I want to make something different!","Old Master Ji muttered, Boring, yet you play them every day...","Rong Yu: Do you know what kind of people are needed to develop a game?","Ji Zhouye scratched his head and guessed tentatively, Programmers? Artists? Planners?","Rong Yu: And?","Ji Zhouye secretly winked, seeking help from Ji Jingchuan.","Ji Jingchuan could only pretend not to see it.","Rong Yu looked at him and said calmly, Did you think that starting a company only requires an idea, and everything else will automatically fall into place?","Ji Zhouye hung his head.","He really had just suddenly come up with this idea.","But having an idea is a good thing, Rong Yu's voice carried encouragement. Any great undertaking begins with a small idea. How about this: for your two-month summer vacation, you go intern at the Ji Corporation first.","Ah? Ji Zhouye looked up, his eyes widening. I just got rid of my identity as a high school student, and now you want me to go slave away at the company?","Rong Yu smiled: You don't even know how a company actually operates, and you want to start one?","Ji Zhouye: ...","He might as well have just honestly played his games. He really asked for trouble and dug a huge pit for himself.","Old Master Ji's birthday fell in midsummer, on the fifteenth of June.","For the banquet on this day, the entire Ji family got busy. Ji Zhiyuan booked a luxury cruise ship, Ji Yanting personally designed the banquet flow, Ji Mohan was in charge of hand-writing the invitations, and Ji Jingchuan and Ji Zhouye led a group of servants to decorate the ship.","At dusk, Rong Yu drove her old son and Duoduo to the banquet venue.","Old Master, happy birthday.","The five good grandsons stood on the deck, welcoming him enthusiastically.","This scene made Old Master Ji think back to his birthday last year.","It had just been a normal day. Yuan gave him a gift in the morning and went to the company; Ah Yan was busy filming and could only call to send his wishes; Ah Mo was far away in Africa and couldn't be reached; Ah Chuan was still suffering at that time; Ah Ye had a bit of a conscience and, along with Duoduo, accompanied him for dinner.","But this year, because Mom was here, the whole family was together.","Duoduo took a drawing out of her small backpack and unfolded it: This is my gift for Great-grandfather. It's a drawing of Great-grandfather and Auntie, because I know Auntie is the most, most, most important person to Great-grandfather.","Old Master Ji tapped her little nose: Duoduo is very important too.","Ji Zhiyuan presented tea leaves.","Ji Yanting gave a famous master's calligraphy.","Ji Mohan gifted a massage device.","Ji Jingchuan presented a pot of orchids.","Ji Zhouye gave a book.","The corners of Old Master Ji's mouth twitched: Yuan, you give me tea leaves every year; I'm sick of drinking them. Ah Yan, is this calligrapher a friend of yours? Why do you buy a piece every year? Ah Mo, there are already five or six massagers at home, are you trying to massage me to death? Ah Chuan's pot of orchids is quite beautiful, though. As for Ah Ye, I've had enough of you—isn't this the book your great-grandmother gave to Duoduo!","Ji Zhouye clutched his head: Duoduo said she couldn't understand it, so she gave it to me. Can't I regift it to you, Old Master? I'm so poor, please just bear with it.","Alright, Rong Yu said with a smile. Look at what I prepared for you?","She handed over a box filled with small cards, each with text written on it.","Keep company fishing for one day.","Keep company playing chess for one day.","Allowed to eat some sweets.","Allowed to drink some alcohol.","Looking at these cards, Old Master Ji suddenly felt a prickle in his nose.","He remembered when he was little, a classmate had received such a gift, allowing them to unconditionally ask their parents to play with them for a day.","When he went home, he clamored for one too.","But his mother didn't agree.","Because her work was simply too busy.","He never expected that after seventy years, his tiny childhood wish would actually be fulfilled.","I love it very much. Thank you, Mom.","Old Master Ji carefully placed the cards into his breast pocket.","At this moment.","Old Master Hai, Old Master Si, and a few others arrived with the younger generations of their families.","Old Ji, happy birthday.","Old Ji, you sure are blessed, having so many grandsons throw a birthday banquet for you.","...","The younger generation of the Ji family also went up to welcome the guests.","Ji Zhouye was just about to chat with his friends Si Lin and Hai Chang'an.","Only to see those two, after wishing Old Master Ji well, walk straight over to Rong Yu. Tang Mi and Zhou Shiyu also came over, and the four of them surrounded Rong Yu as they walked onto the cruise ship.","Si Lin cleared the path in front.","Hai Chang'an helped carry a wine glass.","Tang Mi gently supported Rong Yu.","Zhou Shiyu adjusted Rong Yu's skirt hem...","These four wealthy young masters and ladies were acting like obedient grandchildren around Rong Yu.","Ji Zhouye was furious: Are you kidding me... Hey, you jerks, get out of the way!","He was Great-grandmother's real grandson! No one was allowed to steal her from him!","Just then, Steward Yu hurried over: Old Master, this is a package sent from the military zone of Base Four. It specifies that you must sign for it yourself.","Old Master Ji opened it suspiciously.","The other old men nearby also leaned in: What is it? So mysterious?","Upon opening it, they found it was a mecha vehicle made out of bullet casings."]},{"number":286,"title":"Chapter 286: What is he giving me a gift for, who cares","paragraphs":["It was a mecha vehicle model completely welded together from bullet casings.","The front of the vehicle was spliced into a wedge shape using anti-aircraft artillery shells, and the doors were made of neatly arranged rifle casings. The most amazing part was that every joint could move, and the tracks were actually formed by stringing together hundreds of small-caliber bullet casings. It was exceptionally exquisite.","Old Master Ji's hands trembled slightly. \"Who sent this?\"","He thought of his childhood. When he was six or seven, the fathers of Old Hai and Old Si were both in the military and would give them bullet casing toys as birthday gifts. On the surface, he acted dismissive, but as soon as he got home, he would cry and throw a tantrum, pestering his mother for one too.","At that time, his mother's eyes were red, but he didn't care. He just kept crying, determined not to stop until he got what he wanted.","He vaguely remembered that his mother seemed to have gone out and brought back a box of bullet casings for him. However, she wasn't good at crafts, so those casings just sat in his bookcase. One day, they were snatched away by Old Hai and Old Si, which made him burst into loud tears out of anger.","Rong Yu walked over. \"It's Sheng Qingyan. I've talked to him about this.\"","Old Master Ji's excitement vanished in an instant.","He curled his lip. \"Why is he sending me a gift? Who cares for it?\"","Old Master Hai: \"I care. Let me see.\"","Old Master Si: \"This little gadget is really exquisitely made. The craftsmanship is incredible...\"","\"Don't touch it, you might break it.\" Old Master Ji slapped the backs of their hands and shouted, \"Yuan, quickly put it away for me. Be careful, if you break it, I'll hold you responsible!\"","Rong Yu: \"...\"","This old guy, acting both disdainful and cherishing at the same time. His expressions were truly rich.","More and more guests gradually arrived.","The Rong family also arrived. Rong Wangtian and Shen Lin brought Rong Ruoyao to the banquet. They gifted tea leaves because they had found out that the Old Master loved drinking tea, specifically Da Hong Pao, so they specially commissioned someone to buy a premium batch.","Old Master Ji took a glance. It was actually the exact same tea as the one Yuan had gifted. It was quite thoughtful of them.","He spoke calmly, \"President Rong, Madam Rong, feel free to eat and drink. Make yourselves at home.\"","The couple smiled and nodded.","Shen Lin gave Rong Ruoyao a push. \"Your sister is over there. Go over and chat with her.\"","Rong Ruoyao originally didn't want to go.","But when she looked up, she saw Rong Yu surrounded by a group of wealthy heirs. Those usually aloof young ladies and gentlemen were surprisingly friendly towards Rong Yu.","She thought for a moment, lifted the hem of her dress, and walked over.","Rong Yu was hanging out with a group of wealthy youths. Ji Zhouye was talking about his grand plan: \"After I intern at the Ji Corporation for two months, I'm going to open a gaming company. You guys all need to invest. You hear me? All of you, invest in me!\"","Si Lin was speechless. \"Investing in you is worse than throwing money into the water just to hear a splash.\"","Tang Mi took a sip of champagne. \"Ji Zhouye, show me the business plan first before we talk.\"","Zhou Shiyu rolled her eyes. \"Opening a company right after finishing high school. Miss Rong, tell us, can he really do it?\"","Just then, Rong Ruoyao's voice rang out: \"Sister.\"","Rong Yu turned her head and gave a soft affirmative hum.","\"Sister, you know a lot. I wanted to ask you, what university and major do you think I should apply for?\" Rong Ruoyao put on a humble expression. \"I had my homeroom teacher estimate my score, and it's around seven hundred points.\"","\"Seven hundred points!\" Si Lin was completely shocked. \"If I could have scored that high back then, I probably would have inherited the Si family by now.\"","Ji Zhouye rolled his eyes. \"What's so great about seven hundred points? My fourth brother is estimated to get seven hundred and thirty, and he didn't go around shouting it for everyone to know. What a show-off.\"","Rong Ruoyao's smile froze on her face.","Rong Yu said calmly, \"Aye.\"","This kid's own estimated score was only a little over five hundred, yet he had the nerve to look down on someone with seven hundred points.","Seven hundred points in the liberal arts was definitely not low. Although Rong Ruoyao was a bit scheming, it had to be admitted that when it came to studying, her abilities were unquestionable.","She spoke up, \"Choosing a university and major all depends on your own plans for the future.\"","Rong Ruoyao smiled and nodded. \"Thank you for the advice, Sister.\"","She was just looking for a conversation starter to blend in; she wasn't actually looking for any specific advice.","At that moment, a guest suddenly arrived.","Old Master Ji brought Ji Zhiyuan and personally went down the deck to welcome them.","Rong Yu looked down and saw an elderly lady wearing a deep purple qipao. She was about seventy years old, dressed elegantly and luxuriously, and her hands were tightly clasped with the Old Master's.","The two stood below and began conversing.","\"Brother-in-law, it's been at least ten years since we last saw each other, hasn't it?\" The elderly lady looked deeply moved. \"I thought we would meet at your eightieth birthday celebration. I didn't expect you to throw a big party for your seventy-ninth. As soon as I received the news, I rushed over immediately. Thankfully, I'm not late.\"","Rong Yu was taken aback.","Brother-in-law?","Then who was this person?","\"It's Great-Aunt. Her husband's family surname is Xie, and they are from the capital,\" Ji Zhouye said. \"When I was very young, Great-Aunt seemed to have visited the Ji family. Later, as she got older, we interacted less.\"","\"My sister left us too early.\" Old Madam Xie wiped the corner of her eye. \"I still remember when my sister was sick, I stayed at the Ji family home for over half a year, praying every day for her to get better quickly. Who could have imagined that she would still pass away just like that, leaving behind my brother-in-law and such a young child...\"","Old Master Ji's eyes turned red. \"During those years when your sister was sick, it was indeed hard on you. Sigh, if only your sister were still alive...\"","\"Old Master, Great-Aunt, let's go up and chat,\" Ji Zhiyuan spoke up. \"This way, please.\"","Old Madam Xie's gaze swept over the children of the Ji family. \"They've all grown up and are so tall. They are truly promising. My sister's spirit in heaven can rest in peace.\"","She patted all five children and even wanted to pick up Duoduo, but unfortunately, due to her old age, she couldn't lift her.","Duoduo said obediently, \"Great-Auntie can just give me a kiss.\"","Old Madam Xie couldn't help but laugh. \"Other people's children usually shy away from the elderly, but this little granddaughter of yours actually asked for a kiss. You've raised her so well.\"","\"Of course.\" Old Master Ji said proudly. \"Duoduo used to be very timid, but ever since...\"","At this point, he paused.","Old Madam Xie didn't press the matter. She pressed her temples and said, \"Brother-in-law, I feel a bit dizzy. Could you take me to a room to rest for a while first?\"","Old Master Ji nodded and personally escorted her over.","As soon as the two of them left, Old Master Si pulled Rong Yu into a corner. \"Miss Rong, let me tell you, this Old Madam Xie was quite something in her youth.\"","Rong Yu looked curious. \"How so?\"","Old Master Hai winked and grimaced. \"Back then, she was the flower of the Haicheng Art Troupe, known as the number one beauty of Haicheng. She was exceptionally beautiful and very smart.\"","\"When Old Ji married her sister, she strongly opposed it. She looked down on Old Ji and said that marrying him would bring bad luck. She even reminded us to transfer our family wealth, and sure enough, there was political turmoil later.\" Old Master Si shrugged. \"She later married a military officer in the capital and became an official's wife. She was very glamorous, but unfortunately...\"","Old Master Hai shook his head. \"Unfortunately, her husband died very early. Thirty or forty years ago, the Xie family was quite prominent in the capital, but now hardly anyone knows of them.\"","The two of them rambled on and talked about many things.","Rong Yu listened quietly.","\"Splash!\"","Suddenly, the sound of a heavy splash echoed nearby.","Rong Yu sprinted toward the commotion, only to find that a few seven- or eight-year-old children, daring each other to see who was the bravest, had climbed onto the railing and accidentally tumbled into the sea."]},{"number":287,"title":"Chapter 287: Asked if I could lend her five hundred million to get through the crisis","paragraphs":["The cruise ship's lounge area.","Ji Mohan was not good at exchanging pleasantries and socializing with guests. He grabbed a book and leaned against the railing to read.","As he was reading, the sudden sound of someone falling into the water caught his attention. He immediately turned his head and saw that the splash on the sea surface had not yet settled; a small figure was struggling desperately.","After nearly drowning in college, he had spent a whole year training hard in swimming. Although he was no professional athlete, saving someone was not an issue.","Without hesitation, Ji Mohan took off his jacket, preparing to dive into the sea.","Suddenly, a slender figure brushed past him and jumped in first.","Splash!","Water splashed into the air as the girl, like an agile fish, swam swiftly toward the child.","The girl managed to grab the child's collar, but the child, panicked and thrashing wildly, was dragging her down and making it difficult for her.","Ji Mohan followed closely and plunged into the sea.","He hooked his arm around the child's neck, supporting the small body from behind. Lying steadily on the surface of the water, the child finally calmed down.","He took a brief moment to glance at the girl beside him.","She didn't have a traditionally beautiful face, but she had a few light freckles that made her quite unique.","Her wet black hair clung to her cheeks, making her skin look even more translucent. Water droplets hung on her eyelashes, fluttering like dew-kissed butterfly wings when she blinked. Her eyes were incredibly bright, reflecting the sparkling sea with an astonishing brilliance.","He only took one look before quickly withdrawing his gaze.","Working together in tacit understanding, the two guided the child toward the cruise ship. A crowd had already gathered on the deck, and someone threw down a lifebuoy and ropes.","Ji Mohan supported the child first, letting the girl grab the rope and climb up before he hoisted himself onto the deck.","The child was fine, but was immediately snatched up by a parent and given a loud, wailing spanking.","Rong Yu brought over a few blankets and draped them over the two. \"Every guest room has spare evening wear. Hurry up and change so you don't catch a cold.\"","Ji Mohan nodded, gesturing for the girl to go first.","The girl lowered her head in embarrassment. \"Well, I, I'm actually not an invited guest. I don't have a room, so I'll be leaving now!\"","She turned around, ready to flee.","Rong Yu firmly pressed a hand onto her shoulder. \"Are you a reporter?\"","The girl hurriedly shook her head. \"Of course not.\"","Ji Mohan asked curiously, \"If you aren't a reporter, why did you sneak in?\"","\"I, I...\" the girl felt extremely guilty. \"I am a screenwriter. Because I have to write a plot about a wealthy family's cruise banquet, I snuck in to experience it. Otherwise, I would write it as a group of rich heirs ripping open disposable chopsticks and drinking iced tea with their meals... It's just really hard for poor people to write about the lives of the rich. But, I am truly sorry. I shouldn't have snuck in.\"","Rong Yu was amused.","She picked up a towel and dried the girl's soaking wet hair. \"We have a similar figure. Come to my room and change into some of my clothes. By the way, what is your name?\"","The girl relaxed and smiled. \"My name is Ye Weiwan.\"","When she smiled, two dimples appeared at the corners of her mouth.","Ji Mohan froze for a moment. He didn't know why, but those dimples looked a bit familiar. Had he seen them somewhere before?","Rong Yu led Ye Weiwan into her guest room.","The walk-in closet in her room was filled with all sorts of evening gowns.","Ye Weiwan was completely stunned. \"Oh my god, these dresses are so beautiful. Are the gems on them real? Are these sapphires or amethysts? They are blindingly gorgeous... I've truly broadened my horizons today! I won't wear these dresses. If I ruin them, I won't be able to afford the compensation. I'll just stay in my wet clothes, it's fine. I have a strong constitution, so I won't get sick.\"","Rong Yu suddenly felt that the screenwriting profession was quite interesting.","She picked out a nude-colored long dress from the closet and handed it over. \"This one is a bit too big for me, but it should fit you perfectly. Consider it a gift.\"","A girl who could jump into the sea without hesitation to save someone was fundamentally kind-hearted. Letting a kind person leave in wet clothes would be a disrespect to that kindness.","Ye Weiwan took a closer look. The dress didn't have any accessories and didn't look overly extravagant; it was within her acceptable range. She nodded. \"Then I won't be polite.\"","She didn't act pretentious and offer to pay for it either.","Because she knew that rich people did not lack such a small amount of money.","Rong Yu left the room to give Ye Weiwan some privacy.","As she walked out, she surprisingly heard crying coming from the room next door. Wasn't that Yingbao's crying?","She immediately pushed open the door to the adjacent room.","She saw her old son and Old Madam Xie sitting on the sofa, holding each other's hands. Both of them were teary-eyed, crying non-stop.","Rong Yu frowned and looked at Ji Zhiyuan, who was standing to the side.","The elderly were advanced in age; crying like this would easily make them sick.","Ji Zhiyuan spoke helplessly, \"The old man and my great-aunt started talking about my father. As they talked, they started crying, and I couldn't stop them.\"","\"Yuan's father had a bitter life.\" Old Master Ji wiped his tears. \"He grew up without a mother. I was busy with work and didn't spend much time with him. Fortunately, he had an aunt who came by from time to time to help take care of him. He finally grew up, married a wife, and started a family. Who would have thought that he would pass away at such a young age...\"","\"Alright,\" Rong Yu interrupted him. \"That is ancient history from so many years ago. There is no need to bring it up again. It hurts the heart and the body, so why bother?\"","Old Madam Xie raised her head. \"Yuan, is this young lady your girlfriend?\"","\"No.\" Old Master Ji's emotions calmed down a bit as he explained. \"This is Miss Rong. She saved my life and is the most honored guest of our Ji family.\"","\"Miss Rong looks very kind.\" Old Madam Xie took an emerald green bracelet off her wrist. \"Please take this bracelet as a meeting gift, Miss Rong. Please do not disdain it and accept it.\"","Old Master Ji chimed in, \"Accept it. We are all family, it's fine.\"","Rong Yu smiled. \"Then thank you, Old Madam.\"","Ji Zhiyuan spoke up at the right moment, \"The guests outside have all arrived. Shouldn't the old master make an appearance first?\"","Old Master Ji told Old Madam Xie to get some good rest, and the group walked outside together.","Right as they were about to step onto the deck, Old Master Ji tugged at Rong Yu's sleeve and whispered, \"Mom, I have something to tell you.\"","Rong Yu stopped in her tracks. \"Does it have to do with that old madam?\"","Old Master Ji's eyes widened. \"Mom, how do you know everything?\"","Rong Yu's expression remained calm.","In the accounts given by Hai Dadun and Sima Gang, Old Madam Xie was a smart, proud, and courageous woman. A woman like that would not easily take the initiative to get close to others.","Yet Old Madam Xie had actively hugged Duoduo, offered her a gift, and repeatedly reminisced about the past with Yingbao.","One look was enough to know that she definitely wanted something.","\"Xiaohui, who is the children's great-aunt, indeed has something she wants my help with,\" Old Master Ji said. \"She mentioned that the Xie family has encountered some difficulties recently and needs capital turnover. She asked if I could lend her five hundred million to tide over the crisis.\"","Rong Yu nodded. \"Yuan, go and transfer the funds.\"","Old Master Ji was stunned for a moment, and then overjoyed. \"Mom, you agreed? You really are the best mother in the world!\"","Rong Yu couldn't help but laugh. \"During the years I was away, she extended a helping hand to the Ji family. Now that she has encountered difficulties, we naturally cannot just stand by and watch.\""]},{"number":288,"title":"Chapter 288: The cruelest yet gentlest part of youth","paragraphs":["Ji Zhiyuan had just transferred five hundred million.","Old Madam Xie then took her leave, hurrying off the cruise ship with her assistant.","Old Master Ji could not help but sigh. \"I never expected the Xie family to fall into such ruin. When she was young, she was a fiercely competitive and ambitious person. She racked her brains to marry into a superior family and got her wish to become an official's wife. Unfortunately, her husband died early, and her son failed to live up to expectations. People's destinies are truly unpredictable.\"","Rong Yu said gently, \"Fortunes rise and fall. Therefore, one should not be arrogant in times of success, nor should one despair in times of low ebb. Who can really say for sure what life will bring? Don't dwell on these things anymore. With your mother here, you can just enjoy your retirement in peace.\"","The mother and son walked out.","Old Master Ji walked onto the stage and addressed all the guests: \"Thank you all for taking time out of your busy schedules to attend my birthday banquet...\"","The cruise ship dinner banquet concluded smoothly.","That evening after the event, Ji Yanting came to chat with Rong Yu. \"Great-grandmother, I've recently been involved in the production of a patriotic movie. The movie's theme song praises all the builders who have silently dedicated themselves to the motherland over the past seventy years. The melody is grand, and the lyrics are already written, but we haven't been able to decide on a singer. I wonder if you might be interested, Great-grandmother?\"","He handed over the lyric sheet.","Rong Yu took it and glanced at it.","She was not particularly skilled with words, so she deeply admired those who could write. In just a few lines, the lyrics sketched out the turbulent years of the early days of the nation's founding. Between the lines, one could almost hear the roar of artillery fire and see the red flags fluttering in the west wind.","With a shift in tone, the modern spectacle of satellites launching into space and high-speed railways crisscrossing the land rushed to the fore.","The most shocking part was the last two lines, which compared generations of builders to fallen flowers turning to mud, yet silently nourishing this land.","She looked up and said, \"I'll sing it.\"","Ji Yanting was overjoyed. \"Wait a couple of days until the college entrance examination scores come out, and then we'll go to Beijing to record it.\"","It was a tradition at Haicheng No. 1 High School that every year when the college entrance examination scores were released, the students of each class would sit in their classrooms and check their scores together.","Although Rong Yu did not take the college entrance examination, she still came along with Ji Jingchuan and Ji Zhouye.","Pei Yaru's fingers hovered over the keyboard. The breathing of the fifty students in the class was suppressed to the extreme. They watched the loading icon on the computer screen spin three times before it finally changed.","\"They're out, the scores are out!\"","The whole class boiled over. No one used their mobile phones to check; instead, they waited for Pei Yaru at the podium to enter their ID numbers one by one to check.","The first was Ji Jingchuan.","The second the score appeared, the whole class exploded.","\"Holy crap! Shielded! Ji Jingchuan's score is shielded!\"","\"Only the top fifty scores get shielded. He's guaranteed for Tsinghua or Peking University. Ji Jingchuan is too strong!\"","\"Our Class 20 actually produced a Tsinghua or Peking University student!\"","Sitting next to the podium, Ji Jingchuan looked calm and smiled. \"Everyone, go back to your seats and sit down. Teacher Pei is going to check the class monitor's score now.\"","Pei Yaru's hands were shaking a little.","She had been teaching for so many years, and this was her first time checking a shielded score. The shock in her heart had not yet subsided when, the next moment, the score on the computer screen was shielded once again.","\"Oh my god, the class monitor's score is also shielded!\"","\"Damn, damn, damn, the study commissary is also shielded!\"","\"Quick, look at the Youth League Secretary's. Ahhh, 701 points! Youth League Secretary, you actually got a 701! Your highest mock exam score before was 680. You totally overperformed on the actual exam!\"","Pei Yaru covered her mouth with her hand.","Only the top fifty in Haicheng City would have their scores shielded. Her class of underachievers actually accounted for three of them. It was unbelievable!","Her hands were trembling so much that she could barely press the keys on the keyboard accurately.","Rong Yu, the person who hadn't taken the exam, was quite calm. She walked up to the podium. \"Teacher Pei, let me help you check the rest.\"","Pei Yaru's head was spinning, and she immediately gave up her seat.","Rong Yu directly opened multiple windows and queried a batch all at once.","Her calm voice slowly rang out.","\"Above 700 points: Ji Jingchuan, the class monitor, the study commissary, and the Youth League Secretary, a total of four.\"","\"Above 650 points: two people.\"","\"Above 600 points: a total of nine people.\"","\"Above 550 points...\"","The students in the classroom all went crazy.","Because the final results were better than everyone's expectations.","Those who previously thought they couldn't get into a university had scores high enough for a relatively good junior college.","Those who previously only planned to attend a traditional third-tier university reached the cutoff for second-tier universities.","Those who previously thought they could only get into a second-tier university could actually touch the edge of the first-tier cutoff...","Ji Zhouye jumped directly onto his desk, waving his school uniform jacket like a flag. \"Hahaha, I got 562 points! I can go to college! Hahahaha, I'm so awesome!\"","Chen Nian also climbed onto a desk and shouted, \"I got 596 points! Thank you, teachers, thank you, classmates, and especially thank you, Rong Yu...\"","The students of Class 20 suddenly began to chant Rong Yu's name in perfect unison.","\"Rong Yu!\"","\"Rong Yu!\"","The shouts shook the heavens.","Even the elite class a corridor away heard the cheers.","Teacher Yang's face was as dark as the bottom of a pot.","The elite class she led actually only had four people with shielded scores. Although there were only five last year... one must know that the students who entered this class were all among the top fifty in the school, while Class 20 was full of underachievers.","Now, the slacker class and the elite class were actually on par.","This was like a loud slap in the face.","She gritted her teeth and said, \"Are you proud of being overtaken by a bunch of slackers?\"","Zhang Haoyu said softly, \"Who asked their class to have Rong Yu.\"","Rumor had it that three days before the exam, Rong Yu had predicted the exam questions for the whole class. Whether she guessed right or not was unknown, but Class 20's rapid progress, as if they had been completely reborn, definitely had something to do with Rong Yu.","Song Huai looked out the window.","The whole of Class 20 was over there taking graduation photos.","Even though there were so many people there, he could only see Rong Yu. She was surrounded in the middle, with Ji Zhouye on her left and Ji Jingchuan on her right. The three of them had their arms around each other's shoulders, looking very intimate, completely exceeding the boundaries of normal classmates.","He pursed his lips and withdrew his gaze.","After the people of Class 20 took group photos with their teachers and classmates, they started to plan their teacher appreciation banquet.","With fifty people in the class, one day per person wouldn't be enough to split the bill.","Ji Zhouye said loudly, \"There's no time like the present. Let's do it today. The whole class will host the teacher appreciation banquet together. Let's go, we'll go to Ji's Grand Hotel.\"","Rong Yu smiled and said, \"It will be hard to gather everyone so completely in the future. For today's meal, not a single person is allowed to be missing.\"","The grand banquet hall of Ji's Grand Hotel was booked out.","\"Teacher Pei! A toast to you!\"","The class monitor led all the students to stand up, raising their wine glasses as they rushed forward in a chaotic swarm. Pei Yaru was surrounded in the middle, laughing so hard that tears fell from her eyes. \"Three years... you little brats, you finally didn't make me worry in vain!\"","The study commissary started to lead a song.","\"I once found it hard to pull myself away from the vastness of the world.\"","\"And indulged in its dreamlike words.\"","\"Unable to tell truth from falsehood, not struggling, not fearing being a joke.\"","\"I once turned my youth into her.\"","\"And played the midsummer at my fingertips...\"","The whole class sang in chorus, ridiculously out of tune.","Fortunately, Rong Yu was quite good at singing. Relying on her own strength, she pulled the tune back on track. After the whole class finished singing, they cried their eyes out.","The class monitor downed a mouthful of his drink, his face flushed as he yelled, \"I'm going to apply to Huaqing University too, so I can still be classmates with Rong Yu!\"","The study representative laughed out loud, \"I knew you had a crush on Rong Yu.\"","The class monitor's face grew even redder. \"Nonsense, stop talking nonsense! I just purely want to keep being classmates with her, that's all.\"","Chen Nian's nose stung with sudden emotion. \"My scores are too low to be classmates with Sister Yu anymore. Sob, it's going to be so hard to see each other from now on, so hard...\"","Rong Yu's eyes also grew a little red.","Perhaps the cruelest yet gentlest part of youth was this grand, irreversible farewell."]},{"number":289,"title":"Chapter 289: My Favorite Goddess Comes to Haicheng for Her First League Match","paragraphs":["The graduation appreciation banquet lasted until after eight o'clock in the evening.","Having had a bit to drink, Ji Zhouye was even more excited. He grabbed Rong Yu's hand and coaxed, Great-Grandma, there is an esports tournament in Haicheng tonight at nine-thirty. My absolute favorite goddess is coming to Haicheng for a league match for the first time. I have to get a photo with her no matter what. Great-Grandma, Fourth Brother, do you want to go together?","Rong Yu always had a desire to explore new things.","She had tried playing video games before but did not find them particularly difficult. She never expected it could develop into an international league.","She also wanted to see what level truly skilled gamers were at.","Rong Yu nodded.","Ji Jingchuan immediately followed suit. After making a quick call to inform Old Master Ji, the trio drove off to the competition center.","Inside the esports arena, the lights were dazzling. The giant screen was broadcasting the showdown between Team XY and Team Thunder live. The audience seats were packed, with cheers and shouts rising one after another.","Great-Grandma, let me tell you, my goddess is the captain of Team XY, Ji Zhouye said, pointing excitedly at the big screen. See that? The one in the middle, the only girl, that is the esports goddess, Yaoyao. She is so cool.","No sooner had his voice faded than a disdainful laugh came from nearby.","Hilarious, Yaoyao actually has fans.","She spends all day marketing her esports goddess persona while her gameplay is absolute trash. She would be better off being an internet celebrity!","She only knows how to play utility heroes to get by. If you actually make her carry, her true colors show immediately!","Ji Zhouye was instantly furious. Pointing right at their noses, he shouted, Team XY could not even make it to the playoffs before. Yaoyao came and completely carried them! Last year in the national tournament, she pulled off an extreme one-versus-three counter-kill and became a legend on the spot. She fully deserves the title of esports goddess, okay!","On the giant screen, the character Yaoyao was controlling suddenly executed a beautiful dash, leading her teammates to complete a flawless team wipe.","Did you see that? That is pure skill! Ji Zhouye stood up in excitement. Yaoyao is the main reason Team XY made it to where they are today!","Faced with the facts, that group of people could only shut their mouths.","Rong Yu watched the gaming competition in awe.","Yaoyao's positioning was incredibly precise, and every skill release was timed perfectly. The opponents' attacks surged like a tidal wave, yet she could calmly tear open a breach in the rapidly changing battlefield.","Rong Yu's fingertips tapped unconsciously on her knee, her brain working at lightning speed. If it were her, could she calculate such a tactic?","Not necessarily.","Gaming was not just math; it was intuition, experience, and split-second situational reactions.","No wonder the kid Ji Zhouye was so addicted to it. This was far more thrilling than she had imagined.","In the final team fight, Yaoyao baited the enemy into overextending, while her teammates flanked them with perfect synergy, annihilating the opponents in one fell swoop. The moment the crystal exploded, the entire arena erupted!","We won! Ji Zhouye stood up and cheered. Yaoyao won! That was so awesome, so cool!","He grabbed Rong Yu and Ji Jingchuan. Let us go, to the backstage! I want to get a photo and autograph from Yaoyao. Hurry, if we are late, we will not be able to squeeze in!","There were people everywhere. Rong Yu was pushed along by the crowd as a throng of people squeezed toward the exit.","Security guards maintained order, escorting the team members out from backstage. The girl leading the pack wore a black leather jacket, her long, straight black hair draped over her shoulders. Her skin was incredibly pale, her lips a vibrant red, and her eyes carried a hint of sharpness.","Yaoyao!","Yaoyao, I love you!","The fans were mostly male, screaming at the top of their lungs.","Fourth Brother, quick, lift me up! I need to get Yaoyao's attention! Ji Zhouye climbed onto the railing and sat on Ji Jingchuan's shoulders, shouting, Yaoyao, look at me, look over here! I have been following you for three years, please let me get a picture with you!","Ji Jingchuan was speechless.","He was honestly struggling to hold him up.","Rong Yu was thoroughly exasperated.","She reached out and helped support the kid's rear end.","Yaoyao, who was just about to get into her car, suddenly turned her head to look over. When she saw Ji Zhouye in the crowd, she was visibly stunned for a good moment.","Soon, she walked toward Ji Zhouye's direction, her bright red lips curving up slightly. You have been watching my matches since three years ago?","Ji Zhouye's breathing quickened, his cheeks flushing red. Yes! Three years ago, right when you became a professional esports player, I started following you. Goddess, please give me an autograph, please take a photo with me!","Yaoyao smiled and nodded. Okay.","Ji Zhouye was so excited he was about to faint. He shoved his phone into Ji Jingchuan's hands. Fourth Brother, make me look handsome.","Rong Yu's brow suddenly twitched.","For some reason, when this girl named Yaoyao walked over, her heart suddenly felt very uncomfortable... She did not know where this discomfort was coming from.","After the photo was taken.","Yaoyao offered, Very few people started following me three years ago. Why do we not add each other as friends? I will notify you directly when there are matches in the future.","Ji Zhouye nodded frantically. Yes, that is great! Yaoyao, I will support you forever!","After exchanging contact info, Yaoyao's gaze swept lightly over Rong Yu. Her slender brows furrowed imperceptibly before she turned around and got into the car.","Countless people around them cast envious glances at Ji Zhouye.","Smug, Ji Zhouye edited the photo and uploaded it to his social media, where it instantly garnered over ten thousand likes.","Rong Yu's brows remained tightly furrowed.","Ji Jingchuan asked in a low voice, Great-Grandma, is there a problem with this girl named Yaoyao?","Rong Yu occasionally believed in a woman's sixth sense.","Previously, there was He Liuguang kidnapping Duoduo.","She did not want the Ji family to go through such terrible things again.","She spoke up, Achuan, go look into her.","Ji Jingchuan nodded. Rest assured, Great-Grandma, I will definitely find out everything.","The very next day, he brought back the information.","Yaoyao's real name was Zhao Yaomei, an ordinary girl from a rural village in the south. She dropped out of high school to work in an electronics factory. Three years ago, she suddenly chose to enter the esports industry and became famous after a single battle. From then on, everything went smoothly for her. In just three short years, she reached the absolute pinnacle of the esports world, becoming the esports goddess idolized by countless male fans.","Looking at her resume, she was a very outstanding girl with no major issues.","Rong Yu temporarily put the matter aside. Next, she had to go to the capital to record the theme song for a mainstream movie.","Her octogenarian son, naturally, was clinging to her and insisting on tagging along."]},{"number":290,"title":"Chapter 290: Did you ask her why she borrowed so much money","paragraphs":["Old Master Ji took Butler Yu and a few servants, packed over a dozen suitcases, and headed to the capital in a grand procession.","Wherever his mother was, he would go. Regardless, he refused to be separated from his mother.","Compared to the Furong Manor in Haicheng, the villa in the capital was slightly smaller, and the courtyard wasn't as spacious, but it was enough to house the family.","On the first floor, besides the servants' quarters, there was a large bedroom for Old Master Ji to stay in.","Old Master Ji prepared the largest single room on the second floor for Rong Yu, decorating it exactly like her bedroom in Haicheng.","Ji Yanting and Ji Mohan simply moved over as well, staying in the rooms on the third floor.","Once the university semester began, Ji Jingchuan and Ji Zhouye would also live here after successfully being admitted to universities in the capital.","\"Great-Grandma, here is the sheet music and lyrics.\" Ji Yanting sent over a document. \"It's the work of Qi Su, a musical genius in the industry. It's written very well, and he composed the music too. Great-Grandma can familiarize herself with it first.\"","Rong Yu looked at the sheet music and began to hum softly.","She really liked the artistic conception conveyed by the lyrics, which was why she decided to take on this job, but she felt that something was a bit off about the melody.","Just as she was pondering this.","Butler Yu suddenly walked in. \"Old Master, Old Madam Xie has arrived.\"","Old Madam Xie, dressed in an elegant qipao and followed by her personal assistant, walked in with a beaming smile. \"Now that brother-in-law is living in the capital, it will be much more convenient for our two families to visit each other. I picked out a housewarming gift; it will look perfect hanging in the living room.\"","She presented a traditional Chinese landscape painting.","Old Master Ji immediately had Butler Yu arrange for the servants to hang it on the wall.","Old Madam Xie's gaze fell upon the people in the living room: Ji Yanting, Ji Mohan, and that Miss Rong she had seen previously on the cruise ship.","Her gaze lingered on Rong Yu's face for quite a while.","Old Master Ji secretly glanced at Rong Yu.","Rong Yu understood the meaning behind his look: he was asking if they should just go ahead and tell Old Madam Xie her true identity.","Rong Yu gave a faint shake of her head.","The younger generations of the Ji family were related to her by blood, so she could trust them.","But this old madam was merely Yingbao's wife's younger sister and had no solid ties to the Ji family.","Perhaps, the second after telling Old Madam Xie, her sons, daughters-in-law, and grandchildren would all know that Rong Yu was a wandering soul from seventy years ago...","Old Master Ji took a sip of tea and spoke, \"Miss Rong's biological mother died early, and her biological father remarried. With no place for her at home, she has always lived with the Ji family. I treat Miss Rong as my own... own, own granddaughter. We are all family.\"","Old Madam Xie smiled and said, \"Your Ji family hasn't had a girl for several generations. Taking in a granddaughter is good; granddaughters are caring.\"","She suddenly sighed. \"Back then, when my sister was pregnant, she loved eating the spicy radish and spicy tofu I made the most. We thought it would be a daughter, but unexpectedly it was a son. That boy also loves spicy radish. Oh right, brother-in-law loves it too, doesn't he? It just so happens I'm in the mood today, so let me cook a dish for brother-in-law.\"","Old Master Ji hurriedly said, \"You are a guest, there's no need for you to cook...\"","However, Old Madam Xie had already rolled up her sleeves and walked into the kitchen.","Rong Yu looked up and glanced over.","This old madam might have done these things in her youth, but after decades of living a pampered life, she probably wasn't very good at it anymore. Even so, the elderly lady insisted on cooking, with a group of servants waiting on her from the side.","Rong Yu turned her eyes. \"A-Yan.\"","Ji Yanting walked over. \"Please give your orders, Great-Grandma.\"","\"Go investigate.\" Rong Yu tapped her finger. \"What exactly has happened to the Xie family?\"","For an arrogant noblewoman to lower her posture to this extent, something major must have absolutely happened.","Dinner was soon ready, and a dish of spicy radish appeared very abruptly on the dining table.","Ji Mohan was someone who didn't quite understand the ways of the world. He picked up a piece with his chopsticks, and as soon as he put it in his mouth, he spat it out, his face scrunching up. \"Why does the taste seem a bit weird...\"","Old Madam Xie looked embarrassed. \"I put a bit too much soy sauce, but it's fine, it's edible. It's just right for recalling past bitterness and appreciating present sweetness.\"","Old Master Ji chewed the radish with a crunching sound. \"Delicious, truly delicious. Mo... my, just an exclamation, don't mind it. Miss Rong, you should have some too.\"","Rong Yu took a small bite. If the soy sauce and salt had been moderate, the taste would actually be quite okay.","After dinner ended, Rong Yu didn't disturb the two of them catching up. She took her phone and went to the pavilion in the garden, eating fruit while scrolling through the news on her phone.","She happened to come across a news article about astronauts. Two astronauts from the Lighthouse Nation were actually stranded in space for several months. She simply couldn't believe that in this day and age, such a thing could happen, and moreover, it happened to the superpower Lighthouse Nation...","If they could just leave living people in space, who knows how much garbage they had thrown out there.","She was reading with great interest.","\"Mom.\"","Her elderly son leaned over.","Rong Yu turned off her phone and turned her head. \"What's wrong?\"","\"Um, it's just...\" Old Master Ji scratched his head. \"Mom, Xiaohui came over today because she still wants to ask me for a favor. She used to be very proud, so lowering herself to borrow money is a particularly difficult thing for her to do. Since she opened her mouth to ask, I feel too embarrassed to refuse.\"","Rong Yu asked, \"How much does she want to borrow?\"","Old Master Ji held up both hands. \"One billion.\"","Rong Yu frowned. \"Did you ask her why she needs to borrow so much money?\"","\"Something happened to the Xie family. I couldn't really ask about the specifics, afraid of embarrassing her.\" Old Master Ji sighed. \"Lending out a billion should be able to solve the Xie family's troubles. Once she catches her breath, she will slowly pay off this debt.\"","\"A billion probably isn't enough.\" Ji Yanting walked into the pavilion. \"Old Master, the incident with the Xie family is no ordinary matter.\"","He threw a stack of documents onto the table.","Old Master Ji quickly picked them up to look.","As he saw the contents of the files, the elderly man's eyes widened more and more.","Rong Yu saw them too.","Illegal fundraising contracts, joint letters from victims, bank statements... Her brow immediately darkened. It turned out that Old Madam Xie's son had used the bait of high returns to illegally raise billions from the public. He had even forged government approval documents to lure a large number of ordinary citizens into the trap.","The matter could barely be covered up anymore.","Old Madam Xie spent almost every day running around, borrowing money to fill the massive hole.","Old Master Ji looked completely incredulous. \"This, this is impossible...\"","\"A Ponzi scheme,\" Ji Yanting said slowly. \"Using new investors' money to pay interest to older investors, creating the illusion of making money... Now the capital chain has broken, and the hole can't be filled. All the fixed assets of the Xie Group have been mortgaged, but it still can't contain the fire. Once this blows up, the several heads of the Xie family will all have to go to prison.\"","Having navigated the ups and downs of the business world for many years, Old Master Ji naturally knew how serious this matter was. His personality felt as if it had been torn in half.","One side said he should help; after all, she was the biological younger sister of his beloved wife, and she had once extended a helping hand to the Ji family.","The other side said he couldn't help; this was a crime. Once he helped, he would be aiding and abetting evil..."]},{"number":291,"title":"Chapter 291: When involved with family children, it's hard for anyone to see reason.","paragraphs":["Rong Yu sighed.","Her Yingbao, inherently kind, even after decades of deception in the business world, still retained a pure goodness in his bones, let alone when facing his sister-in-law with whom he once had a close relationship.","She spoke slowly, \"Yingbao, this matter cannot be solved just by you lending them money.\"","\"Last time you lent them five hundred million, this time a billion, and tomorrow? Another two billion?\"","\"What the Xie family swindled was pension money, life-saving money, and hard-earned money! Those people crying and howling on their knees at the Xie family's door, those victims who jumped off buildings because their families were destroyed—are their lives not lives?\"","\"If you help the Xie family escape legal sanctions today, tomorrow, the century-old reputation of the Ji family will turn into being an accomplice sheltering criminals, a co-conspirator indulging evil deeds, and an executioner trampling on justice!\"","\"By the time Old Madam Xie drags the entire Ji family down with her, by the time the Securities Regulatory Commission seals the group's accounts, and by the time the police come to the old mansion to take you away for questioning, it will be too late.\"","Old Master Ji was stunned.","He was about to say something.","Turning his head, he saw Old Madam Xie standing there at some unknown point. Her silver hair was combed meticulously, and her dark qipao made her complexion look even gloomier.","Gritting her teeth, her voice trembled, \"Brother-in-law, even if she is your biological granddaughter related by blood, she shouldn't have the right to interfere in matters between elders, should she?\"","Old Master Ji slowly let out a heavy breath. \"Miss Rong is not wrong. Our Ji family cannot intervene in this matter concerning the Xie family.\"","Old Madam Xie's face turned ashen. \"Brother-in-law, when my sister passed away back then, her dying wish was for you to take good care of me. For so many years, I have never asked anything of you. This is the only time, and the last time. If you help the Xie family overcome this crisis, the Xie family will definitely repay your kindness ten or a hundred times over in the future. I...\"","\"Great-Aunt!\" Ji Yanting interrupted her. \"This is a crime. Surrendering to the authorities in time is the only way to help the Xie family and those victims.\"","Old Master Ji nodded. \"Xiaohui, a mistake is a mistake. Facing the problem head-on and accepting the trial is the only way.\"","\"Good, good, good!\" Old Madam Xie clutched her chest. \"I understand.\"","She turned around and staggered outward. Her personal assistant hurriedly supported her out the door and into the car, quickly disappearing from the villa's main gate.","Old Master Ji remained silent for a good while before his hoarse voice sounded, \"When she was young, although she was competitive and strong-willed, she was also reasonable. How did she become...\"","\"When it comes to the children of the family, it is hard for anyone to remain reasonable,\" Rong Yu said softly. \"You have already done what you can. What happens next depends on Old Madam Xie's own choice.\"","The five hundred million the Ji family had given previously was not a small amount; they couldn't risk the entire Ji family for this.","Old Master Ji nodded gloomily.","That night, while scrolling through the news, Rong Yu saw that the Xie Group's Ponzi scheme had been exposed to the public. Old Madam Xie's son and daughter-in-law were both taken away, and the Xie family residence was sealed...","Old Master Ji whispered, \"Mom, the Ji family still has a few properties in the capital. I want to offer one to Xiaohui to stay in temporarily. Would that be alright?\"","Rong Yu nodded. \"Just handle it as you see fit.\"","The next morning.","Ji Yanting drove, taking Rong Yu to meet the songwriter, Qi Su.","Also present was the director of this mainstream movie, surnamed Fang. She was a female director who had collaborated with Ji Yanting on a creative film. Director Fang won the Best Director award because of it, and Ji Yanting won Best Actor. The two of them had achieved mutual success and had a close relationship.","\"Yan Ting, it's been a long time. It's too hard to see you nowadays.\" Director Fang walked over in her high heels and shook his hand. \"If it weren't for temporarily adding a few scenes for you, I wouldn't know when I'd see you. Are you planning to retire from the entertainment circle?\"","Ji Yanting replied, \"I have a family company to manage, so I'll gradually retire from the circle in the future. Oh, by the way, let me introduce you, Director Fang. This is Rong Yu.\"","Director Fang looked at Rong Yu with great appreciation. \"When you participated in the talent show last year, I noticed you. At that time, I even wanted you to play a role in my movie, but I heard you weren't planning to act, so I dropped the idea. Singing is even better; I really like your voice.\"","Rong Yu smiled and said, \"As long as Director Fang doesn't mind that I'm a newcomer.\"","\"Come on, let's go inside to talk.\" Director Fang led them inside and called out, \"Qi Su, come here. The person I found for you has arrived.\"","A young man around thirty years old walked towards them. He was wearing a black short-sleeved shirt, knee-length shorts, and flip-flops. His hair was messy, making him look exactly like a creative type.","He had probably stayed up all night, as his complexion was not very good. Upon seeing Rong Yu, he frowned. \"Director Fang, this song is the movie's theme song, praising the builders of the motherland over the past seventy years. It needs a voice that can carry the weight of history. She is too young; it's not very suitable.\"","Rong Yu spoke up, \"Teacher Qi Su, how do you know I'm not suitable without giving it a try?\"","Qi Su twitched the corners of his lips. \"Since Miss Rong is so confident, you must have made ample preparations in advance. Then let's sing a section first. Go into the recording studio, and I'll raise the key for you to better suit your vocal range.\"","Ji Yanting knew it was Rong Yu's first time in a recording studio, so he went in with her and helped her put on the headset.","Qi Su glanced at them, a mocking smile appearing on his lips.","So she was someone relying on connections.","She got the singing rights to this song by leveraging the connections of the top-tier star, Ji Yanting.","He lowered his head and began tuning.","Ji Yanting's brows immediately furrowed.","He was an actor and also a singer. Although not a singer-songwriter, he was no stranger to this field. He could clearly hear that Qi Su had raised the pitch by at least three degrees, needlessly pushing the difficulty to the absolute peak.","\"Wait.\"","Just as Ji Yanting spoke, he was stopped by Rong Yu.","She looked up at the control room on the other side of the glass. Qi Su was looking at her with a half-smile.","She smiled back.","Back in the day, she had studied folk vocal music. The techniques of sinking the breath to the dantian and projecting the voice to the crown had long tempered her vocal range to be both wide and stable.","She closed her eyes.","The prelude flowed by. At the moment the first note was about to arrive, she adjusted her breathing.","\"When the years carve rings into the bricks and tiles...\"","The clear and translucent high notes pierced the silence like a ray of light, causing everyone in the control room to suddenly sit up straight.","Qi Su's expression froze.","He hadn't expected that Rong Yu's voice wouldn't tremble at all. Instead, in this deliberately raised vocal range, she displayed an astonishingly stunning texture.","Rong Yu was completely immersed in the music.","Her voice was very pure, soaring freely in the high-pitch areas that ordinary people found hard to reach, yet without losing its sense of weight.","When singing the last line, she even improvised a melodious portamento, adding a touch of moving narrative feeling to the originally solemn melody.","As the final note faded away, the recording studio was dead silent.","Rong Yu opened her eyes and saw that everyone in the control room was standing.","Qi Su's face was extremely ugly.","Ji Yanting was the first to applaud. Immediately after, the others followed suit, clapping as if waking from a dream.","\"That was fantastic!\" Director Fang's face was full of pleasant surprise. \"This is exactly the feeling I want—it has both height and warmth.\"","She grabbed Rong Yu's hand in excitement. \"Rong Yu, this song is yours to sing.\"","Qi Su's expression was incredibly sour. \"Director Fang, this was only a test run. We need to consider a lot of factors for the official recording...\"","\"What is there to consider?\" Director Fang replied with a smile. \"Rong Yu's emotion, technique, and vocal tone are all spot on. Furthermore, to be able to sing so perfectly on the higher key you set leaves absolutely no doubt about his talent.\"","Qi Su fell silent, unable to argue further.","Director Fang patted Rong Yu on the shoulder. \"Then it is settled. Come in at nine tomorrow morning for the official recording.\"","\"Director Fang,\" Rong Yu spoke up, voicing his doubts. \"The lyrics of the entire song flow as smoothly as running water. However, the melody, especially the way the vocal transition is handled right here at the beginning, feels a bit disjointed from the artistic mood of the rest of the track.\""]},{"number":292,"title":"Chapter 292: Idle time is idle time; a good curse clears the mind.","paragraphs":["Rong Yu's words instantly plunged the recording studio into silence.","Qi Su laughed out of anger, \"I've been writing songs for thirty years, and it's not the place of a newcomer to dictate what I should do.\"","Ji Yanting looked at the lyrics and suddenly paused, \"It does seem... a bit abrupt.\"","\"What do you know?\" Qi Su's face darkened. \"This is an artistic treatment. This kind of contrast effect is exactly what I want.\"","Rong Yu spoke calmly, \"Teacher Qi Su, I don't mean to question your creative ability. The lyrics are great, and the melody is also wonderful, but if we switch to a pentatonic scale modulation, plus... perhaps it would better reflect the sense of historical weight.\"","In the recording studio, several professionals also began to express their opinions.","\"Indeed, a pentatonic scale would flow better.\"","\"When we were cutting the record earlier, I felt something was a bit off. Now that it's pointed out, it all makes sense.\"","\"This main theme deserves to be more perfect.\"","Qi Su's face was as black as the bottom of a pot. \"This is the blood, sweat, and tears of my creation. Director Fang, since Miss Rong doesn't agree with this song, I suggest we find someone else.\"","\"The copyright of this song currently belongs to the film production,\" Director Fang paused and said. \"How about this, I'll invite Professor Wang from the Central Conservatory of Music and Mr. Li from the Composers Association to take a look tonight.\"","Ji Yanting still had to stay to shoot his final few scenes.","Embracing the mindset of \"since I'm already here, it won't hurt to watch,\" Rong Yu followed him into the soundstage.","She sat next to the director, watching Ji Yanting act.","Being stared at by two large, piercing eyes, Ji Yanting's pressure instantly spiked.","In the past, it might have taken several takes to pass, but with Great-Grandma holding down the fort, he passed everything in one take. Before the sky even turned dark, the day's tasks were completed.","\"Great-Grandma, is filming interesting?\" he asked. \"Do you want me to recommend a role for you?\"","Rong Yu quickly shook her head, \"Watching you act is quite interesting, but doing it myself would be a different story.\"","Singing was her hobby.","But acting was not.","Taking a look to satisfy her curiosity and knowing what it was all about was enough.","As soon as the two walked out of the set, Ji Yanting's phone rang. From far away, Rong Yu could hear her old son's booming voice: \"Lao Er, your Great-Grandma went out with you to your comfort zone, surrounded by people you know. How could she still get ambushed by someone? How are you handling things!\"","Ji Yanting looked bewildered: \"What happened?\"","Old Master Ji said angrily, \"Can't you look at your phone? I'm so mad! I don't have time to argue with you, I'm going to go scold some people!\"","Rong Yu got into the car, took out her phone, opened Weibo, and saw her name trending.","Number one trending topic on Weibo:","#Rong Yu Questions Genius Creator#","An audio recording had been maliciously edited and was going viral.","\"The lyrics of the whole song flow like water, but the melody, especially here at the beginning... is somewhat disjointed.\"","Qi Su's angry voice was amplified: \"What do you know? This is artistic treatment!\"","And Rong Yu's subsequent professional explanation was completely cut out, leaving only the clip of her supposedly dictating things.","The comment section exploded.","\"Hilarious. Does a newly debuted rookie have the right to question Qi Su? Does she know who Qi Su is? He wrote a song at sixteen that became a hit all over Asia. A true genius!\"","\"No works of her own, yet she's bossing people around? Who picked her?\"","\"I heard she only got this song through Ji Yanting's connections. Is she getting a big head now?\"","\"Isn't this an insult to the main theme works?\"","\"I suggest the motherland takes the lead in banning this problematic artist...\"","\"...\"","Soon, the hashtag #Rong Yu Get Out Of The Music Industry# was pushed to the trending list.","Those people had nowhere to vent their anger, so they flooded into Rong Ruoyao's Weibo. Her Weibo was instantly swamped with tens of thousands of insults, and her direct messages were full of vicious curses.","Rong Ruoyao finished shooting a commercial, and when she saw the messages on her phone, she was dumbfounded.","\"Mom, I'm getting cursed to death.\" She irritably pulled off her earphones. \"Every time something happens to her, I get dragged down and scolded too.\"","Shen Lin spoke earnestly, \"But, every time public opinion is extremely unfavorable to her, she always manages to turn the tide against the wind. Then, a large group of people who scolded you will come to apologize, thereby turning into your fans. You have to be able to withstand the scolding to be qualified to ride on the coattails of her popularity. Do I still need to teach you such a simple logic?\"","Rong Ruoyao pursed her lips: \"When will the news of my admission by the Jinghua University admissions office be released? I want to attract fans on my own.\"","\"What's the rush? Wait until school starts, and fans will naturally bump into you and release the news,\" Shen Lin guided her. \"You and Rong Yu are sisters. The haters have already cursed their way to your page. You are usually quite active on Weibo; you could post something right now, what do you think?\"","Rong Ruoyao didn't want to post anything.","However, she understood Rong Yu very well. A person with her personality would never inexplicably dictate to others.","There would definitely be a plot twist to this matter.","She threw her phone to Shen Lin: \"Mom, you post it. Post whatever you want.\"","Shen Lin shook her head: \"I can't be by your side forever. You have to learn to handle these things yourself.\"","Rong Ruoyao had no choice.","She thought hard for a long time and posted a Weibo: \"My sister respects academics and respects music. To the person who maliciously edited the audio, don't you have a guilty conscience?\"","\"Your sister's singing skills are just so-so, and so are yours. Don't come here and embarrass yourself too!\"","\"Daring to indiscriminately change a main theme song. Do people like you and your sister, who don't respect originality, deserve to sing a song dedicated to the motherland?\"","\"The two Rong sisters should both get out of the entertainment circle...\"","Someone even released the demo of the song for the whole internet to appreciate, degrading Rong Yu beyond belief.","The public opinion on the internet intensified.","When Rong Yu returned home, Old Master Ji and Butler Yu were sitting on the sofa, each holding five phones, frantically arguing with the haters.","\"Yingbao,\" she walked over and said helplessly, \"Tomorrow we will release the two audio tracks, and the audience will be able to distinguish which one is better for themselves. The public opinion will defeat itself. Why are you in such a frantic rush?\"","Old Master Ji scratched his head: \"I'm idle anyway. Scolding them makes me feel refreshed. Don't you agree, Old Yu?\"","Old Yu's head felt like it was splitting in two.","He originally didn't even know how to type using Pinyin, but he had been forced to train into an octopus tentacle monster, able to curse out three trolls in a minute.","There were too many haters; he couldn't scold them all.","He quickly put down his phone and found a random excuse: \"Miss Rong, I'll go over there and see if the sun has set yet.\"","Old Master Ji: \"...\"","Rong Yu took away his phones: \"Let me teach you how to check who released the recording.\"","She opened her laptop, logged into Weibo, and brought up the developer mode. Lines of code scrolled rapidly in the black window.","\"Yingbao, look here,\" she tried to use simple language. \"Every audio file has a unique digital fingerprint, just like human DNA.\"","She typed a few commands and brought up an IP address tracking map. A red line started from the Weibo server, passed through three jump nodes, and finally stopped at a familiar coordinate.","Ji Yanting frowned: \"Isn't this the place we went to today?\"","Rong Yu brought up a background log: \"Now let's check the device connection records at this specific time.\"","The screen displayed the MAC addresses of all the devices connected to the recording studio's network that day. Exactly five minutes before the recording was leaked, one of these devices had uploaded an audio file using a personal hotspot.","Elder Ji's eyes widened. \"It was Qi Su! He secretly recorded it on his own phone, edited it, and then uploaded it. Mom, you are incredible!\"","Rong Yu's voice was calm and indifferent. \"I pointed out his flaws, and he flew into a humiliated rage. That is why he launched this public smear campaign. His petty character is entirely unworthy of his reputation as a genius creator.\""]},{"number":293,"title":"Chapter 293: No wonder he always likes to mentor newcomers.","paragraphs":["Rong Yu's phone kept buzzing with notifications.","She picked it up and opened the screen, only to see that her former talent show group chat had blown up.","The few of them who were close had created a private group chat. It included Rong Yu, Su Tian, Li Ying'er, Tian Tian... eight girls in total.","\"Why is the song Qi Su wrote so similar to Tian Tian's lyric-writing style?\"","\"Tian Tian loves writing lyrics and has a lyric notebook. I remember most of her work is in this exact style.\"","\"Although I don't want to think in that direction, how could anyone who clashes with Sister Yu be a good person? Just in case, right?\"","\"Tian Tian, come out quickly! What are you doing? Come out!\"","Tian Tian: \"I just looked at Qi Su's composition. It's not just like my style; it is exactly the same as the song I wrote... Three months ago, I went to Qi Su's studio for an interview. The HR department asked me to write lyrics on the spot, and this is the one I wrote. At the time, the examiner's evaluation was that it had a fake premise, was pretentious, and lacked substance... Three months later, the lyrics that were harshly criticized have actually become Qi Su's proudest work.\"","Everyone in the group chat exploded in an uproar.","\"Isn't he supposed to be a genius creator? How could he plagiarize!\"","\"Could it be that he built his reputation as a genius entirely by copying others' works?\"","\"This guy is really worth digging into. Sisters, I'll go do some scouting first.\"","Rong Yu: \"Tian Tian, can you produce any evidence on your end?\"","Tian Tian uploaded a picture. It was a handwritten lyric sheet she had taken a photo of during her interview at Qi Su's studio. The bottom right corner showed the timestamp and location.","Rong Yu saved the picture.","She opened the piece written by Qi Su.","And compared them.","Out of the three hundred and sixty-one words in the entire song, only a dozen or so were different.","This was absolutely blatant plagiarism.","Ji Yanting was so angry he laughed.","He had recommended that Great-Grandma sing this song for two reasons: first, it was a mainstream patriotic theme song; second, the creator was the genius Qi Su. He felt that only a song like this was worthy of Great-Grandma.","He never expected it to be such a piece of trash.","Would someone who plagiarizes lyrics also plagiarize the composition?","Ji Yanting walked into the study, put on his headphones, and began the work of comparing the tracks...","At eight-thirty in the morning, Rong Yu and Ji Yanting arrived at the recording studio. As they walked to the door, they saw a large group of people standing there, arguing about something.","Qi Su was the first to see her. \"Rong Yu is here.\"","The producer looked at Rong Yu critically. \"You're just in time. We're discussing the public relations risks associated with the theme song.\"","Several people nearby chimed in.","\"The movie is going in for censorship review next month, and right now the whole internet is blasting us for unprofessional casting.\"","\"If we insist on using Miss Rong, the estimated box office loss for the opening week during the National Day holiday will be at least a hundred million.\"","An investor spoke coldly, \"Replace her. I don't care about vocal skills or image. In short, a mainstream patriotic movie does not need a controversial artist.\"","Qi Su chimed in at the right moment, \"I recommend a female singer. She has been in the industry for over ten years, has a clean voice, and perfectly matches the vibe of this song. She will definitely be able to sing out the grand scale of a mainstream movie. Her name is...\"","Ji Yanting whispered, \"Great-Grandma, this female singer Qi Su is recommending is his college classmate. The two of them are living together, but they don't publicly acknowledge their relationship.\"","Rong Yu understood immediately.","It turned out he wanted to save this opportunity for his rumored girlfriend. So, no matter how she performed, Qi Su would always find a way to push her out.","She was just about to speak.","But Director Fang beat her to it, saying coldly, \"That audio clip on the internet was maliciously edited to amplify conflicts and deliberately start a war. There is absolutely nothing wrong with Rong Yu. I do not agree to replacing her!\"","The investors frowned. \"Her problem is that she loves trending on hot searches too much. This is a mainstream movie; trending frequently is not a good thing!\"","The cold wind from the air conditioner blew noisily.","Rong Yu stood in the center of the recording studio, her gaze slowly shifting from the investors to Qi Su's face.","She smiled. Her voice was very light, yet it made the entire room fall silent. \"Trending... indeed isn't a good thing. But the question is, is it me who likes to trend, or is there someone who insists on making me trend?\"","Her eyes locked straight onto Qi Su.","Qi Su's expression changed, and he glared at her. \"Rong Yu! What do you mean? You caused a controversy yourself, and now you want to shift the blame?\"","Rong Yu said calmly, \"Teacher Qi Su, the audio recording that caused the public uproar online was edited and uploaded by you. Yes or no?\"","Qi Su froze all over.","Before he could even open his mouth to retort.","Ji Yanting had already opened his laptop and pulled up the Weibo tracking path. The final result showed that the person who uploaded the recording was Qi Su.","A few young staff members began to whisper among themselves.","\"Teacher Qi Su actually secretly recorded and uploaded it. He's a genius creator, yet he would do something so low?\"","\"Just because he's a genius and can't accept being questioned, he maliciously edited it to get Rong Yu cursed at?\"","\"I really couldn't tell he was this kind of person...\"","Director Fang's face was full of disbelief. \"Qi Su, Rong Yu merely offered a small suggestion. Moreover, a professor from the Central Conservatory of Music also thought there was nothing wrong with Rong Yu's suggestion. As a creator, it's one thing not to humbly accept advice, but to maliciously edit this recording and upload it to the internet, causing a massive uproar... You really shouldn't have done this!\"","Qi Su's face turned from red to pale, and fine beads of sweat seeped out on his forehead. \"I, I just... accidentally clicked the wrong button.\"","\"Fine, let's say you clicked the wrong button,\" Rong Yu's voice remained clear and lucid. \"Then what about this? Did Teacher Qi Su make a mistake with this too?\"","She pulled out a document. \"This is the original work of rookie Tian Tian from her interview at Qi Su's studio three months ago. And this one is the lyrics Teacher Qi Su composed last month.\"","Director Fang took the two documents, his frown deepening.","The sound engineer couldn't help but lean over to look, exclaiming, \"This... this is almost exactly the same!\"","\"Tian Tian debuted through Ji Entertainment's talent show. Three months ago, she hadn't signed with any agency, so she went to interview at Qi Su's studio, hoping to get a training opportunity.\" Rong Yu's voice grew colder bit by bit. \"But Teacher Qi Su did not give her this opportunity. Instead, without her consent, he took her work. Taking without asking is stealing; it's plagiarism. Is this how the title of 'genius creator' came about?\"","Qi Su flew into a rage. \"Slander! This is naked slander!\"","\"Is that so?\" Rong Yu took out her phone. \"Everyone might as well listen to the voices on the internet.\"","Everyone present took out their phones and opened Weibo, only to see countless musicians speaking out.","Independent musician Xiaolin: \"I am Qi Su's junior. He used to guide me in music creation, but soon enough, my works would become his works. I cut ties with him three years ago, but I was a nobody and didn't dare to say anything publicly. Today, the opportunity has finally come.\"","Arranger Chengfeng: \"The work Qi Su released last year has an eighty percent similarity in composition style to one of my songs. I urge netizens to evaluate it.\"","Soloist Zhoushan: \"A heavy metal song of Qi Su's that became popular all over Asia five years ago shares a striking resemblance with an extremely niche Nordic song from ten years ago...\"","Online, countless newcomers spoke out. Their voices, like tiny streams converging into a mighty river, firmly dominated the top ten trending searches.","In the recording studio, the staff couldn't help but whisper among themselves.","\"No wonder he always liked giving pointers to the rookies.\"","\"No wonder his music style is so versatile. Turns out he was just copying a little from here and a little from there.\"","\"I can't believe he's that kind of person. It's terrifying.\"","\"...\""]},{"number":294,"title":"Chapter 294: Aren't you worried that some scandal might break out","paragraphs":["Qi Su was asked to leave. Standing under the blazing sun, he broke out in a cold sweat.","His mind was still in a daze.","When he was sixteen, he had followed his father to a recording studio and picked up a discarded draft that someone else didn't want. He revised it, refined it continually, and after releasing it, shot to fame overnight. This laid the foundation for his reputation as a genius creator.","Having tasted the sweetness of success, he never looked back and continued down this path.","In the past, it wasn't that no one had publicly accused him of plagiarism on Weibo. However, with his massive fanbase and high web traffic, and the accusers being nothing more than obscure newcomers, these voices of dissent vanished before they could even make the news.","He had thought he could continue sailing smoothly like this forever.","Today's incident struck him like a heavy blow to the head, leaving him with no time to even react.","Just then, his manager called, sounding grave. \"Brother Qi, the company just received a lawyer's letter from the production crew. They are demanding the termination of our collaboration and compensation for copyright losses.\"","\"Furthermore, those newcomer composers and musicians have taken the company to court on the grounds of infringement.\"","\"And the Music Association has sent a letter stating they will launch an investigation into all the musical works produced by Qi Su's studio...\"","Qi Su's fingers froze in mid-air, his pupils shrinking drastically.","At the main entrance, he saw Director Fang actually walking Rong Yu out in person. \"I have complete faith in the person you recommended. Once my assistant contacts Tian Tian and finalizes the lyrics, you can come to the recording studio for the official recording.\"","Rong Yu smiled and nodded.","Tian Tian also spoke out on Weibo.","After debuting through a talent show last year, she hadn't signed with an agency in time, causing her popularity to plummet until she slowly faded into obscurity.","After she posted the Weibo about the lyrics, her direct messages instantly blew up.","It was Qi Su's die-hard fans.","Even though Qi Su's reputation was currently in ruins, his fans wouldn't just abandon him over some public opinion. Instead, they became even more aggressive, hurling insults at the music industry newcomers who had stepped forward.","\"The matter hasn't even been concluded yet, and so many people are coming out to clout-chase. Are they all crazy for fame?\"","\"Does a D-lister like Tian Tian even deserve to leech off Teacher Qi's fame? How shameless!\"","\"She actually dares to claim her elementary-school-level lyrics were plagiarized? Even Qi Su's casual scribbles are ten thousand times better than hers!\"","\"...\"","Tian Tian's eyes were a little red.","Just this small amount of abuse was almost too much for her to bear.","Meanwhile, Rong Yu had endured constant questioning and doubt ever since her debut. Just how strong of a heart did she need to have to ignore all these remarks?","Tian Tian turned off her phone.","Right then, her phone rang. She glanced at it; it was her manager calling.","This was the manager she had signed with this year. She heard that her manager used to represent the great Best Actor, Yan Ting. After her contract with Yan Ting expired, she struck out on her own to establish a talent agency. Although the company had only been established for a little over three months and was just starting, Qiu Sang's rich experience had already earned the agency quite a reputation in the industry.","Qiu Sang offered very generous terms, giving even newcomers a fifty-fifty split. In this industry, that was almost non-existent, yet Qiu Sang actually did it.","Being able to sign with Qiu Sang was a stroke of luck for her.","\"Tian Tian, wonderful news!\" Qiu Sang's voice came through the phone. \"Just now, the staff of that mainstream production contacted me. They specifically asked for you to be in charge of optimizing the lyrics, and the remuneration will be paid according to B-list standards!\"","Tian Tian was completely stunned. \"What?\"","\"You heard me right,\" Qiu Sang paused and said. \"If I'm not mistaken, it should be Miss Rong, Rong Yu, who recommended you to the director.\"","Tian Tian's eyes instantly welled up with tears. \"Can I... can I really meet Sister Yu's expectations?\"","\"You are already excellent,\" Qiu Sang said gently. \"Cheer up and show off your talents tomorrow. Once this job is over, we will treat Miss Rong to a meal.\"","Working with a veteran composer, Tian Tian revised the lyrics and rearranged the music, elevating the entire song to another level. Rong Yu spent a day recording the track, and with that, the job was considered complete.","It wasn't until that evening that Rong Yu found out Tian Tian's manager was actually Qiu Sang.","It had been over half a year since she last saw Qiu Sang. Back then, Qiu Sang was melancholic, lost, helpless, and panic-stricken...","But now, she exuded a gentle aura. Wearing a sharply tailored beige suit without any superfluous decorations, she looked exceptionally capable and professional.","\"Miss Rong.\" Qiu Sang greeted Rong Yu first before looking at Ji Yanting beside her. \"Yan Ting, long time no see.\"","Her voice was very calm, devoid of any inappropriate emotions.","Ji Yanting lowered his long eyelashes slightly and gave a gentle nod. \"Qiu Sang.\"","Qiu Sang smiled and said, \"I've booked a table across the street. If you don't mind, let's have a meal together.\"","Ji Yanting paused for a moment. \"Alright.\"","During the meal, Qiu Sang chatted a bit about the past.","The rapist who had brought disaster upon her was sentenced to nine years in prison for his combined crimes of rape and extortion.","Her son, Wei Xu, was kept by her side and was attending junior high school in the capital.","The mother and son never brought up the past and were able to get along peacefully.","After the meal ended and they got into the car, Rong Yu asked Ji Yanting, \"A-Yan, have you let it go?\"","\"She has completely walked out of the gloom, so of course I've let it go too,\" Ji Yanting replied, his expression relaxed and at ease. \"She will get better and better, and so will I.\"","The car drove back to the villa.","As soon as Rong Yu walked through the front door, she saw an uninvited guest sitting on the sofa.","Ji Yanting spoke up to greet her, \"Great-Aunt.\"","Old Madam Xie sat on the sofa with a cup of tea in her hand. She glanced at Rong Yu, her gaze very indifferent.","Old Master Ji coughed and walked over to Rong Yu, whispering, \"Something happened to the Xie family, and Xiaohui is feeling depressed. She wanted to stay here for a few days to clear her mind. Mom, do you think that's okay?\"","Rong Yu met Old Madam Xie's gaze.","The other party's aged eyes carried scrutiny as well as dissatisfaction.","If she refused to let Old Madam Xie stay, given Yingbao's personality, he would only worry about her more. They might even meet privately and cause trouble in secret. It was really better to keep her right under their noses.","She smiled and said, \"Of course.\"","Old Master Ji let out a massive sigh of relief.","If Mom had refused, he really wouldn't have known what to do.","He called out loudly, \"Old Yu, arrange for the servants to tidy up the bedroom on the second floor.\"","\"Thank you, Brother-in-law,\" Old Madam Xie lowered her eyes. \"Once there is news from the court, I will move out. I won't bother you for too long.\"","Old Master Ji said, \"How could it be a bother? We are all family. You can stay for as long as you like.\"","Rong Yu looked helplessly at her elderly son.","At his advanced age, how could he still be so naive?","She took a step, went upstairs, and entered her room.","Sitting on the sofa, Old Madam Xie immediately narrowed her eyes.","Wasn't that room on the second floor the master bedroom?","A girl with no blood relation is staying in the largest and best room in the entire villa?","Isn't that a bit too absurd?","\"Brother-in-law,\" Old Madam Xie spoke slowly. \"There is something I don't know if I should say.\"","Old Master Ji scratched his head. \"Xiaohui, how about you just don't say it then.\"","\"Even if it offends you, brother-in-law, I still have to say what needs to be said.\" Old Madam Xie glanced upstairs. \"The Ji family only has boys, and they are all single. With so many grown men living under the same roof as an eighteen-year-old girl, brother-in-law, aren't you worried about a scandal breaking out?\"","Old Master Ji didn't understand. \"What scandal?\"","Old Madam Xie looked up at him. \"She is just an outsider after all. What if she wants to become the young mistress of the Ji family?\"","\"How could that be!\" Old Master Ji stood up abruptly. Suppressing his anger, he enunciated every word. \"Xiaohui, Rong Yu is not the kind of person you think she is. She, she... Anyway, she is a member of the Ji family. It is impossible for any scandal to happen between family members!\"","Old Madam Xie frowned. \"Brother-in-law, how can you trust an outsider with a different surname so much? She...\"","\"Enough, Xiaohui, say no more.\" Old Master Ji pursed his lips. \"I never want to hear such words a second time!\"","He threw his hands down in frustration and walked away, going into his room and shutting the door behind him."]},{"number":295,"title":"Chapter 295: Why Are All of Ji's Shares Registered Under Rong Yu's Name","paragraphs":["Old Madam Xie's hand, holding the teacup, trembled slightly.","She had only reminded him out of the goodness of her heart, but her good intentions were treated like dirt.","She looked up just in time to see Ji Mohan returning from work.","\"Great-Aunt.\"","Ji Mohan greeted her and was about to head upstairs to his room.","But Old Madam Xie stopped him. \"Mo, come here and sit with me for a while.\"","Ji Mohan had no choice but to go over and sit down.","Seeing a small box in his hands, Old Madam Xie asked casually, \"What's that?\"","Ji Mohan replied, \"It's from a newly opened bakery that usually has a super long line every day. When I got off work today, there happened to be no one waiting, so I bought one. Great... Miss Rong should like it.\"","Old Madam Xie suddenly smiled. She looked at Ji Mohan and asked, \"Mo, do you like Miss Rong?\"","\"What?\" Ji Mohan was so startled he almost dropped the little cake in his hands. \"Great-Aunt, you've misunderstood. I don't like Miss Rong!\"","Old Madam Xie gave a knowing smile. \"The Ji family doesn't have any female elders to guide you, so it's normal for you to be confused about these things. Tell your Great-Aunt honestly, when did you start liking Miss Rong?\"","\"I don't! I really don't!\" Ji Mohan was going crazy. \"Great-Aunt, please don't talk nonsense. It wouldn't be good if someone heard you. I respect and admire Miss Rong; it has absolutely nothing to do with romantic feelings. I'm not talking about this anymore, I'm leaving!\"","He turned around and quickly ran upstairs.","Old Madam Xie sat in the living room for quite a while. It wasn't until her assistant walked in that she stood up. \"How is it?\"","The assistant shook his head. \"Old Madam, the situation is very bad. Because the amount of money involved is massive, and a victim jumped to their death over it, I'm afraid sir might be sentenced to life imprisonment...\"","Old Madam Xie's head spun, and she almost fainted.","In her entire life, she only had this one son. All her heart and soul were devoted to him. If her son was sentenced to life, she wouldn't want to live anymore.","The assistant said in a low voice, \"If we can fill the financial hole, appease the victims, and pull some strings behind the scenes, we might be able to reduce the life sentence to about three years.\"","Old Madam Xie stayed awake all night.","Early the next morning, Old Master Ji had just gotten up and was having breakfast with Rong Yu. A servant walked over and said, \"Old Madam Xie is ill. She just coughed up blood. Would you like to go up and see her, Old Master Ji?\"","Old Master Ji dropped his chopsticks and ran upstairs. Pushing the door open, he saw Old Madam Xie lying there, looking extremely haggard. He quickly ordered, \"Old Yu, hurry and arrange a car to take her to the hospital...\"","\"Going to the hospital is useless. This is an illness of the heart,\" Old Madam Xie coughed. \"Brother-in-law, as long as my son is locked up in a prison cell, my illness will never be cured.\"","Old Master Ji was silent for a moment before saying, \"He committed a major crime and won't be getting out anytime soon. You shouldn't torture yourself like this.\"","\"Cough, cough, cough...\"","Old Madam Xie coughed violently, as if she were going to cough her lungs out.","She knew that her brother-in-law was susceptible to persuasion but not coercion. As long as she pretended to be sick and pitiful, taking this guilt trip to the extreme, he would definitely soften his heart.","\"Since you don't want to go to the hospital, I'll have the private doctor come over,\" Old Master Ji looked away. \"I have things to do, so I won't stay here and disturb your rest.\"","He walked downstairs, looking deeply troubled.","Rong Yu glanced at him. \"What's wrong, Yingbao?\"","\"Mom, sigh... I...\" Old Master Ji sighed. \"I don't know what I can do to make Xiaohui feel less pain.\"","Rong Yu spoke up, \"Those victims whose families were ruined because of the Xie family are also in pain.\"","Old Master Ji fell silent.","\"Let's go. We should go out for a stroll,\" Rong Yu stood up. \"A-Yan has arranged a trip to the theater. Let's go listen to some opera and relax.\"","The mother and son went out together.","Old Madam Xie leaned against the balcony, perfectly positioned to see Old Master Ji carrying Rong Yu's bag and opening the car door for her.","Her eyes darkened.","Last time, it was this girl's words that made her brother-in-law unwilling to help the Xie family.","Who exactly was this girl named Rong Yu?","She dialed her assistant's number. \"Investigate Rong Yu thoroughly, especially her relationship with the Ji family.\"","Rong Yu took her elderly son out to watch an opera and they had dinner while they were out, before taking a car back home.","As soon as they entered the house, Butler Yu walked over and said in a low voice, \"Old Master Ji, Old Madam Xie said she has something very important to discuss with you. She asked that you please go to her room.\"","Old Master Ji felt a bit reluctant.","He could already guess what Xiaohui was going to say; it was nothing more than hoping he could help the Xie family.","If it were anything else, he would let it go.","But this was a major criminal case that violated the law. He didn't want to help, nor did he have the ability to do so.","He sighed and reluctantly went upstairs.","\"Brother-in-law,\" Old Madam Xie sat on the sofa by the bed, her face extremely grim. With a backhand toss, she threw a stack of documents onto the table. \"Why are all the shares of the Ji Group under Rong Yu's name? Brother-in-law, don't you think you owe me an explanation?\"","Old Master Ji looked incredulous. \"Xiaohui, you actually investigated the Ji family?\"","Just investigating his mother wouldn't yield any information because his mother had already been integrated into a confidential national unit, making her files classified.","One had to specifically investigate the Ji Group. Only by starting from there could one discover that the current largest shareholder and chairman of the Ji Group was Rong Yu.","There were too many people with the same first and last name; it was hard for anyone to make the connection unless they knew Rong Yu personally.","\"Brother-in-law, have you been bewitched by that little girl? You actually transferred all the shares to her name. Are you crazy?\" Old Madam Xie's anger rushed straight to her head. \"The Ji Group also contains my sister's blood, sweat, and tears. By giving it all to an outsider, how can you face my sister's spirit in heaven!\"","Old Master Ji took a deep breath. \"I don't need to explain this matter to you.\"","\"Foolish, you're so foolish!\" Old Madam Xie clutched her chest. \"You'd rather give a massive fortune to an outsider than help the Xie family! When Yuan, A-Yan, and the others find out you've done such a ridiculous thing, they will definitely turn against you!\"","Ji Yanting had already appeared at the door of the room. He spoke in a calm voice, \"Miss Rong is the Old Master Ji's savior. Without Miss Rong, there would be no Old Master Ji. This was a unanimous decision made after an internal meeting of the Ji family. Everyone in the Ji family has no objections to this, and Great-Aunt shouldn't have any either.\"","\"Crazy, are you all crazy?\" Old Madam Xie widened her eyes. \"Do you know what transferring the shares to an outsider means? It means the Ji Group will change its surname. It means you all won't inherit anything in the future...\"","\"This is our Ji family's business,\" Old Master Ji said slowly. \"Xiaohui, I agreed to let you move in to give you peace of mind. If you are always going to obsess over these things, I will arrange for someone to send you back right now.\"","\"Pfft—\"","Old Madam Xie was so furious that her chest tightened, and she violently coughed up a mouthful of fresh blood."]},{"number":296,"title":"Chapter 296: Not Even a Chance to Compete for the Genius","paragraphs":["The private doctor came to the house and prescribed a large pile of medication for Old Madam Xie.","After taking her medicine, Old Madam Xie fell asleep.","Ji Yanting's brows furrowed tightly. \"Grandpa, Great-Aunt wants to control too much. I suggest we arrange a new place for her to live.\"","Old Master Ji glared at him. \"Your Great-Aunt is this sick, how can I be at ease letting her live alone?\"","\"That's true,\" Rong Yu said. \"A-Yan, for the next few days, try to push back all your work and just stay home to accompany Old Madam Xie.\"","Ji Yanting had recently been slowly withdrawing from the entertainment industry, so he didn't have much work on hand to begin with.","He understood Rong Yu's implied meaning and nodded. \"Don't worry, Great-Grandma, I understand.\"","The next day, Rong Yu was to attend a lecture.","The main speaker for this lecture was her teacher, Academician Yun Xiaoyuan.","She arrived at the venue more than half an hour early.","\"Xiao Yu.\" Yun Xiaoyuan walked toward her with a gentle expression. \"Let me tell you something. Didn't you apply for the Aerospace Engineering major at Huaqing University? After a comprehensive evaluation by several professors at Huaqing, they believe you have outstanding aptitude and recommended you to enter Huaqing's Tianxingjian Class. This is a special class dedicated to cultivating specialized talents for our country's scientific endeavors, which will fully utilize your strengths. What do you think?\"","Rong Yu smiled and said, \"I'll follow your arrangements, Professor.\"","Yun Xiaoyuan said, \"I am the Dean of the School of Mathematics at Huaqing University. I teach two classes a week—one for the mathematics department and one for the Tianxingjian Class. We'll have plenty of opportunities to see each other then. After school starts, just enjoy your college life first. Once you're a sophomore, I'll start bringing you into projects. You're still young, and youth is precious. Don't be in too much of a hurry to dedicate yourself to the country.\"","Rong Yu nodded.","\"Come, let me introduce you to another academician.\" Yun Xiaoyuan led her a few steps to the side and called out, \"Academician Liu.\"","Liu Jinyue was among the newest batch of academicians. Standing among a large group of big shots, he appeared very young. He said humbly, \"Academician Yun.\"","\"For this year's Tianxingjian Class at Huaqing, if I remember correctly, Academician Liu has taken on the physics teaching duties, right?\" Yun Xiaoyuan said with a smile. \"This student is named Rong Yu. She has been recommended for the Tianxingjian Class and is my student. I hope Academician Liu will look after her in the future.\"","Liu Jinyue naturally recognized Rong Yu.","Such a genius young girl was already quite famous within the academician circle.","But it was a pity.","He had been an academician for too short a time, so he didn't even have the chance to compete for such a genius.","Rong Yu reached out her hand. \"I look forward to your guidance in the future, Academician Liu.\"","\"Not at all.\" Liu Jinyue gently shook her hand and let go. \"I've merely walked a few more steps than you young kids. If my experience can help you avoid some detours, that would be my greatest achievement as a teacher.\"","Yun Xiaoyuan checked the time and said, \"I'm about to start my lecture. Xiao Yu, go help me organize my notes.\"","Rong Yu nodded and went over.","When Song Huai arrived at the venue, the first thing he saw was Rong Yu organizing documents by the podium.","She was dressed very simply in a white top, jeans, and a pair of little white shoes. She radiated youthfulness, making her particularly eye-catching in the crowd.","Song Huai was a bit surprised. How did Rong Yu manage to attend such a high-profile lecture?","He was able to come because his teacher, Academician Liu Jinyue, had given him an admission ticket. Ordinary people had no qualifications to enter at all.","He suddenly became very curious. Who exactly was Rong Yu's teacher?","Just as Rong Yu stepped down from the podium, Song Huai went up to greet her. \"Rong Yu, you're here too, you...\"","He had only spoken half his sentence.","When he was interrupted by a pleasantly surprised voice. \"Rong Yu, I knew you would come!\"","Rong Yu looked up and saw Sheng Ciyuan.","A smile appeared on her face. \"Ciyuan, long time no see. What have you been busy with during the summer vacation?\"","Song Huai was stunned.","Calling him Ciyuan so casually—since when did these two have such an intimate relationship?","Before he could figure it out, Rong Yu and Sheng Ciyuan had already taken their seats, chatting enthusiastically as if there was no one else around.","\"I've been busy with projects over the summer,\" Sheng Ciyuan said endlessly. \"Since my eldest brother has recovered, my youngest uncle took the opportunity to retire from the military. He was just coasting along in the army every day and couldn't get promoted, so it's good that he retired. With him retired, there's someone to help manage the Sheng family's business, and I can wholeheartedly devote myself to my studies.\"","Rong Yu smiled and said, \"Then congratulations.\"","\"My eldest brother is amazing,\" Sheng Ciyuan said with a proud face. \"He had just joined the military and immediately earned a first-class merit. My dad said that at this rate, my brother will be promoted very soon. Once his career is stable, he can consider marriage.\"","\"Oh right, my youngest uncle is finally getting married.\" He pulled Rong Yu closer to vent. \"When my uncle was young, he was a playboy who changed girlfriends every few days. He was the biggest headache for our Sheng family. In a flash, he's in his thirties and still had no prospects for marriage. My grandmother was going crazy with anxiety. Fortunately, things are finally settling down. Once the date is set, I'll send you an invitation. You definitely have to come to the Sheng family to drink to their happiness.\"","Rong Yu nodded and agreed.","The lecture soon began. Yun Xiaoyuan took the stage and started discussing the most cutting-edge mathematical research. Everyone present listened attentively. An hour and a half passed in a flash, and Rong Yu gained a lot from it.","\"Academician Yun is truly a leading authority in the field of mathematics. Listening to one of her lectures is better than studying for ten years.\" Sheng Ciyuan looked amazed. He closed his notebook and turned his head. \"It's only a ten-minute drive from this venue to my house. Rong Yu, why don't you come to my house for lunch? My grandmother has been talking about you for a long time. She even said that if I didn't have the ability to invite you over, my room would belong to Pangpang in the future. Speaking of Pangpang, that little guy has been really pitiful lately. It used to live a comfortable life with my brother accompanying it every day. Now that it's missing a companion, it almost seems depressed.\"","Rong Yu was just about to refuse.","When she saw Yun Xiaoyuan walking toward her with four or five other academicians.","Her eyelid couldn't help but twitch.","She could already guess that Academician Yun definitely wanted to take her out to eat with a large group of academicians and professors.","One could just imagine: during the New Year, a five- or six-year-old child at home would be forced by their elders to perform songs and dances, and be asked about their studies—what is one plus one, can you recite Ode to the Goose...","If she dined with her teacher, she would face the exact same predicament.","Rong Yu spoke up first, \"Teacher, I have something else to do, so I'll be leaving first. Excuse me.\"","Yun Xiaoyuan said to the people beside her with great regret, \"Then I can only let you witness my student's super-brain calculation abilities next time. She is no inferior to any computer.\"","Rong Yu: \"...\"","Fortunately, she had spoken fast.","After bidding farewell to everyone, she hurriedly left with Sheng Ciyuan.","Song Huai followed Liu Jinyue into a private room in the restaurant. He looked around the private room but didn't see Rong Yu.","He thought silently to himself that it seemed Rong Yu's teacher wasn't an academician after all; otherwise, she would have been able to come dine with the academicians. Such an occasion was considered the most high-end dinner gathering in the academic circle.","What a pity."]},{"number":297,"title":"Chapter 297: Don't you want to arrange a good marriage for Miss Rong","paragraphs":["Even though Sheng Ciyuan invited her earnestly, Rong Yu still refused. She really couldn't handle Old Madam Sheng's overwhelming enthusiasm.","When she returned home, she found unexpected guests. It was someone from the Xie family—Old Madam Xie's grandson, a man in his twenties named Xie Yajun.","Ji Yanting leaned close to Rong Yu's ear and whispered, \"Ever since he arrived, he's been asking me about Great-grandmother. He's up to no good.\"","\"If he doesn't stir up some trouble, how can I make your grandfather see the Xie family for who they really are?\" Rong Yu raised her eyes. \"Your grandfather is just too soft-hearted. He knows the Xie family harbors ill intentions, yet he keeps holding back and tolerating them. We need to cut the Gordian knot and make him see the truth.\"","Ji Yanting thoroughly agreed.","Old Master Ji was chatting with Xie Yajun. Seeing Rong Yu return, he stood up to introduce them. \"This is the youngest of the Xie family. Recently, Xie Yajun has been handling all of the Xie family's affairs.\"","Xie Yajun stood up and extended a hand to Rong Yu. \"Miss Rong, a pleasure to meet you.\"","Rong Yu smiled. \"Young Master Xie, please have a seat.\"","Taking advantage of the offer, Xie Yajun sat down right next to Rong Yu.","Old Master Ji raised an eyebrow.","Just a moment ago, he had been thinking that Xie Yajun was a promising young man for taking on the burden of the crumbling Xie family at such a young age.","But now, this punk was sitting next to his mother, with a look of interest in his eyes that only a man could understand, which thoroughly disgusted him.","He was just about to speak.","When Ji Yanting pulled him back. \"Old Master, I have something to discuss with you.\"","Old Master Ji was dragged into the study.","Ji Yanting didn't actually have much to say; he just casually mentioned some of Ji Entertainment's upcoming plans.","Old Master Ji scolded him in annoyance, \"You need to consult me for this trivial nonsense? Are you not weaned yet? If you really don't understand, call your older brother and ask him.\"","Ji Yanting: \"...\"","Who was the one clinging to Great-grandmother every day like an unweaned child...","Old Master Ji walked out of the study and saw that Rong Yu and Xie Yajun had actually gone to the garden together. The two were sitting in a pavilion, chatting happily about who knows what.","He took a step forward, wanting to go over and see.","\"Brother-in-law.\" Old Madam Xie came down from upstairs and stopped him. \"The two young people are chatting. Let's not join the fun as old folks.\"","Old Master Ji belatedly snapped back to his senses.","He stared intently at Old Madam Xie. \"Xiaohui, what exactly are you trying to do?\"","\"Nothing,\" Old Madam Xie sat on the sofa. \"Miss Rong is so outstanding. A good woman is sought after by ten thousand men; it's only natural for Xie Yajun to pursue her. Besides, since you value Miss Rong so much, brother-in-law, don't you want to choose a good marriage for her?\"","Old Master Ji was so angry he laughed. \"A good marriage? Xie Yajun is a good marriage?\"","This punk couldn't even compare to a single finger of Sheng Qingyan!","He would rather it be Sheng Qingyan!","However, turning his head, he saw that his mother, who was usually so aloof, was actually smiling so radiantly. She even reached out and adjusted Xie Yajun's collar.","He was completely dumbfounded.","Wait...","Who exactly did his mother like?","Wasn't she treating Sheng Qingyan exceptionally differently before?","How come she was lured away the moment she saw Xie Yajun?","Xie Yajun was ugly, short, and a bit chubby. He walked with his legs splayed out, looking completely frivolous. Was his mother blind?","\"Brother-in-law, look at how well-matched the two youngsters are,\" Old Madam Xie smiled faintly. \"Fate between people is sometimes just this wondrous. Back then, weren't you and my sister also struck by love at first sight?\"","Old Master Ji felt as uncomfortable as if he had swallowed a fly.","He stood up, flicked his sleeves, and went into his room.","Old Madam Xie leisurely drank her tea. After a good while, Xie Yajun came in looking smug. The grandmother and grandson went upstairs together and entered a room.","\"Grandma, that Miss Rong is way too easy to flirt with.\" Xie Yajun leaned back on the sofa, stroking his chin. \"On our very first meeting, she agreed to go out to the movies with me. The movie starts at ten o'clock tonight, and it will be past midnight when it ends. At that time, I'll just book a hotel room, and she probably won't refuse too much. Once the deed is done, I'll slowly coax her into transferring those shares under her name to me.\"","Old Madam Xie frowned. \"Is it really going that smoothly?\"","Xie Yajun nodded. \"She looks aloof, but in reality, she's desperate for a man. As long as I crook my finger, she'll immediately fall for me. Just wait, Grandma. Once I get the shares of the Ji Group, the Xie family will be saved...\"","\"Good, good, good,\" Old Madam Xie looked relieved. \"The survival of the Xie family all depends on you...\"","Before her voice could even fade.","Bang!","The bedroom door was suddenly pushed open.","When she saw the two people standing at the door, Old Madam Xie's face instantly changed. \"Brother-in-law, why didn't you knock before coming in?\"","Old Master Ji's face was livid to the extreme. \"You... you two are actually scheming for my Ji family's shares?\"","\"Brother-in-law, you must have misheard,\" Old Madam Xie maintained her composure. \"Xie Yajun and I were discussing the handling of the Xie Group's shares. You misunderstood.\"","\"A misunderstanding?\"","Rong Yu turned on the listening device. The voices of the grandmother and grandson conversing—every word, every pause—were broadcasted with crystal clarity.","Xie Yajun abruptly lowered his head.","He looked at his collar; on the underside, there was actually a miniature listening device.","He had thought Rong Yu had taken a fancy to him and intentionally made physical contact, but it turned out she was planting a bug. He pointed at Rong Yu's nose and cursed furiously, \"Fuck you! You actually eavesdropped on me!\"","Old Master Ji raised his hand and delivered a resounding slap to his face. \"You uneducated brat! Who allowed you to point at your elder's nose and curse!\"","Xie Yajun covered his face, feeling extremely wronged. \"Great-uncle, I wasn't cursing at you. I was cursing Rong...\"","\"Shut up!\"","Old Master Ji delivered a backhand slap, shoving him aside, and walked straight up to Old Madam Xie.","Old Madam Xie sat there, suddenly feeling a chill run down her spine.","Her lips were tightly pursed as she said in a deep voice, \"Brother-in-law, you've been bewitched by this little girl. That's why I had Xie Yajun come over—to take back the shares for the Ji family. I was doing this for the good of the Ji family...\"","Old Master Ji abruptly raised a hand, directly cutting off Old Madam Xie's words.","\"Enough!\" His voice was as cold and hard as iron. \"You use the banner of doing what's good for the Ji family, but behind my back, you instigate Xie Yajun to transfer the shares. Do you really think I'm a senile old fool?\"","Old Madam Xie held onto the chair and stood up. \"Brother-in-law, I...\"","\"Old Yu!\" Old Master Ji didn't listen to her defense at all and barked out sharply.","The butler, Old Yu, immediately pushed the door open and entered with two bodyguards, standing expressionlessly behind Old Madam Xie.","\"Pack Old Madam Xie's luggage, arrange a car, and see our guests out.\"","Old Madam Xie violently grabbed Old Master Ji's sleeve. \"Brother-in-law! Are you really this heartless? What did my sister tell you on her deathbed back then? Is this how you treat me?\"","Old Master Ji forcefully shook off her hand, his eyes frighteningly cold. \"If your sister knew you came to scheme against the Ji family, even her coffin lid wouldn't be able to hold her down!\"","Old Yu stepped forward and bowed slightly, his tone respectful yet brooking no refusal. \"Old Madam Xie, please.\"","The two bodyguards stood on either side of Xie Yajun. Although they didn't make a move, their presence exuded an overwhelming sense of pressure.","\"Good, very good!\" Old Madam Xie glared viciously at Rong Yu, her voice cold and sinister. \"The Ji family can now tolerate an outsider walking all over them, yet there is no room for me, your own relative! My sister was truly blind!\"","With that, she flicked her sleeves in a huff and strode outside.","Old Master Ji stood rooted to the spot, his back ramrod straight. Only when the car had driven away did he slowly close his eyes and let out a long sigh. \"Mom, I am sorry.\"","It was all his fault for holding on too tightly to old sentiments.","In the end, all those old ties were torn to shreds, leaving not a single ounce of dignity.","Rong Yu patted him on the back. \"Valuing old relationships is not a mistake. The mistake is that some people take a mile when given an inch. Yingbao, do not dwell on this too much.\""]},{"number":298,"title":"Chapter 298: This is the dream academy for learning","paragraphs":["The two months of summer vacation passed by in a flash.","Rong Yu was admitted early to Huaqing University. Ji Jingchuan, with his excellent result as the top scorer in Haicheng's college entrance examination, was admitted to Jingbei University. Ji Zhouye's grades were a bit worse, but he still managed to get into a regular first-tier university in the capital.","Early on the morning of September 1st, after finishing breakfast, they prepared to head to their schools for registration.","\"Why isn't that brat Ah Ye here yet?\" Old Master Ji glanced at his wristwatch. \"We agreed to leave at 8:30 AM, and it's already 8:35. Forget it, let's not wait for him. It's not like they are going to the same school anyway.\"","As soon as he finished speaking, a car pulled up to the gate.","Ji Zhouye pushed the door open, stepped out, and ran into the courtyard dragging his suitcase. \"Thank goodness, I'm not too late!\"","Rong Yu looked at him.","The boy had dark circles under his eyes, messy hair, and a piece of gauze stuck to his forehead. He looked completely disheveled. She frowned and asked, \"What happened to your head?\"","Ji Zhouye looked nonchalant. \"Last night I went to watch my goddess Yaoyao's live competition and got hit by a falling light fixture. It's just a minor injury, nothing serious. I just stayed up all night without sleeping, so I'm a bit tired...\"","He yawned as he spoke.","\"You were let loose for just over a month, and you've turned into this miserable state again!\" Old Master Ji kicked him. \"No one is dropping you off; go register by yourself!\"","Ji Zhouye shrank his neck. \"I was wrong.\"","Rong Yu spoke up, \"Alright, get in the car. We're leaving.\"","The family got into the car.","The driver first dropped Ji Zhouye off at his school, then Ji Jingchuan, and finally drove to the main entrance of Huaqing University.","The sunlight poured down like melted gold onto the gates of Huaqing University. Rong Yu stood at the entrance, slightly narrowing her eyes as she examined the plaque of this century-old prestigious institution.","The two of them passed through the gates and stepped onto the main road of Huaqing University. Tall, lush old trees lined both sides of the street, their branches and leaves intertwining to form a natural archway. The campus was filled with freshmen dragging their luggage and upperclassmen helping them out. The sound of cheerful laughter brimmed with youthful vitality.","\"This is truly the dream hall of learning,\" Old Master Ji sighed with emotion. \"Back when I went to school, we didn't have such great conditions!\"","The old man was wearing a dark blue Zhongshan suit. Although he was nearly eighty years old, he was hale and hearty, and his eyes were strikingly bright. Among the parents dropping their children off at school, he was certainly the oldest.","He looked around with great interest, much like an overgrown child.","Rong Yu chuckled. She wasn't in a hurry to register, so she took her elderly son for a leisurely stroll around the campus.","\"Look, what a beautiful junior!\"","\"With those looks, she's more than qualified to be the campus belle, right?\"","\"She looks a bit familiar. I think that's Rong Yu, the one who represented Huaxia and won first place in the International Physics Olympiad!\"","\"She was already beautiful on camera, but I didn't expect her to look even better in person!\"","\"Junior, which college are you registering at? Let me carry your suitcase for you...\"","\"Shoo, shoo, get out of here!\" Old Master Ji waved his hands with exaggerated motions, driving away a large group of eager male students. \"You are all the proud sons of Huaqing University. What kind of behavior is this, not being able to walk when you see a pretty girl? Hurry up and go study in the classrooms, kids!\"","One boy braced himself and spoke up, \"I'm a member of the student union, and my task today is to help the freshmen register. Junior Rong Yu, let me take you to the registration area.\"","Rong Yu smiled and nodded. \"Thank you, senior.\"","Old Master Ji curled his lips to the side.","He had wanted to say something, but was stopped by a glance from Rong Yu. Forget it, it really was getting late, and it was time to register.","The three of them made their way through the bustling crowd, walking along the tree-lined path toward the College of Science. Along the way, people kept turning their heads to look, and whispers rose and fell.","\"That must be Rong Yu who's always on the news. She's really beautiful.\"","\"She won a prize in the International Physics Competition, so she must have applied for the Physics Department.\"","\"A girl in the Physics Department, she's truly amazing!\"","Rong Yu turned a deaf ear to these discussions and followed behind the senior with a calm and unhurried pace.","When they reached the College of Science, there were many subdivided majors. The senior stopped and asked, \"Junior, this is the place. Which college and department are you in?\"","Rong Yu replied, \"The Tianxingjian Class.\"","The senior's footsteps came to an abrupt halt, and he almost tripped over his own feet. He turned his head with wide eyes. \"Wh-what? The Tianxingjian Class?\"","This exclamation caused several passing students nearby to stop in their tracks, their shocked gazes uniformly fixed on Rong Yu.","The Tianxingjian Class was a legend at Huaqing University. It only recruited about twenty top geniuses each year, and they were all cultivated to become future leaders in the scientific community.","\"That's impossible...\" A boy wearing thick glasses pushed them up his nose. \"Aren't the students in the Tianxingjian Class all nerds?\"","\"Who are you calling a nerd?\" Old Master Ji immediately bristled with anger. He puffed out his chest and said, \"Our Rong Yu was admitted early to Huaqing because of a special contribution award. She led the Huaxia team to win the gold medal in the International Physics Competition, and she's also the project founder for the innovative application of the new element Shi...\"","Rong Yu coughed several times in a row.","Old Master Ji felt the sharp glare from his own mother, so he could only swallow the rest of his unfinished words.","The senior swallowed his shock and said, \"The T-Tianxingjian Class is over here. Come with me.\"","Rong Yu followed him inside, walking all the way to the innermost area.","At the registration desk was a female teacher in her thirties. She took one look at Rong Yu and immediately recognized her. She smiled and said, \"Welcome to the Tianxingjian Class, student Rong Yu. I will be your counselor from now on. My surname is Cheng, just call me Ms. Cheng. Here is your university ID card, and here is your dorm key. Go to your dorm and settle in first. There's an evening study session tonight at seven o'clock, and we'll formally introduce ourselves then.\"","Rong Yu took the items. \"Thank you, Ms. Cheng.\"","The senior led Rong Yu toward the girls' dormitory building.","When they reached the ground floor, Rong Yu looked at her elderly son who was about to follow her up. She said helplessly, \"Yingbao, dropping me off here is fine. You can go back now, be a good boy.\"","Old Master Ji looked reluctant to part. \"Mom, we agreed you would come home every weekend. You can't break your promise.\"","\"Don't worry.\" Rong Yu assigned him some tasks. \"You must keep up with your morning exercises every day and send me a video to check in. Also, remember to read those books I bought for you...\"","\"Oh, Mom, I know.\" Old Master Ji rubbed his face. \"Then Mom, you go upstairs first.\"","Rong Yu turned around and dragged her suitcase into the dormitory building.","After walking in, she looked back and saw that her elderly son had met up with the bodyguards before she finally went upstairs.","Her dorm was at the end of the corridor on the second floor. She unlocked the door with her key and walked in. It was very spacious, a room for three with three beds. Her other two roommates had already arrived.","Rong Yu had seen the roster. There were a total of twenty-eight students in this year's Tianxingjian Class, and only three of them were girls—the three of them.","She smiled and spoke, \"Hello, I'm Rong Yu.\"","The two girls, who were making their beds, turned their heads.","A slightly chubby girl with straight bangs smiled and said, \"My name is Yu Kexin.\"","The other girl, wearing thick glasses, had an expressionless face. \"I'm Xue Yun.\""]},{"number":299,"title":"Chapter 299: Can I make an on-site nomination I nominate Rong Yu.","paragraphs":["The dorm room was bright and clean.","Outside the second-floor window, the lush, leafy branches of green trees swayed gently in the wind.","Rong Yu's bed was by the window. After making her bed, folding her quilt, and tidying up her desk, she looked up at her two roommates. \"Should we grab lunch together first and then look around the campus?\"","Yu Kexin immediately closed her laptop. \"Sure! When I was registering earlier, I saw a lot of clubs recruiting new members out there. Let's go see what it's all about.\"","Xue Yun kept her eyes glued to the English book in her hands, not even lifting her head as she replied, \"I'm not going.\"","\"Oh, come on, let's go.\" Yu Kexin practically hoisted her up by the arms. \"You've been studying for almost twenty years, aren't you sick of it yet? We finally have a chance to relax. Let's go, let's go together.\"","Xue Yun wasn't used to being held so intimately.","Neither was Rong Yu.","But Yu Kexin seemed completely oblivious to their resistance. Wrapping her left and right arms around each of them, the three walked out of the dorm building looking very close. They grabbed a bite at the cafeteria first and then strolled around the campus.","Various clubs were showing off their unique skills, trying to reel in freshmen from all directions.","Yu Kexin had a bubbly personality; she was interested in everything and wanted to try it all.","Xue Yun, on the other hand, was very interested in the tech and innovation clubs.","Rong Yu looked into the distance. Laughter from the drone club's test flights drifted from a glass-walled academic building. A senior girl holding a laptop brushed past a senior boy explaining model aircraft construction to freshmen in the plaza... Students from seventy years ago could never have imagined that the transmission of knowledge would become so easily accessible.","The three roommates wandered around all afternoon, their relationship advancing by leaps and bounds.","At seven o'clock in the evening, the Tianxingjian Class had its first evening study session.","By the time the three of them arrived at the classroom, most of the students were already there.","As soon as they walked in, a loud voice rang out, \"Rong Yu!\"","Rong Yu looked up and saw Sheng Ciyuan.","She already knew Sheng Ciyuan was in her class, as they had chatted about it before. She gave him a smile.","Sweeping her gaze across the room, she also spotted a few familiar faces.","One was Song Huai, whom she knew all too well.","Another was Ding Zhe, who had participated in the International Physics Olympiad alongside her.","The Tianxingjian Class was a top-tier scientific research talent training program established a few years ago by the dean of Huaqing University. The students in this class were either top scorers in their province's college entrance exams, gold medalists in various academic competitions, or silver and bronze medalists across multiple interdisciplinary fields... In short, anyone who made it into this class was exceptionally brilliant.","\"Hello everyone, I am your counselor. My surname is Cheng, Cheng Rui,\" Cheng Rui said with a smile as she stood at the podium. \"For the rest of your university life, you can come to me with any issues. First, everyone please add my contact info... Next, starting from the first group, please come up to the stage one by one to introduce yourselves.\"","Twenty-eight chosen ones went up on stage one after another to introduce their names, hometowns, and so on. Some were humorous, some were introverted, some were quirky, and some were people of few words... A diverse array of personalities made up this unique Tianxingjian Class.","\"It's a pleasure to meet you all,\" Cheng Rui said, looking out at everyone. \"Next up is the election for class president. Any student who is interested can come up and volunteer themselves.\"","A tall, thin boy was the first to stand up.","As soon as he rose, Yu Kexin whispered, \"Duan Fei. During high school, he participated in scientific research projects, published patent papers, and was featured in international scientific journals...\"","Sitting next to her, Xue Yun silently pushed up her glasses.","She was the top scorer of the college entrance exam in her province. When the results came out, she had been thrilled beyond measure, but upon arriving here, she realized that being a top scorer was nothing worth mentioning.","Because she had no idea how to participate in research projects, let alone what publishing a paper entailed. She hadn't even participated in the Math Olympiad; she was just a bookworm who only knew how to study.","The bookworm had accidentally stumbled into a high-level game, and she needed to work even harder.","Uninterested in running for class president, Xue Yun pulled out a book and lowered her head to read.","\"Hello everyone, I'm Duan Fei,\" the tall boy said as he stepped onto the stage. \"I served as the student council president for all three years of high school. I have management experience and hope to serve you all.\"","Most people knew that serving as a class officer in college meant getting noticed by teachers, which in turn led to more opportunities to get involved in projects. Thus, several students stood up one after another to run for the position.","\"Anyone else?\" Cheng Rui asked. \"If not, we will begin voting.\"","\"Teacher!\" Sheng Ciyuan suddenly stood up. \"Can we make live nominations? I nominate Rong Yu. I believe she has the leadership skills to guide our class to greater heights!\"","As soon as his voice fell, someone chimed in to support him.","Ding Zhe agreed, \"Rong Yu was able to lead her team to win an international award. She definitely has the ability to be the class president!\"","Song Huai pursed his lips.","Back in the elite class at Haicheng No. 1 High School, he had been the class president, but here, he simply didn't have the confidence to run for the position.","He might as well do Rong Yu a favor.","With this in mind, he spoke up, \"I also nominate Rong Yu.\"","Yu Kexin shouted excitedly, \"Yes, choose Rong Yu! I vote for Rong Yu too!\"","Although the students in the class weren't celebrity chasers, they had all more or less seen the news about Rong Yu. She had been specially recruited by the Aerospace Institute, participated in new materials research, and competed in international competitions...","Furthermore, there were only three girls in the class; the rest were all boys.","Boys had absolutely no resistance against beautiful girls, so the vast majority of them joined in the uproar, chanting Rong Yu's name.","The face of Duan Fei, the first to volunteer on stage, visibly darkened.","He just couldn't understand it. In a sacred hall like Huaqing University, in a top-tier talent cultivation program like the Tianxingjian Class, why were there still so many vulgar people...","If Rong Yu's gender were male, or if she were a less attractive girl, with the exact same resume, there was no way she would have such a high approval rating.","\"Quiet, everyone quiet down,\" Cheng Rui said, looking at Rong Yu. \"Rong Yu, what are your thoughts?\"","Rong Yu stood up, her voice clear. \"My energy is limited, and I probably won't be able to spare the time to manage the class. Thank you all for your generous support.\"","She cast a light glance at Sheng Ciyuan.","Sheng Ciyuan shrank his neck with a guilty conscience.","Alright, he got the message. He wouldn't stir up trouble anymore.","Cheng Rui nodded. \"Then, everyone, let's begin the voting.\"","In the end, Duan Fei received the highest number of votes.","But his expression wasn't all that pleased. He pressed his lips tightly together and cast an imperceptible glance at Rong Yu.","This class president title of his was something Rong Yu had given up to him.","Since when did he, Duan Fei, ever need someone else to step aside for him?","\"Congratulations to Duan Fei for becoming our class president.\" Cheng Rui's expression turned serious. \"Tomorrow is the first day of military training. Everyone must strictly abide by the discipline. We will gather on the sports field at six o'clock in the morning. Class president, make sure to do a headcount. Everyone, get a good rest. I hope to see you all full of enthusiasm again tomorrow. That's all for today, class dismissed!\"","As soon as the counselor walked out, the entire class let out a collective groan.","\"Gathering at six o'clock is going to kill me!\"","\"Why do we still have to suffer like this after getting into college?\"","\"Why do we even have military training? Can I ask for a leave of absence...\"","Duan Fei spoke in a calm, even voice, \"Military training is a mandatory requirement for every college student. I hope you all take it seriously and bring honor to our class.\""]},{"number":300,"title":"Chapter 300: Everyone, look to Rong Yu and follow her standard.","paragraphs":["Rong Yu and her roommates walked back to their dormitory under the night sky of Huaqing University.","Just as they opened the dorm door, Yu Kexin suddenly let out a scream.","\"Rong Yu, look at this!\" she said with intense excitement. \"The school forum is voting for the new campus beauty, and you made the list! You're currently in ninth place!\"","Rong Yu frowned. \"Huaqing University actually does this kind of thing?\"","Xue Yun also looked puzzled. \"What's the point of electing a campus beauty?\"","\"You two are such dinosaurs. What university doesn't elect a campus beauty nowadays?\" Yu Kexin casually cast a vote for Rong Yu. \"This is the face of the school. In the future, the campus beauty will play a major role in Huaqing's promotional events, student recruitment, and various performances and galas.\"","Xue Yun looked up. \"Isn't this just objectifying women as ornamental items? This kind of activity should have been banned a long time ago.\"","Rong Yu deeply agreed.","Yu Kexin suddenly felt that the whole thing was rather meaningless.","The night was as calm as water, the dormitory was quiet, and Rong Yu slept soundly.","Early the next morning, they were awakened by the campus broadcast. A new day had begun.","When Rong Yu opened her eyes, the sky outside the window was still a pale grayish-blue. She got up and found that Xue Yun was already awake, sitting at her desk reading a book. Judging by her focus, she must have finished washing up before five o'clock.","Meanwhile, Yu Kexin was still fast asleep under her covers.","Rong Yu tugged at her blanket. \"Fifteen minutes until assembly.\"","Yu Kexin climbed out of bed, whining.","The three of them finished washing up, changed into their military training uniforms, and quickly ran to the sports field.","It was September. The sun had barely risen, but the heat wave was already hitting them. Standing among her classmates, Rong Yu could clearly feel the sweat rolling down her spine, pooling at the belt buckle on her waist and instantly soaking a patch of her clothes.","Sheng Ciyuan ran over and whispered to her, \"Rong Yu, can your body handle this? If you can't, my family can get a doctor to write you a sick note...\"","Rong Yu shook her head. \"It's just military training, it's nothing.\"","She was someone who had come from that era where almost everyone joined the army. This level of military training intensity was truly nothing to her; it even allowed her to reminisce about the arduous years of the past.","\"Attention all! Prepare for military posture!\"","The instructor's voice suddenly exploded. Everyone jolted in fright and hastily stood up straight.","The instructor wasn't old, looking to be in his early twenties. He had dark skin and an imposing aura. He said coldly, \"I am your instructor for this military training. My surname is Yan.\"","He paced to the front of the formation, his shoes making dull thuds on the field. \"Yan, as in strict.\"","\"Head up! Chest out!\" Instructor Yan pressed down on Song Huai's shoulder. \"With this soft and weak posture of yours, you'd be the first to be taken prisoner when the enemy comes!\"","As soon as he finished speaking, someone in the formation laughed out loud.","The instructor's voice was icy. \"What are you laughing at? The rest of you are the same. Stand properly! Let me see who dares to move even an inch.\"","The entire square formation instantly fell dead silent. Even the cicadas seemed to be frightened off by his reprimand. Only the sounds of rising and falling breaths, and the grinding of teeth, remained.","Instructor Yan paced to the center of the formation, his gaze coldly sweeping over everyone.","As time ticked by, the sun rose higher and grew hotter. Everyone was covered in sweat, and their postures began to waver.","\"You, step forward!\"","Instructor Yan suddenly stood in front of Rong Yu and spoke loudly.","Rong Yu took a step forward and stood in front of the formation.","Instructor Yan: \"Name?\"","Rong Yu: \"Reporting to the instructor, my name is Rong Yu.\"","Instructor Yan looked at her with appreciation.","From the very beginning, he had noticed that although this girl had a slender figure, her standing posture was as straight as a javelin. Her shoulder line, hip line, and heels formed a perfect straight line, flawlessly meeting military standards.","What was even more rare was that after standing under the blazing sun for thirty minutes, her eyes were still clear and spirited.","Instructor Yan spoke, \"Everyone, look to Rong Yu and follow her standard. Those who can't do it, prepare for push-ups!\"","Song Huai's face looked a bit ugly.","He had been criticized by the instructor for being soft, while Rong Yu was held up as the gold standard.","In terms of academics, he had lost to Rong Yu.","In terms of physical fitness, he was still inferior to her...","Just then, a sudden, dull thud came from nearby.","They saw Yu Kexin pitch forward stiffly. Her eyes were tightly shut, and a few loose strands of hair were plastered to her pale cheeks by sweat.","\"Someone fainted!\"","The formation instantly broke into a commotion.","\"Silence!\" Instructor Yan said coldly. \"Everyone, maintain your military posture!\"","He dashed over to Yu Kexin in a single stride, dropping to one knee. He pressed three fingers against her carotid artery and deftly peeled back her eyelids with his other hand.","\"Heatstroke.\" Instructor Yan turned his head. \"Class Monitor, step forward. Rong Yu, step forward. You two, take her to the infirmary for treatment.\"","Rong Yu helped Yu Kexin up, and Duan Fei hoisted her onto his back. The two of them quickly headed toward the infirmary.","The corridor of the infirmary was crowded with people. Some were freshmen in their military training uniforms, huddled together scrolling through their phones, smiling cheerfully without looking sick in the slightest.","Duan Fei let out a cold laugh. He tossed Yu Kexin onto a hospital bed.","The jolt made Yu Kexin let out a muffled groan.","\"Putting on a pretty good act.\" Duan Fei looked around. \"A whole room full of drama queens.\"","Rong Yu looked up coldly. \"What do you mean?\"","\"Isn't she just faking sick?\" Duan Fei wore an impatient expression. \"If you ask me, some people should just get a sick note and skip the entire military training, saving us from being dragged down during the final performance.\"","Yu Kexin had just opened her eyes when she heard these words. Tears immediately welled up, and she choked out, \"I'm not, I really don't feel well...\"","Rong Yu asked the doctor to come over and check.","After the examination, the doctor said, \"Her temperature is thirty-eight degrees Celsius. Mild heatstroke. She needs to rest for at least two hours. I'll write you a sick note.\"","Rong Yu's voice was frigid. \"Class Monitor, you call this faking sick?\"","Duan Fei was speechless.","He had seen girls from other classes faking illnesses, so he instinctively assumed that Yu Kexin was faking it too.","\"Severe heatstroke can develop into heat exhaustion and cause organ failure. Does the Class Monitor not even have this basic common sense?\" Rong Yu enunciated every word clearly. \"Apologize.\"","Duan Fei remained silent for a moment before speaking. \"I'm sorry.\"","He put on his military cap, turned around, and walked out.","\"Rong, what courage.\"","A voice spoke in broken Chinese.","Rong Yu turned around and saw a familiar face. It was actually the Japanese student, Sato. A few months ago, at the International Physics Competition in Hong Kong, she and Sato had had a rather unpleasant falling out.","\"I didn't expect that I would be able to become your schoolmate.\" Sato wore a warm smile and spoke fluently in Japanese, \"I am an international student at Huaqing, so I don't need to participate in military training. I will cheer for you in spirit, Rong. After the military training is over, I'll treat you to Japanese food. I hope we can become good friends.\"","Rong Yu shrugged. \"I have plenty of friends. I'm not missing one like you.\"","She had no desire to be friends with someone from Japan; just seeing him was annoying enough."]}]);
